{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is mandatory present when the field msgA-IntraSlotFrequencyHopping is configured. Otherwise, the field is absent.","paragraph_zero_based":25560},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"GroupBConfigured","paragraph_zero_based":25561},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present if groupB-ConfiguredTwoStepRA is configured in RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA, otherwise the field is absent.","paragraph_zero_based":25562},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"InitialBWPConfig","paragraph_zero_based":25563},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present when MsgA-ConfigCommon is configured for the initial uplink BWP, or when MsgA-ConfigCommon is configured for a non-initial uplink BWP and MsgA-ConfigCommon is not configured for the initial uplink BWP, otherwise the field is optionally present, Need S.","paragraph_zero_based":25564},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":25565},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–MultiFrequencyBandListNR","paragraph_zero_based":25566},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE MultiFrequencyBandListNR is used to configure a list of one or multiple NR frequency bands.","paragraph_zero_based":25567},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MultiFrequencyBandListNR information element","paragraph_zero_based":25568},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":25569},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-MULTIFREQUENCYBANDLISTNR-START","paragraph_zero_based":25570},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":25571},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MultiFrequencyBandListNR ::=        SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofMultiBands)) OF FreqBandIndicatorNR","paragraph_zero_based":25572},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":25573},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-MULTIFREQUENCYBANDLISTNR-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":25574},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":25575},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":25576},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–MultiFrequencyBandListNR-SIB","paragraph_zero_based":25577},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE MultiFrequencyBandListNR-SIB indicates the list of frequency bands, for which cell (re-)selection parameters are common, and a list of additionalPmax and additionalSpectrumEmission.","paragraph_zero_based":25578},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MultiFrequencyBandListNR-SIB information element","paragraph_zero_based":25579},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":25580},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-MULTIFREQUENCYBANDLISTNR-SIB-START","paragraph_zero_based":25581},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":25582},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MultiFrequencyBandListNR-SIB ::=            SEQUENCE (SIZE (1.. maxNrofMultiBands)) OF NR-MultiBandInfo","paragraph_zero_based":25583}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["d7a815d7c3f283c1d24ebbf8aefb4967de9d460057850a2543f38ce99de80ca9","ee27ce5a1997235bd29696eca4e5d1d4351f18f7b4626fc97aed37fa996ea3a8","0f3efa8c6c293214f425bed16ef28e233912085fe5ceafa1fd0da06d55d89815","56efcacad5488503303b1f7b26f26448c69f05adf62a3457615c2e0e6f024769","dc7298f92deaef9fd583fb1501e83492b9c4d6b5e168a2d29e23221b597dfde2","6ababacb0e859c768cea679addd6d6424d31d318a9368e4fe05bf9022d26e605","994fca001beb53cbc3b47025ba0bec9f61e4e37d74af584c53708fbd6760c8e3","fe697d439d71680cc975d5e0b5befce351989c4fb67c14b13fcf3bc7738e827f","2ab0c1f14c8446b8bc4a5034dcc7b97eb9bd7e6b88b