{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":26904},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–PCI-Range","paragraph_zero_based":26905},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE PCI-Range is used to encode either a single or a range of physical cell identities. The range is encoded by using a start value and by indicating the number of consecutive physical cell identities (including start) in the range. For fields comprising multiple occurrences of PCI-Range, the Network may configure overlapping ranges of physical cell identities.","paragraph_zero_based":26906},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PCI-Range information element","paragraph_zero_based":26907},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":26908},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PCI-RANGE-START","paragraph_zero_based":26909},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":26910},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PCI-Range ::=                       SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":26911},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    start                               PhysCellId,","paragraph_zero_based":26912},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    range                               ENUMERATED {n4, n8, n12, n16, n24, n32, n48, n64, n84,","paragraph_zero_based":26913},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                    n96, n128, n168, n252, n504, n1008,spare1}                  OPTIONAL    -- Need S","paragraph_zero_based":26914},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":26915},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":26916},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PCI-RANGE-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":26917},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":26918},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":26919},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PCI-Range field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":26920},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"range","paragraph_zero_based":26921},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the number of physical cell identities in the range (including start). Value n4 corresponds with 4, value n8 corresponds with 8 and so on. The UE shall apply value 1 in case the field is absent, in which case only the physical cell identity value indicated by start applies.","paragraph_zero_based":26922},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"start","paragraph_zero_based":26923},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the lowest physical cell identity in the range.","paragraph_zero_based":26924},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":26925},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–PCI-RangeElement","paragraph_zero_based":26926},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE PCI-RangeElement is used to define a PCI-Range as part of a list (e.g. AddMod list).","paragraph_zero_based":26927}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["06ef309915ea37689e6700a883ae9b93b1d2b6435aa021c55a686155305190eb","2febda320ce8709afe095b4e263967faa78508c403ff0c28c55bf5c20af86c5f","8daea38505eae20c528506bcc5884214c4e33b103f7bb918d9a68fe18da42f82","8ade5a34741fdb9094f7eeaa4d17dc2ae980c8fad7f952aa4ab2c88a75f03bde","94d1c0d83693de9b2dba9b9e738a79c99009d65e8c674b633fd372290d63aef2","cc0103063626dddd6177d943cc8d2130ce1c551c28c961265ce85cba8b448b3b","7117a4655999be17f3ea0a52697b6ed5889ccb9ff761e491ec17d878898f4eb7","e7ededde60c3e373610c23c51d2743f6e27c007729081673dc1c4c58eda09c0f","04645bbdbb00342dcaacc31e7e3253689ee80ea7b80bacd60a4fdd48de0b2c59","a2fb10b998eb41d7499817028b4c976fd36a45bf2792288f0