{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28416},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PTRS-DOWNLINKCONFIG-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":28417},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":28418},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28419},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PTRS-DownlinkConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":28420},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"epre-Ratio","paragraph_zero_based":28421},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EPRE ratio between PTRS and PDSCH. Value 0 corresponds to the codepoint \"00\" in table 4.1-2. Value 1 corresponds to codepoint \"01\", and so on. If the field is not provided, the UE applies value 0 (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 4.1).","paragraph_zero_based":28422},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"frequencyDensity","paragraph_zero_based":28423},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Presence and frequency density of DL PT-RS as a function of Scheduled BW. If the field is absent, the UE uses K_PT-RS = 2 (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.6.3, table 5.1.6.3-2).","paragraph_zero_based":28424},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"maxNrofPorts","paragraph_zero_based":28425},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The maximum number of DL PTRS ports specified in TS 38.214 [19] (clause 5.1.6.3). 2 PT-RS ports can only be configured for a DL BWP that is configured, as specified in TS 38.214 [19] clause 5.1, with a mode where a single PDSCH has association between the DM-RS ports and the TCI states as defined in TS 38.214 [19] clause 5.1.6.2.","paragraph_zero_based":28426},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"resourceElementOffset","paragraph_zero_based":28427},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the subcarrier offset for DL PTRS. If the field is absent, the UE applies the value offset00 (see TS 38.211 [16], clause 7.4.1.2.2).","paragraph_zero_based":28428},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"timeDensity","paragraph_zero_based":28429},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Presence and time density of DL PT-RS as a function of MCS. The value 29 is only applicable for MCS Table 5.1.3.1-1 (TS 38.214 [19]). If the field is absent, the UE uses L_PT-RS = 1 (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.6.3, table 5.1.6.3-1).","paragraph_zero_based":28430},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28431},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–PTRS-UplinkConfig","paragraph_zero_based":28432},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE PTRS-UplinkConfig is used to configure uplink Phase-Tracking-Reference-Signals (PTRS).","paragraph_zero_based":28433},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PTRS-UplinkConfig information element","paragraph_zero_based":28434},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":28435},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PTRS-UPLINKCONFIG-START","paragraph_zero_based":28436},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28437},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PTRS-UplinkConfig ::=                   SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":28438},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    transformPrecoderDisabled               SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":28439}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ec3d295430b24a9d73cdfc410ef5cc13d484b56da81e4ccf62236213d573bc53","6051a0b9816c494133fed9a4d6cb438054b4fbb054937a7f4ccc2b9481f53936","4432309404d9d3a844b8cef4667932f3cbea25a939f8488d61edab6bed197346","e0067d1abdb217226bec1a48380c17c39a36311e1d28de38f8ee32d0c4e5e97f","a57dc256274b457863083a2797284f1c19a4981f12baa74ae96d8506202d6ce5","37687ca34dbee75a8a5916707807a852e2e7f6