{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pucch-Resource","paragraph_zero_based":28872},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PUCCH resource for the associated uplink BWP. Only PUCCH-Resource of format 2, 3 and 4 is supported. The actual PUCCH-Resource is configured in PUCCH-Config and referred to by its ID. When two PUCCH-Config are configured within PUCCH-ConfigurationList, PUCCH-ResourceId in a PUCCH-CSI-Resource refers to a PUCCH-Resource in the PUCCH-Config used for HARQ-ACK with low priority.","paragraph_zero_based":28873},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28874},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–PUCCH-PathlossReferenceRS-Id","paragraph_zero_based":28875},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE PUCCH-PathlossReferenceRS-Id is an ID for a reference signal (RS) configured as PUCCH pathloss reference (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 7.2).","paragraph_zero_based":28876},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PUCCH-PathlossReferenceRS-Id information element","paragraph_zero_based":28877},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":28878},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PUCCH-PATHLOSSREFERENCERS-ID-START","paragraph_zero_based":28879},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28880},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PUCCH-PathlossReferenceRS-Id ::=            INTEGER (0..maxNrofPUCCH-PathlossReferenceRSs-1)","paragraph_zero_based":28881},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28882},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PUCCH-PathlossReferenceRS-Id-v1610 ::=      INTEGER (maxNrofPUCCH-PathlossReferenceRSs..maxNrofPUCCH-PathlossReferenceRSs-1-r16)","paragraph_zero_based":28883},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28884},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PUCCH-PathlossReferenceRS-Id-r17 ::=        INTEGER (0..maxNrofPUCCH-PathlossReferenceRSs-1-r17)","paragraph_zero_based":28885},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28886},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PUCCH-PATHLOSSREFERENCERS-ID-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":28887},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":28888},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28889},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–PUCCH-PowerControl","paragraph_zero_based":28890},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE PUCCH-PowerControl is used to configure UE-specific parameters for the power control of PUCCH.","paragraph_zero_based":28891},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PUCCH-PowerControl information element","paragraph_zero_based":28892},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":28893},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PUCCH-POWERCONTROL-START","paragraph_zero_based":28894},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PUCCH-PowerControl ::=              SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":28895}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["f826fcd0495aa29c5b7eff0ae15a37417ef786098b8a4bfef4248ffa4c8ff4da","4cc867c9bfd7991213ff9563b97862cdd7ac114769fe8d2e4a99cc3cf4394b2e","b3b335c51ea83bd87c4a5922584a6e1eef386d0df0d254ebe76dcdc33d8ab708","49c6278c00347f8901157fc39ca597cebe338eddda4543a52058851a54177e2d","11dc72ab7fb6f6f89593157e2c7921af830ece118b9895fd9677900b6c5fec56","7faf2422a2c16bc56f6859e9e5906ddac973a574159106526d69def0f3536a2f","456442f418f09f1c2f2cba7073e4f62ba803f036975121d72d64a5e237d7c94a","0ba29c1d965dc1d44c15ea835ae6524d2a53871ed2ed32cf85ef6b81cc8fc41a","5772c8d25bfbd7cd4d0c63a0870334f5b1242c01865ddb4c51771ff9cfbfcfda","f93e56ac8cd440a12417fa9455a6fd682c2f734b8f5638a2f08c