{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":29784},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SUL-Only","paragraph_zero_based":29785},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is optionally present, Need R, if supplementaryUplink is configured within ServingCellConfig. It is absent otherwise.","paragraph_zero_based":29786},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SUL","paragraph_zero_based":29787},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is optionally present, Need R, if supplementaryUplink is configured within ServingCellConfig. It is mandatory present otherwise.","paragraph_zero_based":29788},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":29789},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–Q-OffsetRange","paragraph_zero_based":29790},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE Q-OffsetRange is used to indicate a cell, beam or measurement object specific offset to be applied when evaluating candidates for cell re-selection or when evaluating triggering conditions for measurement reporting. The value is in dB. Value dB-24 corresponds to -24 dB, dB-22 corresponds to -22 dB and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":29791},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Q-OffsetRange information element","paragraph_zero_based":29792},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":29793},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-Q-OFFSETRANGE-START","paragraph_zero_based":29794},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":29795},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Q-OffsetRange ::=                   ENUMERATED {","paragraph_zero_based":29796},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                dB-24, dB-22, dB-20, dB-18, dB-16, dB-14,","paragraph_zero_based":29797},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                dB-12, dB-10, dB-8, dB-6, dB-5, dB-4, dB-3,","paragraph_zero_based":29798},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                dB-2, dB-1, dB0, dB1, dB2, dB3, dB4, dB5,","paragraph_zero_based":29799},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                dB6, dB8, dB10, dB12, dB14, dB16, dB18,","paragraph_zero_based":29800},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                dB20, dB22, dB24}","paragraph_zero_based":29801},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":29802},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-Q-OFFSETRANGE-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":29803},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":29804},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":29805},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–Q-QualMin","paragraph_zero_based":29806},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE Q-QualMin is used to indicate for cell selection/ re-selection the required minimum received RSRQ level in the (NR) cell. Corresponds to parameter Qqualmin in TS 38.304 [20]. Actual value Qqualmin = field value [dB].","paragraph_zero_based":29807}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["6a8f9d39ab144d1191dc85c167743c3571769a31cccfd69c3bb6e837ef09a9cc","2ee8fb3740b16d42da352890c70105103a7d99d5a04d971540c30fab728c7898","fee4b37a401560cfe2338d95fa09c969bfe9be5494a09858a2b66df96b577c85","e529d3fe2f504f5ed62108bc8e29bfeed7316b1c8aac8865c908e1598adbeb5a","4d6d1893a3495985c163a5a2e93edcbef7ea2afcba70cb0c57c0b28a3e1c4919","fcaa61d4573d7a64708f23ee148b27c3be83064691ca00d70a4b6aaa72b5d495","20e62eff7f3a5ff09487e8b520b5ecf11393b63338c6e6fdda2dbb6ff1d7ff72","b525ce5c7f8d2264db3e08cc5814b1be13e58b7a