{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        four                                                 INTEGER (1..16),","paragraph_zero_based":30024},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        eight                                                INTEGER (1..8),","paragraph_zero_based":30025},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        sixteen                                              INTEGER (1..4)","paragraph_zero_based":30026},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    }                                                                                                                   OPTIONAL, -- Cond 2StepOnly","paragraph_zero_based":30027},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    msgA-CB-PreamblesPerSSB-PerSharedRO-r16              INTEGER (1..60)                                                OPTIONAL, -- Cond SharedRO","paragraph_zero_based":30028},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    msgA-SSB-SharedRO-MaskIndex-r16                      INTEGER (1..15)                                                OPTIONAL, -- Need S","paragraph_zero_based":30029},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    groupB-ConfiguredTwoStepRA-r16                       GroupB-ConfiguredTwoStepRA-r16                                 OPTIONAL, -- Need S","paragraph_zero_based":30030},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    msgA-PRACH-RootSequenceIndex-r16                     CHOICE {","paragraph_zero_based":30031},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        l839                                                 INTEGER (0..837),","paragraph_zero_based":30032},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        l139                                                 INTEGER (0..137),","paragraph_zero_based":30033},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        l571                                                 INTEGER (0..569),","paragraph_zero_based":30034},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        l1151                                                INTEGER (0..1149)","paragraph_zero_based":30035},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    }                                                                                                                   OPTIONAL, -- Cond 2StepOnly","paragraph_zero_based":30036},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    msgA-TransMax-r16                                    ENUMERATED {n1, n2, n4, n6, n8, n10, n20, n50, n100, n200}     OPTIONAL, -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":30037},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    msgA-RSRP-Threshold-r16                              RSRP-Range                                                     OPTIONAL, -- Cond 2Step4Step","paragraph_zero_based":30038},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    msgA-RSRP-ThresholdSSB-r16                           RSRP-Range                                                     OPTIONAL, -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":30039},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    msgA-SubcarrierSpacing-r16                           SubcarrierSpacing                                              OPTIONAL, -- Cond 2StepOnlyL139","paragraph_zero_based":30040},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    msgA-RestrictedSetConfig-r16                         ENUMERATED {unrestrictedSet, restrictedSetTypeA,","paragraph_zero_based":30041},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                                     restrictedSetTypeB}                                OPTIONAL, -- Cond 2StepOnly","paragraph_zero_based":30042},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ra-PrioritizationForAccessIdentityTwoStep-r16        SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":30043},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        ra-Prioritization-r16                                RA-Prioritization,","paragraph_zero_based":30044},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        ra-PrioritizationForAI-r16                           BIT STRING (SIZE (2))","paragraph_zero_based":30045},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    }                                                                                                                   OPTIONAL, -- Cond InitialBWP-Only","paragraph_zero_based":30046},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ra-ContentionResolutionTimer-r16                     ENUMERATED {sf8, sf16, sf24, sf32, sf40, sf48, sf56, sf64}     OPTIONAL, -- Cond 2StepOnly","paragraph_zero_based":30047}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["670cef667fadd9cd50c518420f4efdb12d4627f848c838bb62a4ceae5f4b7c9e","2889fa7808eb6197dd31f62e26a7a5ce025d7522d8aaf439fa21f325c0dd1976","531e99564b02cddd0bb34feec4b55b628b144b746fbb04a93c04a8e212a65ec5","59146fd88649e82b1be795401aa32e229699bbf4678d0ccbeb404efa295496e6","33d744e1a5e0c61605352fe100c64bc26e235abf956b6f18652fbb8d66289d33","a941a857b0a03cdd10540a260940a2011ae309f0cb8ae015cefa825cd0d0ea2c","a9a7888b14cd4df96ed07b538c87d3dcf8e246581efb339b8b813aa842c3ea8a","b60511c17f7aa337da976b145cfa088e26efdd1608e76c316d1bf9e6bf9b0254","82cc6e3eec543c2ceb069b15acd08a21c3252e5a5f49bf2ff1e87aaebc613b04","891fafdd6cb35be161d83207ae35239b052bc2cf38b5ea6903fefa881e02504b","c3d7ac40760c84512e605ac3ef060909724b0d84ef7df760b4f983e7a50e84b5","a318763c554cc84c8bdd7e8f5a3933f161541aae4cf46768b4c0858a673a7e1f","988f51a8eef314e2712a1e8615b1aa356d9356a47a2e493628bdf0dc7b44fb55","036f8ce7047cf6fcc5ddfafba4f3ebf46f104e16ef138de3fccc4ac8db073a49","b7dae0a7e44967f2178098784bb58b4090d07a6c1a78401c9e2851d68de76c6c","549e60d71e09792d82d376b210e26bef55cff1484fe5f227e3608347efcc6af1","deb1a68ed5a2230d01d4426e55187b1bb233cdaefc14b537e83af51a2f518866","e865d82c6ce30213401bff19f42d39792c973e9435cf0d0adea7b89d7b4af87c","1b6b14999c4f3b4603d7a9dd650eb360986a3e2d197467b572c9ccbfa1fcd0a5","314557b07fead26aea2e4b3c6a54182e60d53737ae2002b48b31e97be22205a8","29171f45820e442da655d7c29689b51877cde83f761ea0bbb11490fe210666e9","98e54392e79045cd57d22d12b965240a65937e3b28be986a5a26f1339f253343","97d5ce81b79306e82b0ff18ce9c7ed4214105a83a9b6555ce7d21ad082ed3904","33dc0215fb460af2ebc2e6523fa9aeabeae8f8095bc05f4840bf89b8ea60c81c"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[30024,30047],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx:p30024"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ...,","paragraph_zero_based":30048},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    [[","paragraph_zero_based":30049},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ra-PrioritizationForSlicingTwoStep-r17               RA-PrioritizationForSlicing-r17              OPTIONAL, -- Cond InitialBWP-Only","paragraph_zero_based":30050},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    featureCombinationPreamblesList-r17 SEQUENCE (SIZE(1..maxFeatureCombPreamblesPerRACHResource-r17)) OF FeatureCombinationPreambles-r17 OPTIONAL  -- Cond AdditionalRACH","paragraph_zero_based":30051},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ]]","paragraph_zero_based":30052},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":30053},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30054},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"GroupB-ConfiguredTwoStepRA-r16 ::=                       SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":30055},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ra-MsgA-SizeGroupA-r16                               ENUMERATED {b56, b144, b208, b256, b282, b480, b640, b800,","paragraph_zero_based":30056},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                                     b1000, b72, spare6, spare5, spare4, spare3, spare2, spare1},","paragraph_zero_based":30057},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    messagePowerOffsetGroupB-r16                         ENUMERATED {minusinfinity, dB0, dB5, dB8, dB10, dB12, dB15, dB18},","paragraph_zero_based":30058},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    numberOfRA-PreamblesGroupA-r16                       INTEGER (1..64)","paragraph_zero_based":30059},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":30060},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30061},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-RACH-CONFIGCOMMONTWOSTEPRA-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":30062},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":30063},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30064},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":30065},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"featureCombinationPreamblesList","paragraph_zero_based":30066},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Specifies a series of preamble partitions each associated to a combination of features and 2-step RA. The network does not configure this list to have more than 16 entries.","paragraph_zero_based":30067},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"groupB-ConfiguredTwoStepRA","paragraph_zero_based":30068},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Preamble grouping for 2-step random access type. If the field is absent then there is only one preamble group configured and only one msgA PUSCH configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":30069},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-CB-PreamblesPerSSB-PerSharedRO","paragraph_zero_based":30070},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Number of contention-based preambles used for 2-step RA type from the non-CBRA 4-step type preambles associated with each SSB for RO shared with 4-step type RA. The number of preambles for 2-step RA type shall not exceed the number of preambles per SSB minus the number of contention-based preambles per SSB for 4-step type RA. The possible value range for this parameter needs to be aligned with value range for the configured SSBs per RACH occasion in ssb-perRACH-OccasionAndCB-PreamblesPerSSB in RACH-ConfigCommon. The field is only applicable for the case of shared ROs with 4-step type random access.","paragraph_zero_based":30071}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["7471c6d214ada31ae0d725bcc7b0dc4be725211e66ff8a7d4249895579905177","2dd0fad9f7cf34671d9dcfd9d8d6d6554cd53d71cb6d1a25a51570d3b8360290","93a1484f5f9d118ea005138062a4affe7d7dab8edd56da3d34340d75c5859c52","1e4910d20153d825152ae67a70eafba64a98c6b8460bfeaa5f10773230f282cc","8d20d79c571275cbbfe1e6b0986b59961d40b2058159c0d906424a0d4fcb39a6","8ff88ca3f74a5c7977f34792ed18b0f60ca7b0761c12f07e9348cb0893126546","e25d54c7c9d2fe32c878ff63094b7ce656274a800fc48a0728353d3f9b4d0579","759d28dcedc9bbcfd86120edc71ceb625f61c716d9b21c1a17f243f712d78f5e","651292053ee9d8aa89340a2c89ce60d7549c3cf4920926284b1035a71ba8bc20","c4058f586dfacbe855839b84cfab1029f9f85acce1f9399019345f0070b35e44","80ce7c1e30a3101b06c6a36b6db71134024cfce6a5e70c943caa42c78c116212","0339705b53f41d10e87b2062b0dca18822a9546a8a7f2c771428ea1351c3b0c6","5825fa01f8ec664a790ef62f4610791087c6a8d9e7a621eb149f717c6c6437df","681df347e24da8f1153544828193bab53025281ff1e860c767d3662e30a6e520","7b49e7a50beedd947feddc0148bceb18c3940aed0800bf2e1551621b1e922989","ffad7b72cdbd56f27f23c9cfbf694b4bd911ab48702176344be8228dc3d3586e","cbdb0d85bf2377fe41aad24cbb654fa07868649456d3bb3f0f4eed297e5f846e","5009d27e9be9bc971dfd1d3da00b1e90860cc114b03598eeef13562f7a8497ad","4762a80f36a35eea68b20a2dd686e2acf8e01d2beb9c7363e04d72bbf707563e","876e386315a1efd1265c659e52e0c184565b2e2835c4d10df9d2c9d6a88cda5b","39fcaff6334e36b222205aaf5573af3b78e7cdb2a98b94c205354f80f1b70b38","2948005ce50ab2fb78548ed13431fe0de5dfecb8bc294b514ddfbdb125f7edfa","8c35a7b66bbcae51fdc3426d71a68717b3c5309a7f9d7af832ce5af8f46e117a","c888f0b702598fede46cf0ac8b2ef11105ab93d2472b401cdaa51f5b2c15a9eb"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[30048,30071],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx:p30048"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-PRACH-RootSequenceIndex","paragraph_zero_based":30072},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PRACH root sequence index. If the field is not configured in RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA which is configured directly within a BWP (i.e., not within AdditionalRACH-Config), the UE applies the value in field prach-RootSequenceIndex in RACH-ConfigCommon in the configured BWP. If the field is absent in RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA in AdditionalRACH-Config, the UE applies the corresponding value of prach-RootSequenceIndex in RACH-ConfigCommon in the same AdditionalRACH-Config. When both 2-step and 4-step type random access is configured, this field is only configured for the case of separate ROs between 2-step and 4-step type random access.","paragraph_zero_based":30073},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For FR2-2, only the following values are applicable depending on the used subcarrier spacing:","paragraph_zero_based":30074},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"120 kHz:  L=139, L=571, and L=1151","paragraph_zero_based":30075},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"480 kHz:  L=139, and L=571","paragraph_zero_based":30076},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"960 kHz:  L=139","paragraph_zero_based":30077},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-RestrictedSetConfig","paragraph_zero_based":30078},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configuration of an unrestricted set or one of two types of restricted sets for 2-step random access type preamble. If the field is not configured in RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA which is configured directly within a BWP (i.e. not within AdditionalRACH-Config), the UE applies the value in field restrictedSetConfig in RACH-ConfigCommon in the configured BWP. If the field is absent in RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA in AdditionalRACH-Config, the UE applies the value of restrictedSetConfig in RACH-ConfigCommon in the same AdditionalRACH-Config. When both 2-step and 4-step type random access is configured, this field is only configured for the case of separate ROs between 2-step and 4-step type random access.","paragraph_zero_based":30079},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-RSRP-Threshold","paragraph_zero_based":30080},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE selects 2-step random access type to perform random access based on this threshold (see TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.1.1). This field is only present if both 2-step and 4-step RA type are configured for the BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":30081},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-RSRP-ThresholdSSB","paragraph_zero_based":30082},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UE may select the SS block and corresponding PRACH resource for path-loss estimation and (re)transmission based on SS blocks that satisfy the threshold (see TS 38.213 [13]).","paragraph_zero_based":30083},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-SSB-PerRACH-OccasionAndCB-PreamblesPerSSB","paragraph_zero_based":30084},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The meaning of this field is twofold: the CHOICE conveys the information about the number of SSBs per RACH occasion. Value oneEight corresponds to one SSB associated with 8 RACH occasions, value oneFourth corresponds to one SSB associated with 4 RACH occasions, and so on. The ENUMERATED part indicates the number of Contention Based preambles per SSB. Value n4 corresponds to 4 Contention Based preambles per SSB, value n8 corresponds to 8 Contention Based preambles per SSB, and so on. The total number of CB preambles in a RACH occasion is given by CB-preambles-per-SSB * max(1, SSB-per-rach-occasion). If the field is not configured in RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA which is configured directly within a BWP (i.e. not within AdditionalRACH-Config) and both 2-step and 4-step are configured for the BWP, the UE applies the value in the field ssb-perRACH-OccasionAndCB-PreamblesPerSSB in RACH-ConfigCommon. If the field is not configured in AdditionalRACH-Config and both 2-step and 4-step are configured in AdditionalRACH-Config, the UE applies the value in the field ssb-perRACH-OccasionAndCB-PreamblesPerSSB in RACH-ConfigCommon in the same AdditionalRACH-Config. The field is not present when RACH occasions are shared between 2-step and 4-step type random access in the BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":30085},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-SSB-SharedRO-MaskIndex","paragraph_zero_based":30086},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the subset of 4-step type ROs shared with 2-step random access type for each SSB. This field is configured when there is more than one RO per SSB. If the field is absent, and 4-step and 2-step has shared ROs, then all ROs are shared.","paragraph_zero_based":30087},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-SubcarrierSpacing","paragraph_zero_based":30088},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Subcarrier spacing of PRACH (see TS 38.211 [16], clause 5.3.2).","paragraph_zero_based":30089},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Only the following values are applicable depending on the used frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":30090},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR1:    15 or 30 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":30091},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR2-1:  60 or 120 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":30092},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR2-2:  120, 480, or 960 kHz.","paragraph_zero_based":30093},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the field is absent, the UE applies the SCS as derived from the msgA-PRACH-ConfigurationIndex in RACH-ConfigGenericTwoStepRA (see tables Table 6.3.3.1-1, Table 6.3.3.1-2, Table 6.3.3.2-2 and Table 6.3.3.2-3, TS 38.211 [16]) in case of 2-step only BWP, otherwise the UE applies the same SCS as Msg1 derived from RACH-ConfigCommon. The value also applies to contention free 2-step random access type (RACH-ConfigDedicated).","paragraph_zero_based":30094},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-TotalNumberOfRA-Preambles","paragraph_zero_based":30095}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["97346e5e1ad5d6b5e9bc84f04f38dd963d6df7ed1228a18d53cf8034bef064d7","09f5ae47f1ef16d23261827b8b29e0633bd61fda2f4801b0181b8a2c1ddef7ce","aeb25597e8c9f0db892dd574800ccbb1dd22b90e973c0dc0dd885fc18b9e3380","b15c198405d251d548ab9f6c738270a1cd20b2a9ba55474487e6d7f8695ecdcc","a61a3629bab85baf3b5903cb816a9e865515ad23161fe5930cd281de5f81d78d","02dd0b40ca95a421de04a21349970a7c6eb2de7f3feaa86128fe8a225281377b","0f17ebf1be72ad9712bb94106d8963be5e728d552a3b4e10d98c9518c7780ab2","c9f01788cdf054f16766297b0e59b9e221617521213639e554d71b96dc4d7691","980342aefca7a14f31c2b4482a6839c36a528288f847e130a0e741b4fc3bf3e5","ecf2ab0b384065a9ed7558d6a10bd56ca2364df3df4a799fdfcecae606aee46c","d5bfe4cc1c117676f9e4a1d1a0339020a858d6cd94db760c5e72ad86117f6d7c","babc1ded112d4ad2bd43d0a7e11f35e15430fa0260ee892dd7b989b07af1e762","147d6030fd6638e6c887983edd228373abd9f469ea634ded3d2b2bfa97667a59","f156e9bb3735fdd6ce92c3975114117290b4e6d001acf6e3d701b2f4c212ba33","a35b39252a15bcbc1b8324017b62140d400f03ee74c9525e14294c2c42a6337c","163921da807f90f9025d5f7e983070ce01df323de80475dfef48f13965f0ff1b","e6b7713d18402a40ea2a2ede072675db16deb6d947b7b84e73a00f0f2b2b9580","e2c9b0c0fb72762b199459590984707db67fc870ed81127f20ed6cbef170c485","1c870268cd6227d3cde89c42f3e3a08d809a993632b6a73201fbcdbcb6982977","deb54057fab70b7f7706bde36f10799b7683226846cc25165f7b49190965a461","398e079a56a643cf1ee386903ea2334a650b496e222914a050868a0b81493e39","bbfecddbda6d560076434f2c147bd04ec61a54d0df9e5b521682e4aea6e90603","f80c7578c883194aa9c5fc5648c57f8d597a283691e9d630c9f3a16ec65b6194","8c49d63e768cdd48dc2a9bd78a39606967e86dda548cd1441deebebfd4560a08"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[30072,30095],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx:p30072"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the total number of preambles used for contention-based and contention-free 2-step random access type when ROs for 2-step are not shared with 4-step. If the field is absent, and 2-step and 4-step does not have shared ROs, all 64 preambles are available for 2-step random access type.","paragraph_zero_based":30096},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msgA-TransMax","paragraph_zero_based":30097},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Max number of MsgA preamble transmissions performed before switching to 4-step random access (see TS 38.321 [3], clauses 5.1.1). This field is only applicable when 2-step and 4-step RA type are configured and switching to 4-step type RA is supported. If the field is absent, switching from 2-step RA type to 4-step RA type is not allowed.","paragraph_zero_based":30098},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ra-ContentionResolutionTimer","paragraph_zero_based":30099},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The initial value for the contention resolution timer for fallback RAR in case no 4-step random access type is configured (see TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.1.5). Value sf8 corresponds to 8 subframes, value sf16 corresponds to 16 subframes, and so on. If both 2-step and 4-step random access type resources are configured on the BWP, then this field is absent. If the field is absent in RACH-ConfigCommonTwoStepRA in AdditionalRACH-Config, the UE shall apply the corresponding value in RACH-ConfigCommon in the same AdditionalRACH-Config.","paragraph_zero_based":30100},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ra-Prioritization","paragraph_zero_based":30101},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Parameters which apply for prioritized random access procedure on any UL BWP of SpCell for specific Access Identities (see TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.1.1a).","paragraph_zero_based":30102},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ra-PrioritizationForAI","paragraph_zero_based":30103},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the field ra-Prioritization-r16 applies for Access Identities. The first/leftmost bit corresponds to Access Identity 1, the next bit corresponds to Access Identity 2. Value 1 for an Access Identity indicates that the field ra-Prioritization-r16 applies, otherwise the field does not apply.","paragraph_zero_based":30104},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ra-PrioritizationForSlicingTwoStep","paragraph_zero_based":30105},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Parameters which apply to configure prioritized CBRA 2-step random access type for slicing.","paragraph_zero_based":30106},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"rach-ConfigGenericTwoStepRA","paragraph_zero_based":30107},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2-step random access type parameters for both regular random access and beam failure recovery.","paragraph_zero_based":30108},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30109},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"GroupB-ConfiguredTwoStepRA field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":30110},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"messagePowerOffsetGroupB","paragraph_zero_based":30111},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Threshold for preamble selection. Value is in dB. Value minusinfinity corresponds to –infinity. Value dB0 corresponds to 0 dB, dB5 corresponds to 5 dB and so on. (see TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.1.1).","paragraph_zero_based":30112},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"numberOfRA-PreamblesGroupA","paragraph_zero_based":30113},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The number of CB preambles per SSB in group A for idle/inactive or connected mode. The setting of the number of preambles for each group should be consistent with msgA-SSB-PerRACH-OccasionAndCB-PreamblesPerSSB or msgA-CB-PreamblesPerSSB-PerSharedRO if configured.","paragraph_zero_based":30114},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ra-MsgA-SizeGroupA","paragraph_zero_based":30115},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Transport block size threshold in bits below which the UE shall use a contention-based RA preamble of group A. (see TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.1.1).","paragraph_zero_based":30116},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30117},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":30118},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":30119}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ee8fb124f0f27da5b72138d587a6cf7fd862f62f760eb5e5acf285948fbec379","10f860094fc71b8a89d9b099325e831e2a69f9fb2148ad918a4dee17d79d8842","abe8cd4f440f80a779e9441afef503a88d48dbf4030983ba7ef6831c8ba0f902","4715d3360ee54ad7fbe9bf9e8a4eb80b85548dfddbf26dd3265ea9a40d7e4132","9a0290e02f05500b6c7c956414a973acf3af5cb5115f40249559953bcaebf986","389384b4276aa39a93a022a220754e4ffd8c9bc385a129bb21cfbf9abe5ef17b","4312af3979cb751f9f0b64ab5640298e425134c1e05f73be54921d22da730c4c","c2f37012783d3ce5049124e3f00e2bf74cfadc30f61b35541efc83d94c297a78","45ff12050c25fb1c71234e3588b9934bd6abf2db0a2619b0a56265659976e95b","33055fed65d2fd132f5a185c03918ea2e06156216797a8f262d01e170efba4ed","0dcb4a80e24b5a1641a6bcd563c5d78a13ae65ef18807dd1ad39718a6717f7ec","29cb4440cee3c183f163221173fafd1217496dc441c84be8dd06c74c938bd7f4","325c0853e49fdf0521d37092571c170e73b6b041d8b662e772a005de8ace75f8","6fd2311248e953d67153b363016ea229557b04f169cfb39cdcfafabbc4de3717","0a26db15651682a2d8701da6d45a3db7d893788b467278401b3fe71592fa9ae6","90e4254eb7862bac6c0d10b946e9deb410900cc87a7f5892a4dfbeddddf6da9f","cfddea8d4f3a035c96cac1a90272283aefed13deabe4d36310c8c5a9dd6ac9af","bd1e69be620a7405a7b24d3f38febb1884accfcaf68c3e41c1f93300c750da52","ad823b96172104616582bb821bccdc87eaf5736d5d9ff57dbaccbf657dc545e8","5e57a0340302df932cf92c4691d6bb696c26708350d1871bc85b5e80cf324e22","1b581e082605cb965143463e1f8e7adbbed7e05b1d744337451a9320dc8306ce","8e7feb7a1c9f36b538e9d4d233fd6df985c74544a6d1da5967a0d65a19258522","debe36cfe32e2d11bed760c5470bfb788bcf64cc2d09b33009200c441cdd6818","20c9b5b72d9f30f855d0d667c38027a63a47289b0526ca2f49ae062b532c4c7c"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[30096,30119],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx:p30096"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2Step4Step","paragraph_zero_based":30120},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present if both 2-step random access type and 4-step random access type are configured in the BWP, otherwise the field is not present.","paragraph_zero_based":30121},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present in msgA-ConfigCommon field in AdditionalRACH-Config if both 2-step random access type and 4-step random access type are configured for the same feature combination in the BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":30122},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2StepOnlyL139","paragraph_zero_based":30123},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present if msgA-PRACH-RootSequenceIndex L=139 and no 4-step random access type is configured, otherwise the field is absent, Need S.","paragraph_zero_based":30124},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2StepOnly","paragraph_zero_based":30125},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present in msgA-ConfigCommon field in BWP-UplinkCommon if rach-ConfigCommon field is absent in this BWP-UplinkCommon, otherwise the field is optionally present in msgA-ConfigCommon field in BWP-UplinkCommon, Need S.","paragraph_zero_based":30126},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present in msgA-ConfigCommon field in AdditionalRACH-Config if rach-ConfigCommon field is absent in this AdditionalRACH-Config, otherwise the field is optionally present in msgA-ConfigCommon field in AdditionalRACH-Config, Need S.","paragraph_zero_based":30127},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"AdditionalRACH","paragraph_zero_based":30128},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present if the msgA-ConfigCommon is included in an AdditionalRACH-Config. When included in initialUplinkBWP-RedCap to indicate other feature(s) than redcap, this field is mandatory present with at least two FeatureCombinationPreambles list entries: one list entry indicating only redcap and the other(s) indicating both redcap and one or multiple other feature(s) (e.g. smallData, nsag or msg3-Repetitions).","paragraph_zero_based":30129},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Otherwise, it is optional, Need R.","paragraph_zero_based":30130},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"InitialBWP-Only","paragraph_zero_based":30131},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is optionally present, Need R, if this BWP is the initial BWP of SpCell. Otherwise, the field is absent.","paragraph_zero_based":30132},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SharedRO","paragraph_zero_based":30133},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present if the 2-step random access type occasions are shared with 4-step random access type, otherwise the field is not present.","paragraph_zero_based":30134},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30135},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–RACH-ConfigDedicated","paragraph_zero_based":30136},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE RACH-ConfigDedicated is used to specify the dedicated random access parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":30137},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RACH-ConfigDedicated information element","paragraph_zero_based":30138},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":30139},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-RACH-CONFIGDEDICATED-START","paragraph_zero_based":30140},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30141},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30142},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RACH-ConfigDedicated ::=        SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":30143}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"