{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ...","paragraph_zero_based":30672},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":30673},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30674},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"BeamLinkMonitoringRS-r17 ::=        SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":30675},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    beamLinkMonitoringRS-Id-r17         BeamLinkMonitoringRS-Id-r17,","paragraph_zero_based":30676},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    detectionResource-r17               CHOICE {","paragraph_zero_based":30677},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        ssb-Index                       SSB-Index,","paragraph_zero_based":30678},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        csi-RS-Index                    NZP-CSI-RS-ResourceId","paragraph_zero_based":30679},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    },","paragraph_zero_based":30680},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ...","paragraph_zero_based":30681},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":30682},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30683},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"BeamLinkMonitoringRS-Id-r17 ::=     INTEGER (0..maxNrofFailureDetectionResources-1-r17)","paragraph_zero_based":30684},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30685},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-RADIOLINKMONITORINGCONFIG-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":30686},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":30687},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30688},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RadioLinkMonitoringConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":30689},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"additionalPCI","paragraph_zero_based":30690},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the physical cell IDs (PCI) of the SSBs in the failureDetectionSet2. If candidateBeamRS-List2 is configured in IE BeamFailureRecoveryRSConfig the field indicates the physical cell IDs (PCI) of the SSBs in the candidateBeamRS-List2.","paragraph_zero_based":30691},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"beamFailureDetectionTimer","paragraph_zero_based":30692},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Timer for beam failure detection (see TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.17). See also the BeamFailureRecoveryConfig IE. Value in number of \"Qout,LR reporting periods of Beam Failure Detection\" Reference Signal (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 6). Value pbfd1 corresponds to 1 Qout,LR reporting period of Beam Failure Detection Reference Signal, value pbfd2 corresponds to 2 Qout,LR reporting periods of Beam Failure Detection Reference Signal and so on. ","paragraph_zero_based":30693},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"beamFailureInstanceMaxCount","paragraph_zero_based":30694},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field determines after how many beam failure events the UE triggers beam failure recovery (see TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.17). Value n1 corresponds to 1 beam failure instance, value n2 corresponds to 2 beam failure instances and so on. ","paragraph_zero_based":30695}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ba99ada33558f12fe456c310850ccd5ab1217b90fc202dfbbde41eb748bb1e9f","dcbe4cd3ac53d6913b0fc381ed82dd23b103953c40f4d490b9b1ccbad1533afb","1ccbc999c15020287d3dd049217977a44134b6dd554f98ad260708291e82906f","893f0b96903624e464cbca44e68c55c3e696c85b9931507e3d1d757306b32556","d7ac2a35887f0b2bc6ec7c2f7259bc3567f73f8649c77b8441952765299fa4ac","f80f3bbc62be72d7098a180f59ea902cad3acd22030e732a18288dfbf36ce1d6","ebd687aacf08c03e0bc48149ef1a6f772f7e7a81ec86a7a42ccee1082b16060c","71e309aa40e76b8d4f0f0f0150c3600d0fc9879577fc7a787e348062587abcf1","26b6ad8daead0134be0ca29d11fc56ce2822f1514cb22884b620f5bd7352b42c","178103df7fd224511cbe70a6af4a08a410b49fd3fab6aa502f7ff93db6731d27","89df7056a8aabf08dcddef4a00c342b3e0a53fc7a89c673ab4005b84b130efad","727e03a62a8bc565a5f773c4987c8407d1ce44264584b18e094673352e0a15cf","435ccf8ffd87611b9b32cb7e74d72160ecdc93b8e18cf3ebad42206c6bd13d47","f69561400b8ccdef78e9195ca5ce6315582b9d9a96411039e7beb288d8a320a7","50a6fb2c31a620beb49eb063d4f87a26dc2caeae1a85816fcb1f01fe28a4b721","eb1b5dcb48abf481f162e63ad5b511e6721820906e695a56512ecd1f6814c8d9","330a295f0126117c5cc513ab3070cd82194e10d494a9cf8f95edf835b4f059d6","f25991cb71ab5c514e4247eb801411be1dfd69680fc5a6af3189ce57a1d96a57","a99af960f0e4bf9eff49cbbd3cbb5b51e631f2d6384d7be4713a3553fec329d4","7904ed40ade8d0c847e679206bc0eb10899a45652bd8e3842b645056fdc6a111","689492b6d9f98206210843ed8e6eb8669574f4bbd050653784c46a710c4f7883","3ac3716a24f95dc7fd4f528660665416146852e62066fec5501d7ef72273d6aa","9c838923f6afad65197670d79b128e6bc5292052ac930cc9a3979b47c750a706","3f446d05e52a2cae2696ab9b18abeeeecfa5bdb15c1a083fbe3e24b6ac566b21"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[30672,30695],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx:p30672"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"failureDetectionResourcesToAddModList","paragraph_zero_based":30696},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A list of reference signals for detecting beam failure and/or cell level radio link failure (RLF). The limits of the reference signals that the network can configure are specified in TS 38.213 [13], table 5-1. The network configures at most two detectionResources per BWP for the purpose beamFailure or both. If no RSs are provided for the purpose of beam failure detection, the UE performs beam monitoring based on the activated TCI-State for PDCCH as described in TS 38.213 [13], clause 6. If no RSs are provided in this list for the purpose of RLF detection, the UE performs Cell-RLM based on the activated TCI-State of PDCCH as described in TS 38.213 [13], clause 5. The network ensures that the UE has a suitable set of reference signals for performing cell-RLM. If failureDetectionSet1-r17 and failureDetectionSet2-r17 are present, the purpose of RadioLinkMonitoringRS in failureDetectionResourcesToAddModList only can be set to rlf.","paragraph_zero_based":30697},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"failureDetectionSet1, failureDetectionSet2","paragraph_zero_based":30698},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configures parameters for beamfailure detection towards beam failure detection resources configured in the set. If additional PCIs are configured using additionalPCI-ToAddModList for the serving cell, each RS in one set can be associated only with one PCI. Network always configures the failureDetectionSet1 and failureDetectionSet2 together. failureDetectionSetN is present if and only if candidateBeamRS-List2-r17 is configured. When a failureDetectionSetN is present, after the reconfiguration, the UE shall consider all the reference signals for this failure detection set as activated if at most maxBFD-RS-resourcesPerSetPerBWP-r17 reference signals are configured for each failure detection set, otherwise the UE shall consider all the reference signals in this failure detection set as deactivated. If bfdResourcesToAddModList-r17 in failureDetectionSetN is not present, the UE determines the RS(es) in each failureDetectionSetN as described in TS 38.213 [13], clause 6.","paragraph_zero_based":30699},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30700},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RadioLinkMonitoringRS field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":30701},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"detectionResource","paragraph_zero_based":30702},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A reference signal that the UE shall use for radio link monitoring or beam failure detection (depending on the indicated purpose). Only periodic 1-port CSI-RS can be configured on SCell for beam failure detection purpose.","paragraph_zero_based":30703},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"purpose","paragraph_zero_based":30704},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Determines whether the UE shall monitor the associated reference signal for the purpose of cell- and/or beam failure detection. For SCell, network only configures the value to beamFailure.","paragraph_zero_based":30705},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30706},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–RadioLinkMonitoringRS-Id","paragraph_zero_based":30707},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE RadioLinkMonitoringRS-Id is used to identify one RadioLinkMonitoringRS.","paragraph_zero_based":30708},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RadioLinkMonitoringRS-Id information element","paragraph_zero_based":30709},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":30710},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-RADIOLINKMONITORINGRS-ID-START","paragraph_zero_based":30711},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30712},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RadioLinkMonitoringRS-Id ::=            INTEGER (0..maxNrofFailureDetectionResources-1)","paragraph_zero_based":30713},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30714},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-RADIOLINKMONITORINGRS-ID-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":30715},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":30716},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30717},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–RAN-AreaCode","paragraph_zero_based":30718},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE RAN-AreaCode is used to identify a RAN area within the scope of a tracking area.","paragraph_zero_based":30719}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["48edc913a68770070ccbd8eae07fc8b1a068722a1a50560e37a3851ec211c856","f34e11866cefa3c239945246356c0f3cc8600a8c9fe190f14b4b09f487ab1dee","1970180546e6c56cab0af329d252196168b8bbcbb9e8df93ea5d2fcfc2a8f3bd","0f860cf1b2ad1cd8da5bb3543e714649ed66d21b32abd8692ba7fa360f53e3b3","968ece6dc6262f754daf1503ceb129cd9881196abb58ef131da9027c53c30b1f","2eca086a6ea215eeeeed8127ba5432b4f4ce9c4368b042c8cc4c840560065a86","e12fc705f8ebc0f6dc968afb8f7a0d6047af4b4c4b04a01a1c0365f499dd9d6b","7daf9d1ae30fb72d616a5b418ac8960ad66c200011410937d5f2b978419aabbe","60ac8cbea5248c5a50f7c935892c068eb4892311043968b1e054a6adc6ff293c","17c9f25bc0fdcf89f1b0fe4ae4a5d87ec48185d803fdfddd1d5e2052c5df21c6","3f8d994ae35fb26599ac61e78e37f3784c861a3002cc03d484d76695a2ff71a1","52f2b8a66839edb9919f1f95140cd234db105ae3be5b8292d90e1800d4816300","fd38a8b3812655ddf90af387f1ace3aae53076b441924309e76f230f6f8a99ad","339e8ad89934f4cac16c9936a2690054fb8fc3bb550604d289f549bdb719dec4","8a5d51e1433009731cba1c2e1d24376e44ab9892222215bb9d89a26c45867501","2af678e1f458e87547d4e60b4a701f05