{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"si-WindowPosition","paragraph_zero_based":33888},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the SI window position of the associated SI-message. The network provides si-WindowPosition in an ascending order, i.e. si-WindowPosition in the subsequent entry in schedulingInfoList2 has always value higher than in the previous entry of schedulingInfoList2. The network configures this field in a way that ensures that SI messages scheduled by schedulingInfoList and/or posSchedulingInfoList do not overlap with SI messages scheduled by schedulingInfoList2.","paragraph_zero_based":33889},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sib-MappingInfo","paragraph_zero_based":33890},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates which SIBs or posSIBs are contained in the SI message.","paragraph_zero_based":33891},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sibType","paragraph_zero_based":33892},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The type of SIB(s) mapped to SI for scheduling using schedulingInfoList2. Value type1 indicates SIBs and value type2 indicates posSIBs.","paragraph_zero_based":33893},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":33894},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional presence","paragraph_zero_based":33895},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":33896},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"GNSS-ID-SBAS","paragraph_zero_based":33897},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present if gnss-id is set to sbas. It is absent otherwise.","paragraph_zero_based":33898},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MSG-1","paragraph_zero_based":33899},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is optionally present, Need R, if si-BroadcastStatus is set to notBroadcasting for any SI-message included in schedulingInfoList or any SI-message containing type1 SIB included in schedulingInfoList2. It is absent otherwise.","paragraph_zero_based":33900},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SIB-TYPE","paragraph_zero_based":33901},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present if the SIB type is different from SIB6, SIB7 or SIB8. For SIB6, SIB7 and SIB8 it is absent.","paragraph_zero_based":33902},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NonPosSIB","paragraph_zero_based":33903},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present if the SIB type is type1. For type2 it is absent.","paragraph_zero_based":33904},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SUL-MSG-1","paragraph_zero_based":33905},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is optionally present, Need R, if supplementaryUplink is configured in ServingCellConfigCommonSIB and if si-BroadcastStatus is set to notBroadcasting for any SI-message included in schedulingInfoList or any SI-message containing type1 SIB included in schedulingInfoList2. It is absent otherwise.","paragraph_zero_based":33906},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"REDCAP-MSG-1","paragraph_zero_based":33907},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is optionally present, Need R, if initialUplinkBWP-RedCap is configured in UplinkConfigCommonSIB and if si-BroadcastStatus is set to notBroadcasting for any SI-message included in schedulingInfoList or any SI-message containing type1 SIB included in schedulingInfoList2. It is absent otherwise.","paragraph_zero_based":33908},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":33909},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SK-Counter","paragraph_zero_based":33910},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SK-Counter is a counter used upon initial configuration of SN security for NR-DC and NE-DC, as well as upon refresh of S-KgNB or S-KeNB based on the current or newly derived KgNB during RRC Resume or RRC Reconfiguration, as defined in TS 33.501 [11].","paragraph_zero_based":33911}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table 