{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ...,","paragraph_zero_based":35016},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    [[","paragraph_zero_based":35017},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    startingBitOfFormat2-3SUL               INTEGER (1..31)                                                     OPTIONAL    -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":35018},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ]]","paragraph_zero_based":35019},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":35020},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35021},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SRS-TPC-COMMANDCONFIG-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":35022},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":35023},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35024},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SRS-TPC-CommandConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":35025},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"fieldTypeFormat2-3","paragraph_zero_based":35026},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The type of a field within the group DCI with SRS request fields (optional), which indicates how many bits in the field are for SRS request (0 or 2).","paragraph_zero_based":35027},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Note that for Type A, there is a common SRS request field for all SCells in the set, but each SCell has its own TPC command bits. See TS 38.212 [17] clause 7.3.1 and , TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.3.","paragraph_zero_based":35028},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"startingBitOfFormat2-3","paragraph_zero_based":35029},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The starting bit position of a block within the group DCI with SRS request fields (optional) and TPC commands. The value 1 of the field corresponds to the first/left most bit of format2-3. The value 2 of the field corresponds to the second bit format2-3, and so on (see TS 38.212 [17], clause 7.3.1 and TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.3).","paragraph_zero_based":35030},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"startingBitOfFormat2-3SUL","paragraph_zero_based":35031},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The starting bit position of a block within the group DCI with SRS request fields (optional) and TPC commands for SUL carrier (see TS 38.212 [17], clause 7.3.1 and TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.3).","paragraph_zero_based":35032},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35033},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SSB-Index","paragraph_zero_based":35034},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SSB-Index identifies an SS-Block within an SS-Burst. See TS 38.213 [13], clause 4.1.","paragraph_zero_based":35035},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SSB-Index information element","paragraph_zero_based":35036},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":35037},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SSB-INDEX-START","paragraph_zero_based":35038},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35039}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["f4305d5cce504b5129032485b93ce92ade41ce84dd872361b523dd5587626eaf","4e4f4c6ab6e924e3764f441cc1d3180ee39d985f834d5429f8e7fef162c15a80","634b1dd72c8415431c5fd5abc05330ac4ba332c56410abd9f0a5e3647d8023e2","6a8329dce928040d35f2fd778a95f29bb0f8abfb495a3d8494c4f8008c4ac3cf","266aa0a9142775b18ddce170c49f0dcb53e915c18f1f3f97cb9486860c2f045f","fbf4c6eb4d6f331e296debd917bdf92eff08455386689d2f42cf6d9edd29fb40","5dc4a23d4434d65396389adbfa63cb1638294510d9c00d02822a3e5b609fb059","bf433fb8bd4cdee4981b85512b2b6c4531e986f9fac19a411be77e7f6aa99f63","ca7f7557fe5067d88a4d57257907b9e4079630af404295cc730035f8e912d8