{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE TimeToTrigger specifies the value range used for time to trigger parameter, which concerns the time during which specific criteria for the event needs to be met in order to trigger a measurement report. Value ms0 corresponds to 0 ms and behaviour as specified in 7.1.2 applies, value ms40 corresponds to 40 ms, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":35592},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TimeToTrigger information element","paragraph_zero_based":35593},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":35594},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-TIMETOTRIGGER-START","paragraph_zero_based":35595},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35596},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TimeToTrigger ::=                   ENUMERATED {","paragraph_zero_based":35597},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                        ms0, ms40, ms64, ms80, ms100, ms128, ms160, ms256,","paragraph_zero_based":35598},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                        ms320, ms480, ms512, ms640, ms1024, ms1280, ms2560,","paragraph_zero_based":35599},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                        ms5120}","paragraph_zero_based":35600},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35601},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-TIMETOTRIGGER-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":35602},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":35603},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35604},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–TN-AreaId","paragraph_zero_based":35605},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE TN-AreaId is used to identify a TN coverage area in an NTN system.","paragraph_zero_based":35606},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TN-AreaId information element","paragraph_zero_based":35607},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":35608},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-TN-AREAID-START","paragraph_zero_based":35609},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35610},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TN-AreaId-r18 ::=                  INTEGER (1..maxTN-AreaInfo-r18)","paragraph_zero_based":35611},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35612},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-TN-AREAID-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":35613},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":35614},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35615}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e031e48bf84a2439b9826743d6fd0423b8b4ecc93694397c8fc952feaa7ccad0","306b0a97a0467dc803934aba65bcbe5f7785c30b5e4d49c94315d008d536faef","e0be780e20a9d3ac6005ac424ac76475b70f65b6d44ead53c2dfb03615c5b907","1527aa286025ff2ac14dbda6823d8e62498a44f69f036a4700453cea6a027417","faeaca6f0bdb8a6ab2c670f8078fe2892e2caaebbce13c4890aa1b183cfa0009","3322ce759c345ffe8dd9f1e379e398e1d2e23a5af9b31e5bdad3ae3af4b12297","f60be9942efd668677e940ca42251c528f49176bf2329edcbd20a540e603cf6c","7bb45db036108467669285c17becc6772fef10320c29a0aa0b6438c3ad9ff4d8","3813bfec3a1f54a4cd115fea405102243230084497e72bca4b17b00e37c31df1","d8d58b2bf587656b81fdff15996a3d807191682473f52b7241c0c0ff62a431cb","63c35bef0a14e72a2b0bbe6ebf08250d7e4a24b410acd5eef7e2e8fbaba77467","d355c9a3af98043e10b7e1edf232af187227f81b4896becf9c4e1f2bb83653cd","7dc2d98006580d43b76a446633bc7c3373312de5c75aec457d22e472091355b4","ae6456fbb8a44b3af7d5d125b9bfba6ef7cae1ab5826963773676f3d404a6290","6c2fe2fa47ddeada8ef0e4fdd4031d13f79478dbe4f4e4854068dd67387728ca","1bc787f86bf8a4315c3418755f079d99ad991da16bb2f1296219e648e25a0676","3e13c18c6948fa9eb634754fc19218f4c049278501e3506ad7811c8f2b07738d","286078272030e6bb32d728a2400625ff3af759939f2da22043f7eba58d14dbd0","66f2a7a9825ea0908df424483125f1cd0978e141e93ecd25f280c8b7f43696f0","b98732b0dc23b984330d1d08fcd75cb94bf2f5c6f2556fa571b8ba3d0f73dce1","a48083ad7775b33ed1ffe1cd73cd3167976e45d9f708c2d05007e64209a361e9","72e8be644939812411ce561164ec50ed2c9559b193e309dec8f9b744072a3141","6e213c644e6cd075d2aceea12c989d92119da575be26edaf1abd24fdc06daa28","bbe28b2448dad4ed4f1cf935d50fb79dac20d08b379538253d98f698ee02628c"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[35592,35615],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx:p35592"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–UAC-BarringInfoSetIndex","paragraph_zero_based":35616},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE UAC-BarringInfoSetIndex provides the index of the entry in uac-BarringInfoSetList. Value 1 corresponds to the first entry in uac-BarringInfoSetList, value 2 corresponds to the second entry in this list and so on. An index value referring to an entry not included in uac-BarringInfoSetList indicates no barring.","paragraph_zero_based":35617},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UAC-BarringInfoSetIndex information element","paragraph_zero_based":35618},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":35619},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-UAC-BARRINGINFOSETINDEX-START","paragraph_zero_based":35620},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35621},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UAC-BarringInfoSetIndex ::=                INTEGER (1..maxBarringInfoSet)","paragraph_zero_based":35622},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35623},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-UAC-BARRINGINFOSETINDEX-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":35624},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":35625},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35626},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–UAC-BarringInfoSetList","paragraph_zero_based":35627},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE UAC-BarringInfoSetList provides a list of access control parameter sets. An access category can be configured with access parameters according to one of the sets.","paragraph_zero_based":35628},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UAC-BarringInfoSetList information element","paragraph_zero_based":35629},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":35630},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-UAC-BARRINGINFOSETLIST-START","paragraph_zero_based":35631},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35632},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UAC-BarringInfoSetList ::=          SEQUENCE (SIZE(1..maxBarringInfoSet)) OF UAC-BarringInfoSet","paragraph_zero_based":35633},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35634},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UAC-BarringInfoSetList-v1700 ::= SEQUENCE (SIZE(1..maxBarringInfoSet)) OF UAC-BarringInfoSet-v1700","paragraph_zero_based":35635},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35636},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UAC-BarringInfoSet ::=              SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":35637},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    uac-BarringFactor                   ENUMERATED {p00, p05, p10, p15, p20, p25, p30, p40,","paragraph_zero_based":35638},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                    p50, p60, p70, p75, p80, p85, p90, p95},","paragraph_zero_based":35639}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["52ae547261f54f43a234bd3095f48da146b9a9c23c66a9c3201f499bdb221568","835f42946fccc2c04bde7341e213fe331821e602d13ee36b8f0bdf56afee2202","afad059cdee519c17f4c7241889c87bd547be0460b22d5472c958f0fae2b5f16","f79cd3fa955feb5f8fa3b74e4b3a87f743b1badd62fa31694bd140fdb95f30b8","302425267f20777aa51657ca1b1c8bb1fbd4256d3c04b117c488a3206b67d594","7950342bff8bbe19028fab256e675404b4d3ca64fcdb2eddea6a28d68205d2cc","e0622da47900efc5382c3db9071f78fe1052d88ceb73da61be052faad959eed4","34e3cfa067e658cba282ccf69993d01f54968f1bd9b127363fb3a5baa2e251f4","bb562224451231854bc8e47ae6f2d7f41ec47d256c380602e700ac7c0cd3ce10","ecff9caed98e4ea8ced27a9b336384a5166a8b8b8e8e8cfc9af8cf4fc445d28e","154812102229640b0041d77301944b06528135585d52ab6552d9324c111a462c","005e3f04d9f5dd03c903acb92dddf08824422f1b09d803927cde188b67403b63","2e08cc453bc4f276ee861e9852d5dacfe70c1348ddd17c69febda58abfc07f32","d96d5b449b3eb5348b5fb33def8e4245d090fdb6a60b3ac4996cb6366d26e456","69df5d5e36a9cf917bffc84bd400b94c77839bcd0f2e1455cb12b65664269dfa","797baec1beb47b37fa91dcc7e216bbb62bc5609bceff24afcb6e30c581a26d32","f7322890b9eca78a950596f020e3a2104068843e39d64714bb53ecff3dc7d1d1","5f54efa26a47710600076296b6dabcfc72c5ea5f33122e50fa65285c16110cd9","2d19dd7209857ea6a6ef85ac4e9999c53f2a212156a762be4fb4a32c83843a26","1e3a632be47bc854de07525a9cbd3ac0b784219ab4fa71ad840d752e27c48353","616dc398d9200243dd38f6eaeddd6ac014c4e0f31c1dea23fde6ccae78b723cb","5669fc89a0e54396734d9cffde30e99ec79fd97c1e36511919210445657b28d6","5d6df066d535ae9127d93b4e8ef0ac7d26420024577f6ad9bdad84052295827c","c98a01da5289da6f4a09336a8f1ef6edd7ef7fc54eebada0e15296fa53527d61"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[35616,35639],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx:p35616"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    uac-BarringTime                     ENUMERATED {s4, s8, s16, s32, s64, s128, s256, s512},","paragraph_zero_based":35640},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    uac-BarringForAccessIdentity        BIT STRING (SIZE(7))","paragraph_zero_based":35641},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":35642},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35643},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UAC-BarringInfoSet-v1700 ::= SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":35644},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    uac-BarringFactorForAI3-r17  ENUMERATED {p00, p05, p10, p15, p20, p25, p30, p40, p50, p60, p70, p75, p80, p85, p90, p95}","paragraph_zero_based":35645},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                                       OPTIONAL  -- Need S","paragraph_zero_based":35646},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":35647},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35648},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-UAC-BARRINGINFOSETLIST-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":35649},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":35650},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35651},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UAC-BarringInfoSetList field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":35652},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"uac-BarringInfoSetList","paragraph_zero_based":35653},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of access control parameter sets. Each access category can be configured with access parameters corresponding to a particular set by uac-barringInfoSetIndex. Association of an access category with an index that has no corresponding entry in the uac-BarringInfoSetList is valid configuration and indicates no barring.","paragraph_zero_based":35654},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"uac-BarringForAccessIdentity","paragraph_zero_based":35655},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether access attempt is allowed for each Access Identity. The leftmost bit, bit 0 in the bit string corresponds to Access Identity 1, bit 1 in the bit string corresponds to Access Identity 2, bit 2 in the bit string corresponds to Access Identity 11, bit 3 in the bit string corresponds to Access Identity 12, bit 4 in the bit string corresponds to Access Identity 13, bit 5 in the bit string corresponds to Access Identity 14, and bit 6 in the bit string corresponds to Access Identity 15. Value 0 means that access attempt is allowed for the corresponding access identity.","paragraph_zero_based":35656},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"uac-BarringFactor","paragraph_zero_based":35657},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Represents the probability that access attempt would be allowed during access barring check.","paragraph_zero_based":35658},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"uac-BarringFactorForAI3","paragraph_zero_based":35659},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Barring factor applicable for Access Identity 3. Represents the probability that access attempt would be allowed during access barring check. If absent, the UE considers the access attempt as allowed.","paragraph_zero_based":35660},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"uac-BarringTime","paragraph_zero_based":35661},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The average time in seconds before a new access attempt is to be performed after an access attempt was barred at access barring check for the same access category, see 5.3.14.5.","paragraph_zero_based":35662},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35663}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","p