{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36000},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"P0AlphaSet-r17 ::=           SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":36001},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    p0-r17                       INTEGER (-16..15)                                                            OPTIONAL, -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":36002},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    alpha-r17                    Alpha                                                                        OPTIONAL, -- Need S","paragraph_zero_based":36003},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    closedLoopIndex-r17          ENUMERATED { i0, i1 }","paragraph_zero_based":36004},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":36005},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36006},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Uplink-powerControlId-r17 ::= INTEGER(1.. maxUL-TCI-r17)","paragraph_zero_based":36007},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36008},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-UPLINK-POWERCONTROL-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":36009},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":36010},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36011},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Uplink-PowerControl field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":36012},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"p0AlphaSetforPUSCH, p0AlphaSetforPUCCH, p0AlphaSetforSRS","paragraph_zero_based":36013},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configures power control parameters for PUSCH, PUCCH and SRS (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 7.2). When the field alpha is absent in p0AlphaSetforPUSCH, the UE applies the value 1 for PUSCH power control. When the field alpha is absent in p0AlphaSetforSRS, the UE applies the value 1 for SRS power control. In p0AlphaSetForPUCCH, the field alpha is absent (not used).","paragraph_zero_based":36014},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36015},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–Uu-RelayRLC-ChannelConfig","paragraph_zero_based":36016},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE Uu-RelayRLC-ChannelConfig is used to configure an RLC entity, a corresponding logical channel in MAC for Uu Relay RLC channel between L2 U2N Relay UE and network, or between a N3C relay UE and network in case of MP.","paragraph_zero_based":36017},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Uu-RelayRLC-ChannelConfig information element","paragraph_zero_based":36018},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":36019},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-UU-RELAYRLC-CHANNELCONFIG-START","paragraph_zero_based":36020},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36021},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Uu-RelayRLC-ChannelConfig-r17::= SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":36022},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    uu-LogicalChannelIdentity-r17    LogicalChannelIdentity                    OPTIONAL,   -- Cond RelayLCH-SetupOnly","paragraph_zero_based":36023}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["816b55feccc62ef5f3eb1fc3d5e78e181d34fce29628a911f2a9e43230b2e4f5","606aaadb81961a8685a173bea12ecf3e64fb29f9c4f990052d01b47c3e380f08","bd2e905aa3ef15433b87d2dd0a2d5148a0f48e98015f5d8356d956bd30c96731","52ff24be3668482a57fb046f3a01be30e5bde4d420887a973bc6533b7fa4722e","6d010c3f24e3c5e6e2992a9aaffea814f94f7cdd014767d2292793c92472d9d3","2a1b4ef25ea0bf6329107b3c0bfa29469afcaf2ba2a270df8bc9fd74e77c84db","ddc1506fb0e320cc51f297b070d59bab4cee86affa80b6eaef45804b8db94785","c33f2c52a0cab998c20c9486c781604b1c07bad55ac4b52463d9d4c2