{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":38952},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38953},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FeatureSetUplink field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":38954},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"featureSetListPerUplinkCC","paragraph_zero_based":38955},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates which features the UE supports on the individual UL carriers of the feature set (and hence of a band entry that refers to the feature set). The UE shall hence include at least as many FeatureSetUplinkPerCC-Id in this list as the number of carriers it supports according to the ca-BandwidthClassUL, except if indicating additional functionality by reducing the number of FeatureSetUplinkPerCC-Id in the feature set (see NOTE 1 in FeatureSetCombination IE description). The order of the elements in this list is not relevant, i.e., the network may configure any of the carriers in accordance with any of the FeatureSetUplinkPerCC-Id in this list.","paragraph_zero_based":38956},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38957},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–FeatureSetUplinkId","paragraph_zero_based":38958},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE FeatureSetUplinkId identifies an uplink feature set. The FeatureSetUplinkId of a FeatureSetUplink is the index position of the FeatureSetUplink in the featureSetsUplink list in the FeatureSets IE. The first element in the list is referred to by FeatureSetUplinkId = 1, and so on. The FeatureSetUplinkId =0 is not used by an actual FeatureSetUplink but means that the UE does not support a carrier in this band of a band combination.","paragraph_zero_based":38959},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FeatureSetUplinkId information element","paragraph_zero_based":38960},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":38961},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-FEATURESETUPLINKID-START","paragraph_zero_based":38962},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38963},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FeatureSetUplinkId ::=                  INTEGER (0..maxUplinkFeatureSets)","paragraph_zero_based":38964},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38965},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-FEATURESETUPLINKID-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":38966},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":38967},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38968},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–FeatureSetUplinkPerCC","paragraph_zero_based":38969},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE FeatureSetUplinkPerCC indicates a set of features that the UE supports on the corresponding carrier of one band entry of a band combination.","paragraph_zero_based":38970},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FeatureSetUplinkPerCC information element","paragraph_zero_based":38971},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":38972},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-FEATURESETUPLINKPERCC-START","paragraph_zero_based":38973},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":38974},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FeatureSetUplinkPerCC ::=               SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":38975}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["0e829b1ff6f170a6b4cb02a606ba6e65e35a0302ab02873848fd36759fb95a14","e9fdeb2c1fde495a22eca7a2b76fa1c10afe05835fdd50b0d245f9ceff6a2c2d","e3172b8388519365e0f06249ad89f3818fc8b211396204e3585140e42ef8812a","5a1d2f3b8f3b77b21ea059d49fe0ff0275a8e686c3cd9c29ef