{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44208},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-UE-MeasurementsAvailable-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":44209},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":44210},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44211},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–UTRA-FDD-Q-OffsetRange","paragraph_zero_based":44212},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE UTRA-FDD-Q-OffsetRange is used to indicate a frequency specific offset to be applied when evaluating triggering conditions for measurement reporting. The value is in dB. Value dB-24 corresponds to -24 dB, value dB-22 corresponds to -22 dB and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":44213},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UTRA-FDD-Q-OffsetRange information element","paragraph_zero_based":44214},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":44215},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-UTRA-FDD-Q-OFFSETRANGE-START","paragraph_zero_based":44216},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44217},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UTRA-FDD-Q-OffsetRange-r16 ::=              ENUMERATED {","paragraph_zero_based":44218},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                dB-24, dB-22, dB-20, dB-18, dB-16, dB-14,","paragraph_zero_based":44219},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                dB-12, dB-10, dB-8, dB-6, dB-5, dB-4, dB-3,","paragraph_zero_based":44220},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                dB-2, dB-1, dB0, dB1, dB2, dB3, dB4, dB5,","paragraph_zero_based":44221},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                dB6, dB8, dB10, dB12, dB14, dB16, dB18,","paragraph_zero_based":44222},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                dB20, dB22, dB24}","paragraph_zero_based":44223},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44224},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-UTRA-FDD-Q-OFFSETRANGE-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":44225},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":44226},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44227},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–VisitedCellInfoList","paragraph_zero_based":44228},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE VisitedCellInfoList includes the mobility history information of maximum of 16 most recently visited primary cells or time spent in any cell selection state and/or camped on any cell state in NR or E-UTRA and, in case of Dual Connectivity, the mobility history information of maxPSCellHistory most recently visited primary secondary cell group cells across all the primary cells included in the VisitedCellInfoList. The most recently visited cell is stored first in the list. The list includes cells visited in RRC_IDLE, RRC_INACTIVE and RRC_CONNECTED states for NR and RRC_IDLE and RRC_CONNECTED for E-UTRA.","paragraph_zero_based":44229},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"VisitedCellInfoList information element","paragraph_zero_based":44230},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":44231}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["bf255d94f4835533c6158c0acc0ae4ffc2745b115c8596653f53f1d5d0d57f2b","f78d5854998aac96273d1317763f31f61fafdd1f40f98ee7f3785598c9c28f45","abcd061091c6d3b604f416ea229f1238871fd7f3afa51309ca83a2dc73e7888c","cb9c294ba27a27019024005874f3a6c6815488e29432df34984f56459f13a7d8","212d0fbd27f87b2d60cb4ae6e0873b2507c81ee41493