{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-PRS-TxPoolExceptional-r18      SL-PRS-ResourcePoolConfig-r18                                                  OPTIONAL, -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":44616},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ...","paragraph_zero_based":44617},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":44618},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44619},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-BWP-PRSPOOLCONFIGCOMMON-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":44620},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":44621},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44622},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44623},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44624},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-BWP-PRS-PoolConfigCommon field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":44625},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PRS-TxPoolExceptional","paragraph_zero_based":44626},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the resources by which the UE is allowed to perform NR sidelink transmission in exceptional conditions on the configured BWP. This field is not present when SL-BWP-PRS-PoolConfigCommon is included in SL-PreconfigurationNR","paragraph_zero_based":44627},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44628},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-CBR-PriorityTxConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":44629},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-CBR-PriorityTxConfigList indicates the mapping between PSSCH transmission parameter (such as MCS, PRB number, retransmission number, CR limit) sets by using the indexes of the configurations provided in sl-CBR-PSSCH-TxConfigList, CBR ranges by an index to the entry of the CBR range configuration in sl-CBR-RangeConfigList, and priority ranges. It also indicates the default PSSCH transmission parameters to be used when CBR measurement results are not available, and MCS range for the MCS tables used in the resource pool.","paragraph_zero_based":44630},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-CBR-PriorityTxConfigList information element","paragraph_zero_based":44631},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":44632},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-CBR-PRIORITYTXCONFIGLIST-START","paragraph_zero_based":44633},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44634},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-CBR-PriorityTxConfigList-r16 ::= SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..8)) OF SL-PriorityTxConfigIndex-r16","paragraph_zero_based":44635},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44636},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-CBR-PriorityTxConfigList-v1650 ::= SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..8)) OF SL-PriorityTxConfigIndex-v1650","paragraph_zero_based":44637},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44638},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-PriorityTxConfigIndex-r16 ::=    SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":44639}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["8d90fd82fb5ddfcd013c855fb627348b310c45005bb4b74af19a623c36c3eecb","74bee8c6ac9cd94c3c59ab79a84c93b0aad1017e08d3e2451a5bdd3b6a94f739","6bcbf322bfe258a663c57d1b917372cba14f77ed1dc7b03e3cfec352e9c5cbaa","19141d9705a95681f0025b3baa2c7a152879a02a8f386c2420918aa995497f96","3e40be78b99551e0bd915604291b7cd03ac21d0dd07b1300f0b2c89480c51ffa","c705707388d963944599aa1a2c09e5f84637967584e1cf70b4ee6d50f0189037","049f29328c193680d4d35942d01a3398e2974bb4faf35fa7c2a516dacd3a7371","f17587bcaa20211232e9ba628f2003487b1b177a0e6f65c150377ac797e24c55","26407dd2ee14443