{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":44688},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44689},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-CBR-CommonTxConfigList field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":44690},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-CBR-RangeConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":44691},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Each entry in sl-CBR-RangeConfigList is SL-CBR-LevelsConfig containing the list of CBR ranges. The values within each SL-CBR-LevelsConfig indicate the upper bound of the each CBR range (and implicitly indicate the lower bound of next CBR range) and are configured in ascending order. For the first CBR range of each SL-CBR-LevelsConfig, the lower bound of the CBR range is 0. Value 0 corresponds to 0, value 1 to 0.01, value 2 to 0.02, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":44692},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-CR-Limit","paragraph_zero_based":44693},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the maximum limit on the occupancy ratio. Value 0 corresponds to 0, value 1 to 0.0001, value 2 to 0.0002, and so on (i.e. in steps of 0.0001) until value 10000, which corresponds to 1.","paragraph_zero_based":44694},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-CBR-PSSCH-TxConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":44695},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the list of available PSSCH transmission parameters (such as MCS, sub-channel number, retransmission number and CR limit) configurations.","paragraph_zero_based":44696},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-TxParameters","paragraph_zero_based":44697},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates PSSCH transmission parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":44698},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44699},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-CBR-CommonTxDedicated-SL-PRS-RP-List","paragraph_zero_based":44700},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-CBR-CommonTxConfigListDedicated-SL-PRS-RP indicates the list of SL PRS transmission parameters (such as Maximum SL PRS transmission power, Maximum Number of SL PRS (re-)transmissions, and CR limit) in sl-CBR-SL-PRS-TxConfigList, and the list of CBR ranges in sl-CBR-RangeConfigList-Dedicated-SL-PRS-RP, to configure congestion control to the UE for sidelink positioning.","paragraph_zero_based":44701},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-CBR-CommonTxDedicatedSL-PRS-RP-List information element","paragraph_zero_based":44702},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":44703},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG- SL-CBR-COMMONTXDEDICATEDSL-PRS-RP-LIST-START","paragraph_zero_based":44704},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44705},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-CBR-CommonTxDedicatedSL-PRS-RP-List-r18 ::= SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":44706},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-CBR-RangeDedicatedSL-PRS-RP-List-r18     SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxCBR-ConfigDedSL-PRS-1-r18)) OF SL-CBR-LevelsDedicatedSL-PRS-RP-r18","paragraph_zero_based":44707},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                                                                                 OPTIONAL,    -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":44708},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-CBR-SL-PRS-TxConfigList-r18              SEQUENCE (SIZE (1.. maxNrofSL-PRS-TxConfig-r18)) OF SL-CBR-SL-PRS-TxConfig-r18","paragraph_zero_based":44709},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                                                                                 OPTIONAL     -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":44710},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":44711}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f37