{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of PDSCH parameters which can be configured per G-RNTI. Only one entity is allowed to be configured if included in SIB20.","paragraph_zero_based":47952},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pdsch-TimeDomainAllocationList","paragraph_zero_based":47953},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of time-domain configurations for timing of DL assignment to DL data.","paragraph_zero_based":47954},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field pdsch-TimeDomainAllocationList applies to DCI format 4_0 (see table 5.1.2.1.1-1 in TS 38.214 [19]). When the field is absent, the UE follows PDSCH time domain resource allocation determination rule as specified in TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.2.1.1.","paragraph_zero_based":47955},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"rateMatchPatternToAddModList","paragraph_zero_based":47956},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Resources patterns which the UE should rate match PDSCH around. The UE rate matches around the union of all resources indicated in the rate match patterns (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.4.1).","paragraph_zero_based":47957},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"mcs-Table","paragraph_zero_based":47958},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates which MCS table the UE shall use for PDSCH. If the field is absent the UE applies the value 64QAM. The field mcs-Table applies to DCI format 4_0 with CRC scrambled by MCCH-RNTI/G-RNTI (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.3.1).","paragraph_zero_based":47959},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"xOverhead","paragraph_zero_based":47960},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Accounts for an overhead from CSI-RS, CORESET, etc. If the field is absent, the UE applies value xOh0 (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.3.2).","paragraph_zero_based":47961},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":47962},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PDSCH-ConfigPTM field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":47963},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dataScramblingIdentityPDSCH","paragraph_zero_based":47964},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Identifier(s) used to initialize data scrambling (c_init) for PDSCH as specified in TS 38.211 [16], clause 7.3.1.1. When the field is absent the UE applies the value physCellId configured for this serving cell.","paragraph_zero_based":47965},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dmrs-ScramblingID0","paragraph_zero_based":47966},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"DL DMRS scrambling initialization (see TS 38.211 [16], clause 7.4.1.1.1). When the field is absent the UE applies the value physCellId configured for this serving cell.","paragraph_zero_based":47967},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pdsch-AggregationFactor","paragraph_zero_based":47968},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Number of repetitions for dynamic scheduling of MBS broadcast data for MTCH PDSCH (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.2.1). When the field is absent the UE applies the value 1.","paragraph_zero_based":47969},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":47970},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–TMGI","paragraph_zero_based":47971},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE TMGI is used to identify the MBS session.","paragraph_zero_based":47972},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TMGI information element","paragraph_zero_based":47973},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":47974},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-TMGI-START","paragraph_zero_based":47975}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["eaaa0389ef8d47e0703e00e8ab340065868575c65d0a847937374b8b854b0496","57918edef42b8e7