{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the frequency domain position for sidelink CSI-RS.","paragraph_zero_based":49008},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-CSI-RS-FirstSymbol","paragraph_zero_based":49009},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the position of first symbol of sidelink CSI-RS.","paragraph_zero_based":49010},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-DRX-ConfigUC-PC5","paragraph_zero_based":49011},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the NR sidelink DRX configuration for unicast communication, as specified in TS 38.321 [3]","paragraph_zero_based":49012},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-LatencyBoundCSI-Report","paragraph_zero_based":49013},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the latency bound of SL CSI report from the associated SL CSI triggering in terms of number of slots.","paragraph_zero_based":49014},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-LatencyBoundIUC-Report","paragraph_zero_based":49015},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the latency bound of SL Inter-UE coordination report from the associated SL Inter-UE coordination explicit request triggering in terms of number of slots.","paragraph_zero_based":49016},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-LogicalChannelIdentity","paragraph_zero_based":49017},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the identity of the sidelink logical channel.","paragraph_zero_based":49018},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-MappedQoS-FlowsToAddList","paragraph_zero_based":49019},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicate the QoS flows to be mapped to the configured sidelink DRB. Each entry is indicated by the SL-PQFI, which is used between UEs, as defined in TS 23.287 [55].","paragraph_zero_based":49020},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-MappedQoS-FlowsToReleaseList","paragraph_zero_based":49021},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicate the QoS flows to be released from the configured sidelink DRB. Each entry is indicated by the SL-PQFI, which is used between UEs, as defined in TS 23.287 [55].","paragraph_zero_based":49022},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-MeasConfig","paragraph_zero_based":49023},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the sidelink measurement configuration for the unicast destination.","paragraph_zero_based":49024},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-OffsetToCarrier","paragraph_zero_based":49025},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Offset in frequency domain between Point A (lowest subcarrier of common RB 0) and the lowest usable subcarrier on this carrier in number of PRBs (using the subcarrierSpacing defined for this carrier). The maximum value corresponds to 275*8-1. See TS 38.211 [16], clause 4.4.2.","paragraph_zero_based":49026},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-OutOfOrderDelivery","paragraph_zero_based":49027},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether or not outOfOrderDelivery specified in TS 38.323 [5] is configured. This field should be either always present or always absent, after the sidelink radio bearer is established.","paragraph_zero_based":49028},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PDCP-SN-Size","paragraph_zero_based":49029},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the PDCP SN size of the configured sidelink DRB.","paragraph_zero_based":49030},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-Resetconfig","paragraph_zero_based":49031}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["89cda2d2632e3ba91e34ad2ec544b393116ebdc648c81c121e9708edc373d696","ceb8493ddd4f15e1d85b7508d32351b42a98fe11aa048ee62f6ab9871d5a8b4e","5c744d34c3c18546f2af4011dff206e6f64080b213e34b77ff890e4abfbbfd