{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54024},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–ChildIE2-WithoutEM","paragraph_zero_based":54025},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE ChildIE2-WithoutEM is an example of a lower level IE, typically used to control certain radio configurations. The example illustrates how the new field chIE1-NewField is added in release N to the configuration of the configurable feature.","paragraph_zero_based":54026},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ChildIE2-WithoutEM information element","paragraph_zero_based":54027},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- /example/ ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":54028},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54029},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ChildIE2-WithoutEM ::=              CHOICE {","paragraph_zero_based":54030},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    release                             NULL,","paragraph_zero_based":54031},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    setup                               SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":54032},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"        -- Root encoding","paragraph_zero_based":54033},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    }","paragraph_zero_based":54034},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":54035},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54036},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ChildIE2-WithoutEM-vNx0 ::=         SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":54037},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    chIE2-NewField-rN                   INTEGER (0..31)                 OPTIONAL    -- Cond ConfigF","paragraph_zero_based":54038},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":54039},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54040},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":54041},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54042},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional presence","paragraph_zero_based":54043},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":54044},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ConfigF","paragraph_zero_based":54045},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is optional present, need R, in case of chIE2-ConfigurableFeature is included and set to \"setup\"; otherwise the field is absent and the UE shall delete any existing value for this field.","paragraph_zero_based":54046},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54047}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["75a3ef51d24e81c0af35b38fbc721c65ec4d4bc7e697d3fb51048bc257e07caa","93bc1a98769ac5fc2df2ff24910bcce1a13eb4d13b5a62fded174688ac55d0af","26eeaf4b5e00478e035683e82c397837c24dde15db7e55911381042d713c52af","4a7f0b1c62521c32adbd7dd303ec04064b9de07b204c629bf9a17754e2f10ffd","7486666f2977d1aeb3ea90d13af903fb691ab267d67732db1270fa47c17222d5","849c1a36dd3c82c906a237b36c35f57de81b20e57f27702aab61ed6fe1e1b227","2e3cac593b13c9d9c793158d72ede7aa5057a6f310a242d00fb2addc57f2ed50","be005d5ae2aa96db25ef6e55c8c1682900e51c4ad27831676594812ac869adfa","e3b4b3dcee2e4c1a0106d36dd41697f53d8ff7f2c58e31be9e876596f71be92e","908f1ee4a4aa66ef951cf03170e4d4a2f61309c192ca1eaa15b62b222bf08b9c","d47f1d63db85cddb3bf2395e3c8f3d09d84e332bccbd6bbbcf1d18499e3145cf","c5eb7fc0923f0de7623eab864ec2c59305f2f73f16d1f6f0a7b3ebb58fd0449b","66749ac941351c34c91251be1a805c89d78b6bc4d7fed0fb490b1c49324d5b5e","ae2d58157d7cb6ada51757eaf9f30d6596b0473ae0582f448b3f3fe48ac073f7","0e738f4da8f645c1d4779c6db0e175e2f8dcd38caa73b248ac4d2d34a6a44dca","8962af4a941a314c4c71a52afd2f93380838ba754c8ad3347f0e1c8b4af40e1a","30b61c58fd8050a7f696433c03ac86a42f8bea4be3be159c882a48ada9c083f3","d7bafd7dc213b0dbf9d9cfc3e10d6da93def86798d4c2cfea2abd759b24adc05","053b7bf84301f0d776225b5b837ad65bd310c51e55090f331eb101f8051dd4d6","61a2bcc62ecba33482909fa769699a8127544565d958a11c1b460cf53544d8cc","c0b251ebe4e40efb14b1d7e530e197e753cc331cd0adce407fd931e8955e0ed1","bbbe89f399fa6c7eaf0ce880e31b39bd05d8332fabc1ef4176a0bbc1f43ec0bc","c5168d8386ff91138edaaeab27cd6253fd19f77f883ba29b448f5cde8cfc35f4","c09e009e0c70ed9d2790da3d6909e62ccd7fe188f2ea3d265aab1d6de2a84e2d"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[54024,54047],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx:p54024"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A.4.3.6Non-critical extensions of lists with ToAddMod/ToRelease","paragraph_zero_based":54048},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When the size of a list using the ToAddMod/ToRelease construction is extended and/or fields are added to the list element structure, the list should be non-critically extended in accordance with the following general principles:","paragraph_zero_based":54049},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–When only the size of the list is extended, this extension is reflected in a non-critical extension of the list, with a \"SizeExt\" suffix added to the end of the field name (before the -vNxy suffix). The differential size of the extended list uses the suffix \"Diff\". A new ToRelease list is needed, and its range should include only the increase in list size. In many cases, extending the list size will also require an extended list element ID type to account for the increased size of the list; in these cases the element type will need to be extended to include the extended element ID, resulting in a more complex extension (see example 3 for further discussion of this case). The field description table should indicate that the UE considers the original list and the extension list as a single list; thus entries added with the original list can be modified by the extension list (or removed by the extension of the ToRelease list), or vice versa. The result is as shown in the following example:","paragraph_zero_based":54050},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54051},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- /example 1/ ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":54052},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54053},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ContainingStructure ::=             SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":54054},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    listElementToAddModList              SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofListElements)) OF ListElement             OPTIONAL,    -- Need N","paragraph_zero_based":54055},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    listElementToReleaseList             SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofListElements)) OF ListElementId           OPTIONAL,    -- Need N","paragraph_zero_based":54056},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ...,","paragraph_zero_based":54057},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    [[","paragraph_zero_based":54058},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    -- Non-critical extension lists","paragraph_zero_based":54059},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    listElementToAddModListSizeExt-vNxy  SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofListElementsDiff-rN)) OF ListElement      OPTIONAL,    -- Need N","paragraph_zero_based":54060},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    listElementToReleaseListSizeExt-vNxy SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofListElementsDiff-rN)) OF ListElementId    OPTIONAL     -- Need N","paragraph_zero_based":54061},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ]]","paragraph_zero_based":54062},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":54063},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":54064},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54065},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–When fields are added to the list element structure, an extension marker should normally be used if available. If no extension marker is available or if overhead or other considerations prevent using the extension marker, an extension structure should be created for the new fields, with the suffix \"Ext\" added to the end of the field name and the element structure type name (before the -vNxy suffix), and a parallel ToAddMod list introduced to hold the new structures, also with the \"Ext\" suffix. The field description table should indicate that the parallel list contains the same number of entries, and in the same order, as the original list. No new ToRelease list is typically needed (unless the list element ID type changes). It should typically be ensured that the contained fields in the \"Ext\" elements are releasable without release and add of the entire list element; this can, for instance, be ensured by having the new fields be OPTIONAL Need R. If multiple extensions of the same list are needed, the version suffix should distinguish the lists (e.g. listElementToAddModListExt-vNwz added after listElementToAddModListExt-vNxy). The result is as shown in the following example:","paragraph_zero_based":54066},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- /example 2/ ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":54067},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54068},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ContainingStructure ::=             SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":54069},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    listElementToAddModList             SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofListElements)) OF ListElement             OPTIONAL,    -- Need N","paragraph_zero_based":54070},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    listElementToReleaseList            SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofListElements)) OF ListElementId           OPTIONAL,    -- Need N","paragraph_zero_based":54071}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["f6cc6dd91f06c0d16927ee3ab2623ea78b99e5c643b3dd3abc80a0290eb582cb","ada579851143dceb3ace7d8edc01a72d3e616446f7940c4e33aeae4dd7590dfd","07bb1cc88a742075c4318af6f5d1306e8698e56b5605b548923b45fd77492a3b","3d2b1081327477fb220b5c7d91941b5443390dd8e1085c6e9b0dc251259b0440","6f78fb6dff360d49f3f14f5cb0b910691e40b81f042111b0a6d1a67af396de12","f7ea08f241c32d2be9494b6ccaa21f8a08e5df4034606ab8daa1f9f32dd8a636","c87ad68692e67243ae503286532eeed4ff0b8a1f20fc364