{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54216},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Annex B (informative):RRC Information","paragraph_zero_based":54217},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"B.1Protection of RRC messages","paragraph_zero_based":54218},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The following list provides information which messages can be sent (unprotected) prior to AS security activation and which messages can be sent unprotected after AS security activation. Those messages indicated \"-\" in \"P\" column should never be sent unprotected by gNB or UE. Further requirements are defined in the procedural text.","paragraph_zero_based":54219},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"P…Messages that can be sent (unprotected) prior to AS security activation","paragraph_zero_based":54220},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A – I…Messages that can be sent without integrity protection after AS security activation","paragraph_zero_based":54221},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A – C…Messages that can be sent unciphered after AS security activation","paragraph_zero_based":54222},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NA… Message can never be sent after AS security activation","paragraph_zero_based":54223},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Message","paragraph_zero_based":54224},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"P","paragraph_zero_based":54225},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A-I","paragraph_zero_based":54226},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A-C","paragraph_zero_based":54227},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Comment","paragraph_zero_based":54228},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CounterCheck","paragraph_zero_based":54229},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":54230},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":54231},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":54232},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54233},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CounterCheckResponse","paragraph_zero_based":54234},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":54235},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":54236},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":54237},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54238},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"DedicatedSIBRequest","paragraph_zero_based":54239}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["2a7d52e08fb88c096ca8bb64fb83efd96213971706183ee2fae27f6dfd387639","7d3cd2f7dc98de0198b559942a7c62f599f249e051db027dbd021a4f5dd7cbf7","732b6bade3495ca79205f6b0a7e89ba4271a85e49c91fa10750f58c0d18732ba","96a24c5d6adcfc765012f9f7b5a2c7ceb5c18cd6cfe875bf6770d2ebc1b51e01","538ae67df77ceb5147b06963a1716cbe05c0400d0dd36570dafb832928d85671","f937a6e05e7827ba2023000f78c5aafdefa70e3e3dc312cefc9ce0ac700a3b9b","d44923914ad6fa58bab3cefb1e9e6288eae0b92337c8ad45e02bb2baa45e13ac","2dcb4c621102129005c8a2a68b25dd3d447389198242c056e24ea319d7e5b40b","e72daa7d24eb65159702cc5405718273f7871d1bb64b233c5943beb6f5ed7d1e","d494e4cf05af7269f2ce9dadb697e15285442e93ae20aa1b1cec95d931e3a426","ce58ffadcfcca79e31a1397344c86f86f58fe3f79820242e0aff9579caabaf7a","43f24146ae1a913115f29d2b71acb5ea378a841110c597c5a78367f17e33f9cc","9ae07d1cc89dc4f38c4932a739fe03e6d7ceeb9c9a26a9605c258b74ecaf48d2","b5239e249bc8263fb31f47fbbd439a7988e5926d748624c76f7c6530fd58c38b","d5bea418d71d31679aabc40f5ffca190873799947ebb9bf929546abe2f87357c","fd6073e49aa513638ff5659f9af5f1a5a46eb52e8d954826e6d1a00e665d8e94","f248d67f5bb3f7da6d1f0a4a242161638c6d6d86c48f32b87d558313e1578919","5725dea800da1f17549a3cc3b