{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":54456},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54457},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ULInformationTransferIRAT","paragraph_zero_based":54458},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2","paragraph_zero_based":54459},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ULInformationTransferMRDC","paragraph_zero_based":54460},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":54461},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":54462},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-","paragraph_zero_based":54463},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54464},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:This message type carries segments of other RRC messages. The protection of an instance of this message is the same as for the message which this message is carrying.","paragraph_zero_based":54465},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:This message type carries others RRC messages. The protection of an instance of this message is the same as for the message which this message is carrying.","paragraph_zero_based":54466},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54467},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"B.2Description of BWP configuration options","paragraph_zero_based":54468},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"There are two possible ways to configure BWP#0 (i.e. the initial BWP) for a UE:","paragraph_zero_based":54469},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1)Configure BWP-DownlinkCommon and BWP-UplinkCommon in ServingCellConfigCommon, but do not configure dedicated configurations in BWP-DownlinkDedicated or BWP-UplinkDedicated in ServingCellConfig.","paragraph_zero_based":54470},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2)Configure both BWP-DownlinkCommon and BWP-UplinkCommon in ServingCellConfigCommon and configure dedicated configurations in at least one of BWP-DownlinkDedicated or BWP-UplinkDedicated in ServingCellConfig.","paragraph_zero_based":54471},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The same way of configuration is used for UL BWP#0 and DL BWP#0 if both are configured.","paragraph_zero_based":54472},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"With the first option (illustrated by figure B2-1 below), the BWP#0 is not considered to be an RRC-configured BWP, i.e., UE only supporting one BWP can still be configured with BWP#1 in addition to BWP#0 when using this configuration. The BWP#0 can still be used even if it does not have the dedicated configuration, albeit in a more limited manner since only the SIB1-defined configurations are available. For example, only DCI format 1_0 can be used with BWP#0 without dedicated configuration, so changing to another BWP requires RRCReconfiguration since DCI format 1_0 doesn't support DCI-based switching.","paragraph_zero_based":54473},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54474},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure B2-1: BWP#0 configuration without dedicated configuration","paragraph_zero_based":54475},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"With the second option (illustrated by figure B2-2 below), the BWP#0 is considered to be an RRC-configured BWP, i.e. UE only supporting one BWP cannot be configured with BWP#1 in addition to BWP#0 when using this configuration. However, UE supporting more than one BWP can still switch to and from BWP#0 e.g. via DCI normally, and there are no explicit limitations to using the BWP#0 (compared to the first option).","paragraph_zero_based":54476},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54477},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure B2-2: BWP#0 configuration with dedicated configuration","paragraph_zero_based":54478},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For BWP#0, the BWP-DownlinkCommon and BWP-UplinkCommon in ServingCellConfigCommon should match the parameters configured by MIB and SIB1 (if provided) in the corresponding serving cell.","paragraph_zero_based":54479}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["30deb9ac45513183db70a17d0b3ed50744bfa1aa885f22f0807631400d92f447","a40001be4161d33a75f60ff836a5ce7857e72782c9ffb5a9d7bc1d0d817698fc","04a6e803d36685ce5242533e534a5733a91116a3b0fea6cb1a0773bd2ee069ba","e217ee8ee3b449d0df2f2e9a7c043a38289473e286a9aba13fba642e21de2abb","15e405e4325442a5c75d02aeee2252f9ff23960d6a658119d25f8be37cde0db9","9ff7b254e8c499e7558afa082fe1f0a2af19ca0c8e439313efe4925931cae0b7","45c5b9c400415bceea5fb01c94492104586be8a42d1af2ebfa52d70f25374e99","7b590ee6b4c962c19bcd68c954776d270c8a3a27f5ced2b03621945736d33e82","2bf3452a9de7e2b70e0de11cb9189a9df97baac07f23100fa34e09a3378cb1ed","73d8b20e8cd4eed39b9b80c3f4d5b0fd2796f252a27ae16b445e348769a0ef44","9a9a8e4ae6d00b41e6c276f5b64dd9425bc2985de382cbd8936792f4e4a86468","e67f5ec7d1f37b4529bc51194a45b93785273a95593ea086b837fac8aab41b02","f4fd3148d58d8ae3ed21272aac4955cb7b9106e205d7e0757015f82512dda948","371287b68898b3f5ab72293a4254e3a6c3b8d737670e2be52f0c25e564a248f9","d1dd37ae85440baba0ac28d9971c398341992686d8d32d7e4fd9054873eac8db","a66b0b3cc20a37fbee7b63d096f64b9b6c9656a92976cf87f932277ea4ebfc96","4d44ebb9e253c2efa363fe41db8b2a4f62d3eda5e9c46069c8cc95cbe1fc1982","d3bf6893fe23767b1f5b2bc48046dc25c74fced118c41f49fcae9337405a7410","97d7073ad96a194a90ddbd006655fcaa576f3df5f59b688cebca376f95415ce4","72156d4c618132ca7d29b513e5cec812eb7474f74357952c3d7bfbd509ff45a9","e7d0c6e4a27c8cdc034978fcc37d0e3d29ba20b3d2df2b88d6478114d5b2f5cb","3167a73312104b417637a91873330593146c19c40199c993d5947c2c2f4794ac","a1d784824c68c3407f2a7970e04d2a7161eece81f7ec131e2198acd78caf381c","b35334ec326fee6ed0843c05cc37a1f0187140bfbcc3974956ba3a10038dbafd"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[54456,54479],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx:p54456"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2403537.zip::R2-2403537 RRC.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If an (e)RedCap-specific initial DL BWP is configured, for BWP switching, the BWP #0 always maps to the (e)RedCap-specific initial DL BWP. If a RedCap-specific initial UL BWP is configured, for BWP switching on NUL, the BWP #0 always maps to the RedCap-specific initial UL BWP, for BWP switching on SUL, the BWP#0 always maps to the initial UL BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":54480},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54481},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Annex C (normative):List of CRs Containing Early Implementable Features and Corrections","paragraph_zero_based":54482},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This annex lists the Change Requests (CRs) whose changes may be implemented by a UE of an earlier release than which the CR was approved in (i.e. CRs that contain on their coversheets the sentence \"Implementation of this CR from Rel-N will not cause interoperability issues\").","paragraph_zero_based":54483},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Table C-1: List of CRs Containing Early Implementable Features and Corrections","paragraph_zero_based":54484},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TDoc Number (RP-xxxxxx): CR Title","paragraph_zero_based":54485},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CR Number(s)","paragraph_zero_based":54486},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CR Revision Number(s)","paragraph_zero_based":54487},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Earliest Implementable Release","paragraph_zero_based":54488},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Additional Information","paragraph_zero_based":54489},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RP-200335: Correction on usage of access category 2 for UAC for RNA update","paragraph_zero_based":54490},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1141","paragraph_zero_based":54491},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2","paragraph_zero_based":54492},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release 15","paragraph_zero_based":54493},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54494},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RP-201185: Introduction of signalling for high-speed train scenarios","paragraph_zero_based":54495},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1464","paragraph_zero_based":54496},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5","paragraph_zero_based":54497},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release 15","paragraph_zero_based":54498},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54499},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RP-201216: Release-16 UE capabilities based on RAN1, RAN4 feature lists and RAN2","paragraph_zero_based":54500},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1665","paragraph_zero_based":54501},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2","paragraph_zero_based":54502},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release 15","paragraph_zero_based":54503}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3766e0911ef1aaf617f1c44270e04d314f46e1ea6b971f374458ec068bbc9bb5","original_member_sha256":"0471885931db9d8903847ae27a7db1ede99f912460c3f55d37683308dfbebd05","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["9d6d16e7a6c0b8e8322c1b3c940eb07da0bda7d300029fe01ee5680d9141067a","4408a4367801ac1420787f1ba38812cfcc30a9b40088337bd771ad1aef0f6347","fee8919538f4c5af398862568d903de52b3cd5079d7baf3df481be0d5a210484","03cbe6d3b7ae12be1c9d1aef3bf1a98a52f04cf61d0b2f5a778368ae35f4fcac","7607f0ef7e78e2618b82f3b98e79c8afb845d438ecc390c6bf6b122ee90af2be","3beeeedb21763934bf77755636d7e672695cd8ec2b63be9d6e1fca790e68e592","76723c7f20da0c8c59e87013533176c1d0679fbb2dfeefb76dc02d81f771c68b","e1beef9105ad021270f1826fc04245793847e899395d0e591a99c404a961c35e","f29905117d66b68fef494d30b2175cd897a4d21ce0473a17abb48181dbec13ac","eb2d759483845975ea9db79861d86e96d4ea40c9b7fbde2fb47a1845884be2b2","070549037b4557f14c250197a76d954bc0ca4eb51930bbc1e9f5435c0254e4ca","03d1acf9026c16ffad2da4