{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>except if going to RRC_IDLE was triggered by inter-RAT cell reselection while the UE is in RRC_INACTIVE or RRC_IDLE or when selecting an inter-RAT cell while T311 was running or when selecting an E-UTRA cell for EPS fallback for IMS voice as specified in 5.4.3.5:","paragraph_zero_based":4488},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE is capable of L2 U2N Remote UE:","paragraph_zero_based":4489},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>enter RRC_IDLE, and perform either cell selection as specified in TS 38.304 [20], or relay selection as specified in clause 5.8.15.3, or both;","paragraph_zero_based":4490},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":4491},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>enter RRC_IDLE and perform cell selection as specified in TS 38.304 [20];","paragraph_zero_based":4492},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:Whether to release the PC5 unicast link is left to L2 U2N Remote UE's implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":4493},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:It is left to UE implementation whether to stop T430, if running, when going to RRC_IDLE.","paragraph_zero_based":4494},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.12UE actions upon PUCCH/SRS release request","paragraph_zero_based":4495},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon receiving a PUCCH release request from lower layers, for all bandwidth parts of an indicated serving cell the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":4496},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release PUCCH-CSI-Resources configured in CSI-ReportConfig;","paragraph_zero_based":4497},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release SchedulingRequestResourceConfig instances configured in PUCCH-Config.","paragraph_zero_based":4498},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon receiving an SRS release request from lower layers, for all bandwidth parts of an indicated serving cell the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":4499},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release SRS-Resource instances configured in SRS-Config.","paragraph_zero_based":4500},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon receiving a positioning SRS configuration for RRC_INACTIVE release request from lower layers, the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":4501},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release the configured srs-PosRRC-Inactive.","paragraph_zero_based":4502},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.13RRC connection resume","paragraph_zero_based":4503},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.13.1General","paragraph_zero_based":4504},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":4505},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.3.13.1-1: RRC connection resume, successful","paragraph_zero_based":4506},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":4507},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.3.13.1-2: RRC connection resume fallback to RRC connection establishment, successful","paragraph_zero_based":4508},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":4509},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.3.13.1-3: RRC connection resume followed by network release, successful","paragraph_zero_based":4510},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":4511}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["358f769ab6db76ebd69b1e474543de7e8d83aed2b295488309904bdd1b33aa15","ef51e042c9e9071f67b23080813db821480e23735c6b68fa99a04312a55a4574","897908aff9e5a05ae223b6de3468a879113063a9059fb35a9405b8ca376e4b6b","0c54a59db9190f4558f68d3a5eb36712f9295f11c3f0c943c0f63ac190c5fbf3","3e73b8d62496b7e373500a8677aeb7a96028b4f2ddadf544ecbe6c7864cbd8e0","9424421cbf1824fb0a19463fce65470cfbb1ee99b523d29eefd4ee7539bedfc1","f345765e3a161c274a965e24c721f7cc9671ba90fa6af6b46fc2f9a0f70bb3ab","2ba1349fe013081d51ec3da95e48f0735e5b089a551616ce13675dadc5a5807d","f99ab3b51dbec4383c98c9f33bc38f1f6788650fbf38c4460927e7b18760a0e8","94fe142e6e716e5b5a28ae8a974ce036bf6ce10ee71472a078f20699c39fa49e","ac3b9cbd7c0f9ecdbb370b05a593bc316087fce05d85d1e9269cf1db1f1e0211","9837de869c0f9398df89733ca9ebebeb4bff46f602478c41f0dd926a8a44631c","d41bfaf31ee6659a7bfba57a16fa35d95ca961b01c03576146a25f6f934ab18e","219b7ff42a7b26ada94265e7c2b1b7eb875653df5634df97f9917f7ee63133a7","2786cfd2d4e3c2c5c4c144f7473afcc4ba4b4958aa07ca057857d13e5584a029","db7ab198b306457268bcd28b979fd1646c3785d7787b919bc6604ca368792ed6","e9ec2c51b44572c7bef94dbd86eb3a9949b45c9a2cf5614d7b96c9098704ffba","9306c85707d63957c157e315764d968b172ad645882a43d61ac39e895092979f","b43fc68f39494ce414621200cde437628114bf74ef908055eba8406a1803048e","68c63481f9e53e3ba8f6ca2b41bc64b64525bcdb7aa99ffc926c95c01268db24","bff728e35f833e5b4206820eca2b89808c2f3fbda4fbd561b682ae32b510de53","7e6baaf7f593ef7a10062f56c2efeb11755cc0b5578d8902d834c835a6c64383","4158c41bd0cc3def905fbc6125da9b2370d2109cad9dbd90e21f467508eddd31","e3611707e3bc76d4de9d53eaf1d5671ebcc8763d9e2dd775c32a19cf6aa58563"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[4488,4511],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p4488"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.3.13.1-4: RRC connection resume followed by network suspend, successful","paragraph_zero_based":4512},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":4513},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.3.13.1-5: RRC connection resume, network reject","paragraph_zero_based":4514},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The purpose of this procedure is to resume a suspended RRC connection, including resuming SRB(s), DRB(s) and multicast MRB(s) or perform an RNA update. This procedure is also used to initiate SDT in RRC_INACTIVE.","paragraph_zero_based":4515},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.13.1aConditions for resuming RRC Connection for NR sidelink communication/discovery/V2X sidelink communication","paragraph_zero_based":4516},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For NR sidelink communication/discovery an RRC connection is resumed only in the following cases:","paragraph_zero_based":4517},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink communication and related data is available for transmission:","paragraph_zero_based":4518},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the frequency on which the UE is configured to transmit NR sidelink communication is included in sl-FreqInfoList/sl-FreqInfoListSizeExt within SIB12 provided by the cell on which the UE camps; and if the valid version of SIB12 does not include sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency;","paragraph_zero_based":4519},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink discovery and related data is available for transmission:","paragraph_zero_based":4520},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE is configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink L2 U2N relay discovery messages and sl-L2U2N-Relay is included in SIB12; or","paragraph_zero_based":4521},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE is configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink L3 U2N relay discovery messages and sl-L3U2N-RelayDiscovery is included in SIB12; or","paragraph_zero_based":4522},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE is configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink non-relay discovery messages and sl-NonRelayDiscovery is included in SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":4523},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the frequency on which the UE is configured to transmit NR sidelink discovery is included in sl-FreqInfoList within SIB12 provided by the cell on which the UE camps; and if the valid version of SIB12 does not include sl-DiscTxPoolSelected or sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency;","paragraph_zero_based":4524},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For L2 U2N Relay UE in RRC_INACTIVE, an RRC connection establishment is resumed in the following cases:","paragraph_zero_based":4525},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if any message is received from the L2 U2N Remote UE via SL-RLC0 as specified in 9.1.1.4 or SL-RLC1 as specified in 9.2.4; or","paragraph_zero_based":4526},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if RemoteUEInformationSidelink containing the connectionForMP is received from a L2 U2N Remote UE as specified in 5.8.9.8.3;","paragraph_zero_based":4527},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For V2X sidelink communication an RRC connection resume is initiated only when the conditions specified for V2X sidelink communication in clause 5.3.3.1a of TS 36.331 [10] are met.","paragraph_zero_based":4528},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:Upper layers initiate an RRC connection resume (except if the RRC connection resume is initiated at the L2 U2N Relay UE upon reception of a message from a L2 U2N Remote UE via SL-RLC0 or SL-RLC1). The interaction with NAS is left to UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":4529},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.13.1bConditions for initiating SDT","paragraph_zero_based":4530},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When requesting lower layers to check the conditions for initiating SDT, RRC indicates to lower layers whether the resume procedure is initiated for mobile originated or mobile terminated case.","paragraph_zero_based":4531},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE in RRC_INACTIVE initiates the resume procedure for SDT when all of the following conditions are fulfilled:","paragraph_zero_based":4532},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for the resume procedure initiated by the upper layers (i.e. mobile originated case):","paragraph_zero_based":4533},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>SIB1 includes sdt-ConfigCommon; and","paragraph_zero_based":4534},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>sdt-Config is configured; and","paragraph_zero_based":4535}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["439b921a5927701993d5d3d69f96806255f050d7d1731d8144fbbb3d46d6b69c","770bab2afed216f9768e66728e17d4c59a4c6090cc76fd7abcc2e3a68d64fe6c","0e50f00a8feb2df4d6097f9ac8aedf4175493b97ecd4ad42c197b99d8ef325e2","e725daa302ec65c9d2893fa4a12c45e7e34dd82a4d77e187a1eaf49c4baf175a","466582e905e10ecdc6dda3a848071939da458b93355ec8eda2283c27031bbe58","25fb56bf6aa9e318b4ce13f006282eff7456591a65d9b0af11a921e1d67588de","51d480b0370853669ca642ea839e995fe8973ebec078d7c699bea3eae100c3d5","6cffb613c34bf075e6302c1d3f9ebec42c773bf157a302cdc354215bb26dd30e","acc904291d60f3c4f2ac957751d0e5f1791b4b8d6e7c20a5f19233dc81ecefb9","c247cbb15eb792b0371fa286b92e000519c480c723ee26728718668cfed9ecfb","ce9182a53b7db91705e65722879633dba787eef2a4c15a4c04cf742b2ae8ac9d","d9a979a0cb206a0a27d8246457a8d0596b2c4c66d0f458d726e26dda3fc3696e","454b3b9dfe106f87456e37fcf097e5ee551ae422f95f7c929a3a97fd688d09bb","fbd7444f6af2edd3d581d57387a4c1145fbaab83a9812cd03094f1da0660d5f9","b7df082f8e776605847f32c6bdb65dec907c48b19170cc6321591aa3be7bb9ca","cc08f37e196e2d1a5ea14509c8d368123a44ee01ceb5e8176dd8761e76004de1","a3e8fe3f78363210ef7f6a8e0feb37e3f0f6303c1b3d950d33b717762e64353b","5fa14cf0830597edf255c4dfc768631865795645ddb6a8610d1eeca6d324b8c9","bde9d6d85bc6008ee5dc8b2ff96b5af7a4429cdce7f114cc1b6dc18a544e8fe7","dfdc47c957f673a50fcd6312e99c66817c15908366757319c6817b4175debcfc","9aa8860ce64e4b390baf752b311b7610503b0e8ac01fe7c3bc61f45b27159859","aa74cf612659185922dff45f4417d299a77aee855f2c055b012ce51a5ac936fc","344fbe1c4ac08084077ba6f2023cb0948b4781793d8394edc221c13587abb1bc","7641c17b160a13a36dd69e514e9743bbcce35f44abdc5e9b437d39677eac3d98"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[4512,4535],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p4512"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>all the pending data in UL is mapped to the radio bearers configured for SDT; and","paragraph_zero_based":4536},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for an (e)RedCap UE when RedCap-specific initial downlink BWP includes no CD-SSB, ncd-SSB-RedCapInitialBWP-SDT is configured; and","paragraph_zero_based":4537},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>lower layers indicate that conditions for initiating MO-SDT as specified in TS 38.321 [3] are fulfilled.","paragraph_zero_based":4538},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for the resume procedure initiated in response to RAN paging (i.e. mobile terminated case):","paragraph_zero_based":4539},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>lower layers indicate that conditions for initiating MT-SDT as specified in TS 38.321 [3] are fulfilled.","paragraph_zero_based":4540},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:How the UE determines that all pending data in UL is mapped to radio bearers configured for SDT is left to UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":4541},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.13.1cVoid","paragraph_zero_based":4542},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.13.1dConditions for resuming RRC connection for multicast reception","paragraph_zero_based":4543},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In RRC_INACTIVE state, if configured with MBS multicast reception in RRC_INACTIVE, the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":4544},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRC connection resume procedure is triggered for multicast reception at reception of SIB1, as specified in 5.2.2.4.2; or","paragraph_zero_based":4545},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the PTM configuration is not available in the cell after cell selection or reselection for a multicast session that the UE has joined and for which the UE is not indicated to stop monitoring the G-RNTI; or","paragraph_zero_based":4546},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if mbs-NeighbourCellList included in MBSMulticastConfiguration acquired in the previous cell indicates that a multicast session that the UE has joined and for which the UE is not indicated to stop monitoring the G-RNTI, is not provided for RRC_INACTIVE in the current serving cell; or","paragraph_zero_based":4547},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if either the measured RSRP or RSRQ for serving cell as specified in TS 38.304 [20] is below the corresponding threshold indicated by thresholdIndex for a multicast session that the UE has joined and for which the UE is not indicated to stop monitoring the G-RNTI:","paragraph_zero_based":4548},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>initiate RRC connection resume procedure as specified in 5.3.13.2 with resumeCause set as below:","paragraph_zero_based":4549},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is configured by upper layers with Access Identity 1:","paragraph_zero_based":4550},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set resumeCause to mps-PriorityAccess;","paragraph_zero_based":4551},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else if the UE is configured by upper layers with Access Identity 2:","paragraph_zero_based":4552},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set resumeCause to mcs-PriorityAccess;","paragraph_zero_based":4553},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else if the UE is configured by upper layers with one or more Access Identities equal to 11-15:","paragraph_zero_based":4554},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set resumeCause to highPriorityAccess;","paragraph_zero_based":4555},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else:","paragraph_zero_based":4556},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set resumeCause to mt-Access.","paragraph_zero_based":4557},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.13.2Initiation","paragraph_zero_based":4558},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE initiates the procedure when upper layers or AS (when responding to RAN paging, upon triggering RNA updates while the UE is in RRC_INACTIVE, upon requesting multicast reception as specified in clause 5.3.13.1d, for NR sidelink communication/discovery/V2X sidelink communication as specified in clause 5.3.13.1a, for NR sidelink positioning as specified in clause 5.3.13.1c, for requesting configuration for SRS for positioning, for activation of preconfigured Positioning SRS in RRC_INACTIVE, upon receiving RRCRelease message including resumeIndication) requests the resume of a suspended RRC connection or requests the resume for initiating SDT as specified in clause 5.3.13.1b.","paragraph_zero_based":4559}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["744568bf6293b9f9945de1ef8ce123364180ad3841d44aa05518b61def29af6c","7ca185b01bc1ebdfbef6042ef40306a1fcbac7368738868588a81d89707090a3","c098452344c709fda1636fe6ed7686a8c230e7506b5e79a9fb917cadf5a4bb13","3d11cf736f02efb71bea675d58f19452372813cd6d5c4a10fc362ebe11fbef08","c743337b97d677b1f649a7f2717695916cbec2c7bd20c8c46aeae76d48589082","bf00aab9254b20c54c9ede3b9918cf94a83d0c5e63b4445116bd4c2f2372b87b","3c80a6ecabe4d418e4e8cb7aa82b2f1a9906c983c83e488cde3ddaa3d6bf1fc7","521469a3629322f7829ae46523edbeafc9fcb787e67870cc4c059125dcace233","edb195f729d50b097c1afe81227b48e7925bd5013d673452a3d2033fe7930826","d07f04589601f157b30a0566c00bbd92edf0d7b1ed79cc41061ea09bc59a361a","5ffeffe2852295f835ac7e64ac135e5cc8b5494e1e758f872613ce12af010406","0934fa052adf00e4c14362102c0b901f5adca40be5712a03f934b8ba6011fd15","9a8fcd111fb8a3d177ef1ffa9ea5115691fa9023547e7e1190bb5bd95cd049d4","c5a5de5bb9c2744093e65fe0090b8e54acccb4257a00444209a85717b6fb52c8","c311beb8d3873a3e50f0f596cbfc41a8a7c37a6035e7835b5600f99d48d5e371","bc6f10389c5c4aa2dffe7cba3df64b5ac0bba0c443f359b6c60a1891de925ed1","e9dea60fa2fe5ef64bd9309cdb4006f3e8bfe216fb603f38ec99c95e73ee4a21","ee627056dda424d19f2bbbf245dea246209f0687c39418015d3bb3959bd61ae3","cf0433a7b552fb1ca3b86115de8dae6f2207a9d643a789804d7ba25bfaa80760","d3a0a6a0b4810c69f04a6b1953923b3da53c31fff1ea994d098659f8be81be6c","39ccd5d2b88758c7345af807a54e43084f2c31e70d861715c79a50345feab179","5a309988d425086449707c3225081e76eb98fa4923062e0d973ad622055192cc","dd1771152a2ab5309641af54a275db0eebe622f54b23891145da4779bc6bc3d0","3192d4c09b1df14c6808d39ac2a6dac25d7fd22d933a3dd490879af3a27f1831"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[4536,4559],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p4536"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall ensure having valid and up to date essential system information as specified in clause 5.2.2.2 before initiating this procedure.","paragraph_zero_based":4560},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon initiation of the procedure, the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":4561},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the resumption of the RRC connection is triggered by response to NG-RAN paging; or","paragraph_zero_based":4562},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1> if the resumption of the RRC connection is triggered by receiving RRCRelease message including resumeIndication; or","paragraph_zero_based":4563},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the resumption of the RRC connection is triggered for multicast reception as specified in clause 5.3.13.1d:","paragraph_zero_based":4564},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>select '0' as the Access Category;","paragraph_zero_based":4565},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the unified access control procedure as specified in 5.3.14 using the selected Access Category and one or more Access Identities provided by upper layers;","paragraph_zero_based":4566},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the access attempt is barred, the procedure ends;","paragraph_zero_based":4567},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else if the resumption of the RRC connection is triggered by upper layers:","paragraph_zero_based":4568},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the upper layers provide an Access Category and one or more Access Identities:","paragraph_zero_based":4569},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform the unified access control procedure as specified in 5.3.14 using the Access Category and Access Identities provided by upper layers;","paragraph_zero_based":4570},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the access attempt is barred, the procedure ends;","paragraph_zero_based":4571},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the upper layers provide NSAG information and one or more S-NSSAI(s) triggering the access attempt (TS 23.501 [32] and TS 24.501 [23]):","paragraph_zero_based":4572},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>apply the NSAG with highest NSAG priority among the NSAGs that are included in SIB1 (i.e., in FeatureCombination and/or in RA-PrioritizationSliceInfo), and that are associated with the S-NSSAI(s) triggering the access attempt, in the Random Access procedure (TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.1);","paragraph_zero_based":4573},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 0:If there are multiple NSAGs with the same highest NAS-provided NSAG priority identified for access attempt as above, it is left to UE implementation to select the NSAG to be applied in the Random Access procedure.","paragraph_zero_based":4574},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the resumption occurs after release with redirect with mpsPriorityIndication:","paragraph_zero_based":4575},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the resumeCause to mps-PriorityAccess;","paragraph_zero_based":4576},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":4577},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the resumeCause in accordance with the information received from upper layers;","paragraph_zero_based":4578},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else if the resumption of the RRC connection is triggered due to an RNA update as specified in 5.3.13.8:","paragraph_zero_based":4579},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if an emergency service is ongoing:","paragraph_zero_based":4580},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:How the RRC layer in the UE is aware of an ongoing emergency service is up to UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":4581},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>select '2' as the Access Category;","paragraph_zero_based":4582},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the resumeCause to emergency;","paragraph_zero_based":4583}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["2f4f8a382d72ae1f19c18764bc40078431305e8d88dbcfe881840cbc871e4c70","fe7424b6998efbcc1003794721016f7f587512b423995e4e323b432b02c31aed","90b700396e3f3108af7aa7d87b25a940932deeac91a1687c08c70bdd0316d0c5","3be696e01554893188d1723c6a4a204e12758bff09e94b45e6e05ac466be6894","1dfb10ca0e5f941daa86e9cb08d3468bdf85277c09d81bb3a213e6b864c88363","b7fdf8328a55a539de015d7c542b267de4bbb0a37a8eddf7afab8242e963c773","fd27b7bce68cd89be48e6b6db4489408575d922be2922d4ee8863f3b7c220102","e8d592c6e1f50d90ec3dc1b6ae8f1e18cc30629ed4a7b006541cc5ad20b32baf","23cadb05328df04c4883f0d9a2ca09ab9d4517c9dd6a2254da5c185395e98b48","73530e37cd0ea490a19b85bf4e91333b5d0e2c38a3f39329673db7dab0bc5da6","30ac42c1073812c7c0f735a8523b42023e2665ccaf25a0ebbb74282e56550104","be7377c8f7d746ccb9f81219e9b77e811944f294e563a62e7b447fba2425b790","1b845dbf1db3309b8672cbc3007601c2876be64e8517b9dca779d6bf47a51100","817f37b24f7ecbf314740eab65234473fd425c69bf33a196128f4cab0ee881df","40b3c6904e718adecac043286b7948bac677a8892844d852619b1632388ab360","79e6de8d0d216946a9bea2e3764044f107c3203184f20c9826326b90113e7b4a","371e0ba0b4e17a67360ec036a047c4840133ec67e22ffb3c7b2aa8415d298229","6c5d8e26d9a0a428b3545a1052b77da1cc4b114261bf354a12c0bcc22c7e4e28","17ee2c1f53cc4f0cb4bd67bd26197b007866f4d67dab411e9054510234ac2602","e565e940fc21618b950c760e7933c88685b43bed3bb2356b31bf33cbb0316729","135b8b948f0524e1a25f44bbea67c4643261567f36623959fa4ef79066264104","5af6fea6d55ace78c5a7b44f9757acec38c52a53c7b58ea5da97199d12a9d43f","5abb3146023d62bd320e8c415f1cc05b707c9a9299a2e2e8c1f08eaa91b9c758","79062363a7f9214789eec0036c80d95a238b398f2e96b2cc48277ca972daa189"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[4560,4583],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p4560"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":4584},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>select '8' as the Access Category;","paragraph_zero_based":4585},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the unified access control procedure as specified in 5.3.14 using the selected Access Category and one or more Access Identities to be applied as specified in TS 24.501 [23];","paragraph_zero_based":4586},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the access attempt is barred:","paragraph_zero_based":4587},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set the variable pendingRNA-Update to true;","paragraph_zero_based":4588},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>the procedure ends;","paragraph_zero_based":4589},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else if srs-PosRRC-InactiveValidityAreaPreConfigList or srs-PosRRC-InactiveValidityAreaNonPreConfig is configured:","paragraph_zero_based":4590},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the resumption of the RRC connection is triggered due to cell reselection as specified in clause 5.3.13.6; or","paragraph_zero_based":4591},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the resumption of the RRC connection is triggered due to the need for SRS for positioning configuration and no stored srs-PosRRC-InactiveValidityAreaPreConfigList for the camped cell exists; or","paragraph_zero_based":4592},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the resumption of the RRC connection is triggered for activation of srs-PosRRC-InactiveValidityAreaPreConfigList when the UE is camped in one of the cells indicated in srs-PosConfigValidityArea:","paragraph_zero_based":4593},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if an emergency service is ongoing:","paragraph_zero_based":4594},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>select '2' as the Access Category;","paragraph_zero_based":4595},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set the resumeCause to emergency;","paragraph_zero_based":4596},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else:","paragraph_zero_based":4597},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>select '8' as the Access Category;","paragraph_zero_based":4598},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set the resumeCause to srs-PosConfigOrActivationReq;","paragraph_zero_based":4599},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:In case the L2 U2N Relay UE initiates RRC connection resume triggered either by reception of message from a L2 U2N Remote UE via SL-RLC0 or SL-RLC1 as specified in 5.3.13.1a, or by reception of the RemoteUEInformationSidelink message containing the connectionForMP as specified in 5.3.13.1a, the L2 U2N Relay UE sets the resumeCause by implementation, but it can only set the emergency, mps-PriorityAccess, or mcs-PriorityAccess as resumeCause, if the same cause value in the message received from the L2 U2N Remote UE via SL-RLC0.","paragraph_zero_based":4600},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is in NE-DC or NR-DC:","paragraph_zero_based":4601},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE does not support maintaining SCG configuration upon connection resumption:","paragraph_zero_based":4602},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>release the MR-DC related configurations (i.e., as specified in 5.3.5.10) from the UE Inactive AS context, if stored;","paragraph_zero_based":4603},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE does not support maintaining the MCG SCell configurations upon connection resumption:","paragraph_zero_based":4604},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the MCG SCell(s) from the UE Inactive AS context, if stored;","paragraph_zero_based":4605},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as L2 U2N Remote UE:","paragraph_zero_based":4606},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>establish a SRAP entity as specified in TS 38.351 [66], if no SRAP entity has been established;","paragraph_zero_based":4607}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e60c8cd3fe543ea81c6fd44d94f965d556ba807ad7d10687551d152794dc7be1","0cc2c2653985914a202f1ba0483e974accb319be57af3e9d8cdad5960cac7459","0c759f02bf78ff793a054780d467d8d90c3c3205cba21857338a0bf0026f3c3b","420314310c5bc1557d4edf69216189b35d526ee1c5f1032047fadf6fcdcdec3c","20b02e87735377302fd05070a3cce9ddb6fd067bc9e123b4920238f9549f5767","c926f678a1d870cc29feb5b4de608b3bba07f6323eeb681a043f96f811eac7f0","5ab173198c6577d2c62cc21c7c98b74856ae03b5818becd862c415f63915a17a","c601e54cec05d2e837f2dc19cec92c159833cc288ff8082ca9e1402fcb81f44b","cd3c53fd12c5e55303ec474e5697e02ac5f9765c9ac031765e63977d3e3e4466","a0839a6c796f5aad2a598777531b08709bdb278acfbfc1298ef8757928b1bcf6","fdb4155433a26026c2b383d0aa4bdad81b1f73940db5e65bc176eb8fd7e3aa28","95ccfd8db05f3c39c0844e1e843a1361bc3e726dc02820faff130dd88a044ad5","84cfa2aa914a151abca72fa756347f31cfd20232fd33321944297c7e132410d8","3d77c85d3303c7a75eab41811c917124fdcfec28817611b0c85e6f7b90c478a8","1876d3489d4542a3371f54329e66031aec73ce3df8529f396c2ad46a1dee009f","a2190cabce80f78c69e9591f570247af7b91c344c0fa04ea3ad3819047fc745c","164b6ad0c483fa31be64280d888e81da2ba505ab3194e20ca30f06eb173eaa81","37ede89ab9a9891d36c8affb3b7e19cb66dccff129dbf2e40259c72a6f9df82e","7a7cf6b11c54919ac9c9194c847b8e5ce6be135f0f303ee8526364e27b518534","9c3f990e1e1547e437f784aaf37043dcfaf52c26ac447203dfa0abe37139ce3e","27f7db90b0e41446a4ebebbe5968b03cbfb15b7182053329411e72f28725b2f1","bfed16433be93540c0b83a7b6796f1b2dc84a2073f5c4de1a6c26ee8c1f8cd0a","decae7fccc3bce74ce38da6bb251c9fc80658cc386f6767688a7913ff3063499","87d960aaf2196e2a3ad37c04199fbd38f6a4d2d89a5aa55fcef578859cdc0081"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[4584,4607],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p4584"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>apply the default configuration of SL-RLC1 as defined in 9.2.4 for SRB1;","paragraph_zero_based":4608},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>apply the default PDCP configuration as defined in 9.2.1 for SRB1;","paragraph_zero_based":4609},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>apply the default configuration of SRAP as defined in 9.2.5 for SRB1;","paragraph_zero_based":4610},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":4611},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>apply the default L1 parameter values as specified in corresponding physical layer specifications, except for the parameters for which values are provided in SIB1;","paragraph_zero_based":4612},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>apply the default SRB1 configuration as specified in 9.2.1;","paragraph_zero_based":4613},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>apply the default MAC Cell Group configuration as specified in 9.2.2;","paragraph_zero_based":4614},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release delayBudgetReportingConfig from the UE Inactive AS context, if stored;","paragraph_zero_based":4615},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>stop timer T342, if running;","paragraph_zero_based":4616},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release overheatingAssistanceConfig from the UE Inactive AS context, if stored;","paragraph_zero_based":4617},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>stop timer T345, if running;","paragraph_zero_based":4618},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release idc-AssistanceConfig from the UE Inactive AS context, if stored;","paragraph_zero_based":4619},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release drx-PreferenceConfig for all configured cell groups from the UE Inactive AS context, if stored;","paragraph_zero_based":4620},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>stop all instances of timer T346a, if running;","paragraph_zero_based":4621},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release maxBW-PreferenceConfig and maxBW-PreferenceConfigFR2-2 for all configured cell groups from the UE Inactive AS context, if stored;","paragraph_zero_based":4622},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>stop all instances of timer T346b, if running;","paragraph_zero_based":4623},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release maxCC-PreferenceConfig for all configured cell groups from the UE Inactive AS context, if stored;","paragraph_zero_based":4624},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>stop all instances of timer T346c, if running;","paragraph_zero_based":4625},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release maxMIMO-LayerPreferenceConfig and maxMIMO-LayerPreferenceConfigFR2-2 for all configured cell groups from the UE Inactive AS context, if stored;","paragraph_zero_based":4626},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>stop all instances of timer T346d, if running;","paragraph_zero_based":4627},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release minSchedulingOffsetPreferenceConfig and minSchedulingOffsetPreferenceConfigExt for all configured cell groups from the UE Inactive AS context, if stored;","paragraph_zero_based":4628},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>stop all instances of timer T346e, if running;","paragraph_zero_based":4629},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release rlm-RelaxationReportingConfig for all configured cell groups from the UE Inactive AS context, if stored;","paragraph_zero_based":4630},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>stop all instances of timer T346j, if running;","paragraph_zero_based":4631}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["62542658743571bcee24b1cac8ca71e59296b2c3f2c6a627549edb