{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>include these addresses in non-f1-Traffic-IP-Address.","paragraph_zero_based":8760},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if IPv6 addresses are used for all traffic:","paragraph_zero_based":8761},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>include these addresses in all-Traffic-IAB-IP-Address.","paragraph_zero_based":8762},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else if IPv6 address prefixes are reported:","paragraph_zero_based":8763},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>include these iPv6-Prefix in iab-IPv6-PrefixReport, and for each IP address prefix included;","paragraph_zero_based":8764},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if this IPv6 address prefix is used for F1-C traffic:","paragraph_zero_based":8765},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>include this prefix in f1-C-Traffic-IP-Address.","paragraph_zero_based":8766},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if this IPv6 address prefix is used for F1-U traffic:","paragraph_zero_based":8767},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>include this prefix in f1-U-Traffic-IP-Address.","paragraph_zero_based":8768},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if this IPv6 address prefix is used for non-F1 traffic:","paragraph_zero_based":8769},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>include this prefix in non-f1-Traffic-IP-Address.","paragraph_zero_based":8770},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if this IPv6 address prefix is used for all traffic:","paragraph_zero_based":8771},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>include this prefix in all-Traffic-IAB-IP-Address.","paragraph_zero_based":8772},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the IAB-MT is in (NG)EN-DC, or","paragraph_zero_based":8773},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the IAB-MT is in NR-DC and the IAB Other Information procedure is towards the IAB-donor-CU in the SN:","paragraph_zero_based":8774},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if SRB3 is configured:","paragraph_zero_based":8775},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>submit the IABOtherInformation message via SRB3 to lower layers for transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":8776},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the IAB-MT is in (NG)EN-DC:","paragraph_zero_based":8777},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>submit the IABOtherInformation message via the E-UTRA MCG embedded in E-UTRA RRC message ULInformationTransferMRDC as specified in TS 36.331 [10];","paragraph_zero_based":8778},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":8779},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>submit the IABOtherInformation message via the NR MCG embedded in NR RRC message ULInformationTransferMRDC as specified in clause 5.7.2a.3;","paragraph_zero_based":8780},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":8781},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>submit the IABOtherInformation message to lower layers for transmission.","paragraph_zero_based":8782},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.7.13RLM/BFD relaxation","paragraph_zero_based":8783}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["f0fbb67be3dfdf5cbf8b597fd6079aa4892a5bc18aca8c496f682a5c3d76050e","1a1835dc0dbbac9c4b0d6ae16e2f69222d5c606363e00df04e71b8ea9d4b3c56","ae264612047fa7f73ab0cb1f4d82649ede3866a55d4e7285f8a549b3b92cc73d","d7b843e1bd9ae767781f5c015f4461b521a634282bf66272818835696821c778","fea4d166d2459b22eaa32852ee4826e1ad8f2266653675465645dd8a777bb6b6","846f154e985e8d60551b5fbdbdf02cb3ba41f35c6e50f2472719cccf8c28f873","9d601f9dd2a250527fba764dc10769fbf1181345daaee0283f87ba93e08c0a57","d618732c7dfe31d02544835de753fcf2b3893643da63bc69838e266ccd122ed5","b0cf86ccb2c5572826bd4efc23aadaf88f155751c28989151bbf2ee200785f4c","91b14ae3b27bb911a9f661d9377ccb14068a6c38b9dd42f28026fdea07ff478d","a4041f1623674ae8ef8d8f8af36ef56ac0f243fe927cf8d0d0ca4c6022aa0929","3be48f55b9acf01cdfa3d5c8f1e9f03f1aab0108eea08b577f66bae07c036cc3","ca69d2d94ac7bb367a0df5c940442723c3b4dd13f97d15d48091d36f375acd1c","74d3d1d1a780bbbe44830d6719641372ceda4aa7d777cd253e4968f01e06eae6","f3275aced7d43321216298fe036ff999fa1465de3692b1c08b787e6675aa4afc","d3d0307de965e80179c9c1aeef826caef0563758602e8f9cdf0e8ee3738cbf7f","5a5de1cb8d9c192e732266d195b68a7d7a72527c2255023cb59478055c1b4bba","7550f7b94c6fe1036ae54b2ba058cf76ab55308ebdfd5f00a4042ad7e8742aaf","dc766312bcb0d2b9da827bd6734f2dd477d73203064f37460c415ee7a183d865","472392f60023d0e1b6e5c3bc0f60b131c75c7a5a6c8a8092bf645b688c158a69","3564c6c79f1d4f15e7ab8a36f61bca82fdc92b0ee47c6dca7f9dab6742148126","ce23b223b1154bfe0f049114c679dfc7f734d094b911c1a9fa5bd2f95835e8db","a59596bc85c24773de93f8bfff2d976d97237ff161cebf1694ef7a9a5fe7a4a9","33b14c0f9333ae254ce10d889fb1b0bfdcd54f5d0496f5797c8499829a2c612c"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[8760,8783],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p8760"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In case both low mobility criterion and good serving cell criterion are configured for RLM/BFD relaxation, the UE is allowed to perform RLM and/or BFD relaxation according to requirements specified in TS 38.133 [14] when both relaxed measurement criterion for low mobility and relaxed measurement criterion for good serving cell quality are met.","paragraph_zero_based":8784},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In case only the good serving cell quality criterion is configured for RLM/BFD relaxation, the UE is allowed to perform RLM and/or BFD relaxation according to requirements specified in TS 38.133 [14] when the relaxed measurement criterion for good serving cell quality is met.","paragraph_zero_based":8785},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.7.13.1Relaxed measurement criterion for low mobility","paragraph_zero_based":8786},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The relaxed measurement criterion for UE with low mobility in RRC_CONNECTED is fulfilled when:","paragraph_zero_based":8787},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-(SS-RSRPRef – SS-RSRP) < SSearchDeltaP-Connected,","paragraph_zero_based":8788},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Where:","paragraph_zero_based":8789},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SS-RSRP = current L3 RSRP measurement of the SpCell based on SSB (dB).","paragraph_zero_based":8790},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SS-RSRPRef = reference L3 RSRP measurement of the SpCell based on SSB (dB), set as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":8791},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-After receiving low mobility criterion configuration, or","paragraph_zero_based":8792},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-After MAC of the CG successfully completes a Random Access procedure after applying a reconfigurationWithSync in spCellConfig of the CG while low mobility criterion is configured, or","paragraph_zero_based":8793},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If (SS-RSRP - SS-RSRPRef) > 0, or","paragraph_zero_based":8794},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the relaxed measurement criterion has not been met for TSearchDeltaP-Connected:","paragraph_zero_based":8795},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The UE shall set the value of SS-RSRPRef to the current SS-RSRP value of the SpCell.","paragraph_zero_based":8796},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.7.13.2Relaxed measurement criterion for good serving cell quality","paragraph_zero_based":8797},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The relaxed measurement criterion of good serving cell quality for RLM is fulfilled when the downlink radio link quality on the configured RLM-RS resource is evaluated to be better than the threshold Qin+XdB, wherein","paragraph_zero_based":8798},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Qin is specified in clause 8.1 of TS 38.133 [14].","paragraph_zero_based":8799},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-X is the parameter offset in goodServingCellEvaluationRLM for the evaluated serving cell.","paragraph_zero_based":8800},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The relaxed measurement criterion of good serving cell quality for BFD is fulfilled when the downlink radio link quality on the configured BFD-RS resource is evaluated to be better than the threshold Qin+XdB, wherein","paragraph_zero_based":8801},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Q in is specified in clause 8.1 of TS 38.133 [14].","paragraph_zero_based":8802},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-X is the parameter offset in goodServingCellEvaluationBFD for the evaluated serving cell.","paragraph_zero_based":8803},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.7.14UE Positioning Assistance Information","paragraph_zero_based":8804},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.7.14.1General","paragraph_zero_based":8805},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":8806},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.7.14.1-1: UE Positioning Assistance Information procedure","paragraph_zero_based":8807}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["4956629faa097a8de77d789b17d3c92c816ef7fbafaf51012cd1fc2c8efd4d40","7b8b3542e2ccd670b280eadb6ff99ac0e76a5538805972aedff8a1d26b5c0178","19932e712adbed5d5d6f550bd5b1774440b307ddf82bd6fe1d83a2e1eb7c95a7","9d405adaa1dbe5eb87038fc0dc71c8f3a2d65e7a3eadedb35302c13e569ff34e","9c398fcadf72cc2cbf28f283bf1f60e992cf3a3591cb5590ad28bd74a2a3566f","9c29409ce5c9f11c4250612c7235ee4c7ebd7e24eca0728f221a7ed231108584","cdf93915615636247fc2baf9776ff782d45fb0a849baa00fbbb9a9dec773f262","eee36a60e7e1ced67b892e457088b53ee6b94342a5bde053ff1bb61b418710df","fd9577739558d06316d33b797a3de51f6dc5520581c0f3e50508a3711dcac37b","5329df0b3369a2d272b1c1e36c1abb8704968e3222158fc934d215e691f51548","f112feb1499f599ee49e572aa9f978eb2e697e94be07bf6b88cb45b725c435e0","fdb0209eb3ad708464bd656bd1defd67823383e69da5f1ebc6902b8a28a91f8a","bba8a449b9259afccfb6a07f87bb5129d973a542413ba3b9f4186c236ec17cba","803ff5437b0e523455d4ada3aa48e66c0d9a5c7a445c86c8dcab1c65a726fd24","dc0df42056f4b8204438edbd435c52dd6d0bbb2bddd682dce2e2a445238594fc","41ec71f7ab5098c1bdeaec4628ab4f399ab1fa1ddbc4a12fb64623029eadebdb","129195f8a252dd21285edf370fdf68dd189a78fae7a0f38f9df6f58668512d52","c0ddd536502566da5e614603f1f132856f3e41ded8e2d7d567dc1705961e6971","79633d4ef3307c5db6afeb1fc5b4681038de0c0cd9b979c964f91ea8dfcae438","ad18acaf4290621dbcc9ee9158983071b1793bdee4560d55865a8daaa57589e0","0fc3282cc46dba86024a1dcdc6c9183c51a9d01e56d117ea920650c23b1695a3","2d51359444deadeef621ef05dcf65f08592d45aa804d49da2d5b38093852e3c2","9320796b7b5697d8b45526ebb88455cad388596b8f0c2734f12c6200bc73dd1c","1dc51a420f2fa7c97d88a3b20f12fd9f73a961c76d5327861e6941b5d72ad338"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[8784,8807],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p8784"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE Positioning Assistance Information procedure is used by UE to report the UE Positioning Assistance Information. The UE reports the association between SRS resources for positioning and the UE Tx TEG ID as defined in TS 38.305 [73].","paragraph_zero_based":8808},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.7.14.2Initiation","paragraph_zero_based":8809},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of providing the association between SRS resource for positioning and UE Tx TEG ID in RRC_CONNECTED may initiate the procedure upon being configured to provide this association information.","paragraph_zero_based":8810},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon initiation of the procedure, the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":8811},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>initiate transmission of the UEPositioningAssistanceInfo message in accordance with 5.7.14.3 to provide the association.","paragraph_zero_based":8812},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.7.14.3Actions related to transmission of UEPositioningAssistanceInfo message","paragraph_zero_based":8813},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall set the contents of the UEPositioningAssistanceInfo message as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":8814},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if ue-TxTEG-RequestUL-TDOA-Config in RRCReconfiguration message is configured with periodicReporting:","paragraph_zero_based":8815},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for all the association changes store ue-TxTEG-Association corresponding to each ue-TxTEG-ID with nr-TimeStamp;","paragraph_zero_based":8816},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>include the results in ue-TxTEG-AssociationList in the UEPositioningAssistanceInfo message on expiry of each configured period;","paragraph_zero_based":8817},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>optionally include one ue-TxTEG-TimingErrorMarginValue for each UEPositioningAssistanceInfo message;","paragraph_zero_based":8818},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else if ue-TxTEG-RequestUL-TDOA-Config in RRCReconfiguration message is configured with oneShot:","paragraph_zero_based":8819},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>identify the ue-TxTEG-Association corresponding to each ue-TxTEG-ID with nr-TimeStamp;","paragraph_zero_based":8820},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>include the results in ue-TxTEG-AssociationList in the UEPositioningAssistanceInfo message only one time;","paragraph_zero_based":8821},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>optionally include one ue-TxTEG-TimingErrorMarginValue for each UEPositioningAssistanceInfo message.","paragraph_zero_based":8822},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall submit the UEPositioningAssistanceInfo message to lower layers for transmission.","paragraph_zero_based":8823},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.7.15Void","paragraph_zero_based":8824},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.7.16Application layer measurement reporting","paragraph_zero_based":8825},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.7.16.1General","paragraph_zero_based":8826},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":8827},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.7.16.1-1: Application layer measurement reporting","paragraph_zero_based":8828},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The purpose of this procedure is to send application layer measurement reports to the network.","paragraph_zero_based":8829},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.7.16.2Initiation","paragraph_zero_based":8830},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of application layer measurement reporting in RRC_CONNECTED may initiate the procedure when configured with application layer measurement and reporting, i.e. when at least one measConfigAppLayer and SRB4 and/or SRB5 have been configured by the network.","paragraph_zero_based":8831}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["00c530a8ca11ebb29beeb3f5aacd04f7def349855a2d86978e4a81bc87f6a146","2c64e5653c184624c248f7850a0aec3cb38b8c115f2694a639241e927a285919","59684971ad2d62d656dd1993888f48732950a4377a33b5248af112c076423568","5162034d5a3be8fb66f5c35375473611d177e8ec54231219e65e99d99cf319ff","18cab17bfc11b5b3223b5ffddf8f7b1d161d43322b50ec73ced477ae07a256f1","289e3b7b16e51d47ae275904bbd5b77c11a4c050b286b4ca157ae3616c7d9b08","af5c8093025922fd3eb427ab6fe2bfb443cc0cb91027c95c23fd7c6efd16e498","b0f1a6a1402abc64c517ec5f5adf95c4eae07f0f4b4c30fe6336350e54193b1a","455d459e9cdf852bff65276c0ffcc494ed6bcdb63ea853df3db394f0e958225d","475a012fbdc7241e987dc3cdb6c4883e5965717a6ccb8c7df20a404797081712","2fb38787a0f53b3e56d744f9b04c7682f35356c3004633290776088dfab57533","77f64d93bf319310011519ce0286b7ae5033ad961566a07d37d2bb40df922732","984034042232f6bd74bc70d62ebbfca6a37ab22d142a462541ca72da349e0987","9ea25e802f9fc718407cb5c53f36453ffe89ae6a99ee69b35da574d882827a25","10f06f2cbce5f2b265798f45b201c4b3e3e8a69caa581e7af01332cf87619cfa","9bbe7a24515a8a6338d45a3fd414115eca0a7a916da5950a4ab067b34593af25","8d28565ca2dbff8cbd0956ccaa8296737dadb63cf312de0b222160b79b365fd5","0ea13db6b6765a2fd55477a9ed75820e522f5e86a482a9afe96037ef8f709eec","c4aa134c066f08929580c848618fe0b293ddcb2e1dd97e1befd02a1e6b5f2c79","051bd6a686633b367535ccf4798301e598e6571a2119efa038bd90e40d45735a","afd00d8b853ab50e60c5e3b662d6fdc94318408e7cdc5fcc2cf3f32da11f4de7","f38c4f6c1d64800d93601c52416877fbea22bac71640f02ba13abc47ff3bbf6f","8638a2289b2b4c0096abc05559f5dc2e780054d6b8aa969c1a2d8475d92e79b3","4db6aa4d25c043f40188c3248b2464c022c1048692429c610a0fa022589a3ea5"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[8808,8831],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p8808"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon initiating the procedure, the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":8832},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each stored application layer measurement configuration with appLayerIdleInactiveConfig configured and for which appLayerIdleInactiveConfig has not been transmitted since the UE received the RRCSetup message:","paragraph_zero_based":8833},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set the parameters in appLayerIdleInactiveConfig in the MeasurementReportAppLayer message to the values stored in the UE variable VarAppLayerIdleConfig;","paragraph_zero_based":8834},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the transmissionOfSessionStartStop is set to true:","paragraph_zero_based":8835},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if a session start or stop indication has been received from upper layers:","paragraph_zero_based":8836},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set the appLayerSessionStatus in the MeasurementReportAppLayer message to the value of the latest received session start or stop indication;","paragraph_zero_based":8837},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else:","paragraph_zero_based":8838},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set the appLayerSessionStatus in the MeasurementReportAppLayer message to stop;","paragraph_zero_based":8839},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each measConfigAppLayerId with an application layer measurement report container which has not been transmitted since the UE received the RRCSetup message:","paragraph_zero_based":8840},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set the measConfigAppLayerId in a MeasReportAppLayer in the MeasurementReportAppLayer message(s) to the value of the measConfigAppLayerId received together with the application layer measurement report container;","paragraph_zero_based":8841},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for each application measurement report container stored for that measConfigAppLayerId:","paragraph_zero_based":8842},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the measReportAppLayerContainerList in the MeasurementReportAppLayer message(s) to the stored value of the application layer measurement report container;","paragraph_zero_based":8843},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 0:If the application layer measurement configurations and reports exceed the size of an RRC message, the UE includes the appLayerIdleInactiveConfig and corresponding appLayerSessionStatus in the first MeasurementReportAppLayer message when the UE enters RRC_CONNECTED, and transmits application layer measurement report containers in subsequent MeasurementReportAppLayer messages.","paragraph_zero_based":8844},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each measConfigAppLayerId received from upper layers:","paragraph_zero_based":8845},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE AS has received application layer measurement report container from upper layers which has not been transmitted; and","paragraph_zero_based":8846},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the application layer measurement reporting has not been suspended for the measConfigAppLayerId associated with the application layer measurement report container according to clause 5.3.5.13d:","paragraph_zero_based":8847},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the measReportAppLayerContainer in the MeasurementReportAppLayer message to the received value in the application layer measurement report container;","paragraph_zero_based":8848},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set the measConfigAppLayerId in the MeasurementReportAppLayer message to the value of the measConfigAppLayerId received together with application layer measurement report information;","paragraph_zero_based":8849},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if session start or stop information has been received from upper layers for the measConfigAppLayerId:","paragraph_zero_based":8850},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the appLayerSessionStatus in the MeasurementReportAppLayer message to the latest received value of session start or stop information;","paragraph_zero_based":8851},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if a RAN visible application layer measurement report has been received from upper layers:","paragraph_zero_based":8852},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>for each appLayerBufferLevel value in the received RAN visible application layer measurement report:","paragraph_zero_based":8853},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set the appLayerBufferLevel values in the appLayerBufferLevelList in the MeasurementReportAppLayer message to the buffer level values received from the upper layer in the order with the first appLayerBufferLevel value set to the newest received buffer level value, the second appLayerBufferLevel value set to the second newest received buffer level value, and so on until all the buffer level values received from the upper layer have been assigned or the maximum number of values have been set according to appLayerBufferLevel, if configured;","paragraph_zero_based":8854},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the playoutDelayForMediaStartup in the MeasurementReportAppLayer message to the received value of playout delay for media startup in the RAN visible application layer measurement report, if any;","paragraph_zero_based":8855}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["95ba6875d9bd59979d63210709e6e9ce178a4027d68548ec8ee00506dae0cd63","c88dcdd9561d6b63c8d8259a75b371c2b8c2dfb4b7bee6127c0a58892e440cf1","3e59ed4741d13914fea183482dfe45bc8329a26c0a30ae790895cd5b5e8bce93","2dbc7dbef6db261608f6657ff9d42cb91dc66bca3c5082cd5e426e417d41e1a2","806c8f7c9471326dc8b11f1ae9cca9a51a79d8039e039b4ea548c2902f4296bf","4aa0a0680dc6e3769b517ff077817d6f2422c026fbfe5728400bb3e874756e39","4932282e356704f95e328a5a1e92174989e3d1ecdbb0376287f85b0651a9e292","de0957ae980246feec022b8ed03abd8ad484106cca3c5a0c11baf6af32e55bb8","5bf3dc6cea3dd3fd70f219d34ca1cb3009aba2391a09a1e5e32c608bd9c174e8","9327eb7ae44bc550d4785c2ff3517b5903db8f576d8fbc04a8b36a0a6126edaa","be32701863726ca159e266e1de183c53c70e977b94c68ed52c0c49b757380ee4","988b328b53fa2b4cdc7494ab1e9a4eea4c6f2e085d44331f2e027c7b550f11d0","79378cfe11552a235e022202e7e52f65c3b10de96d5e94121251fda35fad6740","4f4298a78f654f3d4ee20aa4c634760dbadfd645c91393d0b6509d14a06f9f25","7c9225093ff817aab492bc2d43dd2aa660189bbd4fd82439c9449843359ddc84","5334f43695d9e96c56601d04e29bfb2f95541bc1eac23576bcce72c06c55cb43","f52d283e89ce8ea86e6dceff93368b85cadacc61b1799b73c703a0db51bdb1e5","3c5b810c6fc9ce53d53739a347e1c83158c72ade85ac2eb52cf653b9ad6f5cf1","8b297a9d7a3ec0c90d56cbbcc41164d7046a14b7fc1645a3f9f2f760243f8080","f2df59b49ab3bac9efb5e479818dfd2545bcd1244081bcc27403f2e54a2f6ebc","df76b0ac007a91b334b7987637dcb239c3c069a788f6a4f6688af729cf5ca0cd","7339e3c55cfd92ccf05215cf1ecc956337a00f7e1e28fd825ee83c0d23b8e06e","378aae613de7dffb5624834ed5e4ac5595f3321f92b0506eefb764bbf73bd7f7","b5e8c23cc57638afafd2bc9d310e9fbdcd074680668e48d316ed1174936636e3"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[8832,8855],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p8832"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>for each PDU session ID value indicated in the received RAN visible application layer measurement report, if any:","paragraph_zero_based":8856},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set the PDU-SessionID in the pdu-SessionIdList in the MeasurementReportAppLayer message to the indicated PDU session ID value;","paragraph_zero_based":8857},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>for each QoS Flow ID value indicated in the received RAN visible application layer measurement report associated with the PDU Session ID, if any:","paragraph_zero_based":8858},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set the QFI associated with the PDU session ID to the indicated QoS Flow ID value.","paragraph_zero_based":8859},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if reportingSRB and ran-VisibleReportingSRB indicates different SRBs for the measConfigAppLayerId:","paragraph_zero_based":8860},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>include measReportAppLayerContainer and appLayerSessionStatus in a separate MeasurementReportAppLayer message than ran-VisibleMeasurements;","paragraph_zero_based":8861},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each encoded MeasurementReportAppLayer message generated above which contains either only encapsulated application layer measurement reports or both encapsulated application layer measurement reports and RAN visible application layer measurement reports:","paragraph_zero_based":8862},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if reportingSRB is not configured for the measConfigAppLayerId:","paragraph_zero_based":8863},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the encoded RRC message is larger than the maximum supported size of one PDCP SDU specified in TS 38.323 [5]:","paragraph_zero_based":8864},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the RRC message segmentation is enabled based on the field rrc-SegAllowed received in appLayerMeasConfig:","paragraph_zero_based":8865},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>initiate the UL message segment transfer procedure as specified in clause 5.7.7 for transmission via SRB4;","paragraph_zero_based":8866},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>else:","paragraph_zero_based":8867},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>discard the RRC message;","paragraph_zero_based":8868},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else:","paragraph_zero_based":8869},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>submit the MeasurementReportAppLayer message to lower layers for transmission via SRB4.","paragraph_zero_based":8870},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if reportingSRB is configured for the measConfigAppLayerId:","paragraph_zero_based":8871},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the encoded RRC message is larger than the maximum supported size of one PDCP SDU specified in TS 38.323 [5]:","paragraph_zero_based":8872},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the RRC message segmentation is enabled based on the field rrc-SegAllowedSRB4 received in appLayerMeasConfig and the reportingSRB is SRB4, or","paragraph_zero_based":8873},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if RRC message segmentation is enabled based on the field rrc-SegAllowedSRB5 received in appLayerMeasConfig and the reportingSRB is SRB5:","paragraph_zero_based":8874},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>initiate the UL message segment transfer procedure as specified in clause 5.7.7 for transmission via the SRB indicated in the field reportingSRB in MeasConfigAppLayer;","paragraph_zero_based":8875},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>else:","paragraph_zero_based":8876},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>discard the RRC message;","paragraph_zero_based":8877},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else:","paragraph_zero_based":8878},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>submit the MeasurementReportAppLayer message to lower layers for transmission via the SRB indicated in the field reportingSRB in MeasConfigAppLayer.","paragraph_zero_based":8879}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["054689096d1e6532e159f687852375499b5d27b2aaf35d2ecd36543c5f037299","353be674be684f7a4b4b26a616f7ac8374c1e949865c41990adcd63c2d329e82","3d0a72e3dbfde1880bfa0da0a325f96218bff84b9fcc75ef63f54ee0860e505c","5f63ce43f0b2a3bc19c29b6697815e0bcd29e03163a7caa1e5db575f0e851e39","7c0fe0b7fedd52c2cd16520ca6df9beeeb867011a194e788d958726e80c8dd22","e232ffe33b7fc8b40e340e88a5c8ef1b2a33d009acf6612b30f6de0dcb5f65d3","6a1038f44eeb5b418be202e2be2b118f58967677a984204684650e3f6a712489","02127c24f725b5947d3c9de072461451a2fa1fb42ff8a9d1da8035b1da402b98","bb29b3d7758691b66d636ee208420a402dc1623149395721f67b81cbb4a8c2b7","0b8cc2b4ab0e8f9a9890a32d925d812f7a59396163e93d50d1e376850636599c","00bace10e3e0a2a9464812f26c8d642b4c5f7857e8764c85f6609062a7406611","e686f3e90fda03b5bb23ac90f7f85036107feb081f5c318e97b09fd93df66316","f2ecf7fb21a6179f5ad818676853be7cdd5efc7ce6050c1c5f53aa3f58ce647f","c07722396765cba51bcc2a2fd4098e3452cbdc09f96bf06cff4b0e32f5abcb5f","ae86abc380aad7694184e6166f179579ad289e91c5bebf88d9c24ea1849d2c46","0a214bb2235768a4a6f08756f45be1e62e1afb47f04fe704a00d85c5b46f41a6","d4337d4dd15a72d0b84ea55f6bc2f07061bb97cb016e58cf0872a5041be2a8cf","136df8fe6da7b78f3ff81efa5e3c5878908e8a4bbf5e9e945310869ba6148837","49d977211d23c5841f26107f0ef81fb2b64194fd27e8c7850531564d8853aeca","3324cf0c17852916b2622238bb099f61565a8e4663d3ffa9c5e169bb53af5d68","b42f57e3a6023d25b60b34f6cb187d0417bcc206ec444ee165a5f4b11bdc5982","4c324bfb0c3b27a90684519cea80246b2fb40b56d373f42f6db79b67a804d298","cdbdab6321cefe6067808aaac4d5901d41075e64903cb9c670fddfa2694a8e36","83a574887a98ab8b001cac146229528309222c6721624fb1cb8f534325f00ec6"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[8856,8879],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p8856"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each encoded MeasurementReportAppLayer message generated above which contains only RAN visible application layer measurement reports:","paragraph_zero_based":8880},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if ran-VisibleReportingSRB is not configured for the measConfigAppLayerId:","paragraph_zero_based":8881},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>submit the MeasurementReportAppLayer message to lower layers for transmission via SRB4;","paragraph_zero_based":8882},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if ran-VisibleReportingSRB is configured for the measConfigAppLayerId:","paragraph_zero_based":8883},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>submit the MeasurementReportAppLayer message to lower layers for transmission via the SRB indicated in the field ran-VisibleReportingSRB in MeasConfigAppLayer.","paragraph_zero_based":8884},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:If the SRB indicated by reportingSRB is not available or if reportingSRB is absent and SRB4 is not available, the UE may store application layer measurement report containers until the SRB is available. The UE may discard reports when the memory reserved for storing application layer measurement report containers becomes full. Reports with lower appLayerMeasPriority are discarded first. If equal or no appLayerMeasPriority is configured, older reports are discarded first.","paragraph_zero_based":8885},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:If the SRB indicated by ran-VisibleReportingSRB is not available, the UE discards RAN visible application layer measurement reports.","paragraph_zero_based":8886},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.7.17Derivation of pathloss reference for TA validation of SRS for Positioning transmission and CG-SDT in RRC_INACTIVE","paragraph_zero_based":8887},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon request from lower layer for pathloss reference derivation for TA validation for SRS for Positioning transmission or CG-SDT in RRC_INACTIVE, the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":8888},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>acquire SIB2, if stored version is invalid;","paragraph_zero_based":8889},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if nrofSS-BlocksToAverage or absThreshSS-BlocksConsolidation is not present or if absThreshSS-BlocksConsolidation is present and the highest beam measurement quantity value is below or equal to absThreshSS-BlocksConsolidation:","paragraph_zero_based":8890},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>derive the downlink pathloss reference RSRP for TA validation as the highest beam measurement quantity value, where each beam measurement quantity is described in TS 38.215 [24];","paragraph_zero_based":8891},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":8892},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>derive the downlink pathloss reference RSRP for TA validation as the linear average of the power values of up to nrofSS-BlocksToAverage of the highest beam measurement quantity values above absThreshSS-BlocksConsolidation, where each beam measurement quantity is described in TS 38.215 [24].","paragraph_zero_based":8893},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.7.18Void","paragraph_zero_based":8894},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.7.19Satellite switch with resynchronization in RRC_CONNECTED","paragraph_zero_based":8895},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":8896},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>stop timer T430 if running;","paragraph_zero_based":8897},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>inform lower layers that UL synchronisation is lost due to satellite switch with resynchronization;","paragraph_zero_based":8898},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>start synchronising to the DL of the SpCell served by the satellite indicated by ntn-Config in SatSwitchWithReSync, if the UE has not acquired DL synchronization;","paragraph_zero_based":8899},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>start timer T430 with the timer value set to ntn-UlSyncValidityDuration from the subframe indicated by epochTime in ntn-Config in SatSwitchWithReSync;","paragraph_zero_based":8900},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>inform lower layers when UL synchronisation is obtained.","paragraph_zero_based":8901},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8Sidelink","paragraph_zero_based":8902},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.1General","paragraph_zero_based":8903}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e15ab6e7e616f5b00a6b477c4eed745ef48bd93f6df708d0d75276cd6d770c7c","98b93a866f27168abd694aebb9b49a8fe7184915e3f93fce469a9a651eda4d2f","279c7cd2e50ca7bb2724b17bb42a31fd729669c2ddde931b426112afcc9cde0d","ea2b24ecd6b4924df8138387c395186d7d66229557abd13a9263cad4cdedf825","1050d247702fc93d594e0f1e884753002862ac632009d992b82f37fd312a038b","1dd5b0e352e6e72720ed571fc12a01b6a1c128be5bfa5a6ad064a3497e44373f","6739224cc908d3632c2cda783c803a49e88c46e286aa72d6a833c35dfd4d0301","00f9bbcadb2b987dbc9c9295fa2b3fe85322dc6a775d07ddf0016de9b8a78dc6","2ba1d7e4cf26e112a960d8c5462406c518e7143beca182c3bda9ece8a3b66217","6084c2100c2dfb3c9430b76b71a963304e4f2cc4baac52d2d12520d4f51699a4","df7981ff02d834022426fdafdea45b680d02cdc850e6a882a7da142c20d8130b","ababed4349561a95551cf2c68bb0ceffdfb8e6ef83401c17778c456c784ae926","5de5ebf28fdae333a4e0c917a738768720838062f0744edcdec508d62668456d","7d2f3d4c42faa7598f5a860c7f6462075ecaf0aabe5c70c17827c85e89556f6e","39dd7701d762c2768e5c42cd4af0529c863321ad4aca9acd4a8b2e306e8965eb","fe1e8b148808c047e5f52048d5d220f1b23beebcacb259a65b0dbee08fc5d735","cade262ce3f0eab2b494719a4fdc5a9fec65b14bf3289207b70dfaeebb1e1cc7","c2541a0309179c4a9ea0fd619bdcfb34c4b48325597e6236af388dc414d0df7c","754a9dab79e720119321cdebe22ceb30964224534ae79879947138aa92a6fb86","113b12c0086b0626a208f85c4272dff81538de907a3a35c0d6c6767bb5f48ed7","f05bd562dc7658d635e78eef83c36a2e97fe41806a050e9007f92595044868c5","b8dda304787d569e2d075eb06bd772ee97ad040006045ca58f32b216d1b250e8","1f8ae2adff24e8e2fd9302e4a398743bf7f798415dc5dfc05f627d0a9f7108e5","e3d5b15a6f947a163d2867ee19195894e8308784f75d16dfdf1db4c7d763583d"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[8880,8903],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p8880"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR sidelink communication consists of unicast, groupcast and broadcast. For unicast, the PC5-RRC connection is a logical connection between a pair of a Source Layer-2 ID and a Destination Layer-2 ID in the AS. The PC5-RRC signalling, as specified in clause 5.8.9, can be initiated after its corresponding PC5 unicast link establishment (TS 23.287 [55]). The PC5-RRC connection and the corresponding sidelink SRBs and sidelink DRB(s) are released when the PC5 unicast link is released as indicated by upper layers.","paragraph_zero_based":8904},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For each PC5-RRC connection of unicast, one sidelink SRB (i.e. SL-SRB0) is used to transmit the PC5-S message(s) before the PC5-S security has been established. One sidelink SRB (i.e. SL-SRB1) is used to transmit the PC5-S messages to establish the PC5-S security. One sidelink SRB (i.e. SL-SRB2) is used to transmit the PC5-S messages after the PC5-S security has been established, which is protected. One sidelink SRB (i.e. SL-SRB3) is used to transmit the PC5-RRC signalling, which is protected and only sent after the PC5-S security has been established. One sidelink SRB (i.e. SL-SRB4) is used to transmit/receive the NR sidelink discovery messages.","paragraph_zero_based":8905},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For unicast of NR sidelink communication, AS security comprises of integrity protection of PC5 signalling (SL-SRB1, SL-SRB2 and SL-SRB3) and user data (SL-DRBs), and it further comprises of ciphering of PC5 signaling (SL-SRB1 only for the Direct Link Security Mode Complete message as specified in TS 24.587 [57] for V2X service or TS 24.554 [72] for Proximity-services, SL-SRB2 and SL-SRB3) and user data (SL-DRBs). The ciphering and integrity protection algorithms and parameters for a PC5 unicast link are exchanged by PC5-S messages in the upper layers as specified in TS 33.536 [60], and applied to the corresponding PC5-RRC connection in the AS. Once AS security is activated for a PC5 unicast link in the upper layers as specified in TS 33.536 [60], all messages on SL-SRB2 and SL-SRB3 and/or user data on SL-DRBs of the corresponding PC5-RRC connection are integrity protected and/or ciphered by the PDCP.","paragraph_zero_based":8906},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For unicast of NR sidelink communication, if the change of the key is indicated by the upper layers as specified in TS 24.587 [57] or TS 24.554 [72], UE re-establishes the PDCP entity of the SL-SRB1, SL-SRB2, SL-SRB3 and SL-DRBs on the corresponding PC5-RRC connection.","paragraph_zero_based":8907},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:In case the configurations for NR sidelink communication are acquired via the E-UTRA, the configurations for NR sidelink communication in SIB12 and sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration used in clause 5.8 are provided by the configurations in SystemInformationBlockType28 and sl-ConfigDedicatedForNR within RRCConnectionReconfiguration as specified in TS 36.331 [10], respectively.","paragraph_zero_based":8908},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:In this release, there is one-to-one correspondence between the PC5-RRC connection and the PC5 unicast link as specified in TS 38.300[2].","paragraph_zero_based":8909},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 3:All SL-DRBs related to the same PC5-RRC connection have the same activation/deactivation setting for ciphering and the same activation/deactivation setting for integrity protection as specified in TS 33.536 [60].","paragraph_zero_based":8910},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 4:When integrity check failure concerning SL-SRB1 for a specific destination is detected, the UE sends an indication to the upper layers [57].","paragraph_zero_based":8911},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 5:The selection of NULL algorithms means that the PC5 messages are considered protected for the purposes of being allowed to be sent or received.","paragraph_zero_based":8912},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.2Conditions for NR sidelink communication/discovery/positioning operation","paragraph_zero_based":8913},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall perform NR sidelink communication/positioning operation only if the conditions defined in this clause are met:","paragraph_zero_based":8914},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE's serving cell is suitable (RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE or RRC_CONNECTED); and if either the selected cell on the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery/positioning operation belongs to the registered or equivalent PLMN as specified in TS 24.587 [57] or TS 24.554 [72] or the UE is out of coverage on the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery/positioning operation as defined in TS 38.304 [20] and TS 36.304 [27]; or","paragraph_zero_based":8915},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE's serving cell (RRC_IDLE or RRC_CONNECTED) fulfils the conditions to support NR sidelink communication/discovery/positioning in limited service state as specified in TS 23.287 [55]; and if either the serving cell is on the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery/positioning operation or the UE is out of coverage on the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery/positioning operation as defined in TS 38.304 [20] and TS 36.304 [27]; or","paragraph_zero_based":8916},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE has no serving cell (RRC_IDLE).","paragraph_zero_based":8917},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.3Sidelink UE information for NR sidelink communication/discovery/positioning","paragraph_zero_based":8918},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.3.1General","paragraph_zero_based":8919},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":8920},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.3.1-1: Sidelink UE information for NR sidelink communication/discovery","paragraph_zero_based":8921},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The purpose of this procedure is to inform the network that the UE:","paragraph_zero_based":8922},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is interested or no longer interested to receive or transmit NR sidelink communication/discovery/positioning,","paragraph_zero_based":8923},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is requesting assignment or release of transmission resource for NR sidelink communication/discovery/positioning,","paragraph_zero_based":8924},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting QoS parameters and QoS profile(s) related to NR sidelink communication,","paragraph_zero_based":8925},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting mapped frequency(ies) for each QoS flow related to NR sidelink communication,","paragraph_zero_based":8926},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting associated Tx Profile for each QoS flow related to NR sidelink groupcast and broadcast communication,","paragraph_zero_based":8927}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["8742b1ffeb92e432ed6c7e72ea33bc73c23f7d9b868330b5d1547ce1e623c5bf","bc347d51e38ee9b028a6b2df827adda9d8ca5a621e90906ee76055838077e80a","6d94d49167bc197a09e1c727c3292ba7a0a5492ca6b3c6971ebf71df2b9d4fb0","34df268c3a87a134b66f21ba201e7c653e717c0a8b1e772331776457b0737b47","3dd6e1c0988f2ccd52f26dbb83c966397c4c2e835f6847a8994b9b496031045f","cdf8983330712e2aff721cf912670fed45aa7a810a0ef7a806000e4a1b211501","50e83027240d3fac7ebc2037f462a3f81cb69f35fc7ba2f55764285d5fbadd70","82f1ae8b08afbc9fb5e615b60ad436cb000a7212a63f9e493ff807f307dafaac","f275c33e2f5e6b7149e0b355c1019e31d515a8504eb9f855859e09fa5a85ebf2","16df94c23e66eefba0e606c27f05a7d213b21231f746fe2d858cac48e52d90ca","984e698286cc58521fbd2de70b40a7970eff85c798ec0fa9224e64aaf6e5ca32","a10cbcb19353d6cda8a8cb27cacab951630bf5a5a11931b29ff3f1c7c6eb2211","52ffd0d8acbe26969daea7aa457ffb06086e02964fd4e6b9f129cbbb52e03ec2","cd5dc6d2de77750dd78bebb404f95e49fe9d089fe4e084ddd742d9006c1e5227","7c77a95b9fcdcf208de6248eb8b5b0b0b3d3887b323dd1b1334eb399d52486db","3bff5b2d47133565d90b4cfaccec280b4b04c7b42325445760181d238d026741","bf513b012230777849a8517bb9122d209505d6657eff5ff43d235048f4966c4c","4ecf08832a151317f3b761ac094ef208c6b33e9cafc9e0ac244935397984da84","b7ceef7c0dd0e2c9debf56340708107abf230ba44c8acaf2bdc6b6073454fb8b","db789eba6a32e77bbdf43a1e3dd25822ca0e8a989886d996dc5136cb1c6d21dd","6da9767b7976e91636291323f7a37b892e492a3d0df35671d34a359f78c69e47","06599e44dcd0f0229f9a6eb497e6c26cf5f923fe98d1d290d72205ecc6c20da6","40b95bbdc9552c1b802658d623bf211f746205f376555501724a6627dd69a3d6","fa41091542a09c6f095a956a690702d7d7c67925c19b28830510b2d0f5866384"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[8904,8927],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p8904"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting that a sidelink radio link failure, sidelink RRC reconfiguration failure or a sidelink carrier failure has been detected,","paragraph_zero_based":8928},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting the sidelink UE capability information of the associated peer UE for unicast communication,","paragraph_zero_based":8929},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting the RLC mode information of the sidelink data radio bearer(s) received from the associated peer UE for unicast communication,","paragraph_zero_based":8930},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting the accepted sidelink DRX configuration received from the associated peer UE for NR sidelink unicast reception,","paragraph_zero_based":8931},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting the sidelink DRX assistance information received from the associated peer UE for NR sidelink unicast transmission, when the UE is configured with sl-ScheduledConfig,","paragraph_zero_based":8932},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting, for NR sidelink groupcast transmission, the sidelink DRX on/off indication for the associated Destination Layer-2 ID, when the UE is configured with sl-ScheduledConfig,","paragraph_zero_based":8933},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting, for NR sidelink groupcast or broadcast reception, the Destination Layer-2 ID and QoS profile(s) associated with its interested services to which sidelink DRX is applied,","paragraph_zero_based":8934},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting DRX configuration reject information from its associated peer UE for NR sidelink unicast transmission, when the UE is configured with sl-ScheduledConfig,","paragraph_zero_based":8935},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting parameters related to U2N relay operation,","paragraph_zero_based":8936},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting parameters related to U2U relay operation.","paragraph_zero_based":8937},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.3.2Initiation","paragraph_zero_based":8938},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink communication or NR sidelink discovery or NR sidelink U2N relay operation or NR sidelink U2U relay operation or NR sidelink positioning that is in RRC_CONNECTED may initiate the procedure to indicate it is (interested in) receiving or transmitting NR sidelink communication or NR sidelink discovery or NR sidelink U2N relay operation or NR sidelink U2U relay operation or SL-PRS transmission/reception in several cases including upon successful connection establishment or resuming, upon change of interest, upon changing QoS profile(s), upon receiving UECapabilityInformationSidelink from the associated peer UE, upon RLC mode information updated from the associated peer UE or upon change to a PCell providing SIB12 including sl-ConfigCommonNR, or upon change to a PCell providing SIB23 including sl-PosConfigCommonNR. A UE capable of NR sidelink communication may initiate the procedure to request assignment of dedicated sidelink DRB configuration and transmission resources for NR sidelink communication transmission. A UE capable of NR sidelink communication may initiate the procedure to report to the network that a sidelink radio link failure, sidelink RRC reconfiguration failure or sidelink carrier failure has been declared. A UE capable of NR sidelink discovery may initiate the procedure to request assignment of dedicated resources for NR sidelink discovery transmission or NR sidelink discovery reception. A UE capable of U2N relay operation may initiate the procedure to report/update parameters for acting as U2N Relay UE or U2N Remote UE (including L2 Remote UE's source L2 ID). A UE capable of U2U relay operation may initiate the procedure to report/update parameters for acting as U2U Relay UE or U2U Remote UE. A UE capable of NR sidelink positioning may initiate the procedure to request it is interested or no longer interested in either transmitting SL-PRS or receiving SL-PRS.","paragraph_zero_based":8939},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink operation that is in RRC_CONNECTED may initiate the procedure to report the sidelink DRX configuration received from the associated peer UE for NR sidelink unicast reception, upon accepting the sidelink DRX configuration from the associated peer UE. A UE capable of NR sidelink communication that is configured with sl-ScheduledConfig and is performing sidelink unicast transmission may initiate the procedure to report the sidelink DRX assistance information or the sidelink DRX configuration reject information received from the associated peer UE, upon receiving either of them from the associated peer UE. A UE capable of NR sidelink communication that is configured with sl-ScheduledConfig and is performing sidelink groupcast transmission may initiate the procedure to report the sidelink DRX on/off indication for the associated Destination Layer-2 ID.","paragraph_zero_based":8940},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink operation that is in RRC_CONNECTED may initiate the procedure to report the Destination Layer-2 ID and QoS profile(s) associated with its interested service(s) that sidelink DRX is applied, and to report the frequency(ies) and Tx Profile associated with each QoS flow, for NR sidelink groupcast or broadcast reception.","paragraph_zero_based":8941},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon initiating this procedure, the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":8942},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if SIB12 including sl-ConfigCommonNR is provided by the PCell:","paragraph_zero_based":8943},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>ensure having a valid version of SIB12 for the PCell;","paragraph_zero_based":8944},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if configured by upper layers to receive NR sidelink communication on the frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList/sl-FreqInfoListSizeExt in SIB12 of the PCell:","paragraph_zero_based":8945},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE did not transmit a SidelinkUEInformationNR message since last entering RRC_CONNECTED state; or","paragraph_zero_based":8946},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if since the last time the UE transmitted a SidelinkUEInformationNR message the UE connected to a PCell not providing SIB12 including sl-ConfigCommonNR; or","paragraph_zero_based":8947},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message did not include sl-RxInterestedFreqList; or if the frequency configured by upper layers to receive NR sidelink communication on has changed since the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message:","paragraph_zero_based":8948},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate the NR sidelink communication reception frequency of interest in accordance with 5.8.3.3;","paragraph_zero_based":8949},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":8950},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message included sl-RxInterestedFreqList:","paragraph_zero_based":8951}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["9ae8cbb819513155c411b3989245dc3ea90e81b0894e556304eceba5d785ace8","6083a7662fab7ff52c1a89c65fe707f9a80a225dcbe1ac7b282e44355cae3122","59cfb0864bcd23c3f9437754152482f1596139cea511b569bbad81a07d3eaa01","c07cfd8863cb872a3af597459614502b2392cb80bcfbf54fe6a69d0efe425c3d","d7aa1af971d660d60e0a9a0f5c62db68a9acefa9f47ab7a92a982aa5c71c1340","4801229708bd4a1482cd2ac65dc5dce01314d98f024131bdfe0c459e31b917f1","8c5e9f2c909176c18cfb5f64ae8ce8c584f2c299ff4e0bf6f60bb100cf301f9d","b198f4931d44576780a14904ffe2917eb8d9bea1a71b5a078430111beab53a79","669e7162b037a874b17094487f38ee6afb282b43b0587fa6a3c3130bf52196e6","b5ba35625ed10b5ee1b85eefcb5341e656228176ffc8f84c7d5fbf6de395444e","e23f39a780c8ed0544bec6c2b01f6956f413156ed1134fd6f77b5eb917f8cdc0","58c214b5b2d5797da209c05e24ed58fa37f8ee07fbd3e8ee0544b4f79c463adc","20ab95dfb862c4126d2ab3c555a0635fbc344f95b9c4bca9eaf2b74933306aa3","46a9252a6474ec9c1c8d8c9e30a2b476996d09b9a92cebdbcd72a0f1c7a5896e","17207290703c1b6e51ed60364d2ca76461db7529479d41cd24d86e88382c96c7","d8dad92459eb845a2d9bb28e033dfbd613183b1d5a124c9ab9dab8d187e6ed99","ecc27ee0eadbe32731eb3ef802d62789724d0b3e2c32be54c4fca328495f49be","11d9f5b7ded3cba1dc6935a66e02b83967f1b5e1e4c0557b02d1a02fbf537bf9","438099fe900b27373288cb1707ba9582be6220cbd67a2148b5f0c6f6d439e73b","3b2b7ccfaafd2a65b7fd1766231b47dcd3f74098e0edd231faf51db9dd950f02","3fe2370f95b32b625e5d376d0c73d9f7bcecd4cfabcf2be0bed020104618f72b","8618897f1f5ac22d5ec54d300a03d9ceed527a31e8491b0a5b71a9cc968243c8","9049ee82e4d21f2d7de3d9ea9b667b78d216376b36e6273ea02c5a0bbd70288a","ab7e4463717d0a1d8eb4c344320311c40a0493f1e8d6b4d2fc6f86ec446bb161"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[8928,8951],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p8928"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate it is no longer interested in NR sidelink communication reception in accordance with 5.8.3.3;","paragraph_zero_based":8952},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if configured by upper layers to transmit non-relay NR sidelink communication on the frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList/sl-FreqInfoListSizeExt in SIB12 of the PCell; or","paragraph_zero_based":8953},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if configured by upper layer to transmit NR sidelink L3 U2U relay communication on the frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList in SIB12 of the PCell including sl-L3-U2U-RelayDiscovery:","paragraph_zero_based":8954},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE did not transmit a SidelinkUEInformationNR message since last entering RRC_CONNECTED state; or","paragraph_zero_based":8955},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if since the last time the UE transmitted a SidelinkUEInformationNR message the UE connected to a PCell not providing SIB12 including sl-ConfigCommonNR; or","paragraph_zero_based":8956},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message did not include sl-TxResourceReqList; or if the information carried by the sl-TxResourceReqList has changed since the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message:","paragraph_zero_based":8957},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate the NR sidelink communication transmission resources required by the UE in accordance with 5.8.3.3;","paragraph_zero_based":8958},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":8959},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message included sl-TxResourceReqList:","paragraph_zero_based":8960},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate it no longer requires NR sidelink communication transmission resources in accordance with 5.8.3.3;","paragraph_zero_based":8961},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if configured by upper layer to receive NR sidelink non-relay discovery messages on the frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList in SIB12 of the PCell including sl-NonRelayDiscovery:","paragraph_zero_based":8962},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE did not transmit a SidelinkUEInformationNR message since last entering RRC_CONNECTED state; or","paragraph_zero_based":8963},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if since the last time the UE transmitted a SidelinkUEInformationNR message the UE connected to a PCell not providing SIB12 including sl-ConfigCommonNR or connected to a PCell providing SIB12 but not including sl-NonRelayDiscovery; or","paragraph_zero_based":8964},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message did not include sl-RxInterestedFreqListDisc; or if the frequency configured by upper layers to receive NR sidelink non-relay discovery messages on has changed since the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message:","paragraph_zero_based":8965},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate the NR sidelink discovery reception frequency of interest in accordance with 5.8.3.3;","paragraph_zero_based":8966},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":8967},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message included sl-RxInterestedFreqListDisc:","paragraph_zero_based":8968},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate it is no longer interested in NR sidelink non-relay discovery messages reception in accordance with 5.8.3.3;","paragraph_zero_based":8969},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if configured by upper layer to receive NR sidelink L2 U2N relay discovery messages on the frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList in SIB12 of the PCell including sl-L2U2N-Relay; or if configured by upper layer to receive NR sidelink L3 U2N relay discovery messages on the frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList in SIB12 of the PCell including sl-L3U2N-RelayDiscovery; or","paragraph_zero_based":8970},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if configured by upper layer to receive NR sidelink L2 U2U relay discovery messages on the frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList in SIB12 of the PCell including sl-L2-U2U-Relay; or","paragraph_zero_based":8971},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if configured by upper layer to receive L3 NR sidelink U2U relay discovery messages on the frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList in SIB12 of the PCell including sl-L3-U2U-RelayDiscovery:","paragraph_zero_based":8972},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE did not transmit a SidelinkUEInformationNR message since last entering RRC_CONNECTED state; or","paragraph_zero_based":8973},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if since the last time the UE transmitted a SidelinkUEInformationNR message the UE connected to a PCell not providing SIB12 including sl-ConfigCommonNR; or connected to a PCell providing SIB12 but not including sl-L2U2N-Relay in case of L2 U2N relay operation; or connected to a PCell providing SIB12 but not including sl-L3U2N-RelayDiscovery in case of L3 U2N relay operation; or","paragraph_zero_based":8974},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if since the last time the UE transmitted a SidelinkUEInformationNR message the UE connected to a PCell providing SIB12 but not including sl-L2-U2U-Relay in case of L2 U2U relay operation; or","paragraph_zero_based":8975}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coor