{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>perform acquisition of the system information indicated in sl-RequestedSIB-List in accordance with 5.2.2;","paragraph_zero_based":10104},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform the Uu message transfer procedure in accordance with 5.8.9.9;","paragraph_zero_based":10105},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sl-RequestedSIB-List is set to release:","paragraph_zero_based":10106},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>release received SIB request in sl-RequestedSIB-List;","paragraph_zero_based":10107},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RemoteUEInformationSidelink includes the sl-RequestedPosSIB-List:","paragraph_zero_based":10108},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sl-RequestedPosSIB-List is set to setup:","paragraph_zero_based":10109},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3> if the L2 U2N Relay UE has not stored a valid version of posSIB(s) indicated in sl-RequestedPosSIB-List:","paragraph_zero_based":10110},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>perform acquisition of the positioning system information indicated in sl-RequestedPosSIB-List in accordance with 5.2.2;","paragraph_zero_based":10111},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform the Uu message transfer procedure in accordance with 5.8.9.9;","paragraph_zero_based":10112},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sl-RequestedPosSIB-List is set to release:","paragraph_zero_based":10113},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>release received posSIB request in sl-RequestedPosSIB-List.","paragraph_zero_based":10114},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RemoteUEInformationSidelink includes the connectionForMP:","paragraph_zero_based":10115},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the L2 U2N Relay UE is in RRC_IDLE:","paragraph_zero_based":10116},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>initiate an RRC connection establishment as specified in 5.3.3;","paragraph_zero_based":10117},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the L2 U2N Relay UE is in RRC_INACTIVE:","paragraph_zero_based":10118},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>initiate an RRC connection resume as specified in 5.3.13;","paragraph_zero_based":10119},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The L2 U2U Relay UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10120},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RemoteUEInformationSidelink includes the sl-DestinationIdentityRemoteUE:","paragraph_zero_based":10121},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>consider the end-to-end PC5 connection release for the end-to-end PC5 connection between the L2 U2U Remote UE and the peer L2 U2U Remote UE identified by sl-DestinationIdentityRemoteUE;","paragraph_zero_based":10122},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>initiate the end-to-end PC5 connection failure/release related actions as specified in 5.8.9.3b;","paragraph_zero_based":10123},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.9Uu message transfer in sidelink","paragraph_zero_based":10124},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.9.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10125},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":10126},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.9.9.1-1: Uu message transfer in sidelink","paragraph_zero_based":10127}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["61d09e487f3e97b816cdd075ef484b233a4349dd181652b782ffebfbdf323210","42590547954a6a360012aedc13a22fa9ddde5883b15ea028c6c4c11eeb030bf2","46bff7161e324c9d3a3e598bf8990d117a563ca2578360afef5e2ae149cfbd2a","b0327a89fc8f02146a42f3ad938ee646585f64ee1bc0d2f4a805dd188d7a948f","d1e62050dd0d13917e62844f18f838d4ea60e0607092414076c510c986469a82","2ccc0ab129acfaea5139bbcabe31a6ac5fd6d764b00f7e8a67172b03374cb533","17fe7362d0e0e1cea13dffbe8074d2724769024010b4bbcc589529a1c871aae6","84d25681c8b5502e2e69ee46eae89c5ee951f6492f6c3988a1d2a4816416378c","6092906c16e50824d4121b6bcdd7aa906d7b2821c3fd44e8f8ae6cdb5c779698","b4b22961cb56c6878acfb00184650245e4863819d3a020809384ee15852a2322","4fd0f77c22bba053780a58ba95eb1dcb8d8e686b7670e5c8e9fa4bbc40020f2c","f9e7b06541640ff6a0ee344e9a4bedd658ffa2002375fd1fd19ac95163b9fd5c","3831cc107019bffe83e64b29d5d9adeef4d20601acca8af62d8c8390347ae63d","be1818ef98906de47430a2cb0e19bba32bf5b5632398bf3d86d38300ae985483","bd7b456e0d65742a734ddd9fe168fd05456bec4b52c85eb433cb129f3657de3c","88904e1c5bb3263ef9961820f62f98f79dd3f60d4f33ad403698ff2796658c31","5020be8ab258b06a63d16fc61cfc52c0e245f49811bc08fb3aeab855ed805e4d","a56dd515502c75ec74a892fcf678b9d9b997dff5eddf89bda62352d269c21c60","fd7415d24b7941e424001cb4139d621c1cac044772a9827109782a5b0a3dbc74","774ae3a223b03b656eedd88a04d8838c4c82cc5ac646a89c2a054b2dc4c34986","f76ccbb8ecd894e13147eaccf594dce2765cff65892dfe5c6de2531f42a9f813","9f005e905905ce7d08e5b694103d6e0287f6f7bbefcfd822f62a79fb174f6845","1f66505536b00332d81494e2a5426595759821a19e09d2a159f008de2bb46a6d","bcc0f5f78b7a53f06094a7c031a0741d8087bac4644e191405f4cb0ab20928e5"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10104,10127],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10104"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The purpose of this procedure is to transfer Paging message and System Information from the L2 U2N Relay UE to the L2 U2N Remote UE in RRC_IDLE/RRC_INACTIVE.","paragraph_zero_based":10128},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.9.2Actions related to transmission of UuMessageTransferSidelink message","paragraph_zero_based":10129},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The L2 U2N Relay UE initiates the Uu message transfer procedure when at least one of the following conditions is met:","paragraph_zero_based":10130},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>upon receiving Paging message related to the connected L2 U2N Remote UE from network (including Paging message within RRCReconfiguration message);","paragraph_zero_based":10131},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>upon acquisition of the SIB(s) requested by the connected L2 U2N Remote UE (as indicated in sl-RequestedSIB-List in the RemoteUEInformationSidelink) or upon receiving the updated SIB(s) from network which has been requested by the connected L2 U2N Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":10132},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>upon acquisition of the posSIB(s) requested by the connected L2 U2N Remote UE (as indicated in sl-RequestedPosSIB-List in the RemoteUEInformationSidelink) or upon receiving the updated posSIB(s) from network which have been requested by the connected L2 U2N Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":10133},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>upon unsolicited SIB1 forwarding to the connected L2 U2N Remote UE or upon receiving the updated SIB1 from network;","paragraph_zero_based":10134},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For each associated L2 U2N Remote UE, the L2 U2N Relay UE shall set the contents of UuMessageTransferSidelink message as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":10135},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>include sl-PagingDelivery if the Paging message received from network containing the ue-Identity of the L2 U2N Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":10136},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>include sl-SIB1-Delivery if any of the conditions for initiating Uu message transfer procedure related to SIB1 are met;","paragraph_zero_based":10137},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>include sl-SystemInformationDelivery if any of the conditions for initiating Uu message transfer procedure related to System Information are met;","paragraph_zero_based":10138},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>submit the UuMessageTransferSidelink message to lower layers for transmission.","paragraph_zero_based":10139},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:The L2 U2N Relay UE may perform unsolicited forwarding of SIB1 to the L2 U2N Remote UE based on UE implementation. A L2 U2N Remote UE configured with MP does not apply the SIB1 received from the L2 U2N Relay UE on the indirect path, if any.","paragraph_zero_based":10140},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.9.3Reception of the UuMessageTransferSidelink","paragraph_zero_based":10141},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon receiving the UuMessageTransferSidelink message, the L2 U2N Remote UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10142},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if sl-PagingDelivery is included:","paragraph_zero_based":10143},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the paging reception procedure as specified in clause 5.3.2.3;","paragraph_zero_based":10144},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if sl-SystemInformationDelivery and/or sl-SIB1-Delivery is included:","paragraph_zero_based":10145},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the actions specified in clause 5.2.2.4.","paragraph_zero_based":10146},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.10Notification Message","paragraph_zero_based":10147},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.10.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10148},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":10149},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.9.8.1-1: Notification message in sidelink","paragraph_zero_based":10150},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This procedure is used by a U2N Relay UE to send notification to the connected U2N Remote UE, or used by a L2 U2U Relay UE to send notification to the L2 U2U Remote UE for an end-to-end PC5 connection when condition(s) as specified in 5.8.9.10.2 is met for the hop between the L2 U2U Relay UE and the peer L2 U2U Remote UE.","paragraph_zero_based":10151}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["2643e1a2663c7e6d74b107c863f0862bf43efb6473110f88042280fc9dc35b36","43b81431395da7bcb4f1d5f75943d92c8be69ee0446bea452fd1c1f62e6cfb6f","3988ba6b88683c165d777094731cdf09bc5f69545f8640876fcc29d72a71b4d5","5da75a101ad3c2c580719909c8f63deacc1db29faea108b1c77acda8261c3e97","747722b1f2ff88909223b0ceaf0ec95c4be1765c89f49112d77e6ec6aa073425","af8d70a3081e3bd5a4e03c939970764685a2f42833974718dde42c5bbb0050fc","381cb33f72003a8cd0061150e5200e941568674e2184cea1a05eb16094bd4a19","0e0835ba163f76c406ccac173f9185daaa4128566330f02ddcc6621b5d4963cb","960822fe7cee57eb93754858bea39613f7c86549069b8bcd9e87810d304503b0","b2013ccd5a0b390bda00526fb88af210136842393e7d944972b47d43f704b31b","3cb4ee836d4e3772d4da05544e991503edfcd190075aabb26a7a711bf1b95cc6","5aee7fc52e9c62b07be0ba48ab544cd39fad1c43def9168227f128acba52f131","25f17fb46c1ed7cd72ba6c7c94644ae93780d2c727e4db87a393555edfde675a","82276c4bc46f6e46a16c2a22e85e2ec1de9daaa6b0826f737885726eea9824fa","96407dc50d3a80ada71af7ac1448e966bb1c01e3075daf20ab027c7bf67d497a","e722547125cab0a04f5a3d2209a3c839b8c681546a64c039ccd37d69582f475f","94041d224e54ae23e5dab1e55ac5dda41203e43d949a1be9e9d9710e1921dd2f","3d466a86b274798b4c0d697f36a6b4fb09ff8e43d12e80d67de5d5267e784b84","17f0757fc12eff73157d25a2fe688744b201a5c23165e6dea537dfa2897d5423","718c73dd83bbc57eb9544c848bc0029f81fd3efdf7a86d452913c3939044010d","6a8d72ec18ce1502ec0b4d3f23e5a9091b4c04d183490bdc14a22d6e6dc07902","41741c97eced36264eb4d4a9ec45a7212cb7871536606ff9ea3bd56f9d895018","4ed6bc054d373dc3789fc87bf412916e04691d2200fa882d7bb0102ce1fcc4d5","b48e9201103a180f86b6b91bc4956c6f0e99bc00cb5a1b411ee4f1257993a1f7"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10128,10151],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10128"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.10.2Initiation","paragraph_zero_based":10152},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The Relay UE may initiate the procedure when one of the following conditions is met:","paragraph_zero_based":10153},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as U2N Relay UE:","paragraph_zero_based":10154},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>upon Uu RLF as specified in 5.3.10;","paragraph_zero_based":10155},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>upon reception of an RRCReconfiguration including the reconfigurationWithSync;","paragraph_zero_based":10156},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>upon cell reselection;","paragraph_zero_based":10157},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>upon L2 U2N Relay UE's RRC connection failure including RRC connection reject as specified in 5.3.3.5 and 5.3.13.10, and T300 expiry as specified in 5.3.3.7, and RRC resume failure as specified in 5.3.13.5;","paragraph_zero_based":10158},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as L2 U2U Relay UE:","paragraph_zero_based":10159},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>upon detection of PC5 RLF for the hop between the L2 U2U Relay UE and L2 U2U Remote UE as specified in 5.8.9.3;","paragraph_zero_based":10160},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>upon PC5-RRC connection release for the per-hop link between the L2 U2U Relay UE and L2 U2U Remote UE as specified in 5.8.9.5;","paragraph_zero_based":10161},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.10.3Actions related to transmission of NotificationMessageSidelink message","paragraph_zero_based":10162},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The Relay UE shall set the indication type as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":10163},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as U2N Relay UE:","paragraph_zero_based":10164},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE initiates transmission of the NotificationMessageSidelink message due to Uu RLF:","paragraph_zero_based":10165},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the indicationType as relayUE-Uu-RLF;","paragraph_zero_based":10166},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the UE initiates transmission of the NotificationMessageSidelink message due to reconfiguration with sync:","paragraph_zero_based":10167},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the indicationType as relayUE-HO;","paragraph_zero_based":10168},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the UE initiates transmission of the NotificationMessageSidelink message due to cell reselection:","paragraph_zero_based":10169},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the indicationType as relayUE-CellReselection;","paragraph_zero_based":10170},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE initiates transmission of the NotificationMessageSidelink message due to Uu RRC connection establishment/Resume failure:","paragraph_zero_based":10171},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the indicationType as relayUE-Uu-RRC-Failure;","paragraph_zero_based":10172},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>submit the NotificationMessageSidelink message to lower layers for transmission.","paragraph_zero_based":10173},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as L2 U2U Relay UE:","paragraph_zero_based":10174},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE initiates transmission of the NotificationMessageSidelink message due to PC5 RLF with L2 U2U Remote UE; or","paragraph_zero_based":10175}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["fd25892ba363e01c5a8695f7a6145c9be269ecf483357de074ada3bd43c73c98","77d93b729998a60cca4da8b2628489b2502dae43c0e2ea338bcb66ba43d17a4e","ac96ae2ebaffc0d7b17249543ab135e0709a8167f9207b79939b004b337a390d","c70a2e47123b7140dba2d5342d0ce93eebd652308fa5e3f80f0826e6d787e051","ba40d77c87fc60603c70b654f22a221eea1be87fbc1a9396815a0691503d6784","77b9e604b793a1077fb6da5469947e214e7a0317cac39c63992206639e0fc341","ae663197917928d6f10876a9b4e92d1290d04a831e37e037fea1663a763ccec8","0902385e97ab923dc20c846d47513c337f4bf8cc1109c3c0b91b7ba5baa3d4a1","85d4e36ed91861dda8257577440340bfcedc784197e8c0695faaebc5b790299c","1ac917f4deec46d0b76f7e16592a2d6959c8836d226488027ea273d03c47c26b","48b1eef8a014b5749390d931af3dae6b8ef3df9ed8407256f1890c10753898a3","fb0538ae3b0416f6a905a7e832e75e87448d3144fe534440f1844a7819a457a0","37e3a9b3b53df0e9e5bd2cf7a8927b0fdc573acbcb17849a5a721ee6a4fbd6d3","2cba813ea785c0a8099200e06b5a567f436ca4291b11a2acbcd77174aef1a6a6","390dd114a794101313cc9a5c890082403a0ab70c72e92fc442909f4e23a2db84","e5026c00b4f3e3fb6148a3a8f2f35746f19c661021f483949790cc073b9a85e9","854d1b02567825807c8285ea79958f98711326599f9f38e2e4e3076b62d6c0be","423697ff8b3106ab27a0d6617b29b160146e6e12b999dca341f72f48d421f4b6","99eaa1887a2378dc2e08c5df9d5c102a3f318b6da1d11c93340215d14d648db6","50036b807f20f48d4b7289b402965492686d9c224d9fe180d3d5fed94958905c","52d5b7573161d5ffd1270bc7ac2d4ab00ce2ca5aa74d838760e27f4d1daa6c8d","1a820720e06a9d094ba70b55eaa0e6a87ca034af52d8d85032d49304af1bcf12","bc7a09eceffa9d44046e1a7e9b0c8b95f7c077daafa76b54ae2a7d4d7715fb56","021c2deeb9e202c50b428b6f09144486e2803db4664789acb0e2b0d6332d5b8a"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10152,10175],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10152"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE initiates transmission of the NotificationMessageSidelink message due to PC5-RRC connection release for the per-hop link between the L2 U2U Relay UE and L2 U2U Remote UE:","paragraph_zero_based":10176},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the sl-IndicationType as relayUE-PC5-RLF;","paragraph_zero_based":10177},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the sl-DestinationIdentityRemoteUE as the associated destination for L2 U2U Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":10178},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>submit the NotificationMessageSidelink message to lower layers for transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":10179},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.10.4Actions related to reception of NotificationMessageSidelink message","paragraph_zero_based":10180},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon receiving the NotificationMessageSidelink, the Remote UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10181},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as U2N Remote UE:","paragraph_zero_based":10182},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the indicationType is included:","paragraph_zero_based":10183},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is L2 U2N Remote UE in RRC_CONNECTED:","paragraph_zero_based":10184},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if MP is configured and MCG transmission (i.e. direct path) is not suspended;","paragraph_zero_based":10185},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if the indicationType is relayUE-HO;","paragraph_zero_based":10186},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>suspend indirect path transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":10187},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10188},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>initiate the indirect path failure information procedure as specified in 5. 7. 3c to report indirect path failure;","paragraph_zero_based":10189},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>else if T301 is not running, initiate the RRC connection re-establishment procedure as specified in 5.3.7;","paragraph_zero_based":10190},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else (the UE is L3 U2N Remote UE, or L2 U2N Remote UE in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE):","paragraph_zero_based":10191},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the PC5-RRC connection with the U2N Relay UE is determined to be released:","paragraph_zero_based":10192},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>indicate upper layers to trigger PC5 unicast link release;","paragraph_zero_based":10193},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>else (i.e., maintain the PC5 RRC connection):","paragraph_zero_based":10194},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if the UE is L2 U2N Remote UE and the indicationType is relayUE-HO or relayUE-CellReselection:","paragraph_zero_based":10195},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>consider cell re-selection occurs;","paragraph_zero_based":10196},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:For L3 U2N Remote UE, or L2 U2N Remote UE in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE, it is up to Remote UE implementation whether to release or keep the PC5 unicast link.","paragraph_zero_based":10197},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:The L2 U2N Remote UE may ignore the NotificationMessageSidelink if it does not release the PC5 unicast link in source side yet during an indirect-to-direct path switch, i.e. T304 is running.","paragraph_zero_based":10198},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as L2 U2U Remote UE:","paragraph_zero_based":10199}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["9e22578accfddb53cd73b98c8e5703a5ae10f41559e11c9bd7c6d054088e6b25","e86b28f005f94dd00e8f84046ea92517aeea12c11087de687fd47989aa4fc7e0","d91c48b312cb1ab40b4f72db3a181c5683ef7aff49fe2f786a2a575d37843abd","16f0390ab5e99153060135ed4197e9371e5240abb0d73c78fc648d4e5e890b98","f0c07dc461b1aaabb53b9a016c1167c3fb7ce615ecab6caf2a12dc77767639da","eef2afd2c4aaa3336b9e90c9396c2f95b28ec301bd1bb31bd538e9bbf1abd727","a907f1dc27f071bc439ef9498d61cdfae5348d775d9bf8ccc4c47940bdbd9284","92e089b8072356aec477fe7cdb9ff20fac343daced04489fbda08ed3f94ff43a","4f67b381e481f54b31bd8dd280429080bf8d31e9a7a6b68e5e70b5c7be68bab7","67a15375734ffdf73fc1672ab83e0210510dad5b27de873af95ebf5fadda526d","f23080235fd742ac52c9458fabd0a265eedb2b221502ff9c158afab2fcc3b17c","b17a957870c61a3e5092b1fe8e243a73106dbab3e5572ef6f4cbcda8c04eb5c8","f3b64ea28c62c1f606648aa63bc4007a529209c357139b365615b576dc545646","66ea549173bafdf5bf7496ba4bac90a82be6d898f3750800eb9dcd0a4f85c100","cf5a1f6dee6727ca368d6b8c18cac53fc9c9900e1b1142e716a9b1b77ef5bf96","36f5cd29ff24c347a7402f597578a1287d0eff203a7c262792094a9093b0de5c","98a80c2f155403b7527f20ae2960e8149aa6c3c92fe5acc0b47c7b6a2ec48fdd","9b7a53f45c9282a4d7bfaadd701e64b2d7737b5111d44b43269de8a2ec0c1820","0a03420befd8c47d2fcf450e439208b968f85082a8aeb0303da2ebd1764b12ff","798c4e3d543e224f8d345719424aca72be855eeab207c523a0944f1ced6688ff","ddd9e8cfe8cfaedf7fa5afde160bf3272084eb4c5df89b2a9cbdba02110a51c0","e228588ae5aa0c9b051562f2388b355f3a895549b0fbd9b9f97fe5793a65a8cf","b38102561f7bde3816ab677bfd7136a76dbc59f05e0f01607dfe8ef4832a93a2","5a892fd25cb01f0328bd41ba0dd018f127731b60f8f391bd292b7788a9b6996d"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10176,10199],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10176"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if sl-IndicationType is relayUE-PC5-RLF:","paragraph_zero_based":10200},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>indicate PC5 RLF received from L2 U2U Relay UE to the upper layers for the indicated L2 U2U Remote UE based on the received sl-DestinationIdentityRemoteUE;","paragraph_zero_based":10201},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider the end-to-end PC5 connection failure for the end-to-end PC5 connection(s) over the per-hop PC5 link between the L2 U2U Relay UE and the L2 U2U Remote UE identified by sl-DestinationIdentityRemoteUE;","paragraph_zero_based":10202},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform the end-to-end PC5 connection failure related actions as specified in 5.8.9.3a;","paragraph_zero_based":10203},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 3:It is up to the upper layers on whether to trigger U2U Relay reselection and whether to keep or release the PC5 link with the U2U Relay UE after the PC5 RLF indication received from U2U Relay UE.","paragraph_zero_based":10204},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.11UE information transfer on sidelink","paragraph_zero_based":10205},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.11.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10206},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":10207},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.9.11.1-1: Sidelink UE information procedure","paragraph_zero_based":10208},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The purpose of this procedure is to transfer the UE information in sidelink. The L2 U2U Remote UE informs its end-to-end QoS information and end-to-end QoS flow-to-SLRB mapping to its connected L2 U2U Relay UE in the UEInformationRequestSidelink message, and the L2 U2U Relay UE delivers the split QoS information of the first-hop to the Remote UE in the UEInformationResponseSidelink message.","paragraph_zero_based":10209},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.11.2Actions related to transmission of the UEInformationRequestSidelink by the UE","paragraph_zero_based":10210},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For initial information transfer (e.g. for QoS split) or upon change in any of the information in the UEInformationRequestSidelink, the UE shall set the contents of UEInformationRequestSidelink message as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":10211},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as L2 U2U Remote UE:","paragraph_zero_based":10212},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set sl-E2E-QoS-InfoListPC5 to include the end-to-end QoS profile(s) of the sidelink QoS flow(s) towards the peer L2 U2U Remote UE if configured by the upper layer, and for each entry:","paragraph_zero_based":10213},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set sl-DestinationIdentityRemoteUE to include the associated identity for peer L2 U2U Remote UE ;","paragraph_zero_based":10214},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set sl-E2E-SLRB-Index to include the associated end-to-end SLRB configuration index;","paragraph_zero_based":10215},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set sl-QoS-InfoList to include the end-to-end QoS profile(s) of the sidelink QoS flow(s);","paragraph_zero_based":10216},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>submit the UEInformationRequestSidelink message to lower layers for transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":10217},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.11.3Actions related to reception of the UEInformationRequestSidelink by the UE","paragraph_zero_based":10218},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall perform the following actions upon reception of the UEInformationRequestSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":10219},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as L2 U2U Relay UE:","paragraph_zero_based":10220},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UEInformationRequestSidelink includes the sl-E2E-QoS-ConnectionListPC5:","paragraph_zero_based":10221},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform QoS split based on the sl-QoS-InfoList for each QoS flow to decide the split PDB value for each PC5 hop;","paragraph_zero_based":10222},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the contents of UEInformationResponseSidelink message as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":10223}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["877e47e5d9f9ea4d15d74a57f2df4d1f366fdce120bdd6c27444d9fd7329b705","ddbfb680f2a8aac0fb8349ce8f22e9b36cb6d6d0eee96ea8890c8a4d209a079e","eebaa5161381911a8a034e3fab293567c52798388e26221d93b3c7a648f13658","f4d20d873b7b3d9cb2aaab760690e1ed61d535d89570020607c251f7ead16437","f5597ac1f0986ec89cdb6b5451b6681b277cd519eb7ab6ae908b42bd910d0a1f","b838d7ec8c48aa90c1b0481011fd030084df9a8b2dbdfd50fc68fcbdb7cb19fd","bc5a9fca135913392986f88b1f2a0dc26833f374153fe909315d280ea7df8fe2","e16e9ae2d319b535cba4ec7720d2589c1d39994a78e25c5279d86dfb48c8a4e9","8e70c159d8f3c6548c45d59f71ce3001921ce9f638bb873ec2226b6317848bf1","8f6ec020a1dbae1de374d9219f20c412164277a3df19771690e6dd3b0a77165e","0ce3100888919f7130423cc592bbcda657a70457f9386f1b6cb6fc17dc63d85c","8c3ef1ddf2e3f58379c86de99bc8deb8807278c06297cc415c143b7cc9f68590","e448d14923f5553f68e383f080c9fab1abb53ec46c8a7d91883520ed14c585b3","c87449e6ebf1fec2a14b8dd084dd067575cb5c2096bef5d3d75a981725351686","dcd9d705d7be8384acdec7fe0cf11ba3e1cc83ee1c185061902028fc862a8476","95f21192e49703e15d9194322ac7e08516f2b2e8d076e1ec2bcefc544fb9cd4b","6edce6a060df56b0ffa4f74fd71ec1057d5e2e3840294e044f074154f0e09b9c","ecca3871dee4dffb1ae5df8d7f77f7f2331a607612b4597af0a85f9df7acc6a2","b484c50e37790785ca0dc50f24fb2c2d0bf8f27ddab00a963edd3388f3fdcea8","9821d393929e103916d706d2a3765a7cd8c86cb7504c20ffa6a81af8d082d3ad","baf03ce0243f3f299d408d12770404a6944c2289a08d482929760d9e125387dc","b155e3a342b71e8ee2df1ea94739cfaa82ecf2c3119154ebe0e8a7edf529cf16","e317a79ab567945b81918d09103fb92cd81b4002107eabdf52149b9701f79696","a43e4ac2903dbef814774f19329e39338485aceea35c8e946ed63d036cf599c0"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10200,10223],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10200"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set sl-SplitQoS-InfoListPC5 to include the split PDB value for each QoS flow on the first PC5 hop between L2 U2U Relay UE and L2 U2U Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":10224},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>submit the UEInformationResponseSidelink message to lower layers for transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":10225},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>for the end-to-end SLRB which is in the current UE configuration but not included in the sl-E2E-QoS-InfoListPC5 that (end-to-end DRB release):","paragraph_zero_based":10226},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate the end-to-end sidelink DRB release procedure according to clause 5.8.9.1a.1;","paragraph_zero_based":10227},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>for each sl-E2E-SLRB-Index value included in the sl-E2E-QoS-InfoListPC5 that is not part of the current UE configuration (end-to-end DRB addition); or","paragraph_zero_based":10228},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3> for each sl-E2E-SLRB-Index value included in the sl-E2E-QoS-InfoListPC5 that is part of the current UE configuration (end-to-end DRB modification):","paragraph_zero_based":10229},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>merge the split per-flow QoS on the second PC5 hop into a per-SLRB level QoS profile; ","paragraph_zero_based":10230},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the UE is in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE:","paragraph_zero_based":10231},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>derive the PC5 RLC channel configuration for the second PC5 hop based on the per-SLRB level QoS profile of this end-to-end sidelink DRB according to the configuration in SIB12;","paragraph_zero_based":10232},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>else if the UE is out of coverage:","paragraph_zero_based":10233},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>derive the PC5 RLC channel configuration for the second PC5 hop based on per-SLRB level QoS profile of this end-to-end sidelink DRB according to the configuration in SidelinkPreconfigNR;","paragraph_zero_based":10234},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate the end-to-end sidelink DRB addition/modification procedure according to clause 5.8.9.1a.2.2 if needed;","paragraph_zero_based":10235},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is in RRC_CONNECTED:","paragraph_zero_based":10236},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate sidelink UE information procedure according to clause 5.8.3.2 to report per-SLRB level QoS.","paragraph_zero_based":10237},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:It is left to Relay UE implementation on how to split the PDB. ","paragraph_zero_based":10238},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE X:For a L2 U2U Relay UE, how to merge the split per-flow QoS on the second PC5 hop into a per-SLRB level QoS profile is up to UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":10239},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.11.4Actions related to reception of the UEInformationResponseSidelink by the UE","paragraph_zero_based":10240},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall perform the following actions upon reception of the UEInformationResponseSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":10241},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each sl-E2E-SLRB-Index value included in the sl-E2E-QoS-InfoListPC5 in UEInformationRequestSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":10242},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE is in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE:","paragraph_zero_based":10243},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>merge the split per-flow QoS on the first PC5 hop into a per-SLRB level QoS profile; ","paragraph_zero_based":10244},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>derive the PC5 RLC channel configuration for the first PC5 hop based on the per-SLRB level QoS profile of this end-to-end sidelink DRB according to the configuration in SIB12;","paragraph_zero_based":10245},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the UE is out of coverage:","paragraph_zero_based":10246},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>merge the split per-flow QoS on the first PC5 hop into a per-SLRB level QoS profile; ","paragraph_zero_based":10247}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["75180e75803fd091f34f0eb10b748b6e107ee2471833ffe4f97e008d4dd1b320","68ea5eeb0d4d1de675f6762c2d0c699ddd7859755e2d67217995231972469129","58326f94aa36c053b12824fc95e3ea9c5ee31f59f1d1827beeac119ffc4e7f63","00d5d32e6666f2eae44e8852286d1b79bffb3ffd8d27500169e2108563ae70b7","1ff662113d669f43cedb250b7a2d73ad08350a6328e2e1c031339e2d74a43cf9","74c694b2e640c82787ad1b92ffc22d1c4bb5084626b5ba57b3da88fe9b7faebb","4705d56ca0ada211a2404516d62ca1d32d34c301c0e216712dc72a7df57064fe","9a6b71f9c90632c770f7ffa75868c207e48dc9faabdded7461d375876a9b0ecc","f9c04f981b5592c0cb3c73296edf51dbf12895cc1cab60b8d1cafaa351f1b520","7896a882972545c130095258baac33a966c93bb260f3dac55a3fcd82cabb90c1","fe713f03e8bd00b8cb98384279b48357bd4081e39109fb94ce50738982baca28","ef25fdbf11e8f01e0f5b33254fb89e4948c5c01ceb31ae79bd5bcde3e6c63522","643c8c78d03310143ec63f042e7e7126ea70f8c34848625a0ef39ebd0b3010bd","53131bcb9dd2a5a2b67c42f1c0012759a729bccbf61530a5c90eeb8f8ebbdfe7","dd5024cc6f5e83d99b9e34ed0fec1a81627d66e6e061ecfc8e819b586436e13b","c6e60b0435c8902238961963cf54f4f72497c0c95bb020d4896bc0ca8e8ffef4","30fbb01de6b7f83462eb3b60cf533981b94409d30c6cdec0ab1417a7aa37e921","732d7f320d31d112b9ab0f574b21e453ef8592946fb57d16a2044331f81a15b6","99b860d6f6e19757c8da125ddfb6b5c41e7367c438a28145695ee59deceef047","61a7d4ebfec376aa76a1b6ee224583b302e4c0afb439212be4b769b85a732cd3","7fadeaad8054af0c28814cb7356dafb723ef781652669966b0f79569a142adf4","c41fdd8a37642e2b6dba52c3e5f4d591bd8e5ad370d9ae7cff66cd1e24d8842e","f08176cc30e296bc9ac1f42e1bd571ea0d7e0f07c038b84246c697bc68f3e771","c2e490c97e3b9e2f31a349d471ae94015bdd705dab78d6f6446675b6d9a342ad"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10224,10247],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10224"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>derive the PC5 RLC channel configuration for the first PC5 hop based on per-SLRB level QoS profile of this end-to-end sidelink DRB according to the configuration in SidelinkPreconfigNR;","paragraph_zero_based":10248},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is in RRC_CONNECTED:","paragraph_zero_based":10249},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>initiate sidelink UE information procedure according to clause 5.8.3.2 to report the split QoS profile for the first PC5 hop.","paragraph_zero_based":10250},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:For a L2 U2U Remote UE in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE or out of coverage, how to merge the split per-flow QoS on the first PC5 hop into a per-SLRB level QoS profile is up to UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":10251},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10Sidelink measurement","paragraph_zero_based":10252},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.1Introduction","paragraph_zero_based":10253},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE may configure the associated peer UE to perform NR sidelink measurement and report on the corresponding PC5-RRC connection in accordance with the NR sidelink measurement configuration for unicast by RRCReconfigurationSidelink message.","paragraph_zero_based":10254},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The NR sidelink measurement configuration includes the following parameters for a PC5-RRC connection:","paragraph_zero_based":10255},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1.NR sidelink measurement objects: Object(s) on which the associated peer UE shall perform the NR sidelink measurements.","paragraph_zero_based":10256},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For NR sidelink measurement, a NR sidelink measurement object indicates the NR sidelink frequency of reference signals to be measured.","paragraph_zero_based":10257},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2.NR sidelink reporting configurations: NR sidelink measurement reporting configuration(s) where there can be one or multiple NR sidelink reporting configurations per NR sidelink measurement object. Each NR sidelink reporting configuration consists of the following:","paragraph_zero_based":10258},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Reporting criterion: The criterion that triggers the UE to send a NR sidelink measurement report. This can either be periodical or a single event description.","paragraph_zero_based":10259},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-RS type: The RS that the UE uses for NR sidelink measurement results. In this release, only DMRS is supported for NR sidelink measurement.","paragraph_zero_based":10260},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Reporting format: The quantities that the UE includes in the measurement report. In this release, only RSRP measurement is supported.","paragraph_zero_based":10261},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3.NR sidelink measurement identities: A list of NR sidelink measurement identities where each NR sidelink measurement identity links one NR sidelink measurement object with one NR sidelink reporting configuration. By configuring multiple NR sidelink measurement identities, it is possible to link more than one NR sidelink measurement object to the same NR sidelink reporting configuration, as well as to link more than one NR sidelink reporting configuration to the same NR sidelink measurement object. The NR sidelink measurement identity is also included in the NR sidelink measurement report that triggered the reporting, serving as a reference to the network.","paragraph_zero_based":10262},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4.NR sidelink quantity configurations: The NR sidelink quantity configuration defines the NR sidelink measurement filtering configuration used for all event evaluation and related reporting, and for periodical reporting of that NR sidelink measurement. In each configuration, different filter coefficients can be configured for different NR sidelink measurement quantities.","paragraph_zero_based":10263},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Both UEs of the PC5-RRC connection maintains a NR sidelink measurement object list, a NR sidelink reporting configuration list, and a NR sidelink measurement identities list according to signalling and procedures in this specification.","paragraph_zero_based":10264},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.2Sidelink measurement configuration","paragraph_zero_based":10265},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.2.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10266},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10267},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the received sl-MeasConfig includes the sl-MeasObjectToRemoveList in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":10268},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink measurement object removal procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.4;","paragraph_zero_based":10269},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the received sl-MeasConfig includes the sl-MeasObjectToAddModList in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":10270},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink measurement object addition/modification procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.5;","paragraph_zero_based":10271}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["6e015d0b2b60508f7433bb30012445055799304e0349181872525c49b70f68b1","f469d3d8173d38445bde1f9cc02cfb605ea8672f8a6c5e8b09159e1339cb09ef","6d306677bc298b3258afc23e5bd0d36afaf608f5da6e3ef41c2a3653c92c899d","ddd0c3b9de3ee1e646ed9edb293b14eb861109e223db8ec17906ee76aa724cc5","2070e43ce6a9700f76775ad3f55ddb807cbae623165fb39788ea6f8e046b99c9","4fd31f7103cac8cec9eaf0c321942ae5367dc3a00b32666814ed4e3cb49bc53a","02ce8ee48d40152cf3b1b1d17506468bcb5375de898a60b9af4f4c664b9c5524","6f80197a8ad174761c53f63695bd59640fab3345944e774c240275255865e90b","c8fefcf98b4db10345fa08367a37d54eba02a0082819ecd15b8d21b1870036fe","d42a5fe9ed5a8636f69a6b31f1e29a0f71e310cb13c2f611b6749f8613132fdd","04bf27589e12e6c379d03b52d6cc33e971d6c81e8db0472e0758a463daa1a1cb","c103f32301a86f260f9bc9f4f1bb1e6d5b6f09bad191466c7e44d4ee33305a17","86f90fc5683e485c6e3fdfe49df52edca85fc247a01e31165155a78ca40d1473","c32adaa965ea1f4dad941ccbd37eb2655d93667c7860f93f15c77aaa4f871807","af22c1627eb94b8597c45adad7f3b7de486de8a1e96c64f4fbedadfb7e7e58e3","5ff89eadc0bd064fab6941075b7ec79ff5ef21e3fecc8af83cc71517c3e263bc","c78da61725db0c9de96afdfb9ac457ff1150de9c1f6bb9dc74e9d2ba99fb54df","8fff66f1d3fee2169307378cc5ea092526ee829fc9910f83e627e81ebf739c53","f2fcee0888fddc14ea22390c6fcd752437de9b840db049a26f167381a9d6c92b","7a6d396d7b3f0be5c20d2f7b86e332ccef5c45723d761a554621185c4cbecf81","89e2fec510083ed0823fb584aeafe5c64f2c3229d621554e53be12a615c69c4c","c21c734dbadb02a6ea931a9d25e8b6e65f8f805a8e4172855708ce7bad26efad","3f97b6f7697e68c603d3c6227a96130784e46229675914f33a5064eecec9c201","1c0709ca24de89176babc05eda8dde211e07fca90328fa93e4962285f60748d5"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10248,10271],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10248"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the received sl-MeasConfig includes the sl-ReportConfigToRemoveList in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":10272},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink reporting configuration removal procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.6;","paragraph_zero_based":10273},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the received sl-MeasConfig includes the sl-ReportConfigToAddModList in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":10274},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink reporting configuration addition/modification procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.7;","paragraph_zero_based":10275},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the received sl-MeasConfig includes the sl-QuantityConfig in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":10276},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink quantity configuration procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.8;","paragraph_zero_based":10277},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the received sl-MeasConfig includes the sl-MeasIdToRemoveList in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":10278},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink measurement identity removal procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.2;","paragraph_zero_based":10279},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the received sl-MeasConfig includes the sl-MeasIdToAddModList in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":10280},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink measurement identity addition/modification procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.3;","paragraph_zero_based":10281},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.2.2Sidelink measurement identity removal","paragraph_zero_based":10282},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10283},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each sl-MeasId included in the received sl-MeasIdToRemoveList that is part of the current UE configuration in VarMeasConfigSL:","paragraph_zero_based":10284},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>remove the entry with the matching sl-MeasId from the sl-MeasIdList within the VarMeasConfigSL;","paragraph_zero_based":10285},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>remove the NR sidelink measurement reporting entry for this sl-MeasId from the VarMeasReportListSL, if included;","paragraph_zero_based":10286},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>stop the periodical reporting timer and reset the associated information (e.g. sl-TimeToTrigger) for this sl-MeasId.","paragraph_zero_based":10287},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:The UE does not consider the message as erroneous if the sl-MeasIdToRemoveList includes any sl-MeasId value that is not part of the current UE configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":10288},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.2.3Sidelink measurement identity addition/modification","paragraph_zero_based":10289},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10290},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each sl-MeasId included in the received sl-MeasIdToAddModList:","paragraph_zero_based":10291},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if an entry with the matching sl-MeasId exists in the sl-MeasIdList within the VarMeasConfigSL:","paragraph_zero_based":10292},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>replace the entry with the value received for this sl-MeasId;","paragraph_zero_based":10293},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10294},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>add a new entry for this sl-MeasId within the VarMeasConfigSL;","paragraph_zero_based":10295}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["291788487956e00317e9d6259d3c6d34d4a2734b80ede540902b0272b4676a28","020335cc7e533cd992174ed6e3ce9c07c2bc638658fd3ef0039d03960d82c2b2","2759d5e93fb538c1ea3e6ee445e4602a471b2f29aeee98c56b01984f67abcff8","20df1ddb2808ec5f6d3b321e8a2d9ade2dde1d72cce47d2acf54eea0ff45e3b3","1ffc77b21b2220a0acbc56c3ad9ab35a03947bf5f92af0c9b200da624c4fd5f1","7f1db5d7e3c45efa38b0d98cfe6ecbc97d88872b86b4867bf090b3adf4b4bcec","6d9680f6d91509dd068a2c86c74fe2a672a20ce27f9604596220d3d93c165a72","eb861c4da331f3dc25b91bd13f697fbd7ddd614131d2ec3c82cd9f8c8b523225","5cc29b4cc56a885e32bf111d24892d88fbabd89f287c4c55de8d8cb7587d217b","9f9dabe7730454d70e43656989ac462753d7c9a0ca01aee65f03ee8da82cdb19","8fe12ce5c0245f498cd5625cae9bb10d77c491d40c3d48860e3901a6ddb23a37","d7c5bee6f3282bd32a7f280a859d0ce6d7e1747d4eca3ffa0ee24c3c3f8ae17e","cec12bd416f0d16732381e9b0d4e78b21fb643d0929bc2945c46720aac06837f","74b23b26f8bee3e0351932472fef2d5414eca8b812969006e906701df52899ca","74f8100acb7f58afd2ee2f095c138fc052b1e0048d12125debbfc80ccd19f9ef","9760a17bede1d09872629d82005bd1d6641f474fb075e208874bbcad68cc4559","25ec8f1900cea90c8ee97f11e0ca200401ff01e54ee5c4eed91620d1822801c6","150ef83515d86a163d6f297ef8fdada533b2f7b5eee02fc9ec8511dff5c5e2e3","8d30ef0b5da4bd8e2834efd4c2c09bc5717c831578223fb5164e49c888459281","1a10442f4dd1e234f2fffa41e55f440bda9b17170d46b09ea16eb45bffbe9211","32bd8bc8f9eeb51d445ac106418c491d828fc912705bb3f341f4fb223f027a25","fad700daeb77f7343c7316b0c7a6cf472f56332a15f672975873df510426d1a6","bebc0fbe98dacdcd28639c75e26932c89a84783c294dec5b176364423ceb6024","81b294ad32c44cd078015c323c97ff25e21755ff93ece29ee6a03250964783cc"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10272,10295],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10272"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>remove the measurement reporting entry for this sl-MeasId from the VarMeasReportListSL, if included;","paragraph_zero_based":10296},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>stop the periodical reporting timer and reset the associated information (e.g. sl-TimeToTrigger) for this sl-MeasId;","paragraph_zero_based":10297},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.2.4Sidelink measurement object removal","paragraph_zero_based":10298},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10299},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each sl-MeasObjectId included in the received sl-MeasObjectToRemoveList that is part of sl-MeasObjectList in VarMeasConfigSL:","paragraph_zero_based":10300},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>remove the entry with the matching sl-MeasObjectId from the sl-MeasObjectList within the VarMeasConfigSL;","paragraph_zero_based":10301},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>remove all sl-MeasId associated with this sl-MeasObjectId from the sl-MeasIdList within the VarMeasConfigSL, if any;","paragraph_zero_based":10302},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if a sl-MeasId is removed from the sl-MeasIdList:","paragraph_zero_based":10303},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>remove the measurement reporting entry for this sl-MeasId from the VarMeasReportListSL, if included;","paragraph_zero_based":10304},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>stop the periodical reporting timer and reset the associated information (e.g. sl-TimeToTrigger) for this sl-MeasId.","paragraph_zero_based":10305},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:The UE does not consider the message as erroneous if the sl-MeasObjectToRemoveList includes any sl-MeasObjectId value that is not part of the current UE configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":10306},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.2.5Sidelink measurement object addition/modification","paragraph_zero_based":10307},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10308},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each sl-MeasObjectId included in the received sl-MeasObjectToAddModList:","paragraph_zero_based":10309},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if an entry with the matching sl-MeasObjectId exists in the sl-MeasObjectList within the VarMeasConfigSL, for this entry:","paragraph_zero_based":10310},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>for each sl-MeasId associated with this sl-MeasObjectId included in the sl-MeasIdList within the VarMeasConfigSL, if any:","paragraph_zero_based":10311},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>remove the measurement reporting entry for this sl-MeasId from the VarMeasReportListSL, if included;","paragraph_zero_based":10312},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>stop the periodical reporting timer and reset the associated information (e.g. sl-TimeToTrigger) for this sl-MeasId;","paragraph_zero_based":10313},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>reconfigure the entry with the value received for this sl-MeasObject;","paragraph_zero_based":10314},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10315},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>add a new entry for the received sl-MeasObject to the sl-MeasObjectList within VarMeasConfigSL.","paragraph_zero_based":10316},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.2.6Sidelink reporting configuration removal","paragraph_zero_based":10317},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10318},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each sl-ReportConfigId included in the received sl-ReportConfigToRemoveList that is part of the current UE configuration in VarMeasConfigSL:","paragraph_zero_based":10319}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["687efc1098bb75921958a5c6a20d09d69555ab17c904697b3856ddf6f2ae21ae","5d0acaa9f18ceec26bb15644961822d3d874efc330488f2f7e6866f79c0d171c","061dd8fe55875ab98971da027ed26f34d28d5f9f7571ca2cc0c70e25f0a64336","2b617863fa42e4873a5287f94ffe469f1f5739139bc39f221aacde92ca3c9ac5","a25f542da121d1c0cf58b8bef59f7bf6d8c2547500a47398d347ea9c7aef7907","f7dae07367e54f7e0c1fa41c9ba9288b2762cd6ea792f2af3086676bb3984fbd","53c0d9d0b294edd83299be4df0055f7e7dcf773bd6695a17d619a1cd5e02623c","76f5bc0ffdb424ceb5d4d4a4892cb100bf04ee04fb925c1ea5199d4321f4b1f8","1ef020de0d0329a280e03eef703802caaf69aa78aa2798fd562fdf796a595c11","51640254003ded05572cfda1d42b5a54f2998ef8dd33aa1cf6b9670da9191d71","2d64cbdceb1ec06c4eada70f1a3d9853bb265607e25a96940de76ac8f6aeafc4","ce329f1a6317779a0af9b071793384e10d2877f909f2082b238b4dda0cf88b9b","76cf0f8274039e716caff36774885f5060720d5ad84bb0e8828536d674f04d43","bcc0300de4840fb1660a2f65242f4a4523b63c84d9df0f1b7d510ca53fe80d3a","efff2d7a9aa69f3b85bdcf660967cf116d56ee9b94818bee6dc73b60519ed740","f5b9751cb50e8ea26fd271bdb1805d0e2d27a1c23c033b719fed24fc12c10911","1d91042487c65f845fea2dc4fc46e313b489d818bc96c44ce26e2746670e99dd","1fffba38a028206aa95ee9b2ea16b6985ec487e09ae05d4b44a315613006f478","a26dde3015dd2e15101a003f0d5a13435921f19b3f57b746257ee48d130e847d","d2159a61fcb8d436bbf6427cc5427137ba7ec3f2d9982c342a520f88b3639f2a","6ea94174473b89aeb8970e8136d751a0c2e7c6e4f8783d6b1b06d00bf3cdd9bc","68d8f587064de5d0832d03225cddb093e1daa14f6861b8332e917264e7db14c4","aa5b92d263ef82208ae33540d6392021c15af6b7c35af598889ab18affbfbe58","eeec9573fcb4abfa9e0a177183abddd78c81b149f4db5212c1d4f47e0e7782c4"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10296,10319],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10296"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>remove the entry with the matching sl-ReportConfigId from the sl-ReportConfigList within the VarMeasConfigSL;","paragraph_zero_based":10320},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>remove all sl-MeasId associated with the sl-ReportConfigId from the sl-MeasIdList within the VarMeasConfigSL, if any;","paragraph_zero_based":10321},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if a sl-MeasId is removed from the sl-MeasIdList:","paragraph_zero_based":10322},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>remove the measurement reporting entry for this sl-MeasId from the VarMeasReportListSL, if included;","paragraph_zero_based":10323},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>stop the periodical reporting timer and reset the associated information (e.g. sl-TimeToTrigger) for this sl-MeasId.","paragraph_zero_based":10324},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:The UE does not consider the message as erroneous if the sl-ReportConfigToRemoveList includes any sl-ReportConfigId value that is not part of the current UE configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":10325},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.2.7Sidelink reporting configuration addition/modification","paragraph_zero_based":10326},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10327},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each sl-ReportConfigId included in the received sl-ReportConfigToAddModList:","paragraph_zero_based":10328},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if an entry with the matching sl-ReportConfigId exists in the sl-ReportConfigList within the VarMeasConfigSL, for this entry:","paragraph_zero_based":10329},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>reconfigure the entry with the value received for this sl-ReportConfig;","paragraph_zero_based":10330},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>for each sl-MeasId associated with this sl-ReportConfigId included in the sl-MeasIdList within the VarMeasConfigSL, if any:","paragraph_zero_based":10331},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>remove the measurement reporting entry for this sl-MeasId from the VarMeasReportListSL, if included;","paragraph_zero_based":10332},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>stop the periodical reporting timer and reset the associated information (e.g. sl-TimeToTrigger) for this sl-MeasId;","paragraph_zero_based":10333},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10334},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>add a new entry for the received sl-ReportConfig to the sl-ReportConfigList within the VarMeasConfigSL.","paragraph_zero_based":10335},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.2.8Sidelink quantity configuration","paragraph_zero_based":10336},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10337},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each received sl-QuantityConfig:","paragraph_zero_based":10338},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set the corresponding parameter(s) in sl-QuantityConfig within VarMeasConfigSL to the value of the received sl-QuantityConfig parameter(s);","paragraph_zero_based":10339},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each sl-MeasId included in the sl-MeasIdList within VarMeasConfigSL:","paragraph_zero_based":10340},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>remove the measurement reporting entry for this sl-MeasId from the VarMeasReportListSL, if included;","paragraph_zero_based":10341},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>stop the periodical reporting timer and reset the associated information (e.g. sl-TimeToTrigger) for this sl-MeasId.","paragraph_zero_based":10342},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.3Performing NR sidelink measurements","paragraph_zero_based":10343}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["7c65ebb5637184ca0220aa2eb9c7d5100ac1bd712c7247c999cf67604813e273","0d90b609207c80f420cbdf413612d448699a83c7cc6d5fc503d44159392b25ae","f5e2cf792aa3c547c435f53169e666a7f4731776b1221241c34af90818999083","44c82f72fb794b58001ce12a286c0a670ce56a4e465ae60ef9c609179f34a179","f1d2ac090bfdda293b52b8b9cfed503193cf973cc13de41269a6831b30fcf3e0","f943ea14d93a8a42f88145630a22d1b5e4a485305d8c672d1e4c9d9143fd11e2","2ca9128b605f3373270d8de040ee6a859995cf5276a50ea8881882d576478588","332f33cb4b99bb3d933e5a56ead6612daa428b798b8b2d2c8aa29e159ab49ac9","8d8fad071872626f036bf3c7f28550f20f94f869c3b1ed265ef35d1ade149f2c","38b15f1beed538c61572fe13b9fb6bd8ac0655d95ef05159bae98cf4cb9c014d","97b5b11639621b82b7417edd3ad2cae315baa65fd9b0e4fa282f2aac3a526090","940e19bde0c1ba7018ff8758f1cc5839ff340f9b6445fa1087692c9a17c9639b","151aba1299eec966be242c5896b038011daa07341519eeae3c729915bf3bf151","6b710af5095bddf322a46cbb216d7b1e56ce61facf70f7475962b0978dc0369b","03135f9994e71f9da48dda6b093f5f730f60b8691ed5d959689574ca31ad2826","76cc082f8705bba6a216fadf765d3b33b951f532c6e56e4df019f1cd7e2bcf67","f902c6407cacdcfc59568b39ad20c022475128e85e370386f4a6509c591d930e","2d6ab7fb4eed265b9b75a4eb9a770b05c27e457d9792eda18c85224cf6933bdc","52b535d4d12d22d7b292ce861ff9e228cc8465dc59ea152b45a475c08a2e9584","4bd1435fd910b497129952b9a954a8393e0efb4e215754719491376c42daf2a3","8baf1d07b153b8c95561881eabd491a638ab0586f66155dcab3db8156e277e85","be51e04d2a60ecb810a488e08a1e66abcf71be919716955adf2d70d789526e85","19aea99ef00999fe6c4f8e0effb4e85227bc85c0582abb0128752f0951ca831f","3fbcf622a18a3c564b12b8c434362282e527ae23d8c86be723b89d0e5f00334a"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10320,10343],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10320"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.3.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10344},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE shall derive NR sidelink measurement results by measuring one or multiple DMRS associated per PC5-RRC connection as configured by the peer UE associated, as described in 5.8.10.3.2. For all NR sidelink measurement results the UE applies the layer 3 filtering as specified in clause 5.5.3.2, before using the measured results for evaluation of reporting criteria and measurement reporting. In this release, only NR sidelink RSRP can be configured as trigger quantity and reporting quantity.","paragraph_zero_based":10345},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10346},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each sl-MeasId included in the sl-MeasIdList within VarMeasConfigSL:","paragraph_zero_based":10347},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sl-MeasObject is associated to NR sidelink and the sl-RS-Type is set to dmrs:","paragraph_zero_based":10348},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>derive the layer 3 filtered NR sidelink measurement result based on PSSCH DMRS for the trigger quantity and each measurement quantity indicated in sl-ReportQuantity using parameters from the associated sl-MeasObject, as described in 5.8.10.3.2.","paragraph_zero_based":10349},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the evaluation of reporting criteria as specified in 5.8.10.4.","paragraph_zero_based":10350},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.3.2Derivation of NR sidelink measurement results","paragraph_zero_based":10351},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE may be configured by the peer UE associated to derive NR sidelink RSRP measurement results per PC5-RRC connection associated to the NR sidelink measurement objects based on parameters configured in the sl-MeasObject and in the sl-ReportConfig.","paragraph_zero_based":10352},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10353},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each NR sidelink measurement quantity to be derived based on NR sidelink DMRS/SL-PRS:","paragraph_zero_based":10354},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>derive the corresponding measurement of NR sidelink frequency indicated quantity based on PSSCH DMRS/SL-PRS as described in TS 38.215 [9] in the concerned sl-MeasObject;","paragraph_zero_based":10355},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>apply layer 3 filtering as described in 5.5.3.2;","paragraph_zero_based":10356},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.4Sidelink measurement report triggering","paragraph_zero_based":10357},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.4.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10358},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10359},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each sl-MeasId included in the sl-MeasIdList within VarMeasConfigSL:","paragraph_zero_based":10360},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sl-ReportType is set to sl-EventTriggered and if the entry condition applicable for this event, i.e. the event corresponding with the sl-EventId of the corresponding sl-ReportConfig within VarMeasConfigSL, is fulfilled for NR sidelink frequency for all NR sidelink measurements after layer 3 filtering taken during sl-TimeToTrigger defined for this event within the VarMeasConfigSL, while the VarMeasReportListSL does not include a NR sidelink measurement reporting entry for this sl-MeasId (a first NR sidelink frequency triggers the event):","paragraph_zero_based":10361},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>include a NR sidelink measurement reporting entry within the VarMeasReportListSL for this sl-MeasId;","paragraph_zero_based":10362},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the sl-NumberOfReportsSent defined within the VarMeasReportListSL for this sl-MeasId to 0;","paragraph_zero_based":10363},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>include the concerned NR sidelink frequency in the sl-FrequencyTriggeredList defined within the VarMeasReportListSL for this sl-MeasId;","paragraph_zero_based":10364},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>initiate the NR sidelink measurement reporting procedure, as specified in 5.8.10.5;","paragraph_zero_based":10365},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the sl-ReportType is set to sl-EventTriggered and if the entry condition applicable for this event, i.e. the event corresponding with the sl-EventId of the corresponding sl-ReportConfig within VarMeasConfigSL, is fulfilled for NR sidelink frequency not included in the sl-FrequencyTriggeredList for all NR sidelink measurements after layer 3 filtering taken during sl-TimeToTrigger defined for this event within the VarMeasConfigSL (a subsequent NR sidelink frequency triggers the event):","paragraph_zero_based":10366},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the sl-NumberOfReportsSent defined within the VarMeasReportListSL for this sl-MeasId to 0;","paragraph_zero_based":10367}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["8dec57d138cc6d302eb42819121aff97fc6b71f1454977cffb1d3ac172e82b7c","2f61522df4cff477e16c7886e37c00855673f538db076bca29ad72300a265986","d9792e79d58673093f6401484e44881c2b0a78b7d7d0a635ec4870cc1e8554b2","38e1566f1f8af84892f4157a6a44476de579c507665b13f1783a2dde4d5bc41f","2f64313b0a247cbd6a4c9d2bdebdd4fb8f3a0e24a49265bf4f394ac61a06b7b6","764231e79494eaa42b7738d09cf32b33dae8bc049ec68f21648d57895326a67d","1cbfd3851dc74608122cde7e287281f98b846d0455be01dbf27c42c62b2d7ca3","642a8e673a2b06e7af0e67b250ad0b9d0dbb9cc86762a3fe5661478c53f5c9e1","9c270641ca9e1fb97e01aafc41926001bd42a57469ac86b87965abd41fad12ae","0e6a760c036a869f9fb5d4fd7c78fac5d7455d2121ef60a57865fffeef6a7144","df15bec50156668a6b0f1b0dcad1d22cb819c5f2bec44b4c9a73e2f6d31e6aa7","bcefcaed4fc654117a03b2ad608558d2f11cefeea436ff9e6e6c1c165e71dbaf","f2381ce5826c58b701bb91a44979aefc359ef44b89e14cb895ba22cf7af6b457","d848f1ea31f7d47e12ec0a0ceb0a829c67f5d6adcd17bcd4a5ac54ad211147c7","77bee8792e75b507a937d6d9b6e6c1aa06dfa0858b241b9a597d50ad94b3295c","c1f090b9c283a7ae12dcfd86c86f7f6f54bd1bdf09776c61458bd80561688b7d","52b6a808cd588a44ab90554c4a56a38f2e7407c24b37e09af6ab033f27bda239","416967ccb713d9845d3de0c552d846875fd2a5f2d9fa19d7983625f78b72e6ff","a0cc58995d93f956ced78f861c2a82662946d191afb0b8341f1259a1ceaf1f5a","2ede811f1dc46d3039a45f0a22783a6f8390034484f377b9d7d158b8b5345b55","f5ab810408cedf776f9b7ebb5673bf3e071e147b0cbec884c3844ee6d84176ea","58f587ad84a9187db0e87c199e85f2bc65b3c0b5f54a5ac3853830589e8543f8","1d760063f0a8e544af0773823f22250bda1439d46d0433d7d394eb5a0dcfb7f3","8033caace032e94849b9aee95293ae6ac06811223b48f6cf66ea095608933d8a"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10344,10367],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10344"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>include the concerned NR sidelink frequency in the sl-FrequencyTriggeredList defined within the VarMeasReportListSL for this sl-MeasId;","paragraph_zero_based":10368},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>initiate the NR sidelink measurement reporting procedure, as specified in 5.8.10.5;","paragraph_zero_based":10369},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the sl-ReportType is set to sl-EventTriggered and if the leaving condition applicable for this event is fulfilled for NR sidelink frequency included in the sl-FrequencyTriggeredList defined within the VarMeasReportListSL for this sl-MeasId for all NR sidelink measurements after layer 3 filtering taken during sl-TimeToTrigger defined within the VarMeasConfigSL for this event:","paragraph_zero_based":10370},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>remove the concerned NR sidelink frequency in the sl-FrequencyTriggeredList defined within the VarMeasReportListSL for this sl-MeasId;","paragraph_zero_based":10371},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if sl-ReportOnLeave is set to true for the corresponding reporting configuration:","paragraph_zero_based":10372},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate the NR sidelink measurement reporting procedure, as specified in 5.8.10.5;","paragraph_zero_based":10373},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the sl-FrequencyTriggeredList defined within the VarMeasReportListSL for this sl-MeasId is empty:","paragraph_zero_based":10374},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>remove the NR sidelink measurement reporting entry within the VarMeasReportListSL for this sl-MeasId;","paragraph_zero_based":10375},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>stop the periodical reporting timer for this sl-MeasId, if running;","paragraph_zero_based":10376},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if sl-ReportType is set to sl-Periodical and if a (first) NR sidelink measurement result is available:","paragraph_zero_based":10377},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>include a NR sidelink measurement reporting entry within the VarMeasReportListSL for this sl-MeasId;","paragraph_zero_based":10378},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the sl-NumberOfReportsSent defined within the VarMeasReportListSL for this sl-MeasId to 0;","paragraph_zero_based":10379},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>initiate the NR sidelink measurement reporting procedure, as specified in 5.8.10.5, immediately after the quantity to be reported becomes available for the NR sidelink frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":10380},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>upon expiry of the periodical reporting timer for this sl-MeasId:","paragraph_zero_based":10381},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>initiate the NR sidelink measurement reporting procedure, as specified in 5.8.10.5.","paragraph_zero_based":10382},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.4.2Event S1 (Serving becomes better than threshold)","paragraph_zero_based":10383},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10384},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>consider the entering condition for this event to be satisfied when condition S1-1, as specified below, is fulfilled;","paragraph_zero_based":10385},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>consider the leaving condition for this event to be satisfied when condition S1-2, as specified below, is fulfilled;","paragraph_zero_based":10386},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for this NR sidelink measurement, consider the NR sidelink frequency corresponding to the associated sl-MeasObject associated with this event.","paragraph_zero_based":10387},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Inequality S1-1 (Entering condition)","paragraph_zero_based":10388},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Ms – Hys > Thresh","paragraph_zero_based":10389},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Inequality S1-2 (Leaving condition)","paragraph_zero_based":10390},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Ms + Hys < Thresh","paragraph_zero_based":10391}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["c9df09ebe9caf34191b9def8b4f1ee2b286ba6f3589432535ae9eb856cc6da02","63c0a2eb8935abf2d19ce44959ca0d8c4bca89ed3ebc3822e3413b874b24bfb7","ccebde339278a16efb8d7b10a3e2aa7a32718dc6f941a91e9ad0e0f2163c6213","f696d6f3e9f0bf3cb075fab2139b82eb5ca0af8ffa9993d6495d70861ffad38d","90e0cf2657b738d55ce3319d09fbf0047837ea36c22318d4cdd587e68e67593f","61435bcb9d9dfde56b0e0e279f5a99bb1d3ee9507baf6859816c69a1ef96f378","c3cdb4173ccae75ad4a28373d928a00ef8c0cf0fb64b24410321e063c65acc81","9863d9f8640c9297271926acd351a3564b580fbc74d115a6979a161998071704","13eabeb93264d1c522983d9611ed2e374761faa109021d7d658981d8161918f6","6702c91bba37876b7c4af4c4bdd261004bf3cfcf6edf79e5d174a6a6d0f43d74","1ce50ce1cb75f050afec6f8b29a55803b6e835c978db8d91294f260ef637191c","31abaa5aa2e6a885afa55d918f293e939b2cf1dd28481aacdb5d2f01ff8139b1","532368a7f3cb04a48b698bd232997714c1f23b40968212bf1889f50ac2902a47","1f2bd71224884bbc8d07549d1f2d7cb77e669518728b73dfc71db23ad95af7f9","7bbd9c16f7b88a7bde5811d4eebb143d94544d359eb1c3e9e18ffaa36993c0ab","d130224f35b8a15aa7e770c9633210c7c49a7a761a842524e301aaba3069e7f5","b8daa76c17a97c0a135ea88372579f965833e6cd1e22926014a498da7d9dfe4f","a2ab0d26f364d6c6563e67eb76786f54ef79b65b034a23d957c433395aec84da","1cc44a3ff3eeab06716e6a665287461a1f714446754fa755df6da538e3e29e2c","3fd51afec077891b92af66a0ab69d502cc160b08dba43eff75f724526cfd6d05","09cff0cb45312647dcc700565cf126d99a3d776bfbd88929de48ce2b80166f41","7e65f2bc18c43840a32e3334378feb6226dd4183a900eab007840d1ba1d6611b","6fa3c2e7714ae41118cc5c6b6893267a668907d3762bc31fff7bf2b9b1522f67","1e7823c3520819a5faf40682252b33ba3d2243e420f04550af0ec021f70ce97b"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10368,10391],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10368"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The variables in the formula are defined as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":10392},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Ms is the NR sidelink measurement result of the NR sidelink frequency, not taking into account any offsets.","paragraph_zero_based":10393},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Hys is the hysteresis parameter for this event (i.e. sl-Hysteresis as defined within sl-ReportConfig for this event).","paragraph_zero_based":10394},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Thresh is the threshold parameter for this event (i.e. s1-Threshold as defined within sl-ReportConfig for this event).","paragraph_zero_based":10395},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Ms is expressed in dBm in case of RSRP.","paragraph_zero_based":10396},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Hys is expressed in dB.","paragraph_zero_based":10397},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Thresh is expressed in the same unit as Ms.","paragraph_zero_based":10398},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.4.3Event S2 (Serving becomes worse than threshold)","paragraph_zero_based":10399},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10400},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>consider the entering condition for this event to be satisfied when condition S2-1, as specified below, is fulfilled;","paragraph_zero_based":10401},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>consider the leaving condition for this event to be satisfied when condition S2-2, as specified below, is fulfilled;","paragraph_zero_based":10402},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for this NR sidelink measurement, consider the NR sidelink frequency indicated by the sl-MeasObject associated to this event.","paragraph_zero_based":10403},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Inequality S2-1 (Entering condition)","paragraph_zero_based":10404},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Ms + Hys < Thresh","paragraph_zero_based":10405},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Inequality S2-2 (Leaving condition)","paragraph_zero_based":10406},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Ms – Hys > Thresh","paragraph_zero_based":10407},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The variables in the formula are defined as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":10408},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Ms is the NR sidelink measurement result of the NR sidelink frequency, not taking into account any offsets.","paragraph_zero_based":10409},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Hys is the hysteresis parameter for this event (i.e. sl-Hysteresis as defined within sl-ReportConfig for this event).","paragraph_zero_based":10410},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Thresh is the threshold parameter for this event (i.e. s2-Threshold as defined within sl-ReportConfig for this event).","paragraph_zero_based":10411},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Ms is expressed in dBm in case of RSRP.","paragraph_zero_based":10412},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Hys is expressed in dB.","paragraph_zero_based":10413},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Thresh is expressed in the same unit as Ms.","paragraph_zero_based":10414},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.5Sidelink measurement reporting","paragraph_zero_based":10415}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["b520daff5db3c282caa64dbdbba05f9554904f0b828df3eac8e66e428758c524","7722dd2d10d9a1758018cb02f52faccd97570f1f56a981ee7eb27df5b33a4049","49d83090885040d69d485e936b808500b6ccda6b8be12793c7d9845df1dabfce","64497b9a1372906b66d189e3e1b65e467ed252b7c6ed952211c123d7c9d855db","a5a7b035e109f9664274ad173a937b3571a2953f8065685718f37fc6da1bffa7","a9d29341988dfeaae14968e77508d7f5260f994440d6c7b8784bcf2e9fd8e63f","9bd6d06225edb25b30b29df781d44356d2c6831c3c426f1c128d26bcf83079be","2c8487055913c2495c13d89d8aaa96b56e00dc78a0293ada68127be0d29b380c","d0e5462973311ec4578e33525f56e7d42aa5ffb7486129cfe24aa96ea8f1d07b","161f3be96d60924225e4b40a5af114ad1f822a14ec60b2ad90dd48bcf7897b9b","3b3d1e403a6ab818845833f89f95b84f05889317d9b323ccd4b8a72f244e5948","2dec3c3d280d01969e668fc4cf7effc8661135ac971dc424e36a185dcd4a9d9c","12b2a6c71f6ba3dfff6f7d7572120bfa287a52fc001e41385b474a58d6ff6f76","0f64200a3c46540f252c5e8c853e6fbc058540b98f34ba4f99a67422c21c9d1d","ab10f783ed9924218df4f28bc597a5968be870d74cf16e200476007cccd3c40c","4c1bb843a23ea75b230fb82b1433edd03307da48a70e18da3e5dde6acc21b5cc","0d20c358798ffc71149f4d495ba1ee859c791d1359d3db4ef9aa125b951fe631","d5cb846356a541594103246b1f34ddd3f7340123a28d1f9b3504aab70f88f8f3","88a29296fbac4f2cff4d348adc264ec3362ace94bb1875697da9a9e3149388d8","9de3a67aa11a4e916390d5b23d9f8eff1a3853933f650daf864f590cc3b43c25","e197bb763a42a47b4c717b6f025a94eafa65e58bf8fef00176a9a3865b3d1e4f","f18494e6538c53df42ed6da9f863ef3032c1acfd56251c0a75943c6b296da8d5","43dee62ba604945af58b657fed1b590512b98ce40d7957345258036598d83911","343655915e5d1b869384717202a851e0b4d048a29cad53c036eba77022e11f55"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10392,10415],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10392"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.5.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10416},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":10417},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.10.5.1-1: NR sidelink measurement reporting","paragraph_zero_based":10418},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The purpose of this procedure is to transfer measurement results from the UE to the peer UE associated.","paragraph_zero_based":10419},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For the sl-MeasId for which the NR sidelink measurement reporting procedure was triggered, the UE shall set the sl-MeasResults within the MeasurementReportSidelink message as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":10420},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>set the sl-MeasId to the measurement identity that triggered the NR sidelink measurement reporting;","paragraph_zero_based":10421},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the sl-ReportConfig associated with the sl-MeasId that triggered the NR sidelink measurement reporting is set to sl-EventTriggered or sl-Periodical:","paragraph_zero_based":10422},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sl-RS-Type within sl-ReportConfig is set to dmrs:","paragraph_zero_based":10423},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set sl-ResultDMRS within sl-MeasResult to include the NR sidelink DMRS based quantity indicated in the sl-ReportQuantity within the concerned sl-ReportConfig;","paragraph_zero_based":10424},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sl-RS-Type within sl-ReportConfig is set to sl-prs:","paragraph_zero_based":10425},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set sl-Result-SL-PRS within sl-MeasResult to include the NR SL-PRS based quantity indicated in the sl-ReportQuantity within the concerned sl-ReportConfig;","paragraph_zero_based":10426},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>increment the sl-NumberOfReportsSent as defined within the VarMeasReportListSL for this sl-MeasId by 1;","paragraph_zero_based":10427},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>stop the periodical reporting timer, if running;","paragraph_zero_based":10428},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the sl-NumberOfReportsSent as defined within the VarMeasReportListSL for this sl-MeasId is less than the sl-ReportAmount as defined within the corresponding sl-ReportConfig for this sl-MeasId:","paragraph_zero_based":10429},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>start the periodical reporting timer with the value of sl-ReportInterval as defined within the corresponding sl-ReportConfig for this sl-MeasId;","paragraph_zero_based":10430},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10431},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sl-ReportType is set to sl-Periodical:","paragraph_zero_based":10432},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>remove the entry within the VarMeasReportListSL for this sl-MeasId;","paragraph_zero_based":10433},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>remove this sl-MeasId from the sl-MeasIdList within VarMeasConfigSL;","paragraph_zero_based":10434},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>submit the MeasurementReportSidelink message to lower layers for transmission, upon which the procedure ends.","paragraph_zero_based":10435},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.11Zone identity calculation","paragraph_zero_based":10436},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall determine an identity of the zone (i.e. Zone_id) in which it is located using the following formulae, if sl-ZoneConfig is configured:","paragraph_zero_based":10437},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"x1= Floor (x / L) Mod 64;","paragraph_zero_based":10438},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"y1= Floor (y / L) Mod 64;","paragraph_zero_based":10439}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["6796fef68e35def51572e595899573a0ea0cbb2e5fa5850f753d32b2f73df7c9","d8767a997e743d8c1baacc683b70580f9452ee7236c1221c7fb0082bd879ed66","d5fb9812c11ba608b55777c420cb22a000d63c61246d5bde91eba92225d3754b","d10fac05a742a090985c7a2d47d821c5ead8fa3e14308da270bef0a8faf978e3","b3bdb81138105610ce835e13e6144d35607fa5445897bab0428a9a97f51fabb3","1df328cea3cf7cbae7fa91f85f4b6997c65a1a5d2e8d7bcb6ce92e64e67d9311","df7381519e700f7d93f97a2604903e901e6a431b8628ca5305ea5c67b3464572","8273d1b0d4041943b7cb8107e13c0131e9616576f953ce440f6795574b1571a9","ee3c5a7f2126149a35b4b764a6330270d719ba88cca1bb546e3f9e5e99cc26d4","6b20071108c5627d9315e23164516d58e4e64cffe8f1118f536f8e55a81ca336","b7faf017a0ad50ae3ac7f8d0deb79165b03f8d182b0dd6f22789b6ce4af31563","68895aa0375118ad1bec14347beedcb4fdde71b63114165baf3a4dfc11b48572","21cf1ec88cb4663d19a55580739c7906638308ac7834715be34ef2f035140132","e22c0991d05801a17306875f13fc70b6cdd5178f97ce5aa704825bd33cd8e027","04776d3f5c2b758e8d91f52f07396b4656376d39a7102b3258989e861f0fe540","b3b9ee614ccf0813edcb474e2d753a69ffaaab3d3bd9e18f734a11253ac89be4","e31b4a5d13119f8bf1b39d0d5a1f5017c1cc67af52d32b6178b41bc836d0287d","34431e9a27f394886c3c6fa8ca0bb396a49fc462d3b3acab65fe405c92051668","79a8bbd98b86ce78f8b719d46fdace522cef9580b531f53c2a9cfa71c5d9d639","5996ce3d2b41caf2c96cd4bf96498e3631132c013b73081619d7cd47116ad92e","924a19d9cdbb47064cb044e4ba4cdc19b3586beaf79b0ce672e3300e4c3c0901","48ddbc3f57750491cd23e397d57cec493a1ac086a4de699c86ec7977b638e702","bd96e42b468398aacc1966590c013f7ba039c8bb98acdb4426da6ee4a9b4e7c3","0c0e39389de140db40441086ac14d9ba95f142414c5d09dfe321807557f6baa6"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10416,10439],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10416"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Zone_id = y1 * 64 + x1.","paragraph_zero_based":10440},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The parameters in the formulae are defined as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":10441},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"L is the value of sl-ZoneLength included in sl-ZoneConfig;","paragraph_zero_based":10442},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"x is the geodesic distance in longitude between UE's current location and geographical coordinates (0, 0) according to WGS84 model [58] and it is expressed in meters;","paragraph_zero_based":10443},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"y is the geodesic distance in latitude between UE's current location and geographical coordinates (0, 0) according to WGS84 model [58] and it is expressed in meters.","paragraph_zero_based":10444},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:How the calculated zone_id is used is specified in TS 38.321 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":10445},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.12DFN derivation from GNSS","paragraph_zero_based":10446},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When the UE selects GNSS as the synchronization reference source, the DFN, the subframe number within a frame and slot number within a frame used for NR sidelink communication/discovery are derived from the current UTC time, by the following formulae:","paragraph_zero_based":10447},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"DFN= Floor (0.1*(Tcurrent –Tref–OffsetDFN)) mod 1024","paragraph_zero_based":10448},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SubframeNumber= Floor (Tcurrent –Tref–OffsetDFN) mod 10","paragraph_zero_based":10449},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SlotNumber= Floor ((Tcurrent –Tref–OffsetDFN)*2μ) mod (10*2μ)","paragraph_zero_based":10450},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Where:","paragraph_zero_based":10451},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Tcurrent is the current UTC time obtained from GNSS. This value is expressed in milliseconds;","paragraph_zero_based":10452},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Tref is the reference UTC time 00:00:00 on Gregorian calendar date 1 January, 1900 (midnight between Thursday, December 31, 1899 and Friday, January 1, 1900). This value is expressed in milliseconds;","paragraph_zero_based":10453},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"OffsetDFN is the value sl-OffsetDFN if configured, otherwise it is zero. This value is expressed in milliseconds.","paragraph_zero_based":10454},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"μ=0/1/2/3 corresponding to the 15/30/60/120 kHz of SCS for SL, respectively.","paragraph_zero_based":10455},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:In case of leap second change event, how UE obtains the scheduled time of leap second change to adjust Tcurrent correspondingly is left to UE implementation. How UE handles to avoid the sudden discontinuity of DFN is left to UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":10456},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:Void.","paragraph_zero_based":10457},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.13NR sidelink discovery","paragraph_zero_based":10458},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.13.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10459},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The purpose of this procedure is to perform NR sidelink discovery as specified in TS 23.304 [65].","paragraph_zero_based":10460},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.13.2NR sidelink discovery monitoring","paragraph_zero_based":10461},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink discovery that is configured by upper layers to monitor NR sidelink discovery messages shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10462},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the frequency used for NR sidelink discovery is included in sl-FreqInfoToAddModList in RRCReconfiguration message and sl-DiscConfig is included in RRCReconfiguration; or if the frequency used for NR sidelink discovery is included in sl-FreqInfoList included in SIB12 and sl-DiscConfigCommon is included in SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":10463}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["74c733989ec39ad6ce22ab79a60a7f611c15450a09313403d70d5abf37d3ee47","a071efc31847394e3c2f86a8ab8feb621a3e3f8edd62145657aacd5a38201ea1","9e0608510b49c11008a172d41f8a1cb7e0efe66af350f0d39572eb4f7606c2fa","039713a352dbbfe0d09c391f0d7a427f4af0cd5cf0165784f396871d89bc1be6","1837ac0744f78723189c8565e167a8c3b7590c01ac13e2ba7f26ef65091fbb17","d218565ad7d85cf5b8c69dcda4a63c1f95b92e864f6e68d7a02760b9a886669c","35f36a9e3c9f6e5fad76a227dfea9d1f86d9c4d35f9b251bfa8065c9a1f2f53c","515984a1bbf9256a7a66694213ac2e2aa71aa4b40724c62ce91cd52f3908b348","d14e367cc0f28192a2877db3d8fefeecb4a13fdc4c256bfaa358a571f2264b67","9d45a6c609b75c9749b0bb290c333bbb7e0ca7b9471b8d659206e31a895db7ce","becf75945a9b6fe04b2e7f8e910ac69ab2d6e2da5aa09476b06e931238612350","5d01a647e03cbcbcd3382caf7275aedbd23fe93b6bc3677fbd4e0aaf33475b25","91f5162dd6d3c954ae04d0a91f0dcfceeb973f8a4dd39af296a07c812c756bf7","0abe35e873661d9ba641e83096c86dc734c3afb8166220d0e9d58697139dbfc5","6379c400e37f1ec1fe7c1dab07a4a5d3f93e5c8ac82ef66b77b44f06a045888f","f50145d94a1c7cf9064e5f39d91d14118fbce1d2891b9f8d75e8e4981655fd5c","7ce4cee7d56908fc3854174a8d8c57469ce635b5e1d466a78732c5bf21c7dd12","17cbf314f22dd79ce4d69266411da62c1f2bf07b3d103bedebf2de5238b30828","0fed20c82ab697af76c27743a704ba5c5b862f1920d2d08c0e303e7c0f27ded6","98cd5b67c7a2c35f71641cbf19d376b6c37697d06b8d26e5fc5018994f166c63","ea803dec43d80655e0da71b329b679af14d3c964c865e5686c1fbfddaa8ddda2","8a1ceac540086bc38dc507a49f36009b4f1b7ac038d3b4f81a28f8751efd1a9b","fedff3783f27e4b245ecb59630a1ccec9c6c9a3f4d0748e5a0853efcde51f760","f4957c693f7904e5a19531645c9c3418b4d245ea3e2d43e0cc8a1db1a7e3b915"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10440,10463],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10440"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE is configured with sl-DiscRxPool for NR sidelink discovery reception included in RRCReconfiguration message with reconfigurationWithSync (i.e. handover):","paragraph_zero_based":10464},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>configure lower layers to monitor sidelink control information and the corresponding data using the resource pool indicated by sl-DiscRxPool for NR sidelink discovery reception in RRCReconfiguration;","paragraph_zero_based":10465},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the UE is configured with sl-RxPool for NR sidelink discovery reception included in RRCReconfiguration message with reconfigurationWithSync (i.e. handover):","paragraph_zero_based":10466},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>configure lower layers to monitor sidelink control information and the corresponding data using the resource pool indicated by sl-RxPool for NR sidelink discovery reception in RRCReconfiguration;","paragraph_zero_based":10467},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the cell chosen for NR sidelink discovery reception provides SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":10468},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if sl-DiscRxPool for NR sidelink discovery reception is included in SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":10469},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>configure lower layers to monitor sidelink control information and the corresponding data using the resource pool indicated by sl-DiscRxPool for NR sidelink discovery reception in SIB12;","paragraph_zero_based":10470},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else if sl-RxPool for NR sidelink discovery reception is included in SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":10471},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>configure lower layers to monitor sidelink control information and the corresponding data using the resource pool indicated by sl-RxPool for NR sidelink discovery reception in SIB12;","paragraph_zero_based":10472},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10473},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if out of coverage on the concerned frequency for NR sidelink discovery:","paragraph_zero_based":10474},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if sl-DiscRxPool was preconfigured:","paragraph_zero_based":10475},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>configure lower layers to monitor sidelink control information and the corresponding data using the resource pool that was preconfigured by sl-DiscRxPool for NR sidelink discovery reception in SL-PreconfigurationNR, as defined in clause 9.3;","paragraph_zero_based":10476},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10477},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>configure lower layers to monitor sidelink control information and the corresponding data using the resource pool that was preconfigured by sl-RxPool for NR sidelink discovery reception in SL-PreconfigurationNR, as defined in clause 9.3;","paragraph_zero_based":10478},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:If sl-DiscRxPool and sl-RxPool are both included in SIB12 or preconfigured, it is up to UE implementation whether to monitor sidelink control information and the corresponding data using the resource pool indicated by sl-RxPool for NR sidelink discovery reception.","paragraph_zero_based":10479},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.13.3NR sidelink discovery transmission","paragraph_zero_based":10480},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink discovery that is configured by upper layer to transmit NR sidelink discovery message shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10481},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the frequency used for NR sidelink discovery is included in sl-FreqInfoToAddModList in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration message; or if the frequency used for NR sidelink discovery is included in sl-FreqInfoList within SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":10482},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE is in RRC_CONNECTED and uses the frequency included in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration message:","paragraph_zero_based":10483},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is acting as NR sidelink U2N Relay UE and sl-DiscConfig is included in RRCReconfiguration, and if the NR sidelink U2N Relay UE threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.14.2 are met based on sl-RelayUE-Config; or","paragraph_zero_based":10484},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is selecting NR sidelink U2N Relay UE / has a selected NR sidelink U2N Relay UE/ configured with measurement object associated to L2 U2N Relay UEs and sl-DiscConfig is included in RRCReconfiguration, and if the NR sidelink U2N Remote UE threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.15.2 are met based on sl-RemoteUE-Config; or","paragraph_zero_based":10485},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is selecting NR sidelink U2U Relay UE / has a selected NR sidelink U2U Relay UE and sl-DiscConfig is included in RRCReconfiguration, and if the NR sidelink U2U Remote UE threshold conditions associated with the peer NR Sidelink U2U Remote UE as specified in 5.8.17.2 are met based on sl-RemoteUE-ConfigU2U; or","paragraph_zero_based":10486},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE acting as Target Remote UE is performing U2U Relay Discovery with Model B and sl-DiscConfig is included in RRCReconfiguration, and if the NR sidelink U2U Remote UE threshold conditions associated with the NR sidelink U2U Relay UE as specified in 5.8.17.2 are met based on sl-RemoteUE-ConfigU2U; or","paragraph_zero_based":10487}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["f76e9849a545577433dd3b227e938f9e40b203b8df976747ec913e5e215fef56","96fd9b31c6328855a8c6d755bcdfaf07ad5f3f4eb7007adf239f7f69d5187aa7","97aa5508d30b8495589db17d3dd87655bd1c9ba15cc36c7c7e549a4d9e8571c5","b039e2a5a6f295b52d3f07ccf1435d1c8e89933382f6a39a5de31f8e56b4bade","6a7dfaf71fbdd6a62f9dac0ff1820b45957870316f037cafe857e748db76f3ed","066a735b4f171b49a1396253d17fceae04a2c8ef156f1d105092a272c77c0da7","43488bd35a9fc81e2338096c07f1239fa79bb28c22f0e3b12aac88046f08f120","8afb2d0c087da02ef67b81828ed1e51ea5bca9e8ce821eb84c89e056a1a1f7d2","5a887d69a1bc0384f7650368904d5f1496330be92d6e4c48d68fa7c6abc8db22","f65cfb7c94b43a88326f3691130a9e99320ed3bdd9d36cd4b4524daf6bb900c1","4078e3201c47eb9274b998a5cfb2480784104808553b881efcb4a0dcf90c7f4c","ab81a82a08aaa4abf91a793d08457d8586c3cf7ca33c4295e8c1ed2719a55e9a","ea3b9049c92ca747f422c553dd354b73459251941e426c34dcca78cdefc7f27c","423f856f08f4deb81d943cfd568d1a1fb3eef87ab428f03f3a907e14ab2ab1aa","edf905914c474ca1f6eb8ffd6c5a76ebfe43ed7127d38658d69f4e8dd63cc1c4","ef8134a0b7f1f9a6f229ce41baf0e0e2998616c00865ebcb51dda07a400b6554","442043c1e57ce958f2337c8a736c1d16d1dda5544e245e8f1032f7576ebdcecb","26cbff770dd8e9d65f6888106917e30bf542d3e98841101309727353552e0010","f01b52c031787af625703f12ad42def3e460e8ba240e849d207299e9b628ce53","088da9eaf3fa904f9997187be4cceedcfc3a3fe01ce74e6f77fbc923092b68d5","47cee0981abb5403d547b189da90c58da7f3e004c88441405fdccde9091c288b","8f10942bc3d148dd9293468887b0444bb9807262bf2cedb4986fc47e0ef7e5b8","5a90e2321d369d58d2bc409bc153403c1165580b5c9f681324d8ae21bf2b7ac6","5022bdbb2620bf4521afd3c43df89dfed84d2c36e238fc3ef8b32b10bd2f3774"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10464,10487],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10464"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE acting as U2U Relay UE is performing U2U Relay Discovery with Model A as specified in TS 23.304[65], and neighbour UEs in discovery message to be transmitted meet the threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.16.3; or","paragraph_zero_based":10488},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3> if the UE acting as U2U Relay UE is sending Discovery Response message with Model B as specified in TS 23.304[65]; or","paragraph_zero_based":10489},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE acting as U2U Relay UE is sending Discovery Solicitation message with Model B as specified in TS 23.304[65] and sl-DiscConfig is included in RRCReconfiguration, and if the NR sidelink U2U Relay UE threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.16.2 are met based on sl-RelayUE-ConfigU2U; or","paragraph_zero_based":10490},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:For U2U Relay UE and Target Remote UE, it can be up to UE implementation on cross-layer interaction for the AS layer condition check for discovery message forwarding.","paragraph_zero_based":10491},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is performing NR sidelink non-relay discovery:","paragraph_zero_based":10492},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the UE is configured with sl-ScheduledConfig:","paragraph_zero_based":10493},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if T310 for MCG or T311 is running; and if sl-TxPoolExceptional is included in sl-FreqInfoList for the concerned frequency in SIB12 or included in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR in RRCReconfiguration; or","paragraph_zero_based":10494},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if T301 is running and the cell on which the UE initiated RRC connection re-establishment provides SIB12 including sl-TxPoolExceptional for the concerned frequency; or","paragraph_zero_based":10495},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if T304 for MCG is running and the UE is configured with sl-TxPoolExceptional included in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR for the concerned frequency in RRCReconfiguration:","paragraph_zero_based":10496},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation mode 2 based on random selection using the resource pool indicated by sl-TxPoolExceptional as defined in TS 38.321 [3] for NR sidelink discovery transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":10497},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10498},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation mode 1 using the resource pool indicated by sl-DiscTxPoolScheduling or sl-TxPoolScheduling for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency in RRCReconfiguration;","paragraph_zero_based":10499},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if T311 is running, configure the lower layers to release the resources indicated by rrc-ConfiguredSidelinkGrant (if any);","paragraph_zero_based":10500},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the UE is configured with sl-UE-SelectedConfig:","paragraph_zero_based":10501},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if the sl-DiscTxPoolSelected for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency is included in the sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration, and if a result of full/partial sensing, if selected and is allowed by sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig, on the resources configured in sl-DiscTxPoolSelected for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency included in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration is not available in accordance with TS 38.214 [19]; or","paragraph_zero_based":10502},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if the sl-DiscTxPoolSelected for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency is not included in the sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration, and a result of full/partial sensing, if selected and is allowed by sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig, on the resources configured in sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency included in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration is not available in accordance with TS 38.214 [19];","paragraph_zero_based":10503},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>if sl-TxPoolExceptional for the concerned frequency is included in RRCReconfiguration; or","paragraph_zero_based":10504},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>if the PCell provides SIB12 including sl-TxPoolExceptional in sl-FreqInfoList for the concerned frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":10505},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"7>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation mode 2 based on random selection using the resource pool indicated by sl-TxPoolExceptional as defined in TS 38.321 [3] for NR sidelink discovery transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":10506},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>else, if the sl-DiscTxPoolSelected for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency is included in the sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration:","paragraph_zero_based":10507},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation mode 2 based on resource selection operation according to sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig (as defined in TS 38.321 [3] and TS 38.214 [19]) using the pools of resources indicated by sl-DiscTxPoolSelected for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency in RRCReconfiguration;","paragraph_zero_based":10508},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>else, if the sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency is included in the sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration:","paragraph_zero_based":10509},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation mode 2 based on resource selection operation according to sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig (as defined in TS 38.321 [3] and TS 38.214 [19]) using the pools of resources indicated by sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency in RRCReconfiguration;","paragraph_zero_based":10510},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the cell chosen for NR sidelink discovery transmission provides SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":10511}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["5ea3b5324b33ecc53e82acb0e49c148b6a271727fd96d3921a3ad3beefa3e765","6ac33b5fdbc28955ddbf4a52094f62c62f8c3520e57d484999b991fc4ca853dc","0eed441102e66ff803f5724b9f141fd8534a97deff41ab9b09b7241bc47210a2","8cda544a364ca37e92cd9bb5d6c778148540606b29a52f544c4ba70167ee5487","a7c0f1d8b8690df064a975404774b928fd285f7cf4e54cf38ce7e19a2bc75934","da6c0820ab459c1986beb42a715a23a395a727dfff6f2182854de2dde4823d0d","ecdfdec724a886cd14c0dc5492ff18e73224fca6141a6ab6c72b46daa40d74eb","2132472542b2b9d5c9e3498bbe67e2d6182c6be33d96d24e8e6477f6381b39fe","02dd8bcd850f13bef0b775f0db76aedea721c2ecb8a3f086c7a1e9046d8e991c","83388cc1f67182ca7f3ec226580b7ec1e67f71cc0e2b07f9ecd59006e99af903","4a258581ae825db28139702ac9b3fa68ea43a97c602aa5e6638779fb8eadb67c","4aacc2fa029540fd887a7ddb31830ef036ab335914ed769a5af556b8510357ef","aedbaf675ce71ec6a8ddda595d42751af0412f91fae618cbbb881a11025ab348","7ab013c40b89803a7878bfd6cc79565e86e7b618f2ed4b5658063cde7d926661","37a8745e50a26e0f85705aecac4bbe77802d933d9683ef3336b609363c9ba2fb","1931afa9abc255a8126697a6574c82d365a4192eeafc1ce18a72aca81b19a53b","5a8b2672ad36ccbb076dc7fa35fe1ab560ec826ab4c1cfcb9a32409f0a43dc8b","3c08f1a61423e37c084c6721556ad8563d755a1f94cf57bcc458fe6030962ac3","18e4edf563d19460134872d1b0bee68310755e23ec5dcdad872948ac7d9cb341","39dfb9bf798607bb66d7326786621a46f93410eb45461424417d0e4a9e4f3827","fefae55e66d7245e743ca45a035b1de759ec08b830203c1b5bf884e6024ac616","81c092bf0297746dbf7d92c65e5d34d81630eda3c47c9a878f4c2bc81f390ce7","bfd35390a21e0f3b2d15bd6a7e1812d3395ba6bc855549399345726d64bc9092","5013b4567252d0d75718cea1e1f4ec08f8a5a821e1648a79f3d60c3bad82afe8"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10488,10511],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10488"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is acting as NR sidelink U2N Relay UE and sl-DiscConfigCommon is included in SIB12, and if the NR sidelink U2N Relay UE threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.14.2 are met based on sl-RelayUE-ConfigCommon in SIB12; or","paragraph_zero_based":10512},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is selecting NR sidelink U2N Relay UE / has a selected NR sidelink U2N Relay UE and sl-DiscConfigCommon is included in SIB12, and if the NR sidelink U2N Remote UE threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.15.2 are met based on sl-RemoteUE-ConfigCommon in SIB12; or","paragraph_zero_based":10513},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is selecting NR sidelink U2U Relay UE / has a selected NR sidelink U2U Relay UE and sl-DiscConfigCommon is included in SIB12, and if the NR sidelink U2U Remote UE threshold conditions associated with the peer NR Sidelink U2U Remote UE as specified in 5.8.17.2 are met based on sl-RemoteUE-ConfigCommonU2U in SIB12; or","paragraph_zero_based":10514},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE acting as Target Remote UE is performing U2U Relay Discovery with Model B and if the NR sidelink U2U Remote UE threshold conditions associated with the NR sidelink U2U Relay UE as specified in 5.8.17.2 are met based on sl-RemoteUE-ConfigCommonU2U in SIB12; or","paragraph_zero_based":10515},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE acting as U2U Relay UE is performing U2U Relay Discovery with Model A as specified in TS 23.304[65], and neighbor UEs in discovery message to be transmitted meet the threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.16.3; or","paragraph_zero_based":10516},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3> if the UE acting as U2U Relay UE is sending Discovery Response message with Model B as specified in TS 23.304[65]; or","paragraph_zero_based":10517},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE acting as U2U Relay UE is sending Discovery Solicitation message with Model B as specified in TS 23.304[65] and if the NR sidelink U2U Relay UE threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.16.2 are met based on sl-RelayUE-ConfigCommonU2U in SIB12; or","paragraph_zero_based":10518},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is performing NR sidelink non-relay discovery:","paragraph_zero_based":10519},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if SIB12 includes sl-DiscTxPoolSelected for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency, and a result of full/partial sensing, if selected and is allowed by sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig, on the resources configured in the sl-DiscTxPoolSelected for NR sidelink discovery transmission is available in accordance with TS 38.214 [19] or random selection, if allowed by sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig, is selected:","paragraph_zero_based":10520},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation mode 2 based on resource selection operation according to sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig using the pools of resources indicated by sl-DiscTxPoolSelected for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency in SIB12 as defined in TS 38.321 [3];","paragraph_zero_based":10521},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>else if SIB12 includes sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency, and a result of full/partial sensing, if selected and is allowed by sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig, on the resources configured in the sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for NR sidelink discovery transmission is available in accordance with TS 38.214 [19] or random selection, if allowed by sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig, is selected:","paragraph_zero_based":10522},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation mode 2 based on resource selection operation according to sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig using the pools of resources indicated by sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency in SIB12 as defined in TS 38.321 [3];","paragraph_zero_based":10523},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>else if SIB12 includes sl-TxPoolExceptional for the concerned frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":10524},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>from the moment the UE initiates RRC connection establishment or RRC connection resume, until receiving an RRCReconfiguration including sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, or receiving an RRCRelease or an RRCReject; or","paragraph_zero_based":10525},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if a result of full/partial sensing, if selected and is allowed by sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig, on the resources configured in sl-DiscTxPoolSelected for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency in SIB12 is not available in accordance with TS 38.214 [19]; or","paragraph_zero_based":10526},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if sl-DiscTxPoolSelected for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency is not included in SIB12 and if a result of full/partial sensing, if selected and is allowed by sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig, on the resources configured in sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency in SIB12 is not available in accordance with TS 38.214 [19]:","paragraph_zero_based":10527},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation mode 2 based on random selection (as defined in TS 38.321 [3]) using one of the pools of resources indicated by sl-TxPoolExceptional for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency;","paragraph_zero_based":10528},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else if out of coverage on the concerned frequency for NR sidelink discovery:","paragraph_zero_based":10529},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE is acting as L3 U2N Relay UE; or","paragraph_zero_based":10530},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE is selecting NR sidelink U2N Relay UE / has a selected NR sidelink U2N Relay UE and if the NR sidelink U2N Remote UE threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.15.2 are met based on sl-PreconfigDiscConfig in SidelinkPreconfigNR; or","paragraph_zero_based":10531},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE is selecting NR sidelink U2U Relay UE / has a selected NR sidelink U2U Relay UE and if the NR sidelink U2U Remote UE threshold conditions associated with the peer NR sidelink U2U Remote UE as specified in 5.8.17.2 are met based on sl-RemoteUE-PreconfigU2U in SidelinkPreconfigNR; or","paragraph_zero_based":10532},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE acting as Target Remote UE is performing U2U Relay Discovery with Model B and if the NR sidelink U2U Remote UE threshold conditions associated with the NR sidelink U2U Relay UE as specified in 5.8.17.2 are met based on sl-RemoteUE-PreconfigU2U in SidelinkPreconfigNR; or","paragraph_zero_based":10533},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE acting as U2U Relay UE is performing U2U Relay Discovery with Model A as specified in TS 23.304[65], and neighbor UEs in discovery message to be transmitted meet the threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.16.3; or","paragraph_zero_based":10534},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE acting as U2U Relay UE is sending Discovery Response message with Model B as specified in TS 23.304[65]; or","paragraph_zero_based":10535}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["085b4eed85ba281f245937779d88514bab182ad8ee9e1074af25ddf6186068bf","688cef8ba6dd1465ddc8a5b3568e21369787b9a5387ccaf5eaa48e86e0a73688","ba569ea33a17fa338d7607c23d4b723387036718ec970ce5fd54da28ac3aa0d1","6c0a77ab495c801b5fa416bdef5d030d933771d0597d4010a3dbe153549e5e68","1e5326b26688977e5704053d3336482555e5c02693d814bb04dd3f6f22127772","d2f6b577e5dfba1122f9b0501ba4b08ffef87812925a86d7965ca0a52122dbd2","5f43fe43e9304abc4bb58641e24b37ddfe13b4778e22b5305656ec3ce6544b58","66679d53b4719c232b09e2eb9d9f586975f438fccffe80503b7889303b0fa85c","093f7d1e4261cec01b836f1f0da5db0dab92e771a6a1453b505734b27538d7f2","9704045e3d0fa88d7923a4bea0709f33da0f62b943f1480b08d6c45353f2f8e9","7202b5986e852080d1f7c5eeace57be735000e9b8dedfd7f215e2e00ea69ecf4","a7c3dd40dea080e70f24b937337eaf3748d72af0faf2cda49e3017e4e857ddb9","ae1f6584aa527556f9f05123d9b302937ea4a1e61cfb3b13b48543842fbc7f78","654c3a77b0a9a3868e2aabb20126119e3fe484be48217d61ecd5c9807becd8dd","ea824ad2c9f2937ab476a0a327888b7bc5c8987ebec145c00e0e7a0efcb12501","a492a011440f88860cc958499969bc05480f129f81773473e1ccb289471cb134","2d8cb4de0baef8fdea340e3a2770eb234bfef1fcdf400de9011ba1323e7b0d82","fec8ed65661309be12186869105ac345421e98b2b3b25f2469181ba6302d3b9a","d3b37289d5befe60cdf4d584d0a077c410e7ddde0c11261a4f8c474ff7b42e54","6ce046c2181a7fea944678410207ccd45a64ebbb1e976f9b54ec9fcfcf5b494b","2ef3da2561adb08c1f39348d47cac5f813ad9d6770294cff5f15f7f5b1316244","a2981b9cfb0bb0787c2a499946d4f3ca9dd5948c66b79241fdf8d9fb1179cf2c","88e85cd0b0acf2948ec14a74ded992603e0a3c6b2fd7db61dbd3b6a797f602c9","daa9e23676f030643d3191614a6ad7ff5f922cad9b4f78d192ccfcf5cae9a88a"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10512,10535],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10512"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE acting as U2U Relay UE is sending Discovery Solicitation message with Model B as specified in TS 23.304[65] and if the NR sidelink U2U Relay UE threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.16.2 are met based on sl-RelayUE-PreconfigU2U in SidelinkPreconfigNR; or","paragraph_zero_based":10536},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE is performing NR sidelink non-relay discovery:","paragraph_zero_based":10537},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation mode 2 based on resource selection operation according to sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig (as defined in TS 38.321 [3] and TS 38.213 [13]) using the pools of resources indicated in sl-DiscTxPoolSelected or sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for NR sidelink discovery transmission on the concerned frequency in SidelinkPreconfigNR.","paragraph_zero_based":10538},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:It is up to UE implementation to determine, in accordance with TS 38.321[3], which resource pool to use if multiple resource pools are configured, and which resource allocation scheme is used in the AS based on UE capability (for a UE in RRC_IDLE/RRC_INACTIVE) and the allowed resource schemes sl-allowedResourceSelectionConfig in the resource pool configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":10539},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.14NR sidelink U2N Relay UE operation","paragraph_zero_based":10540},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.14.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10541},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This procedure is used by a UE supporting NR sidelink U2N Relay UE operation configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink discovery messages to evaluate AS layer conditions.","paragraph_zero_based":10542},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.14.2NR sidelink U2N Relay UE threshold conditions","paragraph_zero_based":10543},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink U2N Relay UE operation shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10544},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the threshold conditions specified in this clause were previously not met:","paragraph_zero_based":10545},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if threshHighRelay is not configured; or the RSRP measurement of the PCell, or the cell on which the UE camps, is below threshHighRelay by hystMaxRelay if configured; and","paragraph_zero_based":10546},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if threshLowRelay is not configured; or the RSRP measurement of the PCell, or the cell on which the UE camps, is above threshLowRelay by hystMinRelay if configured:","paragraph_zero_based":10547},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider the threshold conditions to be met (entry);","paragraph_zero_based":10548},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10549},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the RSRP measurement of the PCell, or the cell on which the UE camps, is above threshHighRelay if configured; or","paragraph_zero_based":10550},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the RSRP measurement of the PCell, or the cell on which the UE camps, is below threshLowRelay if configured;","paragraph_zero_based":10551},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider the threshold conditions not to be met (leave);","paragraph_zero_based":10552},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.15NR sidelink U2N Remote UE operation","paragraph_zero_based":10553},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.15.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10554},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This procedure is used by a UE supporting NR sidelink U2N Remote UE operation configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink discovery message to evaluate AS layer conditions. The procedure is also used to perform selection and reselection of NR sidelink U2N Relay UE.","paragraph_zero_based":10555},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.15.2NR Sidelink U2N Remote UE threshold conditions","paragraph_zero_based":10556},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink U2N Remote UE operation shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10557},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the threshold conditions specified in this clause were previously not met:","paragraph_zero_based":10558},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if threshHighRemote is not configured; or the RSRP measurement of the PCell, or the cell on which the UE camps, is below threshHighRemote by hystMaxRemote if configured, or","paragraph_zero_based":10559}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["4da308f2581be4b555d09bbafa04acfbf33ae82c002d4d4e16a16ad79e45b3ce","95c464ee3f3ebc50da1593cc9849b4fcc7f63a525c79252178fb1adfb78f2b78","fb6145587b9d7c74fb3208464a1e5319817bdfd8e42ec434bcc55f2a22ad218c","6f8e4e52b395c49d0a9c1be8b6728927d28f1e1a67fe680f3edc6a5e51d86379","ed6c4d36099746f9ca85bad3bb826af933e5fef3b417fdf04491b9f0b8aaa6af","34e16fb54a7f0920179f8970b4bd529e8941fe0667a236e4f24914e6339dc915","b17e98ad7c75885643e2dfd973fd1cafd3d80cd2cf395bce4974ea22c9cbd876","fcac65b9b579fa1f21804e18875ec96244202fc9f7fe8e1dd4b1c77cc4792ed6","abba541b5bd26df1dc1dadc622ace27e2f25c7f24fd9de8f7f043d5097b64aaf","ba18c189237d01feddac18c83692fc92d473658ea95598fcd61ab308f5126a27","ebcf4cd2a58c6c48dcbb7cf16b38b735f5f360ea482e082048e571c59552f314","69ae033dc5a8974a8beb5b61af11796ea200da4571c7591429e549f935b8b249","05e336752bff1e1f137565399ece5a29ba17b6817df4f62aec352ee1f3c6b631","1420166fc01e05e39f78c72950c4ea5c14b2387d23b8993680ae470728473c27","c2fbe5b735438828ac96355a7efd4f0ca125b0a2e2f0c8e901fffcf6bb4477c3","9c5c36b9ec31abc4ae78e263055937d804757017ce136e9ac439a5bb2506d75b","35f5ef5c87b9082d842159a61d42402c49f6a548bf1b2bde93cc11757574c27a","490d7cf2b80bf5eff49c023adcc30bacf6c34ebc948b8201619712c3291cb281","6275a8d9b41f76c779c43eecde1c1693bef0e4c659b5f8315316b1ad2313eb43","89006ea05c2aea783d91729b2befe2bfb5211b8d762128756e99769d40c334b9","8b6395f87391bff5e3b61b8b815f923feba5dbd9b6e31551b3dd7802b18ab18e","eabadb25c305ae75aefe111eb01d4f6cfc5b9d824b273e67e28ca1e8dfbe3f1a","0eb038edeba718a18139980e190dcf87d5d63db9809ea9fc4bac5fe89fb2eb0b","b78744ff8182e8a9064f87e29f8d9cc993b80a9101d2bb945d882f5af89aa64f"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10536,10559],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10536"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2> if the UE has no serving cell:","paragraph_zero_based":10560},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider the threshold conditions to be met (entry);","paragraph_zero_based":10561},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10562},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the RSRP measurement of the PCell, or the cell on which the UE camps, is above threshHighRemote if configured:","paragraph_zero_based":10563},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider the threshold conditions not to be met (leave);","paragraph_zero_based":10564},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The L2 U2N Remote UE not configured with MP considers the cell indicated by sl-ServingCellInfo in the SL-AccessInfo-L2U2N-r17 received from the connected L2 U2N Relay UE as the PCell/camping cell.","paragraph_zero_based":10565},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.15.3Selection and reselection of NR sidelink U2N Relay UE","paragraph_zero_based":10566},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink U2N Remote UE operation that is configured by upper layers to search for a NR sidelink U2N Relay UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10567},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE has no serving cell; or","paragraph_zero_based":10568},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RSRP measurement of the cell on which the UE camps (for L2 and L3 U2N Remote UE in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE)/ the PCell (for L3 U2N Remote UE in RRC_CONNECTED) is below threshHighRemote within sl-RemoteUE-Config:","paragraph_zero_based":10569},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE does not have a selected NR sidelink U2N Relay UE; or","paragraph_zero_based":10570},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE has a selected NR sidelink U2N Relay UE, and SL-RSRP of the currently selected NR sidelink U2N Relay UE is available and is below sl-RSRP-Thresh; or","paragraph_zero_based":10571},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE has a selected NR sidelink U2N Relay UE, and SL-RSRP of the currently selected NR sidelink U2N Relay UE is not available, and SD-RSRP of the currently selected U2N Relay UE is below sl-RSRP-Thresh; or","paragraph_zero_based":10572},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:U2N Remote UE uses SL-RSRP measurements for relay reselection trigger evaluation when there is data transmission from U2N Relay UE to U2N Remote UE, and it is left to UE implementation whether to use SL-RSRP or SD-RSRP for relay reselection trigger evaluation in case of no data transmission from U2N Relay UE to U2N Remote UE. If SD-RSRP is used, the discovery procedure will be performed between the U2N Remote UE and the selected U2N Relay UE.","paragraph_zero_based":10573},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE has a selected NR sidelink U2N Relay UE, and upper layers indicate not to use the currently selected NR sidelink U2N Relay UE; or","paragraph_zero_based":10574},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE has a selected NR sidelink U2N Relay UE, and upper layers request the release of the PC5-RRC connection; or","paragraph_zero_based":10575},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE has a selected NR sidelink U2N Relay UE, and sidelink radio link failure is detected on the PC5-RRC connection with the current U2N Relay UE as specified in clause 5.8.9.3:","paragraph_zero_based":10576},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform NR sidelink discovery procedure as specified in clause 5.8.13 in order to search for candidate NR sidelink U2N Relay UEs;","paragraph_zero_based":10577},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>when evaluating the one or more detected NR sidelink U2N Relay UEs, apply layer 3 filtering as specified in 5.5.3.2 across measurements that concern the same U2N Relay UE ID and using the sl-FilterCoefficientRSRP in SIB12 (if in RRC_IDLE/INACTIVE), the sl-FilterCoefficientRSRP in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR (if in RRC_CONNECTED) or the preconfigured sl-FilterCoefficientRSRP as defined in 9.3 (out of coverage), before using the SD-RSRP measurement results;","paragraph_zero_based":10578},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>consider a candidate NR sidelink U2N Relay UE for which SD-RSRP exceeds sl-RSRP-Thresh by sl-HystMin has met the AS criteria;","paragraph_zero_based":10579},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE detects any suitable NR sidelink U2N Relay UE(s):","paragraph_zero_based":10580},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>consider one of the available suitable NR sidelink U2N relay UE(s) can be selected;","paragraph_zero_based":10581},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:A candidate NR sidelink U2N Relay UE which meets all AS layer criteria defined in 5.8.15.3 and higher layer criteria defined in TS 23.304 [65] can be regarded as suitable NR sidelink U2N Relay UE by the NR sidelink U2N Remote UE. If multiple suitable NR sidelink U2N Relay UEs are available, it is up to Remote UE implementation to choose one NR sidelink U2N Relay UE. The details of the interaction with upper layers are up to UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":10582},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 3:For L2 U2N Remote UEs in RRC_IDLE/INACTIVE and L3 U2N Remote UEs, the cell (re)selection procedure and relay (re)selection procedure run independently. If both suitable cells and suitable NR sidelink U2N Relay UEs are available, it is up to NR sidelink U2N Remote UE implementation to select either a cell or a NR sidelink U2N Relay UE. Furthermore, L3 U2N Remote UE's selection on both cell and NR sidelink U2N Relay UE is also based on UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":10583}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["bf580b8cb8b808014b8558c7e796b1ea5ad847153cdc4347e87d672605c7eb58","3b2a78a3434aa7928c47289b3dfc183356cecb34a032cbd6d8f90a5f58e54312","cb712a5261494248aa91fe47478c1611b434f7a81be317387e6e3e428b5e860f","11e0947970e2fe30cf99ae95b187d53d3d0e31e5e233e4366b5775bf8a229a91","cf549d32a074a34e9a26c8e8d43431b80c050eecee73c628c845a2e86823d520","a283e13e79b151d54f338a35f86747937885f46d1e2408e142b91d63991bb424","49b23a134ac64392dc193b5f6bc2c85b127bc6a9d426390e40705f0ff34cded4","7787fd84b90d32ceed19f46cbdb604e329e034a634fddd40158803d5239e3465","ba12edb109f50cef99023843be24f779cb1bd44ddfffe4c8c0c9beea07017445","0e2ad1fe71fe077759e999ca7bdfbb095ad9611e449c16df77caa9369e633a85","85211db87c5ad3c447d07a0dd21b38227c5c24ba17516b4b88cc431d955cdddc","5b4f63bd324ecb7c2f81f9d66bfd3a05ef2a87e0181f6cfc5736ff3b3945e5cf","b4c9e1679d09ddc0f5bf244793652cbc7d4f968e2a833e418e53333fac2ccb52","606bf4f2b16d4aefa18314c54c4c8774e39b4cda9d8efb6f698e62eb48142236","660fffe7b0d0949a0690dae699fd65d67ba59248a1ef57ebac41152e3d667b06","3f0b40da43ac5b8952ba5778c0af8887fdf330431924f0a98cdf8df9f73b44d3","888c5ce331680736aff91b386afea59fb061714e7fc2a02845e1a71b8aa9a0f8","3ffbca6e7ace477c8965c7daeee0bf068a9ae39e60602fcda972ad03b78455ea","217542b97f059e55aa564ed1a32d01edfbdba510e306aa713e11ede21e25bb93","397c1bd99fe6e139cb3362d11440485e871dfda62de1f9aaf082153be7f32c90","008ea3a73831805ef6a3100cfa867158ab4ed4578b385cde8f7775c8d139af39","750461001214fef9cea8696d27615c2baa12caf7f3a89468f5c18272695880d4","1ed72d7e9c9bc72dba7fb4b99d173fa75cec956f03d0e443c5ca2661947f6695","4b2f2bd846e330494cb3c66ba2fb933dbc0a77afe599d070a9f864b515af981d"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10560,10583],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10560"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10584},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>consider no NR sidelink U2N Relay UE to be selected.","paragraph_zero_based":10585},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.16NR sidelink U2U Relay UE operation","paragraph_zero_based":10586},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.16.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10587},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This procedure is used by a UE supporting NR sidelink U2U Relay UE operation configured by upper layers to forward NR sidelink integrated discovery messages or Model B Discovery messages to evaluate AS layer conditions. The procedure is also used to determine whether a NR sidelink UE is in proximity to NR sidelink U2U Relay UE in Model A Discovery messages.","paragraph_zero_based":10588},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.16.2NR sidelink U2U Relay UE threshold conditions","paragraph_zero_based":10589},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink U2U Relay UE operation shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10590},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the threshold conditions for sending Direct Communication Request message with integrated Discovery specified in this clause were previously not met:","paragraph_zero_based":10591},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sd-RSRP-ThreshDiscConfig is not configured, or if the SL-RSRP of the Direct Communication Request message with integrated Discovery received from the Source NR sidelink U2U Remote UE is available and is above sd-RSRP-ThreshDiscConfig if configured:","paragraph_zero_based":10592},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider the threshold conditions to be met (entry);","paragraph_zero_based":10593},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10594},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the SL-RSRP of the Direct Communication Request message with integrated Discovery received from the Source NR sidelink U2U Remote UE is available and is below sd-RSRP-ThreshDiscConfig by sd-hystMaxRelay if configured:","paragraph_zero_based":10595},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider the threshold conditions not to be met (leave);","paragraph_zero_based":10596},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the threshold conditions for sending Relay Discovery Solicitation message with Model B Discovery specified in this clause were previously not met:","paragraph_zero_based":10597},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sd-RSRP-ThreshDiscConfig is not configured, or if the SD-RSRP of the Model B Discovery message received from the Source NR sidelink U2U Remote UE is available and is above sd-RSRP-ThreshDiscConfig if configured:","paragraph_zero_based":10598},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider the threshold conditions to be met (entry);","paragraph_zero_based":10599},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10600},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the SD-RSRP of the Model B Discovery message received from the Source NR sidelink U2U Remote UE is available and is below sd-RSRP-ThreshDiscConfig by sd-hystMaxRelay if configured:","paragraph_zero_based":10601},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider the threshold conditions not to be met (leave);","paragraph_zero_based":10602},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.16.3Neighbor UE(s) in proximity conditions","paragraph_zero_based":10603},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink U2U Relay UE operation and is performing U2U Relay Discovery with Model A as specified in TS 23.304[65] shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10604},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each of potential neighbor UE(s):","paragraph_zero_based":10605},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the SL-RSRP of the UE is available and is above sl-RSRP-Thresh-DiscConfig if configured; or","paragraph_zero_based":10606},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the SD-RSRP of the UE is available and is above sd-RSRP-ThreshDiscConfig if configured:","paragraph_zero_based":10607}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e4d63763f129e59badd906e9cf6553e5cae6181bf78e61fd03b7a7aad3043a13","acbc51757281d5351ba101026151e9071f19c1901712cccdd635fbed2da8ecc3","740d2f564849e9d3480b6a9f0ade38c36ccbe4ebbd2bda14a356dfa8650b4eed","5acd1208d6c977515d49f8cd16d90d3696af32e45fec22044786d95913731371","90446a2f1e769f33a845e8d892c6e84e56eaf5f803614e1ffb66e341e500bd65","80032f42dc3a14fae65d30874921dc598c77f926b451e81e01367ae7c7670e14","167ac74ee867d02c944a8a474e6a0c4337bd2ecff103b39367ad65dd10cfc6e6","99b988687abb77ad1b576d49f6ae504a3c8a9ccc707ae8a35872ccac96cb371f","5a0531e988d243814f8cb3e0489acb9e6a4e2eb58cca1065cb65677058f461b0","2fe1ef967648f8ee1c1fa18ac71836a87bba354f954f825d4865d26ad2d8dcae","ecca0c3389c0b1b933ce7ac081c39b2e1aca812cc8733fd9fe90b268fddad4a6","2a2c2f5e8824c787dd4769caae12a3344f5c5bd2dfb1c9287518e63561eba6a5","00743f6895f129634a4c22fa9cf8c081b3f2fe99a4a38b4f5ad117efb2e4b07b","38478ca9fc455da8a52201d9fc49b7651b3b88bbb23516a20c2462f52c5c7f84","61f582bbf7d24cb24a06584670b450ceaf14cd7a13a759eaf6b6353f1b7637e6","26a990c886161be05edda32a9090933796fd466022e097740bfc450e4e1fcbc2","19196056d18c49e68c67956697a76ad29a3b7d4627e7a2174bfac0d822aff83e","d070793463889c32ed305cc18af9c687e90c23750155a795c56b065468388e07","030338ac188ed9510786e6806874b0e6fdff8611823b32ec5c284cacdeb1e75d","32c3e7f1d5a3d268cbc396061df39517d4fbe59403016bdf44abc9ec1ca43d72","d9b3a4235f6c4b88f170711cda3dd7c39a53fb9504bf56b795ea1768aa3cd5fd","13103edfa32cc3eb6b69a687882fd14a37792af433ad82bb340a2fca29440ad1","39bcc6171365acc67fe928febd86b49ae9ff4bdbee35013cbe903d3d84e1ab44","1e4fc8015380f098196911b557bbf15d7eba8aa189981b107ec1333fe2ef2cd1"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10584,10607],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10584"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider the UE as neighbor UE in discovery message to be transmitted as defined in TS 23.304 [65].","paragraph_zero_based":10608},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE: The interaction with upper layers is left to UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":10609},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.17NR sidelink U2U Remote UE operation","paragraph_zero_based":10610},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.17.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10611},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This procedure is used by a UE supporting NR sidelink U2U Remote UE operation configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink discovery messages to evaluate AS layer conditions. The procedure is also used to perform selection and reselection of NR sidelink U2U Relay UE.","paragraph_zero_based":10612},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.17.2NR Sidelink U2U Remote UE threshold conditions","paragraph_zero_based":10613},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink U2U Remote UE operation shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10614},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the threshold conditions for sending Relay Discovery Solicitation message with Model B or sending Direct Communication Request message with integrated Discovery specified in this clause were previously not met:","paragraph_zero_based":10615},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the SL-RSRP measurement of the peer NR sidelink U2U Remote UE is to be used, and if sl-RSRP-ThreshU2U is not configured, or the SL-RSRP measurement of the peer NR sidelink U2U Remote UE is below sl-RSRP-ThreshU2U by sl-HystMinU2U if configured; or","paragraph_zero_based":10616},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the SD-RSRP measurement of the peer NR sidelink U2U Remote UE is to be used, and if sd-RSRP-ThreshU2U is not configured, or the SD-RSRP measurement of the peer NR sidelink U2U Remote UE is below sd-RSRP-ThreshU2U by sd-HystMinU2U if configured; or","paragraph_zero_based":10617},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the peer NR sidelink U2U Remote UE is not reachable, i.e. SL-RSRP/SD-RSRP measurement of the peer sidelink U2U Remote UE is not available:","paragraph_zero_based":10618},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider the threshold conditions to be met (entry);","paragraph_zero_based":10619},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10620},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the SL-RSRP measurement of the peer NR sidelink U2U Remote UE is available and is above sl-RSRP-ThreshU2U if configured; or","paragraph_zero_based":10621},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the SD-RSRP measurement of the peer NR sidelink U2U Remote UE is available and is above sd-RSRP-ThreshU2U if configured:","paragraph_zero_based":10622},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider the threshold conditions not to be met (leave);","paragraph_zero_based":10623},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the threshold conditions for sending Relay Discovery Response message with Model B specified in this clause were previously not met:","paragraph_zero_based":10624},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sd-RSRP-ThreshU2U is not configured, or if the SD-RSRP of the NR sidelink U2U Relay UE is available and is above sd-RSRP-ThreshU2U if configured:","paragraph_zero_based":10625},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider the threshold conditions to be met (entry);","paragraph_zero_based":10626},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10627},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the SD-RSRP of the NR sidelink U2U Relay UE is available and is below sd-RSRP-ThreshU2U by sd-HystMinU2U if configured:","paragraph_zero_based":10628},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider the threshold conditions not to be met (leave);","paragraph_zero_based":10629},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.17.3Conditions for selection and reselection of NR sidelink U2U Relay UE","paragraph_zero_based":10630},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink U2U Remote UE operation initiates NR sidelink U2U Relay (re)selection procedure as specified in 5.8.17.4 when one of the following conditions is met:","paragraph_zero_based":10631}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["b2b8d84ba8c3aef9ef73f6f4ad1d06f02cd400b6d48d394fe91a8d2f56430b62","4de2e825c52372592cec56d8c01e95510897732a7c91ee61a5ac8ebf4fb43604","4b0b0d61e70e408cd99ea75406f64441807ff2ac1984ea42149dcc78d82278f9","51bf00a58a44aed83fb2711cfcc4f865c37f9a0fd64305c448526655c65f8339","6b04607a5ca85adb4f0d25c719734e362cfaf090065c5a0aaf364d31eb0200e5","b3a18cdd5140cc94d70c124dcbedbcb9b564cfd48c5156d48eb71f952b8dbe2b","7fb2ff9a3b0e658e560b4a7d02b8eea6b3058584b7ee8af0f34ee2cbc5707ffa","ee74055d1b5d92069ba23c700dbcc0db0210733ed3a0312dcb37755ec9f41942","c8396ddd1912937b001bf997b1ad4b0fe426ca1c4e0e0a63f5d49c0d96a0d8b5","17c13411f9ba859c428b539cc712e358371d7520f3e585b216ff9f8245db277c","bc896eab8037e5a0050097a9f6f73ca5c6c6ba76212d088eb1d8957fdec8eae5","d12ad12a3d4647112507cb1329a0bd233b56ba5b52dfbc861063e4a43f65f3f3","c61329032de4e7d32d900502cc039f01f73165c5bd66d5d7c0eeb2c9aada578c","5b7fa3aede4f74cb53e8b43068190222e55b86087df519915f0eb4202d4f42ae","51dd284c3f7b4a46c44a5776dc1093eaee647e8882a0865489477a666dbbcf37","09ad02a5ad30a5b8397641cdffa99b921bcc8488fb595a7a1758feafe74f1c4b","d326e637ab3136e5e7e57e4b3aa8e59570b21470df54e6984244f2ed200ceacf","032a24acda9ef49874cf5fe9c8181b074f5235f1559ccda06e6e92f631a8dfb6","3845d7494b91909d542f0cd9616014a46dd9f4594c9bf843a61c35708e6f8fff","6c3c1818c421979051a9f490e30b46a6c54ab1da82fee1ab3ad13cac4a7a99ed","4159ef646801ae3e133069f4667d283daac3d4da0abbf837d5fb14f229262a5f","e8078e94feef979da72837e26a796f7cdc4590ec7d19c01ddffd9cdc7056724b","f8c80d6b75446ee19eeaee8f6bd349f28a56f56998f6bf04786d58c5a6218cc9","4c53ed14d6de897a608d027baf960780028c3535ac7cc0a0e163713f1f36e845"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10608,10631],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10608"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE does not have a selected NR sidelink U2U Relay UE:","paragraph_zero_based":10632},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if configured by upper layers to search for or select a NR sidelink U2U Relay UE; or","paragraph_zero_based":10633},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if sl-RSRP-ThreshU2U is not configured, or if the SL-RSRP measurement of the peer NR sidelink U2U Remote UE is available and is below sl-RSRP-ThreshU2U by sl-HystMinU2U if configured; or","paragraph_zero_based":10634},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if sd-RSRP-ThreshU2U is not configured, or if the SD-RSRP measurement of the peer NR sidelink U2U Remote UE is available and is below sd-RSRP-ThreshU2U by sd-HystMinU2U if configured;","paragraph_zero_based":10635},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else if the UE has a selected NR sidelink U2U Relay UE:","paragraph_zero_based":10636},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the SL-RSRP of the currently selected NR sidelink U2U Relay UE is available and is below sl-RSRP-ThreshU2U by sl-HystMinU2U within sl-RemoteUE-ConfigU2U if configured; or","paragraph_zero_based":10637},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the SD-RSRP of the currently selected NR sidelink U2U Relay UE is available, and is below sd-RSRP-ThreshU2U by sd-HystMinU2U within sl-RemoteUE-ConfigU2U if configured; or","paragraph_zero_based":10638},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:For relay selection, U2U Remote UE uses SL-RSRP measurements for relay selection trigger evaluation when there is data transmission from peer U2U Remote UE to U2U Remote UE. For relay reselection, U2U Remote UE uses SL-RSRP measurements for relay reselection trigger evaluation when there is data transmission from U2U Relay UE to U2U Remote UE. And in both cases, it is left to UE implementation whether to use SL-RSRP or SD-RSRP for relay (re)selection trigger evaluation in case of no data transmission.","paragraph_zero_based":10639},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the upper layers indicate to (re)select another NR sidelink U2U Relay UE; or","paragraph_zero_based":10640},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sidelink radio link failure is detected on the PC5-RRC connection with the current NR sidelink U2U Relay UE as specified in clause 5.8.9.3.","paragraph_zero_based":10641},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.17.4Actions related to selection and reselection of NR sidelink U2U Relay UE","paragraph_zero_based":10642},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon initiation of the NR sidelink U2U Relay (re)selection procedure, the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10643},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>perform NR sidelink discovery procedure as specified in clause 5.8.13 or U2U Relay Communication with integrated Discovery as specified in clause 5.8.8, in order to search for candidate NR sidelink U2U Relay UEs;","paragraph_zero_based":10644},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>when evaluating the one or more detected NR sidelink U2U Relay UEs, apply layer 3 filtering as specified in 5.5.3.2 across measurements that concern the same U2U Relay UE ID and using the sd-FilterCoefficientU2U in SIB12 (if in RRC_IDLE/INACTIVE), the sd-FilterCoefficientU2U in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR (if in RRC_CONNECTED) or the preconfigured sd-FilterCoefficientU2U as defined in 9.3 (out of coverage), before using the SD-RSRP measurement results;","paragraph_zero_based":10645},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>consider a candidate NR sidelink U2U Relay UE for which SD-RSRP exceeds sd-RSRP-ThreshU2U has met the AS criteria;","paragraph_zero_based":10646},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE detects any suitable NR sidelink U2U Relay UE(s):","paragraph_zero_based":10647},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>consider one of the available suitable NR sidelink U2U Relay UE(s) can be selected;","paragraph_zero_based":10648},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10649},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>consider no NR sidelink U2U Relay UE to be selected;","paragraph_zero_based":10650},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is performing U2U Relay Communication with integrated Discovery as specified in TS 23.304 [65] and has received Direct Communication Request message(s) from one or multiple NR sidelink U2U Relay UEs:","paragraph_zero_based":10651},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>when evaluating the NR sidelink U2U Relay UE(s), apply layer 3 filtering as specified in 5.5.3.2 across measurements that concern the same U2U Relay UE ID and using the sd-FilterCoefficientU2U in SIB12 (if in RRC_IDLE/INACTIVE), the sd-FilterCoefficientU2U in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR (if in RRC_CONNECTED) or the preconfigured sd-FilterCoefficientU2U as defined in 9.3 (out of coverage), before using the SD-RSRP measurement results;","paragraph_zero_based":10652},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>consider a candidate NR sidelink U2U Relay UE for which SL-RSRP exceeds sd-RSRP-ThreshU2U has met the AS criteria;","paragraph_zero_based":10653},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE detects any suitable NR sidelink U2U Relay UE(s):","paragraph_zero_based":10654},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider one of the available suitable NR sidelink U2U Relay UE(s) can be selected;","paragraph_zero_based":10655}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["d262d11fbfd9648a2a052481704a0d0c3c4be0bf21f364dc4f5fc118e9503f99","ae6257a73170b5e1d9f8d4f771dd8705de061c558894f5f27e311caa27a0f1f6","6856a940219db347858eaab1d08d496a02da34d3b7b726e2e6f9aed762149c6f","2b751f62ed172504e20fe49337deb5cdbb12a1201f7457919f0fb51b3d0310f9","6aa8fc619baaacf500dee24a34d0375a3753fe8efbeeea598dbbda6014a19e88","cec335f96d228450a91d70dd9b37b55cc74911e735b5bc375eb92892332f765b","d32b3ef9146492af61fcaa7523fa9097bb36add0ee58a4f67ece2035579329ec","47d3df616c0ff87d005e69b43176abc4c4c9b1acb19209fc178f4326eb3ca3a9","db7168bfcc18db538e7f110ef755a6b2b2cf5911f3fb4fa335768c8528b8fe3b","c11668d4f8ecaabea1161ad21b02f18845728f43c9dfc03eedfad67ce7d2e85b","0d14a971dd60b7ccb1b87a741bf4fed428875479de6a076c06ea97105a860470","20c041c651b199f7b2c0d29e3eb8ee9551c8a074886a199261115697430078c4","537d88765583ab7359e37177a5c0c9e92157c7778842bbe6b51b63432c2aa3a0","d041df9e8ca0b2acce02af0a270963b40451b3d493aad70479ab1e6b5d9b9133","601be0e48c776cc2727f0f140457555d7ea9a43c071449c2457b23e34eaac957","627f0390fd6cbe3354378092035b6314a8a295b9b7f54bc613a003d0b57a7c7e","54958a182fb5cc9bc489ee1b9eeb50dca7948b6b19de9a405a7d7de1e45adb30","95fcc7326c4e95f4e6683232441b17b7f2f2ad11f3ec3bf1d5244e66baf709c9","0159e099a208e8e64a29182ba583b31202655a11742984da22825dea43b9ce3a","1af6c438f84370edfc70217db78cd3367596fcdb096b7726d9b36b223e64b46f","e2b8bbcad3aba0f8a996acacc9cbfc79b17e352b699e763d01150f986e5e828c","16a358ddca1e2610a0180cb34838182bc782fc8e999fca25e2138df06ecc97b0","f40b7c1ac0b2f9af0660e888431ad81d8205141b695c6886780527430a49e3c0","7389f0b4c6a0e68534e549ba8e1205c3a66dd9ef678abc358185ca7c6cc58cce"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10632,10655],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10632"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10656},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider no NR sidelink U2U Relay UE to be selected.","paragraph_zero_based":10657},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:A candidate NR sidelink U2U Relay UE which meets all AS layer criteria defined in 5.8.17.4 and higher layer criteria defined in TS 23.304 [65] can be regarded as suitable NR sidelink U2U Relay UE by the NR sidelink U2U Remote UE. If multiple suitable NR sidelink U2U Relay UEs are available, it is up to Remote UE implementation to choose one NR sidelink U2U Relay UE. The details of the interaction with upper layers are up to UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":10658},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.18NR sidelink positioning","paragraph_zero_based":10659},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.18.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10660},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The purpose of this procedure is to perform NR sidelink positioning as specified in TS 38.305 [73].","paragraph_zero_based":10661},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.18.2NR sidelink positioning measurement","paragraph_zero_based":10662},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink positioning that is configured by upper layers for performing SL-PRS measurement:","paragraph_zero_based":10663},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the conditions for NR sidelink positioning operation as defined in 5.8.2 are met:","paragraph_zero_based":10664},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the frequency used for NR sidelink positioning is included in sl-FreqInfoToAddModList in RRCReconfiguration message or sl-FreqInfoList included in SIB12 or SIB23:","paragraph_zero_based":10665},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is configured with sl-RxPool and/or sl-PRS-RxPool included in RRCReconfiguration message with reconfigurationWithSync (i.e. handover):","paragraph_zero_based":10666},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>configure lower layers to monitor sidelink control information and the corresponding SL-PRS using the pool(s) of resources indicated by sl-RxPool and/or sl-PRS-RxPool;","paragraph_zero_based":10667},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else if the cell chosen for NR sidelink positioning provides SIB12 or SIB23:","paragraph_zero_based":10668},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>configure lower layers to monitor sidelink control information and the corresponding SL-PRS using the pool(s) of resources indicated by sl-RxPool in SIB12 and/or sl-PRS-RxPool in SIB23;","paragraph_zero_based":10669},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10670},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>configure lower layers to monitor sidelink control information and the corresponding SL-PRS using the pool(s) of resources that were preconfigured by sl-RxPool and/or sl-PRS-RxPool in SL-PreconfigurationNR, as defined in clause 9.3.","paragraph_zero_based":10671},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.18.3NR sidelink positioning transmission","paragraph_zero_based":10672},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink positioning that is configured by upper layers to transmit SL-PRS shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10673},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the conditions for NR sidelink positioning operation as defined in 5.8.2 are met:","paragraph_zero_based":10674},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the frequency used for NR sidelink positioning is included in sl-FreqInfoToAddModList in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration message or included in sl-PosConfigCommonNR within SIB23:","paragraph_zero_based":10675},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is in RRC_CONNECTED and uses the frequency included in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration message:","paragraph_zero_based":10676},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the UE is configured with sl-ScheduledConfig:","paragraph_zero_based":10677},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if T310 for MCG or T311 is running; and if sl-PRS-TxPoolExceptional or sl-TxPoolExceptional is included in sl-FreqInfoList for the concerned frequency in SIB23 or SIB12 or included in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR in RRCReconfiguration; or","paragraph_zero_based":10678},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if T301 is running and the cell on which the UE initiated RRC connection re-establishment provides SIB23 or SIB12 including sl-PRS-TxPoolExceptional or sl-TxPoolExceptional for the concerned frequency; or","paragraph_zero_based":10679}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["39246dcda03060f803c89b8602309dae59551d35be11dc004971bc9e32e21bc9","de3a17c4dd03f01d8072d900c9a1333d200f03addb68036e654973da77d80e68","ae54ad9bca3895d8c4d68d98971b15239de060c06e6d372ecb5142cd5378371e","8ebff79ebff8471afb3d79a705d3177848736a06d52a2cd05c9872168e7472e7","dbc73b4c43bb9f10e56902d5aa40b3649d286a484b270ce4bd4f8b89b8fa791e","86aebd6475cd60dc16cbde0092937894617b4a3efa4409a244a7a17081ea0669","e208120ed1a78fc3e6909da7effcd9da564b5e16a41228e5a9bd856baaab4799","7cbbb28dec66000c94384033551c272770e72299550298aceaa612bc6000584e","af43309eb03ac80b6087120908cf704d3d94b1756bc0798cf87905bc2a4caf88","2ba1442cf093b951bd32b56bca8ea5891c08c0fb1f16e11614965eb2820d423b","afe69a1db0814142718968161a859547bb11950e1ed8b1f07aaacfe1045158a7","6a4bb88825f7b388801507cee04f015e2d8b4c4267c133fc7ced3a09e84b5466","60f1145184401e06ed440a6cbf6bacf5b9699a0ca5a7647cec5386bb7eb617b3","658d57cde899eabde117b81252ed249c65b007078d09902719a15b6da7b283f4","2559f2d5474f10f35ddf6d74d178de4790d2bdb9f51bee3aaf4511b42bf4b1f4","53ff2fe197f2974dcbd24a3ad9d4792e622ab6181e66ec4972bb5ccc44b1dd98","000388e5af3413410ffce3d5d70782b80c670640e72a8b89f9770c90cb6155b4","a2dd86108befa3bb8a2abe884c0f9de57c62d03b3d4512ba4c7eb2678e5a4256","a6dad1f54219d9b1387b19ba56b437e34f83b2000f90e04f7f555951707b36d3","6dc9187c741a544a86c55432ce1464be1660d29e3f119519fecf74e080c4045c","4dcb70f3c5a8a6614d4d19526a9a31cb73546bb6c34bd39eba721e763f2681ea","8aa6bb5be694270730c345ca537f36c8cfb78c01519f31c284e64c6b170749ee","92727b879aab72094cecc01d2f6d87f24500106a34ba9415e433f7e2afe043b0","9048c8ad62b07030d108072a4eb38ef06f5cac9b9c57e83b2c3198644240618e"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10656,10679],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10656"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if T304 for MCG is running and the UE is configured with sl-PRS-TxPoolExceptional or sl-TxPoolExceptional included in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR for the concerned frequency in RRCReconfiguration:","paragraph_zero_based":10680},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation scheme 2 based on random selection using the resource pool indicated by sl-PRS-TxPoolExceptional or sl-TxPoolExceptional as defined in TS 38.321 [3];","paragraph_zero_based":10681},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10682},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation scheme 1 for NR sidelink positioning;","paragraph_zero_based":10683},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if T311 is running, configure the lower layers to release the resources indicated by rrc-ConfiguredSidelinkGrant (if any);","paragraph_zero_based":10684},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the UE is configured with sl-UE-SelectedConfig:","paragraph_zero_based":10685},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if a result of full sensing, if selected and is allowed by sl-PosAllowedResourceSelectionConfig, on the resources configured in sl-PRS-TxPoolSelectedNormal or by sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig, on the resources configured in sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency included in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration is not available in accordance with TS 38.214 [19];","paragraph_zero_based":10686},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>if sl-TxPoolExceptional or sl-PRS-TxPoolExceptional for the concerned frequency is included in RRCReconfiguration; or","paragraph_zero_based":10687},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>if the PCell provides SIB25 including sl-TxPoolExceptional or sl-PRS-TxPoolExceptional in sl-FreqInfoList for the concerned frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":10688},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"7>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation scheme 2 based on random selection using the pool of resources indicated by sl-TxPoolExceptional or sl-PRS-TxPoolExceptional as defined in TS 38.321 [3];","paragraph_zero_based":10689},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>else, if the sl-PRS-TxPoolSelectedNormal or sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency is included in the sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration:","paragraph_zero_based":10690},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation scheme 2 based on resource selection operation according to sl-PosAllowedResourceSelectionConfig (as defined in TS 38.321 [3] and TS 38.214 [19]) using the pools of resources indicated by sl-PRS-TxPoolSelectedNormalNormal for the concerned frequency, or based on resource selection operation according to sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig (as defined in TS 38.321 [3] and TS 38.214 [19]) using the pools of resources indicated by sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency;","paragraph_zero_based":10691},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10692},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the cell chosen for NR sidelink positioning transmission provides SIB23 or SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":10693},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if SIB23 includes PRS-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency, and a result of full sensing, if selected and is allowed by sl-PosAllowedResourceSelectionConfig, on the resources configured in the sl-PRS-TxPoolSelectedNormal is available in accordance with TS 38.214 [19] or random selection, if allowed by sl-PosAllowedResourceSelectionConfig, is selected:","paragraph_zero_based":10694},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation scheme 2 based on resource selection operation according to sl-PosAllowedResourceSelectionConfig using the pools of resources indicated by sl-PosTxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency as defined in TS 38.321 [3];","paragraph_zero_based":10695},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if SIB12 includes sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency, and a result of full sensing, if selected and is allowed by sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig, on the resources configured in the sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal is available in accordance with TS 38.214 [19] or random selection, if allowed by sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig, is selected:","paragraph_zero_based":10696},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation scheme 2 based on resource selection operation according to sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig using the pools of resources indicated by sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency as defined in TS 38.321 [3];","paragraph_zero_based":10697},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>else if SIB23 includes sl-PRS-TxPoolExceptional or SIB12 includes sl-TxPoolExceptional for the concerned frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":10698},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>from the moment the UE initiates RRC connection establishment or RRC connection resume, until receiving an RRCReconfiguration including sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, or receiving an RRCRelease or an RRCReject; or","paragraph_zero_based":10699},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>if a result of full sensing, if selected and is allowed by sl-PosAllowedResourceSelectionConfig, on the resources configured in sl-PRS-TxPoolSelectedNormal or if selected and is allowed by sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig, on the resources configured in sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency in SIB12/SIB23 is not available in accordance with TS 38.214 [19]:","paragraph_zero_based":10700},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"7>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation scheme 2 based on random selection (as defined in TS 38.321 [3]) using the pool of resources indicated by sl-PRS-TxPoolExceptional or sl-TxPoolExceptional for the concerned frequency;","paragraph_zero_based":10701},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10702},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation scheme 2 based on resource selection operation according to sl-PosAllowedResourceSelectionConfig (as defined in TS 38.321 [3] and TS 38.214 [19]) using the pools of resources indicated by sl-PRS-TxPoolSelectedNormal or sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal in SL-PreconfigurationNR for the concerned frequency.","paragraph_zero_based":10703}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["1a86d739b236a50b01d3aa6666a79c3707fdd48a73a5c41f78273106c3ad28ae","cdc602ecc4b292bf6becb24e2952004592c1b886cfbcae8768de36e58cd1fe1c","b27396f2ca72a376e4ab7c464ff290e92182b5f65d6a29f731d40ff2bb08836d","668a1ecbc1cb14d33d4c0cc409f073dd09f42fe9f262f94c081998e6d0aca95f","3ce591168e9c3ea2efc91037e7d1ebcfebc22302a9f269b2ab81d79997845854","1a67a921c9c1ccb5d42e48b95870e69472ab3d0175aa9448d8f8446c0126b31c","0a8bd010cc8745b785acb923013565bddf141b7ac694781d140140ecf09ac680","c8e86f1ab21b4bf9bd3e28c4e9e6a4d6eed5a28d831994a034a30bf82ceda00d","7cd7d1cc56c8e563ab50ea892add9700d5228fd15bdc72398f327bc9fd048ac1","7c1d54250f1a508ad572cc6306d9c06528a59fee74b58460d43d2580dca19421","a60c6723c5a185939e30ad374f6f4cc9da2a35118cc5f0d228c9bd3a42eb4605","44cd264e1980638e8ef64c8a901d5ba3e4cada4b33a0dfe957e88d14f5133fde","4de54fa25654beaf50795ffbf60f5fe3387c126a6b4d4973981f35c38803735e","1e3584feeae10db2528103fb9cb723fb5090f96b21d4a0f6566f08e02e469f8a","cbc49b8825e17ab8edeee3ca440fcdf0727e2366d2515548af8b1da71d8078f1","512ad6351b22bf970711ffa95673f80bdaf30873f2ead5f93acaa3da2cbbcd4a","55865f4289d70b5d979bd7d5dd875433076da8566c6ef49a6b85165fd9e4afb1","0e81f60d9be392f107af574d11d80c2af106b14c533fe1af1840e5bf6cae178d","ed29733450e316d516b06d48d2a11ad1cbea26a12268114ff41484bdffae9cac","d796116b2cb2c90beb3be12056dcc6a7058f841fbf8548730ffd617623e4a380","0431b42eeec3e988208aa241fe7fda3637f337663fcf05c1305d4c118df1987d","a8f5426921476c2da4ca0ffb449bb2ec8c0f6b6b531592b1ccc2b4e300283346","7035e7bb7f85ab40a70ae9fd309aae9a708c63fc4fe041b7851bdfee367770a2","417f79878206591443275b92bfd684ab2945a8b98a6db4478723d0f98e13a7b4"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10680,10703],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10680"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:The same Notes except NOTE 4 as in clause 5.8.8 are applicable for this clause unless otherwise stated.","paragraph_zero_based":10704},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9MBS Broadcast","paragraph_zero_based":10705},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.1Introduction","paragraph_zero_based":10706},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.1.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10707},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UE receiving or interested to receive MBS broadcast service(s) applies MBS broadcast procedures described in this clause as well as the MBS Interest Indication procedure as specified in clause 5.9.4.","paragraph_zero_based":10708},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MBS broadcast configuration information, except CFR configuration for MCCH/MTCH, is provided on MCCH logical channel. MCCH carries the MBSBroadcastConfiguration message which indicates the MBS broadcast sessions that are provided in the cell as well as the corresponding scheduling related information for these sessions. Optionally, the MBSBroadcastConfiguration message may also contain a list of neighbour cells providing the same broadcast MBS service(s) as provided in the current cell. The configuration information required by the UE to receive MCCH is provided in SIB1 and SIB20. Additionally, System Information may provide information related to service continuity of MBS broadcast in SIB21.","paragraph_zero_based":10709},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.1.2MCCH scheduling","paragraph_zero_based":10710},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The MCCH information (i.e. information transmitted in messages sent over MCCH) is transmitted periodically, using a configurable repetition period and within a configured transmission window. MCCH transmissions (and the associated radio resources and MCS) are indicated via the PDCCH addressed to MCCH-RNTI. PDCCH monitoring occasion(s) for MCCH transmission are determined according to the common search space indicated by searchspaceMCCH. If searchspaceMCCH is set to zero, PDCCH monitoring occasions for MCCH message reception in the MCCH transmission window are the same as PDCCH monitoring occasions for SIB1 where the mapping between PDCCH monitoring occasions and SSBs is specified in TS 38.213[13]. If searchspaceMCCH is not set to zero, PDCCH monitoring occasions for MCCH message are determined based on search space indicated by searchspaceMCCH. PDCCH monitoring occasions for MCCH message which are not overlapping with UL symbols (determined according to tdd-UL-DL-ConfigurationCommon) are sequentially numbered from one in the MCCH transmission window. The [x×N+K]th PDCCH monitoring occasion for MCCH message in MCCH transmission window corresponds to the Kth transmitted SSB, where x = 0, 1, ...X-1, K = 1, 2, …N, N is the number of actual transmitted SSBs determined according to ssb-PositionsInBurst in SIB1 and X is equal to CEIL(number of PDCCH monitoring occasions in MCCH transmission window/N). The actual transmitted SSBs are sequentially numbered from one in ascending order of their SSB indexes. The UE assumes that, in the MCCH transmission window, PDCCH for an MCCH message is transmitted in at least one PDCCH monitoring occasion corresponding to each transmitted SSB and thus the selection of SSB for the reception MCCH messages is up to UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":10711},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.1.3MCCH information validity and notification of changes","paragraph_zero_based":10712},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Change of MCCH information only occurs at specific radio frames, i.e. the concept of a modification period is used. Within a modification period, the same MCCH information may be transmitted a number of times, as defined by its scheduling (which is based on a repetition period).","paragraph_zero_based":10713},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When the network changes (some of) the MCCH information, it notifies the UEs about the change starting from the beginning of the MCCH modification period via PDCCH which schedules the MCCH in every repetition in that modification period.","paragraph_zero_based":10714},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon receiving a change notification, a UE receiving or interested to receive MBS services transmitted using MBS broadcast acquires the new MCCH information starting from the same slot. The UE applies the previously acquired MCCH information until the UE acquires the new MCCH information. The notification is transmitted with a 2-bit bitmap, see TS 38.212 [17] clause 7.3.1.5.1. The MSB in the 2-bit bitmap, when set to '1', indicates the start of new MBS service(s). The LSB in the 2-bit bitmap, when set to '1', indicates modification of MCCH information other than the change caused by start of new MBS service(s), e.g. modification of a configuration of an on-going MBS session(s), MBS session(s) stop or neighbouring cell information modification.","paragraph_zero_based":10715},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.2MCCH information acquisition","paragraph_zero_based":10716},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.2.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10717},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":10718},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.9.2.1-1: MCCH information acquisition","paragraph_zero_based":10719},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE applies the MCCH information acquisition procedure to acquire the MBS broadcast configuration information broadcasted by the network. The procedure applies to MBS capable UEs interested to receive or that are receiving MBS broadcast services that are in RRC_IDLE, RRC_INACTIVE or RRC_CONNECTED with an active BWP with common search space configured by searchSpaceMCCH.","paragraph_zero_based":10720},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.2.2Initiation","paragraph_zero_based":10721},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE shall apply the MCCH information acquisition procedure upon becoming interested to receive MBS broadcast services. A UE interested to receive MBS broadcast services shall apply the MCCH information acquisition procedure upon entering the cell providing SIB20 (e.g. upon power on, following UE mobility), upon receiving SIB20 of an SCell via dedicated signalling and upon receiving a notification that the MCCH information has changed due to the start of new MBS service(s). A UE that is receiving data via broadcast MRB shall apply the MCCH information acquisition procedure upon receiving a notification that the MCCH information has changed due to MCCH information modification other than the change caused by the start of new MBS service(s).","paragraph_zero_based":10722},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:It is up to UE implementation how to address a possibility of the UE missing an MCCH change notification.","paragraph_zero_based":10723},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:It is up to UE implementation to use the cell/tracking area list in the USD to avoid acquiring the MCCH when the UE is outside the MBS service area of the MBS broadcast service.","paragraph_zero_based":10724},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Unless explicitly stated otherwise in the procedural specification, the MCCH information acquisition procedure overwrites any stored MCCH information, i.e. delta configuration is not applicable for MCCH information and the UE discontinues using a field if it is absent in MCCH information.","paragraph_zero_based":10725},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.2.3MCCH information acquisition by the UE","paragraph_zero_based":10726},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"An MBS capable UE interested to receive or receiving an MBS broadcast service shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10727}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["410753a82ca61468de43c2597ae9d046c640b2e35bbdc9ed4d3619a7c97928b6","35a55c454234b0e6533638b46c5defa0ae64a8f001a8167cfafa26acb4fe7f0f","855a26354190a3b81d19f654e6cef6a5a4440a572ac86591a83dd5d4a51733c4","43f00b19ea0e0c49f16bcb817592b4fdcf5666a7430d6ad3519c9bf70e9b9008","5888069ce71bcdd95dcee989a9ff61906702035e72cdfd9518a5ef54e74ec5bf","88d5d2de1ee827edbedb9472f82acf8945cb6a8640f21be3a8e541aadc2eaa2e","7564a19fa95bbcc8c55c377cf87592182346f97fc9b7c936812d90c9d8585459","8572b4b3756fb4cb7cfa2f8b503fd59746aaebe1f5e19727e5fe707aebec56e7","b6e31043d9826821bc3be9f1c0056c5569f40e82c1157cf15917158dda750a60","3432278ac6d5d929a71c590958a6561b5e6a4214c6961d2ea34c90d7dc7d027f","8a5bc880785e9ddcddf355d9fe98239cff1a75171dbbe99a67de980a6ed9170b","cc56d757f04583691969fd493be32de87083afde2fef514ac50125b2d3cbb038","41c43b4639996bd1aabe480566f64e862403d94c5cc78ef9d0035f498aeaa759","c61c5e83866133f5e5d6cf34b77a36a0d0d4093a387f6c8e5a328f325899455f","6b2c49f31ee35bd49a396836045074b6ea68d33567e5e36d8fd747c0545f4059","468fcf1fd08ec4cf60abff53aaed0ef7c6501745fbffd7bf973d994e944000e3","fe5e42ea27d65e616235d6eb4eb7f510233551191b36286eb613d527262836c3","903c20cc6b26fdfe94db74f09cce355b694cd5d20226899f99e4455d09453917","515dd393ec4dff2296feb4cad945b8bd86e56ab512cb7b0e24f15ad6dcc9ca43","a44aa220bded9d643ac9830a0982ce5af8647327612dc61f7c6d2b69963d99e0","f06d5e8b3fd06f11727c49634387c31486747d7b6e00141439dae340a77a4a65","2647914a98e29d0b0cc91c29cc9a55ded3c7bdfb2f19578075bdc330e9ee8211","6d5599443a4b52aab470a3e58925dc1bc9884d216c2a56045979e2997ab2e6a3","48a6e58fe0124bf7e1f3f3a000da42305d0d69e317f3fc1a9a55cfb1ad32251d"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10704,10727],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10704"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the procedure is triggered by an MCCH information change notification:","paragraph_zero_based":10728},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>start acquiring the MBSBroadcastConfiguration message on MCCH in the concerned cell from the slot in which the change notification was received;","paragraph_zero_based":10729},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE enters a cell providing SIB20; or","paragraph_zero_based":10730},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE receives sCellSIB20:","paragraph_zero_based":10731},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>acquire the MBSBroadcastConfiguration message on MCCH in the concerned cell at the next repetition period.","paragraph_zero_based":10732},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.2.4Actions upon reception of the MBSBroadcastConfiguration message","paragraph_zero_based":10733},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"No UE requirements related to the contents of the MBSBroadcastConfiguration message apply other than those specified elsewhere e.g. within the corresponding field descriptions.","paragraph_zero_based":10734},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.3Broadcast MRB configuration","paragraph_zero_based":10735},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.3.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10736},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The broadcast MRB configuration procedure is used by the UE to configure PDCP, RLC, MAC and the physical layer upon starting and/or stopping to receive a broadcast MRB transmitted on MTCH, or upon modification of a configuration of a broadcast MRB received by the UE. The procedure applies to MBS capable UEs that are interested to receive or that are receiving an MBS broadcast service that are in RRC_IDLE, RRC_INACTIVE or RRC_CONNECTED with an active BWP with common search space configured by searchSpaceMTCH or searchSpaceMCCH.","paragraph_zero_based":10737},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:How to perform a modification of a broadcast MRB which is already configured in the UE is left to UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":10738},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.3.2Initiation","paragraph_zero_based":10739},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE applies the broadcast MRB establishment procedure to start receiving an MBS session of an MBS broadcast service it is interested in. The procedure may be initiated e.g. upon start of the MBS session, upon entering a cell providing an MBS broadcast service the UE is interested in, upon becoming interested in the ongoing MBS broadcast service, upon removal of the UE capability limitations inhibiting reception of the ongoing MBS broadcast service UE is interested in.","paragraph_zero_based":10740},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE applies the broadcast MRB release procedure to stop receiving a session of an MBS broadcast service. The procedure may be initiated e.g. upon stop of the MBS session, upon leaving the cell broadcasting the MBS service the UE is interested in, upon losing interest in the MBS service, when capability limitations start inhibiting reception of the concerned service.","paragraph_zero_based":10741},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.3.3Broadcast MRB establishment","paragraph_zero_based":10742},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon a broadcast MRB establishment, the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10743},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>establish a PDCP entity and an RLC entity in accordance with MRB-InfoBroadcast for this broadcast MRB included in the MBSBroadcastConfiguration message and the configuration specified in 9.1.1.7;","paragraph_zero_based":10744},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>configure the MAC layer in accordance with the mtch-SchedulingInfo (if included);","paragraph_zero_based":10745},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>configure the physical layer in accordance with the mbs-SessionInfoList, searchSpaceMTCH, and pdsch-ConfigMTCH, applicable for the broadcast MRB;","paragraph_zero_based":10746},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if an SDAP entity with the received mbs-SessionId does not exist:","paragraph_zero_based":10747},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>establish an SDAP entity as specified in TS 37.324 [24] clause 5.1.1;","paragraph_zero_based":10748},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>indicate the establishment of the user plane resources for the mbs-SessionId to upper layers;","paragraph_zero_based":10749},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>receive DL-SCH on the cell where the MBSBroadcastConfiguration message was received for the established broadcast MRB using g-RNTI and mtch-SchedulingInfo (if included) in this message for this MBS broadcast service.","paragraph_zero_based":10750},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.3.4Broadcast MRB release","paragraph_zero_based":10751}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["8779fb7252b7dcf53e27224599b694c7b3cbff1bb5d9b6b566dfd24b6a6fd03a","ee1b2320de4a1aa8b6b88afb88155aec0b0e22af5b40edb9b1820d659a83ac8e","f741a2936016f03915596dd1fe323ae8a907f83f728213828c7b686556196a07","f89503c63ea861d8425fbbe52601368152cd75639703850a2b69e96150b12345","68d6c5e46867b872df37af7c5ff85970216e80eddc400b86fb85843d943897e1","b19a8eacb4f991e4bf875b502cbaee426c3dd6557d126a72e647f1b4b69c4fd7","945bc80321fb114a0d268a51f3d7e49c003f817c458c86c977ea1d26faa3d013","38973006c888d83bf401398c4c48b1f054cf1d673c5884bb166f4a33f05c72b6","c48214daf09570a254ac496e2ff7b1477ea77473a777bbd03c2ebb64f5619a9d","a771de5a59effe39634dce2a892b79dbd7ab7392741b2ae6022d5250c3f8cbf5","be5acdb28e1ca54f4c89342cab76ec6372810bca74b7b5b75a646ddb0cec4fa4","2ab2f81ccdb51f4b565fd30bdc80f0a3c6dab1b1775cd9b1df4e533332f17bbd","bed58893bd8e57ff4a2da368a4d044083867f1b952c951ca18c39242c07ce852","c6d8dd0920306d2ecb8d2546fa3687baf1ff76a1541b9f1f974c779b92f08a4a","4e76b8430ff0ae905b0a71b431071bc7da2fe6c8dcfd9f59a522b48ed17655c7","5a85a177a12af4263bbc8ceb9b970a0fddc8c167918a04102a843c51ee48989c","7d78a5af9b3d57571e8e6276980267bdcf397a6f300657a1e23e3d01f267c43e","a94ee905ca1ae633a59c08c6821d1db509d9f93b34a0018fe02b8fa10996b48c","7ee305d274514e803c81e4efeda584b98e0fbbd46803bfb7e5f7e5ce9f0d60d9","2b9727f716447d5ea3ecc3e8d0c5c354018e29070b383b86d523b9b271d25860","3bc09f3eb0375f5781010976bbf3209a6ac47d6ed457cc0bc0674ee73555ee0c","b9bed9be6143e728953125a6be77e1cd87a23ecb0eea4c172da2a862ed8d0463","a4ef2c116c52dcffed84d5c20868c035294ba62a8e324f6b845a9f6771c6ff02","b8484ac74c95011cdd0db788f3ab0d00769af9ac3bddfeb008905949d7b06038"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10728,10751],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10728"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon broadcast MRB release for MBS broadcast service, the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10752},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release the PDCP entity, RLC entity as well as the related MAC and physical layer configuration;","paragraph_zero_based":10753},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the SDAP entity associated with the corresponding mbs-SessionId has no associated MRB:","paragraph_zero_based":10754},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the SDAP entity, as specified in TS 37.324 [24] clause 5.1.2;","paragraph_zero_based":10755},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>indicate the release of the user plane resources for the mbs-SessionId to upper layers.","paragraph_zero_based":10756},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.4MBS Interest Indication","paragraph_zero_based":10757},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.4.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10758},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":10759},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.9.4.1-1: MBS Interest Indication","paragraph_zero_based":10760},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The purpose of this procedure is to inform the network that the UE in RRC_CONNECTED is receiving or is interested to receive MBS broadcast service(s) and to inform the network about the priority of MBS broadcast versus unicast and multicast MRB reception. MBS Interest Indication can only be sent after AS security activation.","paragraph_zero_based":10761},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.4.2Initiation","paragraph_zero_based":10762},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"An MBS capable UE in RRC_CONNECTED may initiate the procedure in several cases including upon successful connection establishment/resume, upon entering or leaving the broadcast service area, upon MBS broadcast session start or stop, upon change of interest, upon change of priority between MBS broadcast reception and unicast/multicast reception, upon change to a PCell providing SIB21 (i.e. where the SIB1 scheduling information contains SIB21), upon receiving SIB20 of an SCell via dedicated signalling, upon handover, and upon RRC connection re-establishment, upon change to a PCell providing nonServingCellMII in SIB1, upon starting or stopping reception of MBS broadcast service on a non-serving cell, upon change of CFR information or subcarrier spacing for MBS broadcast reception on a non-serving cell. If the UE does not have the CFR information and subcarrier spacing for MBS broadcast reception on a non-serving cell at the time it sends the MBS Interest Indication, the UE sends another MBS Interest Indication after it has acquired this information from the non-serving cell.","paragraph_zero_based":10763},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon initiating the procedure, the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10764},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if SIB21 is provided by the PCell; or","paragraph_zero_based":10765},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if nonServingCellMII is provided in SIB1 by the PCell:","paragraph_zero_based":10766},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>ensure having a valid version of SIB21 for the PCell, if present;","paragraph_zero_based":10767},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE did not transmit MBS Interest Indication since last entering RRC_CONNECTED state; or","paragraph_zero_based":10768},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if SIB21 is provided and since the last time the UE transmitted an MBS Interest Indication to a PCell providing SIB21, the UE connected to a PCell, not providing SIB21; or","paragraph_zero_based":10769},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2> if nonServingCellMII is provided in SIB1 and since the last time the UE transmitted an MBS Interest Indication to a PCell providing nonServingCellMII in SIB1, the UE connected to a PCell not providing nonServingCellMII in SIB1:","paragraph_zero_based":10770},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the set of MBS broadcast frequencies of interest, determined in accordance with 5.9.4.3, is not empty:","paragraph_zero_based":10771},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set the contents of MBS Interest Indication according to 5.9.4.5 and initiate transmission of the MBSInterestIndication message;","paragraph_zero_based":10772},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":10773},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the set of MBS broadcast frequencies of interest, determined in accordance with 5.9.4.3, is different from mbs-FreqList included in the last transmission of the MBS Interest Indication; or","paragraph_zero_based":10774},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the set of MBS broadcast frequencies of interest for MBS broadcast reception on non-serving cell, determined in accordance with 5.9.4.3, is different from freqInfoMBS included in the last transmission of the MBS Interest Indication; or","paragraph_zero_based":10775}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["60419a71bfce12142c4c3de269df9c284c78c516e11b4547cd17f17d314889aa","22c6b612c0175b256c9c0155c382af62ebcc8c16d05c1a4c1c8a5d0bb776305e","ff843a59d32d05b9efef7de0908157efd2a31fd2e0a77b324fdb65404d337773","55fbf749cbae1fb139c4ae79ea725fb764e288409700cba7309b1bebbc87195a","6066d23dcc2e78b42a3e630b605693da6a7dff8d934350145896660f9b61ce6f","90dcd44077958629763bda0a7991f68ddee8a6a86a30c4f94e9bca73a72d38d3","8937201f5dbfff261c2874e98529caa0887f3cd268e09223d2e424412aaab33c","d44e15f63e8d216da4982d2eaa002b789692b8fbe051adf527c0b919ea714d7b","d5065e19d963f34652f64ec6e1674c989a0d217436c1deaacb6a375131aa3659","bede65adb7cd7a2aa58038971dd9fcb75cd07862e1a913c982af0e492acbb1a7","c16c407a27ef5fdca3611c79a815e1b13beb7f59a3e24420e1f2f00aa2327cfb","1600405ae2d3322bb306effc06c6e7f37208a244c11f58e49e22224e087ff779","7ddbda758e7d69dd1972f9dc02ff0885da5c793973aca2326a7d8aba815b6fc6","f12a15504cf3bf658e79465d4e0050c5b00404a828ff922055834992633e2230","431069b912a8fe3e2a225b2bd4e08d737270576ccf4753316e2d110a3e4f015a","7217564bfbb51f5fb431fc687a6aa50400785ce8d257af74b5c0ce74b7eb169e","b0cb3e431c3f50b4e7a8296aa55619d1d12310a294aeddd867adf6fadec514ed","c127743ea1a56f20a8178f0e19001f038b57a334a5aa3a16154c0cc361cc37bd","5f45d02d9264de4a842c01029351af33a5ecb293b5470a1f9e07f8c7acff6e66","99c3d176b4163d02d4581d22ed32f21ae16639be211581fb770ea741d8b70aa0","a9dc1a0aab74d4a990a977b61bd93b728abbbf9e2d48bb361440616396445162","16c0582135755ac5ab82478053a37f8de753ebc8a39bbab38df34f00c512f97a","f26d84c4838fc6c8a36b11bd4cf89a6f122e520279502bffd868882ba6bc3c2f","e5a7618a31c98c44132e6b5552ccd7e38f9eba31cae2773648e19e27acb3e504"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10752,10775],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10752"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if any of the subcarrier spacing and the CFR information for MBS broadcast reception on non-serving cell has changed since the last transmission of the MBS Interest Indication; or","paragraph_zero_based":10776},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the subcarrier spacing and the CFR information for MBS broadcast reception on non-serving cell have been acquired from the non-serving cell which were not reported in the previous MBS Interest Indication; or","paragraph_zero_based":10777},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the prioritisation of reception of all indicated MBS broadcast frequencies compared to reception of any of the established unicast bearers and multicast MRBs has changed since the last transmission of the MBS Interest Indication:","paragraph_zero_based":10778},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set the contents of MBS Interest Indication according to 5.9.4.5 and initiate transmission of the MBSInterestIndication message;","paragraph_zero_based":10779},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:The UE may send MBS Interest Indication even when it is able to receive the MBS services it is interested in, i.e. to avoid that the network allocates a configuration inhibiting MBS broadcast reception.","paragraph_zero_based":10780},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else if SIB20 is provided for the PCell or for the SCell:","paragraph_zero_based":10781},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if since the last time the UE transmitted the MBS Interest Indication, the UE connected to a PCell not providing SIB20 and the UE was not provided with SIB20 for an SCell; or","paragraph_zero_based":10782},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the set of MBS broadcast services of interest determined in accordance with 5.9.4.4 is different from mbs-ServiceList included in the last transmission of the MBS Interest Indication:","paragraph_zero_based":10783},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set the contents of MBS Interest Indication according to 5.9.4.5 and initiate the transmission of MBSInterestIndication message.","paragraph_zero_based":10784},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.4.3MBS frequencies of interest determination","paragraph_zero_based":10785},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10786},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>consider a frequency to be part of the MBS frequencies of interest if the following conditions are met:","paragraph_zero_based":10787},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>at least one MBS session the UE is receiving or interested to receive via a broadcast MRB is ongoing or about to start; and","paragraph_zero_based":10788},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:The UE may determine whether the session is ongoing from the start and stop time indicated in the User Service Description (USD), see TS 38.300 [2] or TS 23.247 [67].","paragraph_zero_based":10789},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for at least one of these MBS sessions, SIB21 acquired from the PCell or a non-serving cell includes mapping between the concerned frequency and one or more MBS FSAIs indicated in the USD for this session, or for at least one of these MBS sessions, the concerned frequency is not included in SIB21 but is indicated in the USD for this session; and","paragraph_zero_based":10790},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:The UE considers a frequency to be part of the MBS frequencies of interest even though NG-RAN may (temporarily) not employ a broadcast MRB for the concerned session, i.e., the UE does not verify if the session is indicated on MCCH.","paragraph_zero_based":10791},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>the supportedBandCombinationList the UE included in UE-NR-Capability contains at least one band combination including the concerned MBS frequency.","paragraph_zero_based":10792},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 3:When evaluating which frequencies the UE is capable of receiving, the UE does not take into account whether they are currently configured as serving frequencies.","paragraph_zero_based":10793},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.4.4MBS services of interest determination","paragraph_zero_based":10794},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10795},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>consider an MBS service to be part of the MBS services of interest if the following conditions are met:","paragraph_zero_based":10796},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>the UE is receiving or interested to receive this service via a broadcast MRB; and","paragraph_zero_based":10797},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>the session of this service is ongoing or about to start; and","paragraph_zero_based":10798},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>one or more MBS FSAIs in the USD for this service is included in SIB21 acquired from the PCell for a frequency belonging to the set of MBS frequencies of interest, determined according to 5.9.4.3 or SIB21 acquired from the PCell does not provide the frequency mapping for the concerned service but that frequency is included in the USD of this service.","paragraph_zero_based":10799}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["24099eaedd2a30500d8b488c361f2ff3994b784eec9bcf23125eba5dad193efc","b009134ce689305ce4ecbfe824071a5355473e081dc76c3bab2e4a44515d7efa","26bfac81ad29451e852da83440a7dafd4d4a7b8d0e9f731961c58b65447e6462","13532155859f456ef2e7ed99fd6abac69dde88f7b73cb1502da94419eb8e31fa","75a09b4538f90f5d6bf033e7bf3fc4c4489784236d552510bbb04b6f7acb75cc","a7f5257aaf5ffa33b7c0df06f1296d518ded481f0a7ad78b762d78ffd340d575","ebe0219db76945441873eafca1723bee8ebaa59bb9dd7128e78ce6c419243f97","10b7acc8429b894bb2d97590ac6c34ecb46443b0cde821813deee53ede4d63dd","80e6eaa6423102a126a63f4aa1bdc6d341cf0ca29c63c9652a6c7a3d3fad6f9c","e0f74d45ec2d56425241d7b83faecebe08c6dc828b970a96d5724454effca9ae","2eceab0198f77615b733f2633ae32b31f33d7ce383bf0b8c1e22597924660436","0a518c00959598412c76e16db5e83ff1d8d3e185b47fe8019e9835e82543a14d","5afca1d087abdaa620c29f2f7ff89748162221874fdbb9641e1b87d26285e193","8d86839687538db4f8c2cc0a3f361f2dc6e2c27eca8cb08c37720f546a51a87e","88e3ef575f6f603bdba35ff754a1acf802c779ef0cd8f6e4f017bf1fb863bf85","1eeac40001c2ebb144f036a73d7424bf24c138f24b76d6258be3dd6a5b62cf63","cb9246c9548c0704949fd3ba759739618c47cf953029783b09c71f078cbef0a9","7cc90705563aa65b4da09a5171e482d91b504f43478d4fef67cfd4a337a3f912","b78b9fe8ba2cd565e3fb3c361449dd920afb0548b615b12e141926e90283dd92","d3f4bd42a31cf6dbdc0d82c5b6f1e5c598e0be744173caa2fcaa114c7553402a","73e311098edb7382455f1db46f62eaabaaecc75676cc0205165a8bdd5694c10c","8d3694d2b2576490b6b93d1186049ae2df8b9f81d2bf7c26ecff11394b4f6808","5ea7426377f29dfd82a72a314abcacee64a73befdb1fe65dcab34f7bb4c24305","7173837aa8ef08c396ed77d0c0b6ac8f21547f4cf866ce510e6a46567a48bd75"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10776,10799],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10776"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:The UE may determine whether the session is ongoing from the start and stop time indicated in the User Service Description (USD), see TS 38.300 [2] or TS 23.247 [67].","paragraph_zero_based":10800},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.9.4.5Setting of the contents of MBS Interest Indication","paragraph_zero_based":10801},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall set the contents of the MBS Interest Indication as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":10802},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE has a valid version of SIB21 for the PCell; and","paragraph_zero_based":10803},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the set of MBS frequencies of interest, determined in accordance with 5.9.4.3, is not empty:","paragraph_zero_based":10804},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>include mbs-FreqList and set it to include the MBS frequencies of interest sorted by decreasing order of interest, using the absoluteFrequencySSB for serving frequency, if applicable, and the ARFCN-ValueNR(s) as included in SIB21 or in USD (for neighbouring frequencies);","paragraph_zero_based":10805},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>include mbs-Priority if the UE prioritises reception of all indicated MBS frequencies above reception of any of the unicast bearers and multicast MRBs;","paragraph_zero_based":10806},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:If the UE prioritises MBS broadcast reception and unicast/multicast data cannot be supported because of congestion on the MBS carrier(s), NG-RAN may for example initiate release of unicast bearers/multicast MRBs.","paragraph_zero_based":10807},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if SIB20 is provided for the PCell or for the SCell:","paragraph_zero_based":10808},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>include mbs-ServiceList and set it to indicate the set of MBS services of interest sorted by decreasing order of interest determined in accordance with 5.9.4.4;","paragraph_zero_based":10809},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:The mbs-ServiceList is not required to be used by the NG-RAN to determine the frequency on which to enable MBS broadcast reception for the UE.","paragraph_zero_based":10810},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if nonServingCellMII is provided in SIB1 by the PCell; and","paragraph_zero_based":10811},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the set of MBS frequencies for MBS broadcast reception on non-serving cell, determined in accordance with 5.9.4.3, is not empty:","paragraph_zero_based":10812},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>include freqInfoMBS;","paragraph_zero_based":10813},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE has acquired cfr-InfoMBS and subcarrierSpacing for MBS broadcast reception on the non-serving cell:","paragraph_zero_based":10814},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>include cfr-InfoMBS and subcarrierSpacing.","paragraph_zero_based":10815},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.10MBS multicast reception in RRC_INACTIVE","paragraph_zero_based":10816},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.10.1Introduction","paragraph_zero_based":10817},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.10.1.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10818},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE configured to receive MBS multicast service(s) in RRC_INACTIVE that the UE has joined applies MBS multicast procedures described in this clause.","paragraph_zero_based":10819},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MBS multicast configuration information is provided in RRCRelease and on multicast MCCH logical channel.","paragraph_zero_based":10820},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When there is temporarily no data for an active multicast session or when the multicast session is deactivated, the network notifies the UE to stop monitoring the corresponding G-RNTI via MBS multicast configuration information. If the UE is notified to stop monitoring the G-RNTI(s) for all the joined multicast sessions, it stops monitoring the Multicast MCCH-RNTI for the cell where it received the notification.","paragraph_zero_based":10821},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Multicast MCCH carries the MBSMulticastConfiguration message which indicates the MBS multicast sessions that are provided in the cell as well as the corresponding scheduling related information for these sessions. Optionally, the MBSMulticastConfiguration message may also contain a list of neighbour cells providing the same MBS multicast service(s) for reception in RRC_INACTIVE as provided in the current cell. The configuration information required by the UE to receive multicast MCCH is provided in SIB24.","paragraph_zero_based":10822},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.10.1.2Multicast MCCH scheduling","paragraph_zero_based":10823}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["58ef4d882a6d75966bdaeb68012ddba7b96333f209d3d30a7027e81fad23ea84","5af511eca1da8e58d9019f74a5285a0bbec3bd89300a9f4b50e9b7d1f140d276","6120dc4dd1b4d1f055bac15e49a8b6fbdcb30d3996bb43c278cd04ee82d37334","8f63e271191a94b66014871da8b3301742e804d7cbb2b1393a4b0f2ed8ecfd84","e10be477570e15356882c003b48c458cc935cee61507d2080263ed6e873e9c44","e0faa326580d1ce0db283c75b5d5da03483a8b811f76d14e882dbb95c7a522e6","f00345951c2a60a04ace8560af0b76724796badf94d41f52065301eaf7481a3a","53ce6247b567b1745167074700ee4f82e6eac8209bc0fcb9b40c4ee04a319c33","9de87209c312ddd63d99a1bec935711d9ab9101ca66668bc61de5ce2d36eabd0","21ef0b4935bda8a0a4776747a6deb93d8738f5d7add16f7d2afd945e85bd6edd","c3dbc94636bc588c9806605fc584d54f6a0841d48b4ea6626a60f3b7e797b2e6","24bdc51a3d18bd967115a76aedc3774cb799cba9c795dc36456e8270774091d1","a9e0ca598ccb53dbdceb63058eb7b8f97f754519300d65cbb20161d0bec4ac47","0476a8496ac588fa37ed1be308ad857605314b7e0e4b4e8ed097699e61927ab4","a2aabb40a3edc7f7eb261d849a6d16d5a08f559665e62cd0c4360abba2f80758","c21f33e6e28397451a2a040ec92d9b85f23adfa9023afc24babcbbc6e39f9b5b","aefeddb1c1c8610c56211eb75367f283284aa5af21120158656f9217c852f2bc","08627bfc996c7f73b115a68d4e0d18b329fb54dc5b1beee6fc0a6f2012d7895c","7751bd80f09590ed1c7f58860a781d90371ba3fff5a1e35cd410f00cd56b1b1f","16f7a31c64e64ddaeee3f01cb6ec01517811898fecd0fee61f9536f9d0f3464c","5cb141d0fadc1a4efdd3ef5271cfb15d78d97d282fbf2f7f97608edae87973ce","da95fcf5b60e4afa1b625ef5355f78c620904019001b12091b874ddff4316596","cc6a6ad2edcf2b7ab93028c2f4355be14ee7356c6915ec8a47aadaabd73642c9","41b0232f355dcb6210783d2283e43a6ba3b5b1a909faae14f4cda9b7214ba4e8"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10800,10823],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10800"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The multicast MCCH information (i.e. information transmitted in messages sent over multicast MCCH) is transmitted periodically, using a configurable repetition period and within a configured transmission window. MCCH transmissions (and the associated radio resources and MCS) are indicated via the PDCCH addressed to Multicast MCCH-RNTI. PDCCH monitoring occasion(s) for the multicast MCCH transmission are determined according to the common search space indicated by searchSpaceMulticastMCCH. If searchSpaceMulticastMCCH is set to zero, PDCCH monitoring occasions for the multicast MCCH message reception in the multicast MCCH transmission window are the same as PDCCH monitoring occasions for SIB1 where the mapping between PDCCH monitoring occasions and SSBs is specified in TS 38.213 [13]. If searchSpaceMulticastMCCH is not set to zero, PDCCH monitoring occasions for the multicast MCCH message are determined based on search space indicated by searchSpaceMulticastMCCH. PDCCH monitoring occasions for the multicast MCCH message which are not overlapping with UL symbols (determined according to tdd-UL-DL-ConfigurationCommon) are sequentially numbered from one in the multicast MCCH transmission window. The [x×N+K]th PDCCH monitoring occasion for the multicast MCCH message in the multicast MCCH transmission window corresponds to the Kth transmitted SSB, where x = 0, 1, ...X-1, K = 1, 2, …N, N is the number of actual transmitted SSBs determined according to ssb-PositionsInBurst in SIB1 and X is equal to CEIL(number of PDCCH monitoring occasions in multicast MCCH transmission window/N). The actual transmitted SSBs are sequentially numbered from one in ascending order of their SSB indexes. The UE assumes that, in the multicast MCCH transmission window, PDCCH for a multicast MCCH message is transmitted in at least one PDCCH monitoring occasion corresponding to each transmitted SSB and thus the selection of SSB for the reception of multicast MCCH messages is up to UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":10824},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.10.1.3Multicast MCCH information validity and notification of changes","paragraph_zero_based":10825},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Change of multicast MCCH information only occurs at specific radio frames, i.e. the concept of a modification period is used. Within a modification period, the same multicast MCCH information may be transmitted a number of times, as defined by its scheduling (which is based on a repetition period).","paragraph_zero_based":10826},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When the network changes (some of) the multicast MCCH information, it notifies the UEs about the change starting from the beginning of the multicast MCCH modification period via PDCCH which schedules the multicast MCCH in every repetition in that modification period.","paragraph_zero_based":10827},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon receiving a change notification, a UE receiving MBS multicast service(s) in RRC_INACTIVE acquires the new multicast MCCH information starting from the same slot. The UE applies the previously acquired multicast MCCH information until the UE acquires the new multicast MCCH information.","paragraph_zero_based":10828},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.10.2Multicast MCCH information acquisition","paragraph_zero_based":10829},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.10.2.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10830},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":10831},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.10.2.1-1: Multicast MCCH information acquisition","paragraph_zero_based":10832},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE applies the multicast MCCH information acquisition procedure to acquire the MBS multicast configuration information from the network. The procedure applies to UEs configured to receive MBS multicast services in RRC_INACTIVE.","paragraph_zero_based":10833},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.10.2.2Initiation","paragraph_zero_based":10834},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If configured to receive MBS multicast services in RRC_INACTIVE, a UE applies the multicast MCCH information acquisition procedure for PTM configuration update and upon selection or reselection to a new cell providing SIB24 (except in case the UE is aware that the multicast sessions that the UE has joined are not available for RRC_INACTIVE in the new cell). A UE that is receiving MBS multicast data in RRC_INACTIVE shall apply the multicast MCCH information acquisition procedure upon receiving a notification that the multicast MCCH information has changed.","paragraph_zero_based":10835},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:It is up to UE implementation how to address a possibility of the UE missing a multicast MCCH change notification.","paragraph_zero_based":10836},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Unless explicitly stated otherwise in the procedural specification, the multicast MCCH information acquisition procedure overwrites any stored multicast MCCH information, i.e. delta configuration is not applicable for multicast MCCH information and the UE discontinues using a field if it is absent in multicast MCCH information.","paragraph_zero_based":10837},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.10.2.3Multicast MCCH information acquisition by the UE","paragraph_zero_based":10838},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE configured to receive an MBS multicast service in RRC_INACTIVE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10839},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the procedure is triggered by a multicast MCCH information change notification:","paragraph_zero_based":10840},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>start acquiring the MBSMulticastConfiguration message on multicast MCCH in the concerned cell from the slot in which the change notification was received;","paragraph_zero_based":10841},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE moves to a different cell providing SIB24; or","paragraph_zero_based":10842},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE receives RRCRelease configuring the UE to receive MBS multicast in RRC_INACTIVE which does not include PTM configuration for at least one multicast session for which the UE is not indicated to stop monitoring the G-RNTI:","paragraph_zero_based":10843},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>acquire the MBSMulticastConfiguration message on multicast MCCH in the concerned cell at the next repetition period.","paragraph_zero_based":10844},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.10.2.4Actions upon reception of the MBSMulticastConfiguration message","paragraph_zero_based":10845},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"No UE requirements related to the contents of the MBSMulticastConfiguration message apply other than those specified elsewhere, e.g., within the corresponding field descriptions.","paragraph_zero_based":10846},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.10.3MRB configuration","paragraph_zero_based":10847}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e3a1322398ac15c5d1fd0ac55d751f7899d7ff0b0cb87237bc9718f082d83063","9045b229a566cc472f3e52c22fde37f18fb4a88a35c15ed7e2ba09dfcc4e5cb1","9962d24703244ebdbf9eb0737f83090ef0717daf0255bde3d31e7db0d67a5b07","4dc84dfae6da3171a0b19c85de73c9c82878010d80de1f1b55132a4021385955","4ee21826b2b4076906152d7c1b53bf20d40723734c42257c6b86e6a10e07518c","5a10b21c3e4e0c112c2a62dda4dddf8ac14f1dacc6ee1f75d585359964cadf4d","2ba23c5451419ba258019ffc1472cd159054d92ba5e8be9c03347127e8619bdb","b1ea0a2cc7e5b1caed80aed867f9d5c9b964d7ac9d277a9bc7d3fad066898e4f","84f43de38a621fa2ded85a66f1f76ee7814156ad487a694b7c0cf66f11096eae","baae8dcfa8fd9cee1165e9a0ba820a077d4edb0c7f309731157005b37686fc2d","34322a66aebf13e74a0f7be957ef18c59ca697c9097ad7e68a13cef2ce3643de","1106ef5c6108143f3f3e3d96e5e4facbc3082436346e1dbcdfb897fc5efa8466","a657bf580548ec6ec416bf1741015ae32706a45b4df5306e331910adde253ab4","7d404c502890c97756a8d9b2733a025f9c475268f0c3b00cbb3b490e35db2c6f","759b22dbcbfe0c71a8722d410609e39d72bb45314ce84e734663674760dd511a","f58ca36b90caead2008f11e1f9845c729a8142bac7e3cf9473d8b9bfcfc619f8","dab79fb479da08a82cb3c8d2a9af558ed316e70683ed136a92895347b9e3e860","e7718149d9194dd9e3d1a0a8a181cc03288333ad81d00ed246797b5535d5a65c","7ab1d87a4c63e18949591180ede8c7ddbab5c9dad79e8eca19628e18b0fd2084","600c1f23fd33a2c84216949c9c6fbb264625375a3b35f845d37e8aef1e72c5d4","b5efdecda7f98c33fb1c98dccca4fcf15b34efb7d2f6f8ad4abbd7f43d6b2805","0aea0524850d06c6b21cec4af4f0dc4569d954ff19984b04f0a680ca1758410d","66c22f998ab3ee9851d2d6da7fee16562a61b021fca379e8524455d544d3ad7b","57f8eda523b13d157d079fabce697101e1fca7eb3b25797b74b0f7b7aa772a93"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10824,10847],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10824"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.10.3.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10848},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The multicast MRB configuration procedure is used by the UE in RRC_INACTIVE state to configure PDCP, RLC, MAC entities and the physical layer upon PTM configuration update and moving to a cell providing SIB24. The UE may perform multicast MRB modification or release/establishment when PTM configuration is updated via multicast MCCH or when it moves to a cell where the PDCP COUNT of the corresponding multicast MRB is not synchronized within the RNA. The UE may perform multicast MRB modification when it moves to a cell where the PDCP COUNT of the corresponding multicast MRB is synchronized within the RNA. The UE resets MAC upon selection or reselection to a new cell.","paragraph_zero_based":10849},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:How to perform modification of a multicast MRB which is already configured in the UE is left to UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":10850},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon moving to a cell where the PDCP COUNT of a multicast MRB is not synchronized, an indication is sent to the lower layer to inform the PDCP COUNT non-synchronization of the corresponding multicast MRB. Upon transition from RRC_CONNECTED to RRC_INACTIVE in the same cell, the UE can continue using the multicast MRBs used in RRC_CONNECTED and in this case, the same LCIDs are used for the same multicast MRBs. Upon transition from RRC_INACTIVE to RRC_CONNECTED, the UE releases the MRBs configured in RRCRelease or multicast MCCH and performs delta configuration based on the stored MRB configuration from RRC_CONNECTED, if not indicated to perform full configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":10851},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.10.3.2Multicast MRB establishment","paragraph_zero_based":10852},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon establishment of a multicast MRB, the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10853},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>establish a PDCP entity and an RLC entity in accordance with mrb-ListMulticast for this multicast MRB included in the MBSMulticastConfiguration message;","paragraph_zero_based":10854},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>configure the MAC layer in accordance with the mtch-SchedulingInfo (if included);","paragraph_zero_based":10855},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>configure the physical layer in accordance with the mbs-SessionInfoListMulticast, searchSpaceMulticastMTCH, and pdsch-ConfigMTCH, applicable for the multicast MRB;","paragraph_zero_based":10856},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if an SDAP entity with the received mbs-SessionId does not exist:","paragraph_zero_based":10857},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>establish an SDAP entity as specified in TS 37.324 [24] clause 5.1.1;","paragraph_zero_based":10858},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>indicate the establishment of the user plane resources for the mbs-SessionId to upper layers;","paragraph_zero_based":10859},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>receive DL-SCH on the cell where the MBSMulticastConfiguration message was received for the established multicast MRB using g-RNTI (if not indicated to stop monitoring this G-RNTI) and mtch-SchedulingInfo (if included) in this message for this MBS multicast service.","paragraph_zero_based":10860},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.10.3.3Multicast MRB release","paragraph_zero_based":10861},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon release of a multicast MRB, the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":10862},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release the PDCP entity, RLC entity as well as the related MAC and physical layer configuration;","paragraph_zero_based":10863},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the SDAP entity associated with the corresponding mbs-SessionId has no associated MRB:","paragraph_zero_based":10864},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the SDAP entity, as specified in TS 37.324 [24] clause 5.1.2;","paragraph_zero_based":10865},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>indicate the release of the user plane resources for the mbs-SessionId to upper layers.","paragraph_zero_based":10866},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":10867},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6Protocol data units, formats and parameters (ASN.1)","paragraph_zero_based":10868},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6.1General","paragraph_zero_based":10869},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6.1.1Introduction","paragraph_zero_based":10870},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The contents of each RRC message is specified in clause 6.2 using ASN.1 to specify the message syntax and using tables when needed to provide further detailed information about the fields specified in the message syntax. The syntax of the information elements that are defined as stand-alone abstract types is further specified in a similar manner in clause 6.3.","paragraph_zero_based":10871}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["555f9b15dbc1f05be08be29fd3edd8a88a16303f17a4a2ebaac712c93a001129","590c89fc5273607b78a5f15b6f70c9c1dabf53450a1b925052527867dd3ad06f","96567c92f8f4668edf3e7b448148a690a222e59a854b832df0bc0cb6986887f0","ecdc94b0887a436e95f26a71d1372cdd094d364a075d1ca442b89fe266798293","fb68a0df5355baf663b33aaf30ea731ead78e3bb08dd26d05310d3a09d94da09","d81ea3a2d6dc0ca3f73abc0b1b0119a8818dfc01d4fbf63db1a0772885522f27","93d7ece2cbf89ae067ce9426031f001e0b50633a8262bcdf77fb2dfab862fb6c","c31bac25e2e532572a72f7d965775c69ca52a8379b6c02981b1b1265e8deaf57","3a0c8310c98e2170c6297c3371bc9b8908d1ed7921601fac0fd506122c2770dd","eb091fd065d2d2da6081360a0505e5d31b8240f176f1314e40ad7ac961682c5b","c23a9a8fd5365fb6ef2f978bf6995dde7f85552e673da48681facb22b936d08a","9fbfac4a2b5b3b0557b48ffb2574da49cc7f8120bac22126af5e7af85725959b","862af0ac7821feb8c51cb7c9c90156ba446741875af2c127e5db01fdf1483bf6","9755f4d788fe6e28608349fb46310370e3319f029a03698f08228ff2692d435a","89b61d87cf9f0e26f5ecb8e70fbb65f7e3413ea8a68ee18c8fd8614cc80a1896","14fb91b6e221a915fd5be1b8f0e5e1203ea19660efe787bbab9b25793df65bb9","53cc46188ae9ade00893aca4ef994f57eb866623a6a6dad2cb2b3694eee538f0","b00904184a5194b193ae1293c4418f2f0918b53a032340fbc41f13a91f286549","121fc17e47f247142c5d2108ab5b5170a23b8f08e18dae3f012f1d9cbb772303","90381d9ad36f86f00bcd6a9eae84538bd4168d097fa9be330e2fc41967717940","265902665e5048e2f180d2a203cbad233d74e76c516ab2acd1fada2d63383fb9","c95348af8a3a9e3eb4010e36e23d89beb3ea2ef088d15e6fb46dae6f995b29ec","86050634191288e25e2c5274dc9d6b4484fc5ea47484094abd5dd11f34c7bca4","d2b77c68d910fb0205e6c0d73844dbc8f8df29cc79e8d11f82cacc55224ca4bd"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10848,10871],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10848"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Usage of the text \"Network always configures the UE with a value for this field\" in the field description indicates that the network has to provide a value for the field in this or in a previous message based on delta configuration (for an optional field with Need M). It does not imply a mandatory presence of the field.","paragraph_zero_based":10872},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6.1.2Need codes and conditions for optional fields","paragraph_zero_based":10873},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The need for fields to be present in a message or an abstract type, i.e., the ASN.1 fields that are specified as OPTIONAL in the abstract notation (ASN.1), is specified by means of comment text tags attached to the OPTIONAL statement in the abstract syntax. All comment text tags are available for use in the downlink direction for RRC message and in the sidelink for PC5 RRC message. The meaning of each tag is specified in table 6.1.2-1.","paragraph_zero_based":10874},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If conditions are used, a conditional presence table is provided for the message or information element specifying the need of the field for each condition case. The table also specifies whether UE maintains or releases the value in case the field is absent. The conditions clarify what the UE may expect regarding the setting of the message by the network for the RRC message or by the peer UE in the sidelink RRC message. Violation of conditions is regarded as invalid network behaviour when transmitting downlink RRC message or invalid UE behavior when transmitting PC5 RRC message, which the UE is not required to cope with. Hence the general error handling defined in 10.4 does not apply in case a field is absent although it is mandatory according to the CondC or CondM condition.","paragraph_zero_based":10875},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For guidelines on the use of need codes and conditions, see Annex A.6 and A.7.","paragraph_zero_based":10876},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Table 6.1.2-1: Meaning of abbreviations used to specify the need for fields to be present","paragraph_zero_based":10877},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Abbreviation","paragraph_zero_based":10878},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Meaning","paragraph_zero_based":10879},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Cond conditionTag","paragraph_zero_based":10880},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditionally present","paragraph_zero_based":10881},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Presence of the field is specified in a tabular form following the ASN.1 segment.","paragraph_zero_based":10882},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CondC conditionTag","paragraph_zero_based":10883},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configuration condition","paragraph_zero_based":10884},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Presence of the field is conditional to other configuration settings.","paragraph_zero_based":10885},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CondM conditionTag","paragraph_zero_based":10886},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Message condition","paragraph_zero_based":10887},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Presence of the field is conditional to other fields included in the message.","paragraph_zero_based":10888},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Need S","paragraph_zero_based":10889},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Specified","paragraph_zero_based":10890},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Used for (configuration) fields, whose field description or procedure specifies the UE behavior performed upon receiving a message with the field absent (and not if field description or procedure specifies the UE behavior when field is not configured).","paragraph_zero_based":10891},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Need M","paragraph_zero_based":10892},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Maintain","paragraph_zero_based":10893},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Used for (configuration) fields that are stored by the UE i.e. not one-shot. Upon receiving a message with the field absent, the UE maintains the current value.","paragraph_zero_based":10894},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Need N","paragraph_zero_based":10895}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["8ff69619f4b4ea741dad65f23a9af0d3d8b468bc338acb68c9827431d7a7028c","db26b0b8845329de30509968e5dfbcf99dbe6b7496294ab07ee5a943c3827306","08ab558a994e1c5eaa2cc7783f6c6ec9bab029bd430b9b36cfeaf9f878b24d96","908799372da5f15c0e2a232fd2d0485193ec716cbdf94d3f2305f9c98b2e7b4a","b4dcabe4a23d80ebc00e39d8c8e4d679445d4d6bfa6684369c0ff0ce24322d17","53f47e043f62436bc3fad486d2e19f5fb967d2a64c99e9e6a4ddb7e8883f62d5","dc5fb09cc6e35b86e1ebf213e128638fa3fc50a1e731d9a6cd0e49a2a8ffe1ad","ca0d488ec7eb8c8290ca24976e1596583efada603053dee07f87a59ba0c3f9de","f1130ef9cf4fbf0887bd29a777af8cd9ed2d4d62e57f4deff0a59158a6cee9fe","7f67f11858a46d00dfcfb78fb8f54ae29d2be359d3baa4895929f755d595278e","1a7dd1f942b2d8af16d8c735bc290498bdf12aad79bc238d40e94739dda5f0ce","784e05a003c61a7088a7f9e625956584fb2fdc50ff4cbd36cf7aaf4635780f5b","0938d98c7fd8ef5353c13d3ee8b1858584aa978e38ad14e95714feda1b6ea238","16a46b3248f0b566739ea640259db7628af38192d5ed44597936061cf41bb3c2","6c1f7b1b8d358adc87186575dd44ab1c9476135a9add1940834944779ebaed32","c3f7e759accc947805250300af7bfd5c0d5bf6c7b63e1f83a60784b37faf28d7","d9fe35600a744478a954ab505f12fbae1531cdcf44fcfa507298434d193f63bd","ce56b7fd68c2e781940811b5394916c3208bbcc844095346eac44a91a4c47c7d","8ffd1abbb3a37be78f3e1836a9e3435702c2e4ee6fbde65e9d39c1367d8129c6","2c6608969e2dccf09ca830958e8d898a7db0fe5fdc23e9d262665089f7fe22f9","c80a68e84cb1a3515b40551130d095ed93fec0b27f0b5aeac0748e7a9fffca0d","eaf411ea2dfffaf479e6c0b6d2fd438fa9cfc7b72364f069d008174a9e31ec3e","b11845d6dfcedfbcf59cef3f28b5b48c9e8a0b6494cffe96d29cc2fd51ae844b","83aa17afec82d876790e9481945f6554afad9bbf678c6b75ee098137026fa2eb"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10872,10895],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p10872"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"No action (one-shot configuration that is not maintained)","paragraph_zero_based":10896},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Used for (configuration) fields that are not stored and whose presence causes a one-time action by the UE. Upon receiving message with the field absent, the UE takes no action.","paragraph_zero_based":10897},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Need R","paragraph_zero_based":10898},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release","paragraph_zero_based":10899},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Used for (configuration) fields that are stored by the UE i.e. not one-shot. Upon receiving a message with the field absent, the UE releases the current value.","paragraph_zero_based":10900},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:In this version of the specification, the condition tags CondC and CondM are not used.","paragraph_zero_based":10901},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Any field with Need M or Need N in system information shall be interpreted as Need R.","paragraph_zero_based":10902},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The need code used within a CondX definition only applies for the case (part of the condition) where it is defined: A condition may have different need codes for different parts of the condition. In particular, the CondX definition may contain the following \"otherwise the field is absent\" parts:","paragraph_zero_based":10903},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-\"Otherwise, the field is absent\": The field is not relevant or should not be configured when this part of the condition applies. In particular, the UE behaviour is not defined when the field is configured via another part of the condition and is reconfigured to this part of the condition. A need code is not provided when the transition from another part of the condition to this part of the condition is not supported, when the field clearly is a one-shot or there is no difference whether UE maintains or releases the value (e.g., in case the field is mandatory present according to the other part of the condition).","paragraph_zero_based":10904},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-\"Otherwise, the field is absent, Need R\": The field is released if absent when this part of the condition applies. This handles UE behaviour in case the field is configured via another part of the condition and this part of the condition applies (which means that network when transmitting downlink RRC message or peer UE transmitting PC5 RRC message can assume UE releases the field if this part of the condition is valid).","paragraph_zero_based":10905},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-\"Otherwise, the field is absent, Need M\": The UE retains the field if it was already configured when this part of the condition applies. This means the network when transmitting downlink RRC message or the peer UE when transmitting PC5 RRC message cannot release the field, but UE retains the previously configured value.","paragraph_zero_based":10906},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use of different Need codes in different parts of a condition should be avoided.","paragraph_zero_based":10907},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For downlink RRC message and sidelink PC5 RRC messages, the need codes, conditions and ASN.1 defaults specified for a particular (child) field only apply in case the (parent) field including the particular field is present. Thus, if the parent is absent the UE shall not release the field unless the absence of the parent field implies that.","paragraph_zero_based":10908},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For (parent) fields without need codes in downlink RRC messages or sidelink PC5 RRC message, if the parent field is absent, UE shall follow the need codes of the child fields. Thus, if parent field is absent, the need code of each child field is followed (i.e. Need R child fields are released, Need M child fields are not modified and the actions for Need S child fields depend on the specified conditions of each field). Examples of (parent) fields in downlink RRC messages and sidelink PC5 RRC message without need codes where this rule applies are:","paragraph_zero_based":10909},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-nonCriticalExtension fields at the end of a message using empty SEQUENCE extension mechanism,","paragraph_zero_based":10910},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-groups of non-critical extensions using double brackets (referred to as extension groups), and","paragraph_zero_based":10911},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-non-critical extensions at the end of a message or at the end of a structure, contained in a BIT STRING or OCTET STRING (referred to as parent extension fields).","paragraph_zero_based":10912},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The handling of need codes as specified in the previous is illustrated by means of an example, as shown in the following ASN.1.","paragraph_zero_based":10913},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- /example/ ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":10914},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":10915},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RRCMessage-IEs ::=                SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":10916},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    field1                            InformationElement1            OPTIONAL,  -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":10917},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    field2                            InformationElement2            OPTIONAL,  -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":10918},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    nonCriticalExtension              RRCMessage-v1570-IEs           OPTIONAL","paragraph_zero_based":10919}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha2