{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":11952},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":11953},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-MBSMULTICASTCONFIGURATION-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":11954},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":11955},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":11956},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MBSMulticastConfiguration field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":11957},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"mbs-NeighbourCellList","paragraph_zero_based":11958},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of neighbour cells providing one or more MBS multicast services for RRC_INACTIVE that are provided by the current cell. This field is used by the UE together with mtch-NeighbourCell field signalled for each MBS session in the corresponding MBS-SessionInfo. When an empty mbs-NeighbourCellList list is signalled, the UE shall assume that MBS multicast services signalled in mbs-SessionInfoListMulticast in the MBSMulticastConfiguration message are not provided in any neighbour cell. When a non-empty mbs-NeighbourCellList is signalled, the current serving cell does not provide information about MBS multicast services of a neighbour cell that is not included in mbs-NeighbourCellList, i.e., the UE cannot determine the presence or absence of an MBS multicast service of a neighbour cell that is absent. When the field mbs-NeighbourCellList is absent, the current serving cell does not provide information about MBS multicast services in the neighbouring cells, i.e. the UE cannot determine the presence or absence of an MBS multicast service in neighbouring cells based on the absence of this field.","paragraph_zero_based":11959},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"mbs-SessionInfoListMulticast","paragraph_zero_based":11960},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Provides the configuration of MBS multicast session(s) in the current cell. ","paragraph_zero_based":11961},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pdsch-ConfigMTCH","paragraph_zero_based":11962},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Provides parameters for acquiring the PDSCH for MTCH. When this field is absent, the UE shall use parameters in pdsch-ConfigMCCH in SIB24 to acquire the PDSCH for MTCH.","paragraph_zero_based":11963},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"thresholdMBS-List","paragraph_zero_based":11964},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of reception quality thresholds for RRC connection resume for a UE receiving multicast in RRC_INACTIVE.","paragraph_zero_based":11965},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":11966},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–MCGFailureInformation","paragraph_zero_based":11967},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The MCGFailureInformation message is used to provide information regarding NR MCG failures detected by the UE.","paragraph_zero_based":11968},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Signalling radio bearer: SRB1","paragraph_zero_based":11969},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RLC-SAP: AM","paragraph_zero_based":11970},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Logical channel: DCCH","paragraph_zero_based":11971},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Direction: UE to Network","paragraph_zero_based":11972},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MCGFailureInformation message","paragraph_zero_based":11973},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":11974},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-MCGFAILUREINFORMATION-START","paragraph_zero_based":11975}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_X