{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the UE can set the establishment cause to mps-PriorityAccess for a new connection following a redirect to NR or set the resume cause to mps-PriorityAccess for a resume following a redirect to NR. If the target RAT is E-UTRA, see TS 36.331 [10]. The gNB sets the indication only for UEs authorized to receive MPS treatment as indicated by ARP and/or QoS characteristics at the gNB, and it is applicable only for this instance of release with redirection to carrier/RAT included in the redirectedCarrierInfo field in the RRCRelease message.","paragraph_zero_based":13152},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"multicastConfigInactive","paragraph_zero_based":13153},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the multicast service(s) that can be received in RRC_INACTIVE in the serving cell where the multicast service(s) was received in RRC_CONNECTED and optionally the corresponding configuration. The presence of this field indicates the UE is configured to receive MBS multicast in RRC_INACTIVE; otherwise, the UE is not configured to receive MBS multicast in RRC_INACTIVE.","paragraph_zero_based":13154},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"noLastCellUpdate","paragraph_zero_based":13155},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Presence of the field indicates that the last used cell for PEI shall not be updated. When the field is absent, the PEI-capable UE shall update its last used cell with the current cell. The UE shall not update its last used cell with the current cell if the AS security is not activated.","paragraph_zero_based":13156},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"redirectedCarrierInfo","paragraph_zero_based":13157},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates a carrier frequency (downlink for FDD) and is used to redirect the UE to an NR or an inter-RAT carrier frequency, by means of cell selection at transition to RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE as specified in TS 38.304 [20]. Based on UE capability, the network may include redirectedCarrierInfo in RRCRelease message with suspendConfig if this message is sent in response to an RRCResumeRequest or an RRCResumeRequest1 which is triggered by the NAS layer (see 5.3.1.4 in TS 24.501 [23]).","paragraph_zero_based":13158},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"srs-PosRRC-Inactive","paragraph_zero_based":13159},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SRS for positioning configuration during RRC_INACTIVE state. The configuration also includes bandwidth aggregation and frequency hopping.","paragraph_zero_based":13160},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"srs-PosRRC-InactiveValidityAreaNonPreConfig","paragraph_zero_based":13161},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Contains the SRS for positioning configuration to be applied immediately and which is valid across a number of cells comprising a validity area during RRC_INACTIVE state.","paragraph_zero_based":13162},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"srs-PosRRC-InactiveValidityAreaPreConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":13163},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Contains the SRS for positioning configurations to be applied when a trigger for an event is met and which is valid across a number of cells comprising a validity area during RRC_INACTIVE state. For each validity area, the UE is preconfigured with only one SRS for positioning configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":13164},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The below fields for the respective IEs are configured commonly in the validity area when srs-PosRRC-InactiveValidityAreaPreConfigList/ srs-PosRRC-InactiveValidityAreaNonPreConfig is configured:","paragraph_zero_based":13165},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IE SRS-PosReseourceSet: srs-PosResourceSetId,srs-PosResourceSetIdList, srs-PosResourceIdList, resourceType, alpha, p0","paragraph_zero_based":13166},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IE SRS-PosResource: srs-PosResourceId, transmissionComb, resourceMapping, freqDomainShift, freqHopping, resourceType, groupOrSequenceHopping, sequenceID","paragraph_zero_based":13167},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"srs-PosTx-Hopping","paragraph_zero_based":13168},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Contains configuration related to the SRS for Positioning with frequency hopping for RRC_INACTIVE state.","paragraph_zero_based":13169},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"suspendConfig","paragraph_zero_based":13170},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates configuration for the RRC_INACTIVE state. The network does not configure suspendConfig when the network redirect the UE to an inter-RAT carrier frequency or if the UE is configured with a DAPS bearer.","paragraph_zero_based":13171},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"voiceFallbackIndication","paragraph_zero_based":13172},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the RRC release is triggered by EPS fallback for IMS voice as specified in TS 23.502 [43].","paragraph_zero_based":13173},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13174},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CarrierInfoNR field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":13175}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["72ce5ec86bf6cd7f97f3afe123e09c716b32659821598ee6db990b2a02fceeba","6f4821392d8da6efb8d115a32a9764a6c1eeef8cb38b878e7f1f3aa5267f3259","38cfd121588ec378ac4158d40aff030f562886df1e7eccdea65746b8f3b6060f","4572aece963e6625ecd0d57beabd845cfa6579fb0ef78ff387661e8abcd79fa2","fa3144355e21ac88275021ef87ff4369f5980be5045f05184e769664cdaa7809","dff96dce63b1085c9b38e9447ca962c1ee619508ec3b6edebdc31721ad910c9d","4513d0cf426e6e60aac47558512e43683ce390de433f932d8db8263c097eed55","7f0e820b6bb87b34d835654dfea8ce48a00a4a9a910fd3ab94b4034e1606686d","99408b3e1ff376953f4f54568690fdd43e8ad178aa47e5ce05db13ce0b467860","5471caacb87049d690684123ed013cef5909c0b4377af6b1919cc46b2e31637d","2ec8d4ce7fd6ef002e77bd325573b9dec9f4a7556b3c3b3a7ff39898fe2043a6","d007e3d42f08c0006ed4516fccb17369b87c820762e043cff7285bda341dcb34","25aa89c4268505e37c898894b7e04dbf8de3c06d1204fa15b2da7f4bec3ad5a5","d80745a9d39fabc11b3faef5cc8e8dbb712daaab517ad1242870ba4309119a7e","15c820101668e56ef794f21336363d7467f8f549c85cc01599e99bfe5a0c29e6","f3ddcd117ff4faaaee8d0604561eb085f63da00d7a953d11f21930835c76cd02","a87ffbdda4413b4da2862e0c25a7a5e342b5307cf336c53bbf1041964252800d","92064890039dc5846a179b1d4a7eb3f550238de5a10ab48b55dbf0dd4f09a990","32519fa312671f4101fe301e1c94ce8849fdd71da93589a8d6c799dd7ef8e7da","ef6eb67416f2a19cfb7f3f6a53d1398355eae58d2cea87cbf00dff8ec3b284cb","73f3e1bd2a71f0f2e50fa0c63ea4096a3f30195a9f5b8480325aa349a1125441","706dd2fd14c516757599462c90a31b4e016ba23e82f9ee24c9e0b0119deb94d4","4136a86776374388f0a0793fa9fbb8bd11f589398311e392b8f20d664e10de91","e5d018be8765b5f542762d538d0d89553746e54683a81d08c20d5c3a0f8f739f"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[13152,13175],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p13152"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"carrierFreq","paragraph_zero_based":13176},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the redirected NR frequency.","paragraph_zero_based":13177},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ssbSubcarrierSpacing","paragraph_zero_based":13178},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Subcarrier spacing of SSB in the redirected SSB frequency.","paragraph_zero_based":13179},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Only the following values are applicable depending on the used frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":13180},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR1:    15 or 30 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":13181},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR2-1:  120 or 240 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":13182},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR2-2:  120, 480, or 960 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":13183},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"smtc","paragraph_zero_based":13184},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The SSB periodicity/offset/duration configuration for the redirected SSB frequency. It is based on timing reference of PCell. If the field is absent, the UE uses the SMTC configured in the measObjectNR having the same SSB frequency and subcarrier spacing.","paragraph_zero_based":13185},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13186},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RAN-NotificationAreaInfo field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":13187},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cellList","paragraph_zero_based":13188},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A list of cells configured as RAN area.","paragraph_zero_based":13189},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ran-AreaConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":13190},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A list of RAN area codes or RA code(s) as RAN area.","paragraph_zero_based":13191},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13192},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PLMN-RAN-AreaConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":13193},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"plmn-Identity","paragraph_zero_based":13194},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PLMN Identity to which the cells in ran-Area belong. If the field is absent the UE not in SNPN access mode uses the ID of the registered PLMN. This field is not included for UE in SNPN access mode (for UE in SNPN access mode the ran-Area always belongs to the registered SNPN).","paragraph_zero_based":13195},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ran-AreaCodeList","paragraph_zero_based":13196},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The total number of RAN-AreaCodes of all PLMNs does not exceed 32.","paragraph_zero_based":13197},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ran-Area","paragraph_zero_based":13198},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether TA code(s) or RAN area code(s) are used for the RAN notification area. The network uses only TA code(s) or both TA code(s) and RAN area code(s) to configure a UE. The total number of TACs across all PLMNs does not exceed 16.","paragraph_zero_based":13199}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["7cd8aec608a56dd15f8af2e66fa4b3e1852c1abe6d435b89ba6abfe27fed334a","5e0f2e6c80a092a9e812b8b02713d9b3a6533c481363ca99eeadbf00c4b5b085","296660ccb9b9f6b208a05f016857ead8644879b39dc5642f601bd47b91b26b6d","9b421bd3491c2ab63d89d40efb3e1a9e9f09a0123c2eec05ad4673c362c918a1","c8dc22283f3dcd94d0106e112d692d4a71543ee5f93cf6aef7404b0aef1950b5","89be421b2b277184063f9c920c805a22418fa0d7ae0abbad33c127f86f599767","31696e05c7d9201e853d58038a7bc4277b9ade9671ec2a15f9378edbc28706ae","814e24f59ebac25b344831c896897c86181ba47d88d8f11b3ae27510f0b4665b","48b2d4ee6b0da01eb5e15403772146571df7bb9c4b012ab3fa2008c109c94bcc","54c0750c3f057ba481f01ec58ed23c95d956ee3360dacf839f7b65aa0543cb37","765da4febd357a2ac131f1f70f73c2ffa5d79fecd26fad6db34fb3bf24e2c213","5988a929541fa0cb4e67feebc3fa39826f998ae90923e35645f4f4b4b19a3592","4b37c0c80d3b26044d1aa5dd434f1a12a8093bfedacb27181ba546738170dcf0","141f6e516717dc4fa539bbcefea376cb59ea583adc1f27dc933e0992b1e55f21","853720ab2a4f3900889779f643f674cf723d087a06d12df3c65d7b768ffd7ddd","6367dc13945761035a35abbe2decf4749c2fbd66fe60f75e90737958dbabd164","ef9f3741b28b79d4afc9987a97cb494ce3a91177052f121591e6ceb09bc0482e","b1e303fef179bb2b88c66c2c421d6a5671e5bb94786c74ac1c987d1ac9c4a844","00facf2263aaa8840fc8541fad07ea8f4103bb0e0c1a6d3f9d32087146e796bb","cd2ab3ce29ae0055e4dbe01d6f70c412bd7e84cf8d0d032c412b17f3ebe894d2","618fb559eb932f6a03ae48fe4d9a7946ff03f250058e1feba117c1b8bf2d595a","a3df29615d4cb808043263924367fad18e75e52e679fa68e02f07fc0f8cfe793","e0926b9e9d3fc88262dbf002fe6b85caab2bc9053ca516a6bf831d097845b8df","4a2cb9050ad91f158f31ab3099379ab69b48cb1bf1fccbdc07d20887679c363a"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[13176,13199],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p13176"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13200},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PLMN-RAN-AreaCell field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":13201},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"plmn-Identity","paragraph_zero_based":13202},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PLMN Identity to which the cells in ran-AreaCells belong. If the field is absent the UE not in SNPN access mode uses the ID of the registered PLMN. This field is not included for UE in SNPN access mode (for UE in SNPN access mode the ran-AreaCells always belongs to the registered SNPN).","paragraph_zero_based":13203},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ran-AreaCells","paragraph_zero_based":13204},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The total number of cells of all PLMNs does not exceed 32.","paragraph_zero_based":13205},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13206},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SDT-Config field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":13207},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sdt-DRB-ContinueROHC","paragraph_zero_based":13208},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the PDCP entity of the radio bearers configured for SDT continues or resets the ROHC header compression protocol during PDCP re-establishment during SDT procedure, as specified in TS 38.323 [5]. Value cell indicates that ROHC header compression continues when the UE resumes for SDT in the same cell as the PCell when the RRCRelease message was received. Value rna indicates that ROHC header compression continues when the UE resumes for SDT in a cell belonging to the same RNA as the PCell where the RRCRelease message was received. If the field is absent, the UE releases any stored value for this field and the PDCP entity of the radio bearers configured for SDT always resets the ROHC header compression protocol during PDCP re-establishment when SDT procedure is initiated, as specified in TS 38.323 [5].","paragraph_zero_based":13209},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sdt-DRB-List","paragraph_zero_based":13210},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the ID(s) of the DRB(s) that are configured for SDT. If size of the sequence is zero, then the UE assumes that none of the DRBs are configured for SDT. The network only configures MN terminated MCG bearers for SDT.","paragraph_zero_based":13211},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sdt-SRB2-Indication","paragraph_zero_based":13212},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indiates whether SRB2 is configured for SDT or not.","paragraph_zero_based":13213},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13214},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SDT-MAC-PHY-CG-Config field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":13215},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cg-MT-SDT-MaxDurationToNext-CG-Occasion","paragraph_zero_based":13216},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The maximum duration until the next CG-SDT occasion as specified in TS 38.321 [3] for MT-SDT. If configured, the CG-SDT resource can only be used for the initial CG-SDT transmission if the duration between the initiation of the CG-SDT procedure and the next CG-SDT occasion is less than the value configured by this field.","paragraph_zero_based":13217},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cg-SDT-ConfigInitialBWP-DL","paragraph_zero_based":13218},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Downlink BWP configuration for CG-SDT. If a UE is an (e)RedCap UE and if the initialDownlinkBWP-RedCap is configured in downlinkConfigCommon in SIB1, this field is configured for initialDownlinkBWP-RedCap, otherwise it is configured for initialDownlinkBWP.","paragraph_zero_based":13219},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cg-SDT-ConfigInitialBWP-NUL","paragraph_zero_based":13220},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UL BWP configuration for CG-SDT on NUL carrier. If a UE is an (e)RedCap UE and if the initialUplinkBWP-RedCap is configured in uplinkConfigCommon in SIB1, this field is configured for initialUplinkBWP-RedCap, otherwise it is configured for initialUplinkBWP for NUL.","paragraph_zero_based":13221},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cg-SDT-ConfigInitialBWP-SUL","paragraph_zero_based":13222},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UL BWP configuration for CG-SDT on SUL carrier configured for the initialUplinkBWP for SUL.","paragraph_zero_based":13223}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["725cbcab02cda5215c0a8440614a50a4ca4ff3480bdf22fc3ab47125e78b1867","7f537982aae6677f7b42d5aea78631198f31d9e0eb1c771b1753f734a9e311a7","f0c10969d708e0d1f7b4164dd7977d910d64e251cced5247f7a895290c6aab17","3ff8b618f6b005e40ec7914c567cac0788927219aa6272f3a63a820a97c56954","ecf490a29a6f5a175525ef8b70572bf81a0b91cd4062219c35727729d0b73912","73e5be2ff16a7ee0c317b9ae343b5d821322858482bc48c694c47b1ae9dbb12e","25b43c3b7d714146e83808e781b827be78e28973082a53cd9850ec99ba3fee43","9d187692021d8e1b9ee5c6900f044d7b85bc352bc874cda13523d4b0f9ffdeaa","4d5ef9a666e2d69783620531b16d73c2e866f897b18812bafe0c767679f4db73","eea8d7ac132b7a1b48e07e22f602b706758c7b2fd3fa88bc776d601031683912","d5279a4947010974f9a1706a8daf664f8d1b79f4650823767a118c827ebaac5c","18b29a0db92e341a0bb952b64cbd5accdea691859187b12a833c37351ed3848f","2b2ed39f3b259be51c5a0453dd99d26f27acf1575deb9179a36e534d4a01295d","8cb100d1c885916fe9aaddc12fb1c22467806d091d4f6c32b12536fa5cbe3935","0025af680aecc088a99287b83dedabd3069d390774803126c648178e1cf459c2","6555681b343708be907f8a2effbad74a900a29317f107fe1b772b166ded46976","3077a694d534ca9c6c54f0eca4eb198a827cb113b44e1b5c81d09eda61f1f1b0","115ba9e38d989fffe132d064d96eb0136af127f370f1970be9f82664b26fb6fb","4c4d1fd476b46d4a607719f8baefc665711eff3f611b5d15d0262128c045fe39","455e7b0af4045f90093e92d5fcdd4973eb9727fb0cab1f4337946aee8b706f7a","11ee2f3261bb28433225d62a1d45c5de531e79eb4c04feb1f727a413e4245b7f","72a0ef845cd978dccfbe844e24286511526b306f567deb84a0ca6b707f091b27","e960786cb96c6ba20e89b51e3f4b0eca7735615904f53e60d4b875e59f35c41c","4c050e3d00bf4ed21d01a77ffca045f84947c2ac274f392817548dee62972738"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[13200,13223],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p13200"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cg-SDT-ConfigLCH-RestrictionToAddModList, cg-SDT-ConfigLCH-RestrictionToAddModListExt, cg-SDT-ConfigLCH-RestrictionToReleaseList","paragraph_zero_based":13224},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Lists for adding and releasing logical channel mapping restrictions for CG-SDT. If the network includes cg-SDT-ConfigLCH-RestrictionToAddModListExt, it includes the same number of entries, and listed in the same order, as in cg-SDT-ConfigLCH-RestrictionToAddModList.","paragraph_zero_based":13225},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cg-SDT-CS-RNTI","paragraph_zero_based":13226},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The CS-RNTI value for CG-SDT as specified in TS 38.321 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":13227},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cg-SDT-RSRP-ThresholdSSB","paragraph_zero_based":13228},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"An RSRP threshold configured for SSB selection for CG-SDT as specified in TS 38.321 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":13229},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cg-SDT-TA-ValidationConfig","paragraph_zero_based":13230},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configuration for the RSRP based TA validation. If this field is not configured, then the UE does not perform RSRP based TA validation.","paragraph_zero_based":13231},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cg-SDT-timeAlignmentTimer","paragraph_zero_based":13232},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TAT value for CG-SDT as specified in TS 38.321 [3]. The network always configures this field when sdt-MAC-PHY-CG-Config is configured.","paragraph_zero_based":13233},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13234},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CG-SDT-ConfigLCH-Restriction field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":13235},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"allowedCG-List","paragraph_zero_based":13236},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This restriction applies only when the UL grant is a configured grant for CG-SDT. If present, UL MAC SDUs from this logical channel can only be mapped to the indicated CG-SDT configured grant configuration. If the size of the sequence is zero, then UL MAC SDUs from this logical channel cannot be mapped to any CG-SDT configured grant configurations. If the field is not present, UL MAC SDUs from this logical channel can be mapped to any CG-SDT configured grant configurations. If the field configuredGrantType1Allowed is present, only those CG-SDT configured grant type 1 configurations indicated in this sequence are allowed for use by this logical channel; otherwise, this sequence shall not include any CG-SDT configured grant type 1 configuration. Corresponds to \"allowedCG-List\" as specified in TS 38.321 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":13237},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cg-SDT-MaxDurationToNext-CG-Occasion","paragraph_zero_based":13238},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The maximum duration until the next CG-SDT occasion for the logical channel identified by the logicalChannelIdentity as specified in TS 38.321 [3]. If configured, the CG-SDT resource can only be used for the initial CG-SDT transmission if the duration between the initiation of the CG-SDT procedure and the next CG-SDT occasion is less than the value configured by this field as specified in TS 38.321 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":13239},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"configuredGrantType1Allowed","paragraph_zero_based":13240},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If present, or if the capability lcp-Restriction as specified in TS 38.306 [26] is not supported, UL MAC SDUs from this logical channel can be transmitted on a configured grant type 1 for CG-SDT. Otherwise, UL MAC SDUs from this logical channel cannot be transmitted on a configured grant type 1 for CG-SDT. Corresponds to \"configuredGrantType1Allowed\" in TS 38.321 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":13241},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"logicalChannelIdentity","paragraph_zero_based":13242},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ID used commonly for the MAC logical channel and for the RLC bearer associated with a servedRadioBearer configured for SDT.","paragraph_zero_based":13243},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13244},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CG-SDT-TA-ValidationConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":13245},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cg-SDT-RSRP-ChangeThreshold","paragraph_zero_based":13246},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The RSRP threshold for TA validation for CG-SDT as specified in TS 38.321 [3]. Value dB2 corresponds to 2 dB, value dB4 corresponds to 4 dB and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":13247}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["71cb136216bd6e7d1790e77cf78c4d034290b8c6ed05875d03c56a9388884055","72d7c0f7b7a46c93fd17e94b52090afe803ade623506ae75f99abccef91a4d50","a9efbf837960413615f9535eaff5c251365bd078ac62f6c8caacac8b715df626","e04c7d26eb0ca68f17049a938575682e9aac066cc27ef063b50733af4d231cba","820abd975481f2e2117fd894d5b9bad99bff9655c44f8fc191fdd42f5a28a060","4373b5ddb687eacc6ea045ee7e427decce5527feb235037b2bfb05946bf79c2d","865477224a4673bb627141095568ef45f0a8b9f04c5059922799615ce6166735","88984e4cb85bb6dd56a2b8720751518f3ecde0f40f8340f22d6193bb03e9a70a","8b00dbe243f0ed463a6e1fab2aaff6cf5a675a96d5eccd28d2131f07181faad0","f59c4c1342edddad268288e33ca9069821f415b60d2845ebd3a1428b3dcbed7d","77929b1e3f5014c773f540319e4031022da110ed4ecafdcc69c94e8975b526e4","0a17f94c96d586f146f097127c51873800a439a1845314cef8db7fa94b9a54b5","12552f6e23b7864b72a8217ad196f251f636f510052b1478d80b3b2b2b9d64aa","9eac48f7465e140e45bc00ffc3fcf3d08c97d1e0acbcaf723b498d139c6e8705","4cfd7af9a9e7650deac30a3633b885466b5a8afaa15f1c3c4b483a9d96388ddf","4a00fe5c4035acc3ddbc4ef61856ae563471b4a459dcb36f0f37f59ddbcb2268","090c6cb210a2c5e8ee0c12262845906754bab5b6108ef37f2e3e7448192b2559","40029b0abe753e2e2c6d2f8865fdcb7b59b1557b1c17b6b987f87956eff19f46","2b87c0aec40e62a57fc4646383511a22a987b488cbe61db365bd63abb80518a7","6ee01580111d7d751b7c359494ed89bf779c6d048431ccd58ce3fbabc36c1273","ddb7817747a76b2e427b3ccb9bea3ba4063e1ac1de705781e1c94fca723806ca","c0fa55d9d16a38d220e98c140cc35524b02ff0b1391bc53c79a0b12be8dc46a5","6fec9a0518362ce3864ed4295e80dbc47f603f8ecd28b31174a582e7d767e3e5","a3fa7ceaad9725e82429184090dc0f3f4b58ab25bcaa1debac127b1d3a52622b"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[13224,13247],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p13224"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13248},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SRS-PosRRC-InactiveConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":13249},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"bwp-NUL","paragraph_zero_based":13250},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"BWP configuration for SRS for Positioning during the RRC_INACTIVE state in Normal Uplink Carrier. If the field is absent UE is configured with an SRS for Positioning associated with the initial UL BWP and transmitted, during the RRC_INACTIVE state, inside the initial UL BWP with the same CP and SCS as configured for initial UL BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":13251},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"bwp-SUL","paragraph_zero_based":13252},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"BWP configuration for SRS for Positioning during the RRC_INACTIVE state in Supplementary Uplink Carrier. If the field is absent UE is configured with an SRS for Positioning associated with the initial UL BWP and transmitted, during the RRC_INACTIVE state, inside the initial UL BWP with the same CP and SCS as configured for initial UL BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":13253},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"inactivePosSRS-RSRP-ChangeThreshold","paragraph_zero_based":13254},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RSRP threshold for the increase/decrease of RSRP for time alignment validation as specified in TS 38.321 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":13255},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"inactivePosSRS-TimeAlignmentTimer","paragraph_zero_based":13256},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TAT value for SRS for positioning transmission during RRC_INACTIVE state as specified in TS 38.321 [3]. The network always configures this field when srs-PosRRC-Inactive is configured.","paragraph_zero_based":13257},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"srs-PosConfigNUL","paragraph_zero_based":13258},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SRS for Positioning configuration in RRC_INACTIVE state in Normal Uplink Carrier.","paragraph_zero_based":13259},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"srs-PosConfigSUL","paragraph_zero_based":13260},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SRS for Positioning configuration in RRC_INACTIVE state in Supplementary Uplink Carrier.","paragraph_zero_based":13261},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"srs-PosResSetLinkedForAggBWInactiveList","paragraph_zero_based":13262},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the SRS resource sets across carriers which are linked for SRS bandwidth aggregation in RRC_INACTIVE state as defined in clause 6.2.1.4 of TS 38.214 [19].","paragraph_zero_based":13263},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"srs-PosRRC-AggBW-InactiveConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":13264},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SRS for positioning configuration with additional one or two carrier(s) configuration where the primary carrier is provided by srs-PosRRC-Inactive-r17 for bandwidth aggregation and to be used in RRC_INACTIVE state.","paragraph_zero_based":13265},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13266},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SRS-PosRRC-InactiveValidityAreaConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":13267},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"autonomousTA-AdjustmentEnabled","paragraph_zero_based":13268},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates that UE may adjust the TA value and stored RSRP autonomously after cell reselection within a validity area, if configured.","paragraph_zero_based":13269},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"bwp-NUL","paragraph_zero_based":13270},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"BWP configuration for SRS for Positioning during the RRC_INACTIVE state in Normal Uplink Carrier. If the field is absent UE is configured with an SRS for Positioning associated with the initial UL BWP and transmitted, during the RRC_INACTIVE state, inside the initial UL BWP with the same CP and SCS as configured for initial UL BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":13271}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e0d1c904668b8e3dc280b8d7dc44e45e81e79abdf0c5e7c27cb2b45b41dfc4ef","70e2f9df8038b913826a883098181c4bfdaba287833e9d4999d146e814bf7cd6","6363b2455841b20182115359a7549bc908a31188095e86ac83fe6ab21b36cb59","46037be6fa491f7684468dacb66c163e4f450f52f95536c81d1657823cc61882","cbe4b021caccaf0ba23906e34a6166843464b6b6a814a7d40edbec18884032a9","1a69406c0be38face0207947975b47b4e77ab0d6d117b13b51214ef698becd51","394a142ae636bd8abe68cba4aa9de2571bf8a748c52ce9e0e97002723e2de5a1","9f724fe45ea7ad87dfa0c3848cffeb5798b726f454dd93b801958637d511f0b9","bac5271e1595e7e08b9e69e4780056356c07fac68299a056a0192bb96fe44e26","4ce5dee79e9ab4cf5685462ad54365150f2778e673e05d680336697958da1494","24c871c8b7689fff3aa6388b173360dc50aaccd94ab4f1a151f7b6710b63c56b","be20b4e83f3542b9c8855c747535bf5fd22b14ed194566cec08ddff9ea5ff9d6","b37286ef408e0c22c22e4c3030f4bfbc95df38f982624b4dfa930fd3aa2690c1","87d6903fd73aa18a51de932bdb011412dd4e3855ac1960a8238347de3ed10cc7","632adcfb16a98205dd2a59642966f49d3ac5176d61e92412036bd59877af03c6","671a06ce48444f8b93318826ca975e3e06a803adda497d6febb9cd89fa404cb6","6e751f2ed3f5957c2cac66efa42b93106112a5cfb56bdeddca6d4fd3df9053fe","bb60537109a3a297157e7255a23c68ce64fab9d4b3c05228b2876c69840cccd1","90d207ef93f29ed415f70ebab4deb3dbebe1bff743ed487083831ed210bada7e","e584c3ee5a2f8740ca3aec81d9c04bcb468ebafe969eb37efe14d17f83c7b10c","3eadecb5229eb868dac3bce5b8f25fd3358f1c87eb20c588f30aa7827818eb36","e2026dff102b4eaa5cfc0e53d1df036f1fabd56a20dd1532cfeeff6ba8179ae0","af73c5f3fee6061622a85f4b9b8635bbc006920101cb7aedfdbd434a18b1e596","1a3507682c143c5ba3277882b4031f0ca658d94bdadf8852a569b76d596290d9"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[13248,13271],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p13248"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"bwp-SUL","paragraph_zero_based":13272},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"BWP configuration for SRS for Positioning during the RRC_INACTIVE state in Supplementary Uplink Carrier. If the field is absent UE is configured with an SRS for Positioning associated with the initial UL BWP and transmitted, during the RRC_INACTIVE state, inside the initial UL BWP with the same CP and SCS as configured for initial UL BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":13273},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"srs-PosRRC-InactiveValidityArea","paragraph_zero_based":13274},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Provides a list of cells where SRS Positioning Configuration in RRC_INACTIVE state is valid.","paragraph_zero_based":13275},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"inactivePosSRS-ValidityAreaTAT","paragraph_zero_based":13276},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Time alignment timer value for SRS for positioning transmission during RRC_INACTIVE state which is applicable in a validity area.","paragraph_zero_based":13277},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"inactivePosSRS-ValidityAreaRSRP","paragraph_zero_based":13278},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RSRP threshold for the increase/decrease of RSRP for validity area time alignment validation as specified in TS 38.321 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":13279},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13280},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SuspendConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":13281},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ncd-SSB-RedCapInitialBWP-SDT","paragraph_zero_based":13282},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates that the UE uses the RedCap-specific initial DL BWP associated with the NCD-SSB for SDT. The network configures this field if an (e)RedCap UE is configured with SDT in the RedCap-specific initial DL BWP not associated with CD-SSB. If configured, the NCD-SSB indicated by this field can only be used during the SDT procedure for CG-SDT or RA-SDT. In the MIB associated with this NCD-SSB, the systemFrameNumber field indicates the frame boundary and frame number of the NCD-SSB. The subCarrierSpacingCommon and dmrs-TypeA-Position field in the MIBs associated with CD-SSB and NCD-SSB in the same cell are configured with the same values, respectively.","paragraph_zero_based":13283},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ran-ExtendedPagingCycle","paragraph_zero_based":13284},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The extended DRX (eDRX) cycle for RAN-initiated paging to be applied by the UE as defined in TS 38.304 [20]. Value rf256 corresponds to 256 radio frames, value rf512 corresponds to 512 radio frames and so on. Value of the field indicates an eDRX cycle which is shorter or equal to the IDLE mode eDRX cycle configured for the UE.","paragraph_zero_based":13285},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ran-ExtendedPagingCycleConfig","paragraph_zero_based":13286},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The extended DRX (eDRX) configuraiton for RAN-initiated paging to be applied by the UE when the eDRX cycle for RAN-initiated paging is longer than 10.24s.","paragraph_zero_based":13287},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ran-NotificationAreaInfo","paragraph_zero_based":13288},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Network ensures that the UE in RRC_INACTIVE always has a valid ran-NotificationAreaInfo.","paragraph_zero_based":13289},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ran-PagingCycle","paragraph_zero_based":13290},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Refers to the UE specific cycle for RAN-initiated paging. Value rf32 corresponds to 32 radio frames, value rf64 corresponds to 64 radio frames and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":13291},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"resumeIndication","paragraph_zero_based":13292},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates that the UE shall trigger the RRC connection resume procedure after receiving this RRCRelease message, as specified in clause 5.3.8.3. The network only includes this field in the RRCRelease message used to terminate an ongoing SDT procedure.","paragraph_zero_based":13293},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-UEIdentityRemote","paragraph_zero_based":13294},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the C-RNTI to the L2 U2N Remote UE.","paragraph_zero_based":13295}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["9fd52d103846e48ec111b8c9a22ef4f1048ee46f68c9e5b1212f64b74325252d","374793d2005cb11c1496ad85ca1333b962367d654576458a13c8a1600788856c","abfcb11ea3029a79a2efaf2fb3456e373f1dfc125e7324d038209cc599455079","fc79ee1dc7ce6fe8143ae708bc8f5b20aded54addcf9b797dfe99a1a3ebccd76","7a63ed394f2c3bca0976f50d03c3de14f7bbd8bcc769099a3ea176492bf6d41c","6c1082312de5d8dff0e036503c9170504167a3601eec73d17edbb3f27b413fff","30135f603565d72a3df85739fed0cb05e01648de2dcc0603d8ef5e2fb7c82761","13086e54cc3d915930b5fdc8f4791c2e51c872acdeb883b35297a8d35b2a4711","4119ec022c4e87a44ecc6b689ac5ec97f27f2ffe5e4184f16c09f2a2f6e9ed1b","b9096e420d66fe961e2aef483d1a9bcaaafe3c2e8f8fa65d16cbf363ab7a62a3","c49b1f0d45703f44afe1598390c2922e0c6f6748e5e0ec63825dbfa3cc3556c0","5a5b0cf140347c92a39c6c234c81885be6480a6107659204b427888ed9849c59","47b95d78d86c4e10ebaad58b5637d83fbefd8bbde345fd0aabede7cdf492a814","4c8a4996558ae194ff9192d9746faa9feaf9111c81b258e3cc5757d303c7ef28","ab3bdfbe7c285769d449db21e4b289a3462897f807a72e8cbbfde01280738d32","ffd711ac0559b10e0587ffae85ddcad299457b68406ce2c3ef77cdf5fd31001a","90c033470a21bb04c9961b11f097c6a1ad71671cb121f5106a6581aa116e0c2d","f2966cc69ed6fceb95b2eb0be5fff67f3e33501e13ced4bc73a5b55dd83d0f57","23bbdc061e38792b0ec90b2d17d10532a590da9066f47d0930462336d8477d8a","64a61f9b5ab0251048b63d547fef2955fe784068f2dab7578c4fb31574509b99","1c7632eb0c00a9afe96850adcfb164256fd698be8e44c0026b7b0f3e4266e491","bbcbbedb190363def9cd817f9a2bc010d8f320ce4c4c0ea9a586fa1561f1a31d","986cdfe9025701797dd793b12a8dd648633a3e620a4f2632f1abf1271e99240f","d4b48c8333ffe031b22710169245b99212e26f91540aacab1bffd3a1eea763d2"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[13272,13295],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p13272"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"t380","paragraph_zero_based":13296},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Refers to the timer that triggers the periodic RNAU procedure in UE. Value min5 corresponds to 5 minutes, value min10 corresponds to 10 minutes and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":13297},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13298},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MulticastConfigInactive field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":13299},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"inactivePTM-Config","paragraph_zero_based":13300},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates PTM configuration for MBS multicast reception in RRC_INACTIVE in the serving cell. If absent, UE considers all joined multicast sessions can be received in RRC_INACTIVE.","paragraph_zero_based":13301},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"inactiveMCCH-Config","paragraph_zero_based":13302},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates multicast MCCH/MTCH configuration for MBS multicast reception in RRC_INACTIVE in the serving cell. Only SIB24 is allowed to be included.","paragraph_zero_based":13303},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13304},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ExtendedPagingCycleConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":13305},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"extendedPagingCycle","paragraph_zero_based":13306},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The eDRX cycle longer than 10.24 s for RAN-initiated paging to be applied by the UE. Value hf2 corresponds to 2 hyper frames, value hf4 corresponds to 4 hyper frames and so on. Value of the field is shorter than or equal to the IDLE mode eDRX cycle configured for the UE.","paragraph_zero_based":13307},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pagingPTWLength","paragraph_zero_based":13308},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The length of paging transmission window for RAN-initiated paging to be applied by the UE as defined in TS 38.304 [20]. Value ms1280 corresponds to 1280 miliseconds, value ms2560 corresponds to 2560 miliseconds and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":13309},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13310},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":13311},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":13312},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"L2RemoteUE","paragraph_zero_based":13313},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present for L2 U2N Remote UE's RNAU; otherwise it is absent.","paragraph_zero_based":13314},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RANPaging","paragraph_zero_based":13315},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is optionally present, Need R, if the UE is configured with IDLE eDRX, see TS 24.501 [23]; otherwise the field is not present.","paragraph_zero_based":13316},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Redirection2","paragraph_zero_based":13317},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is optionally present, Need R, if redirectedCarrierInfo is included; otherwise the field is not present.","paragraph_zero_based":13318},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":13319}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["a421313cd7823a34fd989e6037d7bf4eb7666694b7e93270b877d1dfdbdd9b69","399f1884f6991677d1d22010b8370768a1f14eccacfd1ac56ba7bc10d44e9855","148f80e00a8491a435b2c8989bbd3c5866997f3dfa17cea657bef3bd636aefc7","602fcda230daae1616944345a1d198d4200f4680a917b03e08f4110021763e53","428ccaba18a7020a9b4077fa5a4b54c88a1317fa110df5881c9195980b822d69","8156391a2f83818f28d74e770e86649cfccb55c3ee67a261