7656},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"distanceThresh","paragraph_zero_based":17657},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Distance from the serving cell reference location and is used in location-based measurement initiation in RRC_IDLE and RRC_INACTIVE, as defined in TS 38.304 [20]. Each step represents 50m. This field is only present in an NTN cell.","paragraph_zero_based":17658},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"movingReferenceLocation","paragraph_zero_based":17659},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reference location of the serving cell of an NTN Earth moving system at a time reference. It is used in the evaluation of eventD2 and condEventD2 criteria for the serving cell in RRC_CONNECTED, and location-based measurement initiation in RRC_IDLE and RRC_INACTIVE when distanceThresh is also configured, as defined in TS 38.304 [20]. The time reference of this field is indicated by epochTime in ntn-Config of the serving cell. This field is excluded when determining changes in system information, i.e., changes to movingReferenceLocation should neither result in system information change notifications nor in a modification of valueTag in SIB1. This field is only present in an NTN cell.","paragraph_zero_based":17660},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ntn-Config","paragraph_zero_based":17661},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Provides parameters needed for the UE to access NR via NTN access such as Ephemeris data, common TA parameters, k_offset, validity duration for UL sync information and epoch. In a TN cell, this field is only present in ntn-NeighCellConfigList and ntn-NeighCellConfigListExt.","paragraph_zero_based":17662},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ntn-NeighCellConfigList, ntn-NeighCellConfigListExt","paragraph_zero_based":17663}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["03bf59e63c759e2393f842768f2607e8e4482c25cc999be1e760939cc92cd45e","6b8596d85ea7e57b8f3b20e482c30ab32efd1816b192fe39078f5a0cf52fa150","6fd3fc5f120b587e9b0b1faf848b203ae0e7ba68fa0d897b5ed88e1009d925b8","0603b49501cac15c6ec4daa6ab5ef8c9b94df2dc7be34fc8250a93d61ddc1215","9a104d553ff58e3042251f193954cdea83face52e97066e2a5aab014f8f17168","630718da52af9741386f7bab2a1f331e5199bef3ee5ca4411aa41497e571214a","61b16dc4e263707d0937159ba2e2b9429214f5e5c4e78fcec785b1bd44cb85a3","9dfc1ef1de514cea58812291c4112b11cf915d2aeba9630bb245b1bf86d1dff0","1fdc26af129c75c1dec86de2da932cac3a6746b1c4c8177bbd06e706e62e0375","3dc0ae31ed5c64b2408d7ee35e606ca5ee8aa15680ec0d5b9e8ae2be21c23aec","f2d4d1d8993a6b3f2963466ccfdfce21a4c86cffd644838e279bc47fcdaf3e71","93f42e693dcd56ee751886a0c303f4f356b9a89ed4e4a6a9258370ab08ac64dc","ece83d889983f35fb2e3d77955774acacbbe738726ef9357c4bc92f8dec79897","ce7e45d96e884ecd7b6c912a6241a9044bf35e123cdc57ab452c28c64869be43","9a7d016d7db2bdfaf168a895a43dfcd5676fc004ad38cd3b111ed3b7bc05a189","4ba9ee4998180774bfcba9e02104496b150160bb8d96915e9dec705ca186910d","fa6ff5b7f4789e9a19f179eea26c932527451a71375071659c5cfa8690c521d7","038b4d3aadbe9b8161f6823cff450ac1ab33739785044a62f1f603280621c0a1","e659aa4ecac94c88d75e83366657e3d55823f24246c6ea6269145e423356c98c","e1a99ca12904f16fe72f02187c32b82ef55b85197aeb7bc775eeba3372e3dc85","6d24be794737213e54dd0fc3c9ee1189083a0216f1be1267a135b4282a348182","b7920f7ad5f8afe800cdd6a74d8d78873aa4ab09b36ebad67117017745f318e8","099d2098cb7ee606cca70dc88f162b7a2535ddb1739714463fd5ddf0e57a34e5","eda54305d1f7cb725f314b4461ae8afed967b90466fae2224d297beaad99bedb"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[17640,17663],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p17640"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Provides a list of NTN neighbour cells including their ntn-Config, carrier frequency and PhysCellId. This set includes all elements of ntn-NeighCellConfigList and all elements of ntn-NeighCellConfigListExt. If ntn-Config is absent for an entry in ntn-NeighCellConfigListExt, the ntn-Config provided in the entry at the same position in ntn-NeighCellConfigList applies. Network provides ntn-Config for the first entry of ntn-NeighCellConfigList. If the ntn-Config is absent for any other entry in ntn-NeighCellConfigList, the ntn-Config provided in the previous entry in ntn-NeighCellConfigList applies.","paragraph_zero_based":17664},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"referenceLocation","paragraph_zero_based":17665},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reference location of the serving cell provided via NTN quasi-Earth fixed system and is used in location-based measurement initiation in RRC_IDLE and RRC_INACTIVE, as defined in TS 38.304 [20]. This field is only present in an NTN cell.","paragraph_zero_based":17666},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"satSwitchWithReSync","paragraph_zero_based":17667},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Provides parameters for the target satellite required to perform satellite switch with resynchronization. This field is only present in an NTN cell and its presence indicates that satellite switch without PCI change is supported in the cell.","paragraph_zero_based":17668},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"t-Service","paragraph_zero_based":17669},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the time information on when a cell provided via NTN system is going to stop serving the area it is currently covering. This field applies for both service link switches in NTN quasi-Earth fixed system and feeder link switches for both NTN quasi-Earth fixed and Earth moving system. The field indicates a time in multiples of 10 ms after 00:00:00 on Gregorian calendar date 1 January, 1900 (midnight between Sunday, December 31, 1899 and Monday, January 1, 1900). The exact stop time is between the time indicated by the value of this field minus 1 and the time indicated by the value of this field. The reference point for t-Service is the uplink time synchronization reference point of the cell. This field is only present in an NTN cell.","paragraph_zero_based":17670},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":17671},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NTN-CovEnh field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":17672},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"numberOfMsg4-RepetitionsList","paragraph_zero_based":17673},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The number of repetitions for PUCCH transmission for Msg4 HARQ-ACK, see clause 9.2.6 in TS 38.213 [13]. The value {n1} needs to be configured with another value from the list {n2, n4, n8}. If more than one value is configured, a single value from the configured values is indicated in DCI.","paragraph_zero_based":17674},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"rsrp-ThresholdMsg4","paragraph_zero_based":17675},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This threshold used by the UE for determining the report of the capability of PUCCH repetition for Msg4 HARQ-ACK if numberOfMsg4-RepetitionsList is provided, as specified in TS 38.321 [3]. ","paragraph_zero_based":17676},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":17677},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"satSwitchWithReSync field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":17678},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ssb-TimeOffset","paragraph_zero_based":17679},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the time offset between the SSB from source and target satellite at the uplink time synchronization reference point. It is given in number of subframes.","paragraph_zero_based":17680},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"t-ServiceStart","paragraph_zero_based":17681},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the time information on when the target satellite is going to start serving the area currently covered by the serving satellite. The field indicates a time in multiples of 10 ms after 00:00:00 on Gregorian calendar date 1st January 1900 (midnight between Sunday, December 31, 1899, and Monday, January 1, 1900). The exact start time is between the time indicated by the value of this field minus 1 and the time indicated by the value of this field. The reference point for t-ServiceStart is the uplink time synchronization reference point of the serving satellite.","paragraph_zero_based":17682},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":17683},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SIB20","paragraph_zero_based":17684},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SIB20 contains the information required to acquire the MCCH/MTCH configuration for MBS broadcast.","paragraph_zero_based":17685},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SIB20 information element","paragraph_zero_based":17686},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":17687}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ebba7d11a29e80a1318d28f1717aea1aeb1fc46a37c34b18b0f3657942110280","b00b1926c22a3e8e861b94cbf190a79db3dd2f22da0874207e464f9d7255e841","d64178f9783720cb4610e5a6a4159af8807020bdc0186c61b71cada920b5967c","42fae8170933d5e6b9d6d86ce39950bec1fd6479b9f619eb610da897ab1f07d8","1f957e674d776e4a512378550fd59e18541c28fa4c4ab8268666501dc3f6c75c","4d6527b76ad9051eb3dc9e12e2ec4ea5c8483ad3a809d2743eb36ae0d77216be","bba7c8a53c184dc93771794a270d65a99f4ebd0f77686af65e588b5e28110af3","f5d257f982caf08978b41ad72b523fa15a9b1bb6c4305d0e94cf7ce1e367b82d","f64523