{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    }                                                                                                     OPTIONAL, -- Cond SecondCSICMR","paragraph_zero_based":21216},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    csi-ReportSubConfigTriggerList-r18  CSI-ReportSubConfigTriggerList-r18                                OPTIONAL   -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":21217},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ]]","paragraph_zero_based":21218},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":21219},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":21220},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-CSI-APERIODICTRIGGERSTATELIST-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":21221},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":21222},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":21223},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-AperiodicTriggerState field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":21224},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ltm-AssociatedReportConfigInfo","paragraph_zero_based":21225},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field configures the aperiodic CSI reports of LTM candidate cells. If ltm-associatedReportConfigInfo is configured the UE shall ignore the field associatedReportConfigInfoList.","paragraph_zero_based":21226},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":21227},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-AssociatedReportConfigInfo field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":21228},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ap-CSI-MultiplexingMode","paragraph_zero_based":21229},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates if the behavior of transmitting aperiodic CSI on the first PUSCH repetitions corresponding to two SRS resource sets configured in srs-ResourceSetToAddModList or srs-ResourceSetToAddModListDCI-0-2 with usage 'codebook' or 'noncodebook' is enabled or not.","paragraph_zero_based":21230},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"applyIndicatedTCI-State, applyIndicatedTCI-State2","paragraph_zero_based":21231},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates, for an aperiodic CSI-RS resource set (perSet) or for CSI-RS resource (perResource), if UE applies the first or the second \"indicated\" DL only TCI or joint TCI as specified in TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.5. If more than one value for the field coresetPoolIndex is configured in the DL BWP used to trigger the CSI report, the value 'first' corresponds to the \"indicated\" joint/DL TCI states specific to coresetPoolIndex value 0 and the value 'second' correspond to the value 1, respectively. The applyIndicatedTCI-State is for ResourcesForChannel, and applyIndicatedTCI-State2 is for ResourcesForChannels2.","paragraph_zero_based":21232},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"csi-IM-ResourcesForInterference","paragraph_zero_based":21233},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-IM-ResourceSet for interference measurement. Entry number in csi-IM-ResourceSetList in the CSI-ResourceConfig indicated by csi-IM-ResourcesForInterference in the CSI-ReportConfig indicated by reportConfigId above (value 1 corresponds to the first entry, value 2 to the second entry, and so on). The indicated CSI-IM-ResourceSet should have exactly the same number of resources like the NZP-CSI-RS-ResourceSet indicated in resourceSet within nzp-CSI-RS.","paragraph_zero_based":21234},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"csi-ReportSubConfigTriggerList","paragraph_zero_based":21235},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A list of sub-configuration ID(s) of N sub-configurations out of L configured sub-configurations within a CSI-ReportConfig associated with a triggering state for aperiodic CSI reporting on PUSCH.","paragraph_zero_based":21236},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"csi-SSB-ResourceSet, csi-SSB-ResourceSet2","paragraph_zero_based":21237},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-SSB-ResourceSet for channel measurements. Entry number in csi-SSB-ResourceSetList in the CSI-ResourceConfig indicated by resourcesForChannelMeasurement in the CSI-ReportConfig indicated by reportConfigId above (value 1 corresponds to the first entry, value 2 to the second entry, and so on).","paragraph_zero_based":21238},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"nzp-CSI-RS-ResourcesForInterference","paragraph_zero_based":21239}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["d541570257cad6eef0e6cea8f4f9e2f4c7c10183fa3576ea36541e7cfb8608d1","a232acbba236e07ac6dc648fc19f697a5dfaf74934cb758b7a1a3ced72274cc4","f9bf8a8843ae575cfd47d31501802018f8d22a5c7669fec8e07fd686c22c57de","4c0117be15819a458290e915d3825206aca8eb367a94f9cfd7cc5baca757164b","515a65a8215ee1d65d79d86898c30837c754f10ec7933230bb8b8a7d70fbc04a","ffcc24b5f6b520a54d4e850ef291f6ff63379292bc7d2bfd3bdef886c82edef0","5c09ba53b7d4040dae382986a8aca4c9b3fcc2a68987bc872e911b32836f3d03","6b191d75de2c6fa41c43233399ea00d74cd581974beb8036274c7d7b612aa86c","d579ad36aaf8d036526804c50b82cd38c00dc01a93e261dc056262f61998ac2f","8efee59532feb59dd40bbf2b80776a4b724900fed6f4bf73a4c5dee71c72ed55","b000909a0cd6e58054d32300d0fc2319178e184e61989c174ddd2ee6f3c4cdb6","34de49a598340575a8c1a6c978a37b6196232a172c3e931dd1a7b4ada0d29784","7852b2c11fbbd541a087eb04c3a1092fed78ca8a997a5270061f8711e672f73f","8a7d3fea4f52c4eb928768b97b92797b2dabb3d51e3714e0b282aef37d755898","ef0d92f0f35c20130954da00139f970490f85a5213bd84e9a22e0e8337859500","595bf1c7df0a96dcfc96466daee33bbf84e542f2919411ec7857e169084a1e93","03429f934b29b6055176994c47f47db3fcd4c6f0e891d53eba99d3db61e20b07","e670d95f0d817a97bbb6052b1cfad0c245d1ee88c4747e15a9639078c5cd930a","d092d38e5d2ec73563f905558a00e63d280573e5d7c5628c1de2c8e8784afc7e","ac3b4395f91117327dddfa6544111c1a0ef6079d99a1f20e0517e2c1df8382fe","9df1e2e51c4bacae564bb6a01d0a169f509453bc1a6dffe4c160a4ad096a575c","5369bd62577b6008eb11f8771739eeb1bffa6f562e9d31d0bde23781acee2617","165de2587b85e22f7733b8ef7a6343ca5c1cb8b0e3fac05e304b9bf0c2b92cfd","1d5dc41e02b890138a6d380b790c91ee826e0a0f3c0b2197dd82393a424acf0a"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[21216,21239],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p21216"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NZP-CSI-RS-ResourceSet for interference measurement. Entry number in nzp-CSI-RS-ResourceSetList in the CSI-ResourceConfig indicated by nzp-CSI-RS-ResourcesForInterference in the CSI-ReportConfig indicated by reportConfigId above (value 1 corresponds to the first entry, value 2 to the second entry, and so on). ","paragraph_zero_based":21240},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"qcl-info, qcl-info2","paragraph_zero_based":21241},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of references to TCI-States for providing the QCL source and QCL type for each NZP-CSI-RS-Resource listed in nzp-CSI-RS-Resources of the NZP-CSI-RS-ResourceSet indicated by resourceSet within nzp-CSI-RS. Each TCI-StateId refers to the TCI-State which has this value for tci-StateId and is defined in tci-StatesToAddModList or in dl-OrJointTCI-StateList in the PDSCH-Config included in the BWP-Downlink corresponding to the serving cell and to the DL BWP to which the resourcesForChannelMeasurement (in the CSI-ReportConfig indicated by reportConfigId above) belong to. First entry in qcl-info corresponds to first entry in nzp-CSI-RS-Resources of that NZP-CSI-RS-ResourceSet, second entry in qcl-info corresponds to second entry in nzp-CSI-RS-Resources, and so on (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.2.1.5.1). When this field is absent for aperiodic CSI RS, and applyIndicatedTCI-State or applyIndicatedTCI-State2 is not configured, the UE shall use QCL information included in the  \"indicated\" DL only/Joint TCI state as specified in TS 38.214 [19].","paragraph_zero_based":21242},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"reportConfigId","paragraph_zero_based":21243},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The reportConfigId of one of the CSI-ReportConfigToAddMod configured in CSI-MeasConfig","paragraph_zero_based":21244},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"resourcesForChannel2","paragraph_zero_based":21245},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configures reference signals for channel measurement corresponding to the second resource set for L1-RSRP measurement as configured in IE CSI-ResourceConfig when nrofReportedGroups-r17 is configured in IE CSI-ReportConfig. If this is present, network configures csi-SSB-ResourceSetExt instead of csi-SSB-ResourceSet and the UE ignores csi-SSB-ResourceSet in resourcesForChannel, and the resourcesForChannel configures the reference signals for channel measurement corresponding to the first resource set for L1-RSRP measurement (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.2.1.4).","paragraph_zero_based":21246},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"resourcesForChannelTDCP","paragraph_zero_based":21247},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configures reference signals for channel measurement corresponding to the second resource set and third resource set for TDCP reporting. All CSI resources of these two resource sets always share the same QCL-info with the resource sets indicated by resourcesForChannel as spcified in TS 38.214 [19].","paragraph_zero_based":21248},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"resourceSet","paragraph_zero_based":21249},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NZP-CSI-RS-ResourceSet for channel measurements. Entry number in nzp-CSI-RS-ResourceSetList in the CSI-ResourceConfig indicated by resourcesForChannelMeasurement in the CSI-ReportConfig indicated by reportConfigId above (value 1 corresponds to the first entry, value 2 to the second entry, and so on).","paragraph_zero_based":21250},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":21251},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":21252},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":21253},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Aperiodic","paragraph_zero_based":21254},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present if the NZP-CSI-RS-Resources in the associated resourceSet have the resourceType aperiodic and unifiedTCI-StateType is not configured. The field is optionally present, Need R, if the NZP-CSI-RS-Resources in the associated resourceSet have the resourceType aperiodic and unifiedTCI-StateType is configured. The field is absent otherwise.","paragraph_zero_based":21255},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-IM-ForInterference","paragraph_zero_based":21256},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is mandatory present if the CSI-ReportConfig identified by reportConfigId is configured with csi-IM-ResourcesForInterference; otherwise it is absent.","paragraph_zero_based":21257},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NZP-CSI-RS-ForInterference","paragraph_zero_based":21258},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is mandatory present if the CSI-ReportConfig identified by reportConfigId is configured with nzp-CSI-RS-ResourcesForInterference; otherwise it is absent.","paragraph_zero_based":21259},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SecondCSICMR","paragraph_zero_based":21260},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is optionally present, Need R, if resourcesForChannel2 is configured with aperiodic CSI-RS. It is absent otherwise.","paragraph_zero_based":21261},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TDCP","paragraph_zero_based":21262},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is absent if resourcesForChannel2 is configured. It is optionally present, Need R, otherwise.","paragraph_zero_based":21263}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["0fe5aff224cd93e50b559f6b6a6f4e231cc96052102afc64da34cdd3c87b3587","dad4fb9787ac9623dc20d72dcbb1b5ef9b152fc5944904429915c4f2436bc7f8","4b5090219248ee89c135a4aefeab5d27876bce179d168f859b00f946abe47962","4ca9a674d34db47e528e9dc44a7f3733bfaf43d132e81529ac63597fcb4cae01","015d2bc9257605d6ea0bce9f6b7d0449d9f71ebc78defb85a02bef0b56c2fc49","f8fdee51ceeb827c3b19a5290320fb08780d3b526311ff911fbf6fc5905b4c95","c01b8eff1ec4e998cc0958a89cf74591f45b9848ab64f73cc98c75204079e2c7","d6ec05c775c6e875d0dd775baedcbd8975b93b56de34ae3a3972621d552ea6b1","c7e6bbdef529527152cfa59edbfc1fb6242c56fd9ff7da1bfbf06753ab9c5c9a","f9a5bb714b8e13fb8cc4b0cdaaaca7ea81325ca70f9102a8eff426c036b05c8f","19f65f812e4a355c66e683d93337b4d68ae9d92230235a1d1c936fda482617ab","26baf948920882148e138cdf0040227e69d143f5e1020d62fd33b88dd395238d","5773cfa70d9f751b5f6afda406e99449e4d645f26131725a6c884c833513b221","bbda7f1e4f58f26424c281b2974af80790a60786eeb8dfc33038078d9a45000c","fac3c36101164cecba77b8cb135522b9cdfcf1077aa7a193daa9a4c0f6ba0ff8","91812bef34a6e8eb15c2af22af75941cbee03c6b39168e72ac27cbda5ba1d33f","4c8e061f971ffa6cd8efbb03f79e87bd012f79e9c87d37cde01d2ec73c0e87ef","c7514d00307eb45047d622e75f49bc6f5f9e1c3acb4dad3874411841ceb66a53","46fd49a3b79ff690da16d1deb165c9712760f0ca7acf562baeaa8aaed964076f","7c598abeadab7bf38f8b296d9f37eab4b6fbe8fe4cd307db83785a30e7244871","467ea79a0d437741e6c23936615131d5de64f7d33c27e951357887086c9c28f5","02385f3d96ca0ac6b1ed2b4ae3ee4b1f8b238621b57a6ca956d32a8d8137eb95","8781909e8e7ac571fa42bf9f82e6da4c193188ff2345db875e0ac7dac2dab050","bfeded0477ffc7de1cfc33195b9c5f81f83116d051251d1d178767137c3ecb34"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[21240,21263],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx:p21240"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":21264},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–CSI-FrequencyOccupation","paragraph_zero_based":21265},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE CSI-FrequencyOccupation is used to configure the frequency domain occupation of a channel state information measurement resource (e.g. NZP-CSI-RS-Resource, CSI-IM-Resource).","paragraph_zero_based":21266},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-FrequencyOccupation information element","paragraph_zero_based":21267},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":21268},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-CSI-FREQUENCYOCCUPATION-START","paragraph_zero_based":21269},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":21270},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-FrequencyOccupation ::=         SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":21271},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    startingRB                          INTEGER (0..maxNrofPhysicalResourceBlocks-1),","paragraph_zero_based":21272},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    nrofRBs                             INTEGER (24..maxNrofPhysicalResourceBlocksPlus1),","paragraph_zero_based":21273},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ...","paragraph_zero_based":21274},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":21275},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":21276},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-CSI-FREQUENCYOCCUPATION-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":21277},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":21278},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":21279},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-FrequencyOccupation field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":21280},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"nrofRBs","paragraph_zero_based":21281},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Number of PRBs across which this CSI resource spans. Only multiples of 4 are allowed. The smallest configurable number is the minimum of 24 and the width of the associated BWP. If the configured value is larger than the width of the corresponding BWP, the UE shall assume that the actual CSI-RS bandwidth is equal to the width of the BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":21282},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"startingRB","paragraph_zero_based":21283},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PRB where this CSI resource starts in relation to common resource block #0 (CRB#0) on the common resource block grid. Only multiples of 4 are allowed (0, 4, ...)","paragraph_zero_based":21284},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":21285},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–CSI-IM-Resource","paragraph_zero_based":21286},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE CSI-IM-Resource is used to configure one CSI Interference Management (IM) resource.","paragraph_zero_based":21287}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["31a6a00bbb658c32d7100a2050f80b06231b27fa286b1658906b318273fad5b1","2cff206542246cd11caa716a66ab4cf5f968cc43e3f5d70e5d07045e9429449c","e4db8d6130416f56ea5a25f57faba4262495d89db0eccbedb39c819f54ac91be","c5b96af6de07c88ebb1b26dbe92f6a63a996ec5fd1d6e059efeed9beef00cb25","407dd98b73ad45004490270085e77aac5316b18215ede6bc290c514a9293aa06","51d956ad4ec41d3faa32512b78ef9150b8fef6dfeb95c9f1c3d3051f12a5858d","62c345c929f5806d55d727886a052f5ed62aec04addfa4988dfd2d155e3e4576","c1cec226826a3e3bdd0fd9a94e7ec2274eb442e19a9cebbdf82c21dfedcec584","b7b228c344a958d63b3a8ba41e00361db68e21e3d618cdd0767ed4e75320cf13","88cc95e23cef2b023fef7f107ed17a6cc4e31f77bd8a6897413d0320a65d2f4e","f61b72c9