{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":21768},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NZP-CSI-RS-ResourceIndex-r18 ::= INTEGER (0..maxNrofNZP-CSI-RS-ResourcesPerSet-1-r18)","paragraph_zero_based":21769},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":21770},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-CSI-REPORTSUBCONFIG-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":21771},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":21772},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":21773},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-ReportSubConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":21774},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"codebookSubConfig","paragraph_zero_based":21775},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Applicable codebook parameters for the ports indicated by portSubsetIndicator. Applicable value ranges for codebook subset restriction, rank restriction, N1, N2, and Ng and twoTX-CodebookSubsetRestriction follow existing specification according to the codebookConfig configured within the CSI-ReportConfig, and apply for the number of ports determined by portSubsetIndicator (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.2.1.4.1). In this field, the network always sets the codebookType to type1.","paragraph_zero_based":21776},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"non-PMI-PortIndication","paragraph_zero_based":21777},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Port indication for RI/CQI calculation applicable only for non-PMI feedback. The field shall be configured only if the portSubsetIndicator-r18 is configured.","paragraph_zero_based":21778},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A port indication for each rank R, indicating which R ports out of P ports to use within the sub-configuration. P corresponds to the number of bits with value 1 in the bitmap portSubsetIndicator-r18.","paragraph_zero_based":21779},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"nzp-CSI-RS-ResourceList","paragraph_zero_based":21780},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of NZP CSI RS resources for the sub-configuration that is a (sub)set of NZP CSI-RS resource(s) of the CSI-RS resource set for channel measurement associated with the sub-configuration in the CSI report configuration. Value 0 refers to the first NZP CSI RS resource of the CSI-RS resource set, value 1 refers to the second NZP CSI RS resource of the CSI-RS resource set, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":21781},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"port-SubsetIndicator","paragraph_zero_based":21782},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the number of ports of the NZP CSI-RS resources indicated in nzp-CSI-RS-ResourceList and the (sub)set of CSI-RS antenna ports used for CSI calculation of the sub-configuration. In the bit string, each bit corresponds to an antenna port. When a bit is set to 1, the corresponding port is enabled for CSI calculation corresponding to the sub-configuration. When the bit is set to zero, the corresponding port is not enabled for CSI calcualton corresponding to the sub-configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":21783},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"powerOffset","paragraph_zero_based":21784},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When powerControlOffset is configured in a NZP CSI-RS resources indicated by nzp-CSI-RS-Resources, the power offset of PDSCH RE to NZP CSI-RS RE is equal to powerControlOffset - powerOffset.","paragraph_zero_based":21785},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":21786},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–CSI-ReportSubConfigId","paragraph_zero_based":21787},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE CSI-ReportSubConfigId is used to indicate the index of one CSI-ReportSubConfig within a CSI report configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":21788},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-ReportSubConfigId information element","paragraph_zero_based":21789},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":21790},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-CSI-REPORTSUBCONFIGID-START","paragraph_zero_based":21791}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["86104a775a940f39a11b561774d8f1344845681cfcb85052d226ca93011b425b","61bbd63fdaff145d0bca1ce99a489a7303c1bcaf589cadb0c8c5cec084bb25e0","a9728a41c28e37ea87e2bede14d5e262546bfada03a489fbf3d0a9e88221828c","4a7a5ac4fae27db3be6d5019620e66378b56c9b7f7220ca0e4984958e5bda79e","3b740c4f681b3b29713081d123ffbd3be8426f72e55382c7fb2abc8e9d4b673d","7a023c7d51b99e708cd65ffea8287894ae273c45e342d49ebbde5b1e3d693dd3","b2f3b7c6cf45f7d6306eb428a4d7ed09a8e3e43fb1f6d73b4249cbbad9e08a9d","85b23dcddaa83340511ad0388a9e036820c6ff9837da4399cf82c66a3e1033b6","375c012ba71f30efaf9c317f0396ebc46580d08ec982bdd46bb66e1dc4d6efc3","56daf977e958dce7afd207a85f324e3a06f7e58a1a7227c150cd84f321fe8526","df318613564ca1eb535689d1b8e1353f380794dba928f2ce018c99d4afcaf6a9","b3a2df7582e6f25fd02061afca174cf53884175b07fdcb8597a220728b3c00b9","be3bc0098754e859f87142d552c9f5e11576e143f5fe98f4f8e2f0de0f83b7eb","f580270c9ce2358e2fc83c2b7f6990bea869ea6b8e5e38603c5e2cd274b07e97","e31e4da12ace931eb23f1b01dfecbfe8136d0de74b98daa7f2e391d0db2ae298","1130a9162d18f7e337e02aac0475c12a5274e09151251830e43e6a64375baa17","39b3eb8621fc401ed720f3acfed9b85c42afc61eccae72c181e9eb14ade0e293","f24cb48a166cafe972649327b6fb0acb7ab31b10328a9ce19d01f8db30491fcf","e7e8054a3304dd61f8b1b3402693d36eb6089840f0fefa20665a47084b565143","260e25fe5a4bde540ca430e5567e2f7e18bc5bdff45e29c871922bfc6ae211d7","5736e04ce397c3e6d2f40bf08fb334ebe03eadc7c99e71e92ab0a8cb9eaea100","7711afbdef6b019ff5135e99cfc3ef4f6a180135ef9d0fc92c9e15704b9d709f","137b3fbcfbb5c5ed2e2c11cca5c0f32aa0329e3e6e1a005c4