{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":22848},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":22849},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EARLYUL-SYNCCONFIG-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":22850},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":22851},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":22852},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EarlyUL-SyncConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":22853},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"frequencyInfoUL","paragraph_zero_based":22854},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field provides basic parameters of an uplink carrier for PRACH transmission on a candidate cell.","paragraph_zero_based":22855},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ltm-PRACH-SubcarrierSpacing","paragraph_zero_based":22856},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates subcarrier spacing of PRACH for LTM (see TS 38.211 [16], clause 5.3.2).","paragraph_zero_based":22857},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Only the following values are applicable depending on the used frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":22858},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR1:    15 or 30 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":22859},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR2-1:  60 or 120 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":22860},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR2-2:  120, 480, or 960 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":22861},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If absent, the UE applies the SCS as derived from the prach-ConfigurationIndex in RACH-ConfigGeneric (see tables Table 6.3.3.1-1, Table 6.3.3.1-2, Table 6.3.3.2-2 and Table 6.3.3.2-3, TS 38.211 [16]).","paragraph_zero_based":22862},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"n-TimingAdvanceOffset","paragraph_zero_based":22863},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The N_TA-Offset to be applied for all uplink transmissions on a candidate cell.","paragraph_zero_based":22864},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"rach-ConfigGeneric","paragraph_zero_based":22865},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RACH parameters for performing a random access procedure on a candidate cell.","paragraph_zero_based":22866},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ssb-PerRACH-Occasion","paragraph_zero_based":22867},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicated the number of SSBs for RACH occasion.","paragraph_zero_based":22868},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":22869},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":22870},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":22871}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["20152b2003ab5e25c79bab72506f3873c2f4071a6cbe316bed27cf0d6783e4a0","904058285d61f491ae58ebbc049fb6bdf8b9c75ddd8b8473460770a3d9e33eea","eecdd22a09caec17f5567165b670421ad1a77c7e099916cc766121a84f9bd74d","f5b2c33d881b8f6eaf2acc4b13029006c725a2521d8432f0df426ba9aa535610","225ee0d0fe82e2ef14ee835cafe51b66eed0af88fef7a2d82ae7fdaa22360a27","67af841f5e39f643d2bde8caeaa539f8dec31e9cc46fecc02031eb052b2ab24e","dfbf113f95b9bc22fdc94a019a53b3f5bf3f1e61a5c9750d04a995c13554cb97","e9a057e3ee4d2531f898e62be09daa2c9cd800f40bd27b0ef5b670ec584e396d","bd354ecbe8c8ad7d820e651564fa70ddf3fbeb9ba3149988b18c68daff79dac2","e0ccecdd16676dc2d267b67245fe40ffb10b7ac0d99fa269c9341e9d6d2f2b7d","da6a9f3ffaa3df9064b3088c9cd23fa96db17176f0651093b2b287fe375cfade","bee7e5461e84b038b8bf0800091302edca3762538acce035e240a983a9b80207","ec5bcef4ae696a8a94d0392acf448c1438bcd739f8b3bc9eb1bd6b4a5744f119","21998e244c1617f1f8f66d351e9bff326482205a80dcbdb802f92e79b3dc958e","5ad3817ef33c31b9525802ee