{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Physical cell identity of a cell in the cell list.","paragraph_zero_based":24720},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cellIndividualOffset","paragraph_zero_based":24721},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Cell individual offset applicable to a specific cell. Value dB-24 corresponds to -24 dB, dB-22 corresponds to -22 dB and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":24722},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":24723},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MeasObjectEUTRA field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":24724},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"allowedMeasBandwidth","paragraph_zero_based":24725},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The maximum allowed measurement bandwidth on a carrier frequency as defined by the parameter Transmission Bandwidth Configuration \"NRB\" TS 36.104 [33].","paragraph_zero_based":24726},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"associatedMeasGap","paragraph_zero_based":24727},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the associated measurement gap for measuring this EUTRA frequency. If this field is absent, the associated meaurment gap is the gap configured via gapFR1 or gapUE.","paragraph_zero_based":24728},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"carrierFreq","paragraph_zero_based":24729},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Identifies EUTRA carrier frequency for which this configuration is valid. Network does not configure more than one MeasObjectEUTRA for the same physical frequency, regardless of the E-ARFCN used to indicate this.","paragraph_zero_based":24730},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cellsToAddModListEUTRAN","paragraph_zero_based":24731},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of cells to add/ modify in the cell list.","paragraph_zero_based":24732},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cellsToRemoveListEUTRAN","paragraph_zero_based":24733},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of cells to remove from the cell list.","paragraph_zero_based":24734},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"eutra-PresenceAntennaPort1","paragraph_zero_based":24735},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When set to true, the UE may assume that at least two cell-specific antenna ports are used in all neighbouring cells.","paragraph_zero_based":24736},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"eutra-Q-OffsetRange","paragraph_zero_based":24737},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Used to indicate a cell, or frequency specific offset to be applied when evaluating triggering conditions for measurement reporting. The value is in dB. Value dB-24 corresponds to -24 dB, value dB-22 corresponds to -22 dB and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":24738},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"excludedCellsToAddModListEUTRAN","paragraph_zero_based":24739},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of cells to add/ modify in the exclude-list of cells.","paragraph_zero_based":24740},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"excludedCellsToRemoveListEUTRAN","paragraph_zero_based":24741},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of cells to remove from the exclude-list of cells.","paragraph_zero_based":24742},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"measSequence","paragraph_zero_based":24743}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["09a7e824bdcfa27d6b2575cc081911d8801cb4af33baac3d0faaa193fd433285","6d39a5fba427403bb98ff65694a0f5886ad64d045396cd4d828d4b5699b758f1","bdc63bf4b193c5530756cd59e780d352c6e51e761a4e12ae88223336e801a32d","cfa9efe7197cd3886fcbffd2271c01227572b3ae1c49566a6958b8d5972fbe96","e0b90c9b6209dec10b128badb8c84f8b54a43020ad7fe26385b6ced2dfcea2e8","66e09ee79e536df685834cb44bf25b017800f5146b0