{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"periodicFwdRsrcToAddModList","paragraph_zero_based":26376},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of periodic forwarding resources to be added or modified.","paragraph_zero_based":26377},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"periodicityAndOffset","paragraph_zero_based":26378},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the periodicity and slot offset for the periodic forwarding resource. All the periodic forwarding resources configured within the same resource set should have the same periodicity. If the periodicity is expressed in [ms], the value range of slot offset is from 0 to Periodicity[ms] * referenceSCS[kHz]/15 -1.","paragraph_zero_based":26379},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"priorityFlag","paragraph_zero_based":26380},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the priority for the list of periodic forwarding resources, as specified in TS 38.213 [13], clause 20.","paragraph_zero_based":26381},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"referenceSCS","paragraph_zero_based":26382},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the reference subcarrier spacing for all the time resources in the list. Only values kHz15, kHz30, kHz60, kHz120 and kHz240 are applicable.","paragraph_zero_based":26383},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"symbolOffset","paragraph_zero_based":26384},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the symbol offset in one slot.","paragraph_zero_based":26385},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":26386},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–NCR-PeriodicFwdResourceSetId","paragraph_zero_based":26387},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE NCR-PeriodicFwdResourceSetId is used to identify one NCR-PeriodicFwdResourceSet.","paragraph_zero_based":26388},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NCR-PeriodicFwdResourceSetId information element","paragraph_zero_based":26389},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":26390},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-NCR-PERIODICFWDRESOURCESETID-START","paragraph_zero_based":26391},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":26392},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NCR-PeriodicFwdResourceSetId-r18 ::= INTEGER (0..maxNrofPeriodicFwdResourceSet-1-r18)","paragraph_zero_based":26393},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":26394},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-NCR-PERIODICFWDRESOURCESETID-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":26395},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":26396},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":26397},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–NCR-SemiPersistentFwdResourceSet","paragraph_zero_based":26398},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE NCR-SemiPersistentFwdResourceSet is used to configure a list of semi-persistent forwarding resources for NCR-Fwd access link (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 20). Each semi-persistent forwarding resource configuration includes a list of semi-persistent forwarding resources, a common periodicity and a common reference SCS.","paragraph_zero_based":26399}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["253ea6c7b2acaed6b9dc12e40dc199afff1d5eda8669fdf46d62e0f7510ffc58","861c6706433a7341de3094ca4581a3e86e53b5ea147290de33566aaaa5bef720","1d78fdbb7e5b9719988521ac9a07fd87a45582104781b8aff407562c13813aa0","08907d244fe05b968a6f36763349c27b12820a94fb4815509a11359715b0b438","35102a647aaf1ba8dcfe91cfd24894afc34e64508aafc477626fd5c6b730e3e8","a529eee00c1f36c4fbca661fb448b51eeab1b05c5ac72c265ff7b91ee463790d","277205c9e0105fc2c5f8dad86a70ee89b