{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    subcarrierSpacing-r18               SubcarrierSpacing                               OPTIONAL,   -- Cond LTM","paragraph_zero_based":27096},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    absoluteFrequencyPointA-r18         ARFCN-ValueNR                                   OPTIONAL,   -- Cond LTM","paragraph_zero_based":27097},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    cyclicPrefix-r18                    ENUMERATED {extended}                           OPTIONAL    -- Cond LTM","paragraph_zero_based":27098},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ]]","paragraph_zero_based":27099},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":27100},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":27101},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-NZP-CSI-RS-RESOURCE-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":27102},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":27103},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":27104},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NZP-CSI-RS-Resource field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":27105},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"periodicityAndOffset","paragraph_zero_based":27106},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Periodicity and slot offset sl1 corresponds to a periodicity of 1 slot, sl2 to a periodicity of two slots, and so on. The corresponding offset is also given in number of slots (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.2.2.3.1). Network always configures the UE with a value for this field for periodic and semi-persistent NZP-CSI-RS-Resource (as indicated in CSI-ResourceConfig).","paragraph_zero_based":27107},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"powerControlOffset","paragraph_zero_based":27108},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Power offset of PDSCH RE to NZP CSI-RS RE. Value in dB (see TS 38.214 [19], clauses 5.2.2.3.1 and 4.1). The UE shall ignore this field in case NZP-CSI-RS-Resources is received as part of an LTM-Candidate IE.","paragraph_zero_based":27109},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"powerControlOffsetSS","paragraph_zero_based":27110},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Power offset of NZP CSI-RS RE to SSS RE. Value in dB (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.2.2.3.1).","paragraph_zero_based":27111},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"qcl-InfoPeriodicCSI-RS","paragraph_zero_based":27112},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For a target periodic CSI-RS, contains a reference to one TCI-State in TCI-States for providing the QCL source and QCL type. For periodic CSI-RS, the source can be SSB or another periodic-CSI-RS. Refers to the TCI-State or dl-OrJoint-TCI-State which has this value for tci-StateId and is defined in tci-StatesToAddModList or in dl-OrJointTCI-StateList in the PDSCH-Config included in the BWP-Downlink corresponding to the serving cell and to the DL BWP to which the resource belongs to (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.2.2.3.1). In case NZP-CSI-RS-Resources is received as part of an LTM-Candidate IE, it refers to the TCI state identifier in CandidateTCI-State and is defined in ltm-DL-OrJointTCI-StateToAddModList within the LTM-Candidate IE.","paragraph_zero_based":27113},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"resourceMapping","paragraph_zero_based":27114},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"OFDM symbol location(s) in a slot and subcarrier occupancy in a PRB of the CSI-RS resource.","paragraph_zero_based":27115},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"scramblingID","paragraph_zero_based":27116},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Scrambling ID (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.2.2.3.1).","paragraph_zero_based":27117},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":27118},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":27119}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d925621