{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"phr-ProhibitTimer","paragraph_zero_based":28368},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in number of subframes for PHR reporting as specified in TS 38.321 [3]. Value sf0 corresponds to 0 subframe, value sf10 corresponds to 10 subframes, value sf20 corresponds to 20 subframes, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":28369},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"phr-Tx-PowerFactorChange","paragraph_zero_based":28370},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in dB for PHR reporting as specified in TS 38.321 [3]. Value dB1 corresponds to 1 dB, dB3 corresponds to 3 dB and so on. The same value applies for each serving cell (although the associated functionality is performed independently for each cell).","paragraph_zero_based":28371},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"phr-Type2OtherCell","paragraph_zero_based":28372},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If set to true, the UE shall report a PHR type 2 for the SpCell of the other MAC entity. See TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.4.6. Network sets this field to false if the UE is not configured with an E-UTRA MAC entity.","paragraph_zero_based":28373},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"twoPHRMode","paragraph_zero_based":28374},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates if the power headroom shall be reported as two PHRs (each PHR associated with a SRS resource set) is enabled or not. The network ensures phr-AssumedPUSCH-Reporting-r18 and twoPHRMode-r17 are not configured at the same time for a UE.","paragraph_zero_based":28375},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28376},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–PhysCellId","paragraph_zero_based":28377},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The PhysCellId identifies the physical cell identity (PCI).","paragraph_zero_based":28378},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PhysCellId information element","paragraph_zero_based":28379},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":28380},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PHYSCELLID-START","paragraph_zero_based":28381},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28382},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PhysCellId ::=                      INTEGER (0..1007)","paragraph_zero_based":28383},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28384},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PHYSCELLID-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":28385},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":28386},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":28387},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–PhysicalCellGroupConfig","paragraph_zero_based":28388},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE PhysicalCellGroupConfig is used to configure cell-group specific L1 parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":28389},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PhysicalCellGroupConfig information element","paragraph_zero_based":28390},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":28391}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["c539f02a77c94901032ba7a2ce089772146ab8911de6feddd6025e5f9ba92736","2cb049bbdfd6091ab391422622080c1e71d67133a512afff0ff34a707c95e21f","ba8dbb5dd6f6706afc7d9fcc1cb64a02400964cd37f8fb37af3268e1b16c4aba","baddb2d6dd6acce4c387b4cb025d0a6b647aeec30c342daab474254850dbf7e3","f67f35e2767221da3f8d3b7cd3b8772e1278d7b61b113c74c57fb5a7af0fe348","992e9aff95428e502f8dae8bfe48c17d096f6c50f30251624dd688cdcfb85598","f661200251b330e746cc9b8a74d3a8517d16859027eec346747ae1eab8d18c8f","1f6cbd7954b64b44dc330d6506fba5e88a1ee2ea4514ac7c248807d305dc7712","69d2135e5c5