{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RACH-ConfigTwoTA field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":30840},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"msg1-SubcarrierSpacing","paragraph_zero_based":30841},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Subcarrier spacing of PRACH when prach-RootSequenceIndex has value set to l139 (see TS 38.211 [16], clause 5.3.2). Only the following values are applicable depending on the used frequency: FR1: 15 or 30 kHz FR2-1: 60 or 120 kHz FR2-2: 120, 480, or 960 kHz. If absent, the UE applies the SCS as derived from the prach-ConfigurationIndex in RACH-ConfigGeneric (see tables Table 6.3.3.1-1, Table 6.3.3.1-2, Table 6.3.3.2-2 and Table 6.3.3.2-3, TS 38.211 [16]).","paragraph_zero_based":30842},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"prach-RootSequenceIndex","paragraph_zero_based":30843},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PRACH root sequence index (see TS 38.211 [16], clause 6.3.3.1). The value range depends on whether L=839 or L=139.","paragraph_zero_based":30844},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For FR2-2, only the following values are applicable depending on the used subcarrier spacing:","paragraph_zero_based":30845},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"120 kHz:  L=139, L=571, and L=1151","paragraph_zero_based":30846},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"480 kHz:  L=139, and L=571","paragraph_zero_based":30847},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"960 kHz:  L=139","paragraph_zero_based":30848},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"rach-ConfigGeneric","paragraph_zero_based":30849},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RACH parameters for for contention free random access occasions for CFRA.","paragraph_zero_based":30850},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ssb-perRACH-Occasion","paragraph_zero_based":30851},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Number of SSBs per RACH occasion.","paragraph_zero_based":30852},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30853},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":30854},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":30855},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"L139","paragraph_zero_based":30856},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present if prach-RootSequenceIndex L=139, otherwise the field is absent, Need S.","paragraph_zero_based":30857},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":30858},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–RA-Prioritization","paragraph_zero_based":30859},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE RA-Prioritization is used to configure prioritized random access.","paragraph_zero_based":30860},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RA-Prioritization information element","paragraph_zero_based":30861},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":30862},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-RA-PRIORITIZATION-START","paragraph_zero_based":30863}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["8b382ccbd5f7f2c7a988171fca820cfb9fca2012780b70e13e8e6623bd819b04","0af16c4188f8abd5c9cd758ee6ca548426da3f1b121a7942a641c2f79d47e83a","80e5fe5c353599562b04164dc8f2e8dd143f40acc7e941e44456ab4af2bc540e","e6e5747ef0f35c7d9bcb03a07bae998039480443c1f12e43f68890770799793a","fe5d241a8b58f0cee62de2739f6d66190bbf408bb0b53294b45880da3a4b0ce0","ef00c07155fb990a32086702ef33bb2c37502486fdb4618b6a72aa0565cadd9f","f0ebc45286642d32708f57a9aae8befe49bec55c1d926d11f5d55f631eae695a","7e445412f711a0fe6f60329ff116e2291e2b716bf0bb5fdbb77d792bfd142a12","e12d3837dd540080e23c186226fa72da38c8db8f521fe20526218fff0a6ac9c0","536c29eef87e5a4f205d11f90a924f0c5a86d3