{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Number of measurement reports applicable for eventTriggered as well as for periodical report types","paragraph_zero_based":32160},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"reportQuantityCell","paragraph_zero_based":32161},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The cell measurement quantities to be included in the measurement report.","paragraph_zero_based":32162},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"reportQuantityRS-Indexes","paragraph_zero_based":32163},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates which measurement information per RS index the UE shall include in the measurement report.","paragraph_zero_based":32164},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ul-DelayValueConfig","paragraph_zero_based":32165},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the field is present, the UE shall perform the actual UL PDCP Packet Average Delay measurement per DRB as specified in TS 38.314 [53] and the UE shall ignore the fields reportQuantityCell and maxReportCells. The applicable values for the corresponding reportInterval are (one of the) {ms120, ms240, ms480, ms640, ms1024, ms2048, ms5120, ms10240, ms20480, ms40960, min1,min6, min12, min30}. The reportInterval indicates the periodicity for performing and reporting of UL PDCP Packet Average Delay per DRB measurement as specified in TS 38.314 [53].","paragraph_zero_based":32166},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ul-ExcessDelayConfig","paragraph_zero_based":32167},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the field is present, the UE shall perform the actual UL PDCP Excess Packet Delay per DRB measurement as specified in TS 38.314 [53] and the UE shall ignore the fields reportQuantityCell and maxReportCells. The applicable values for the corresponding reportInterval are (one of the) {ms120, ms240, ms480, ms640, ms1024, ms2048, ms5120, ms10240, ms20480, ms40960, min1,min6, min12, min30}. The reportInterval indicates the periodicity for performing and reporting of UL PDCP Excess Packet Delay per DRB measurement as specified in TS 38.314 [53].","paragraph_zero_based":32168},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"useAllowedCellList","paragraph_zero_based":32169},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether only the cells included in the allow-list of the associated measObject are applicable as specified in 5.5.4.1.","paragraph_zero_based":32170},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32171},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ReportSFTD-NR field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":32172},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cellForWhichToReportSFTD","paragraph_zero_based":32173},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the target NR neighbour cells for SFTD measurement between PCell and NR neighbour cells.","paragraph_zero_based":32174},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"drx-SFTD-NeighMeas","paragraph_zero_based":32175},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates that the UE shall use available idle periods (i.e. DRX off periods) for the SFTD measurement in NR standalone. The network only includes drx-SFTD-NeighMeas field when reprtSFTD-NeighMeas is set to true.","paragraph_zero_based":32176},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"reportSFTD-Meas","paragraph_zero_based":32177},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether UE is required to perform SFTD measurement between PCell and NR PSCell in NR-DC.","paragraph_zero_based":32178},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"reportSFTD-NeighMeas","paragraph_zero_based":32179},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether UE is required to perform SFTD measurement between PCell and NR neighbour cells in NR standalone. The network does not include this field if reportSFTD-Meas is set to true.","paragraph_zero_based":32180},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"reportRSRP","paragraph_zero_based":32181},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether UE is required to include RSRP result of NR PSCell or NR neighbour cells in SFTD measurement result, derived based on SSB. If it is set to true, the network should ensure that ssb-ConfigMobility is included in the measurement object for NR PSCell or NR neighbour cells.","paragraph_zero_based":32182},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32183}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["c3e7b88b9c51b38d1eea12ae3ccbe0c724dc658c47d08562ea9ea82bb73b7545","cda9eeb55a14976052dd2d0d1496124935f2141086e9f139b2157e594a474185","35f89dd3b8610a39640b248cb8b2c47291e673b990a6830d610e628df60d5fce","dc6b7da7dce99c1d40fdde55fcfa563906a4454ebbc5ab007306741b5aa47087","ad25829c50d18e2416898cb5322ff710191ff1bb600c0486da1ce5b4a4b664c4","ce407b1e595dbeda503689ac2dbd5076254ae55fcac3a08c4078faa28741d5bb","7537fe3dd1317f99963105c88676eb66b6e3949492c33c0709167a7483472ee2","1c27f0825faa578ee535642581e8c3b0153c4636dbf113cbdef48ac2a7131b0a","399fa92f0fae6db165ec26e3ee3d0222935f88a5e8279eea7a872d19cb864292","25cf3055d2ce051d3bb89ee6e4db7410d2ad2d0680eecbad6320ba83c4c1af15","3ce1cb8e56a08169e38197fc342e365ff42d7fd21612ee1be6d8a706ff8794ce","9a2d1e7450d7329f1c7d2b7c151f5b193bd53f81e14d2b642a1717e1482811d8","9685e5301efc1cf312e24d88ee8626811680d6c9b921e62435e3fee45d828f70","70775d42ee8717483db24c8250a9a30dad2c784c0f22cfe62a261260df6867a9","462b4e62e3a2605b92b1566d812c0800e7e39696accc4a646144224b95f71473","830b619d54b83188294b31605e41af2359cc4a96703afecdcc5248efe614a5b8","6f5953eb0c2d8a9149f001a2ed5953cda75f8c69d963b2e7a4d4aade7086d295","69710e448550a3ac64e354e8a23d72d74dffa26160e455c1113ba163dbddc4aa","6edbe653af77ade4739d910a818228701c57dbaa43cbac489bec8b18eb933586","fae0a4afd516c06383a82c1d6238a30c522d5b