{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"maxRetxThreshold","paragraph_zero_based":32544},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Parameter for RLC AM in TS 38.322 [4]. Value t1 corresponds to 1 retransmission, value t2 corresponds to 2 retransmissions and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":32545},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pollByte","paragraph_zero_based":32546},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Parameter for RLC AM in TS 38.322 [4]. Value kB25 corresponds to 25 kBytes, value kB50 corresponds to 50 kBytes and so on. infinity corresponds to an infinite amount of kBytes.","paragraph_zero_based":32547},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pollPDU","paragraph_zero_based":32548},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Parameter for RLC AM in TS 38.322 [4]. Value p4 corresponds to 4 PDUs, value p8 corresponds to 8 PDUs and so on. infinity corresponds to an infinite number of PDUs.","paragraph_zero_based":32549},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sn-FieldLength","paragraph_zero_based":32550},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the RLC SN field size, see TS 38.322 [4], in bits. Value size6 means 6 bits, value size12 means 12 bits, value size18 means 18 bits. The value of sn-FieldLength of an RLC entity for the DRB/multicast MRB shall be changed only using reconfiguration with sync. The network configures only value size12 in SN-FieldLengthAM for SRB.","paragraph_zero_based":32551},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"t-PollRetransmit","paragraph_zero_based":32552},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Timer for RLC AM in TS 38.322 [4], in milliseconds. Value ms5 means 5 ms, value ms10 means 10 ms and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":32553},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"t-Reassembly, t-ReassemblyExt","paragraph_zero_based":32554},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Timer for reassembly in TS 38.322 [4], in milliseconds. Value ms0 means 0 ms, value ms5 means 5 ms and so on. If t-ReassemblyExt-r17 is configured, the UE shall ignore t-Reassembly (without suffix).","paragraph_zero_based":32555},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"t-StatusProhibit","paragraph_zero_based":32556},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Timer for status reporting in TS 38.322 [4], in milliseconds. Value ms0 means 0 ms, value ms5 means 5 ms and so on. If t-StatusProhibit-v1610 is present, the UE shall ignore t-StatusProhibit (without suffix).","paragraph_zero_based":32557},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32558},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":32559},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":32560},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reestab","paragraph_zero_based":32561},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present at RLC bearer setup. It is optionally present, need M, at RLC re-establishment. Otherwise it is absent. Need M.","paragraph_zero_based":32562},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32563},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–RLF-TimersAndConstants","paragraph_zero_based":32564},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE RLF-TimersAndConstants is used to configure UE specific timers and constants.","paragraph_zero_based":32565},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RLF-TimersAndConstants information element","paragraph_zero_based":32566},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":32567}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["876d244b6532eb5cf4d2e89f0a1f854614d8a63c78c325391376561c0fac3b83","8e32265d46b726cd64a2e8aee360dc09f9d834413d7de61796af6268da91f0d7","6051db