{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SchedulingRequestToAddMod field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":32736},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"schedulingRequestId","paragraph_zero_based":32737},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Used to modify a SR configuration and to indicate, in LogicalChannelConfig, the SR configuration to which a logical channel is mapped and to indicate, in SchedulingRequestresourceConfig, the SR configuration for which a scheduling request resource is used.","paragraph_zero_based":32738},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sr-ProhibitTimer","paragraph_zero_based":32739},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Timer for SR transmission on PUCCH in TS 38.321 [3]. Value is in ms. Value ms1 corresponds to 1ms, value ms2 corresponds to 2ms, and so on. If sr-ProhibitTimer-v1700 is configured, UE shall ignore sr-ProhibitTimer (without suffix). If both sr-ProhibitTimer (without suffix) and sr-ProhibitTimer-v1700 are absent, the UE applies the value 0.","paragraph_zero_based":32740},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sr-TransMax","paragraph_zero_based":32741},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Maximum number of SR transmissions as described in TS 38.321 [3]. Value n4 corresponds to 4, value n8 corresponds to 8, and so on. ","paragraph_zero_based":32742},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32743},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SchedulingRequestId","paragraph_zero_based":32744},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SchedulingRequestId is used to identify a Scheduling Request instance in the MAC layer.","paragraph_zero_based":32745},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SchedulingRequestId information element","paragraph_zero_based":32746},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":32747},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SCHEDULINGREQUESTID-START","paragraph_zero_based":32748},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32749},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SchedulingRequestId ::=             INTEGER (0..7)","paragraph_zero_based":32750},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32751},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SCHEDULINGREQUESTID-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":32752},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":32753},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32754},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SchedulingRequestResourceConfig","paragraph_zero_based":32755},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SchedulingRequestResourceConfig determines physical layer resources on PUCCH where the UE may send the dedicated scheduling request (D-SR) (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 9.2.4).","paragraph_zero_based":32756},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SchedulingRequestResourceConfig information element","paragraph_zero_based":32757},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":32758},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SCHEDULINGREQUESTRESOURCECONFIG-START","paragraph_zero_based":32759}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["9bb47766154df20dc191bf3ddc256f469ddc1daea977ab3fb65d5b4085702b79","d116349ffbd601ad8d26d398aa52594c8c3fb64e6979b2d8b76da9eb541086de","0f0720477ca5188be1f5145da75cb39739b04397cd85ed01c02f78b801169fc1","51abcd3607035c556d2dec03742fe9fc0a134a5d8a41e4180430447cf76eedb7","b8bd7b15acc9280ff80d30eb7e668ef0cce06ab4886aa79442749e3272709204","1ea974c669b6196328192761c26d4aba3fe48ebf7318f77f92dd0367559f2877","2efd4708cd9869937edf1d83f483f22434d6f1495808cb895219f5f56c9f8303","d4899719b02bf1e6