{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SCS = 960 kHz: 1sl, 2sl, 4sl, 8sl, 16sl, 40sl, 80sl, 160sl, 320sl, 640sl, 1280sl, 2560sl, 5120sl","paragraph_zero_based":32808},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32809},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sym6or7 corresponds to 6 symbols if extended cyclic prefix and a SCS of 60 kHz are configured, otherwise it corresponds to 7 symbols.","paragraph_zero_based":32810},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For periodicities 2sym, 7sym and sl1 the UE assumes an offset of 0 slots.","paragraph_zero_based":32811},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If periodicityAndOffset-r17 is present, any previously configured periodicityAndOffset (without suffix) is released, and vice versa.","paragraph_zero_based":32812},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UE indicates support of the following SR periodicities in additionalSR-Periodicities (see TS 38.306, clause 4.2.6):","paragraph_zero_based":32813},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SCS = 30 kHz: 5sl","paragraph_zero_based":32814},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SCS = 120 kHz: 5sl, 10sl","paragraph_zero_based":32815},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"phy-PriorityIndex","paragraph_zero_based":32816},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether this scheduling request resource is high or low priority in PHY prioritization/multiplexing handling (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 9.2.4). Value p0 indicates low priority and value p1 indicates high priority.","paragraph_zero_based":32817},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"resource","paragraph_zero_based":32818},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ID of the PUCCH resource in which the UE shall send the scheduling request. The actual PUCCH-Resource is configured in PUCCH-Config of the same UL BWP and serving cell as this SchedulingRequestResourceConfig. The network configures a PUCCH-Resource of PUCCH-format0 or PUCCH-format1 (other formats not supported) (see TS 38.213 [13], clause 9.2.4)","paragraph_zero_based":32819},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"schedulingRequestID","paragraph_zero_based":32820},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The ID of the SchedulingRequestConfig that uses this scheduling request resource.","paragraph_zero_based":32821},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32822},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SchedulingRequestResourceId","paragraph_zero_based":32823},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SchedulingRequestResourceId is used to identify scheduling request resources on PUCCH.","paragraph_zero_based":32824},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SchedulingRequestResourceId information element","paragraph_zero_based":32825},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":32826},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SCHEDULINGREQUESTRESOURCEID-START","paragraph_zero_based":32827},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32828},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SchedulingRequestResourceId ::=     INTEGER (1..maxNrofSR-Resources)","paragraph_zero_based":32829},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32830},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SCHEDULINGREQUESTRESOURCEID-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":32831}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["f6ab8c81680bac7efbc45c01dab3e0e3d154960287eaaa30e7a3c49bdae9e4a8","ee68e62d687e41f46ad9b09b7f75293a0bd0334923c4aa9265788ba0bd57c6bc","d82a822d6ffa58276248c893db9a453b551a8d52911edde64d483017dd4db64f","a0691e504f86a9e1dae686fd9c9040610e69fe3943a284408251fe410d3b21b0","bf4ae60ac0f2784dc385d85b4ba224