{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    startingBitOfFormat2-3SUL               INTEGER (1..31)                                                     OPTIONAL    -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":35472},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ]]","paragraph_zero_based":35473},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":35474},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35475},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SRS-TPC-COMMANDCONFIG-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":35476},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":35477},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35478},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SRS-TPC-CommandConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":35479},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"fieldTypeFormat2-3","paragraph_zero_based":35480},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The type of a field within the group DCI with SRS request fields (optional), which indicates how many bits in the field are for SRS request (0 or 2).","paragraph_zero_based":35481},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Note that for Type A, there is a common SRS request field for all SCells in the set, but each SCell has its own TPC command bits. See TS 38.212 [17] clause 7.3.1 and , TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.4.","paragraph_zero_based":35482},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"startingBitOfFormat2-3","paragraph_zero_based":35483},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The starting bit position of a block within the group DCI with SRS request fields (optional) and TPC commands. The value 1 of the field corresponds to the first/left most bit of format2-3. The value 2 of the field corresponds to the second bit format2-3, and so on (see TS 38.212 [17], clause 7.3.1 and TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.4).","paragraph_zero_based":35484},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"startingBitOfFormat2-3SUL","paragraph_zero_based":35485},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The starting bit position of a block within the group DCI with SRS request fields (optional) and TPC commands for SUL carrier (see TS 38.212 [17], clause 7.3.1 and TS 38.213 [13], clause 11.4).","paragraph_zero_based":35486},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35487},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SSB-Index","paragraph_zero_based":35488},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SSB-Index identifies an SS-Block within an SS-Burst. See TS 38.213 [13], clause 4.1.","paragraph_zero_based":35489},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SSB-Index information element","paragraph_zero_based":35490},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":35491},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SSB-INDEX-START","paragraph_zero_based":35492},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35493},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SSB-Index ::=                       INTEGER (0..maxNrofSSBs-1)","paragraph_zero_based":35494},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":35495}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["634b1dd72c8415431c5fd5abc05330ac4ba332c56410abd9f0a5e3647d8023e2","6a8329dce928040d35f2fd778a95f29bb0f8abfb495a3d8494c4f8008c4ac3cf","266aa0a9142775b18ddce170c49f0dcb53e915c18f1f3f97cb9486860c2f045f","fbf4c6eb4d6f331e296debd917bdf92eff08455386689d2f42cf6d9edd29fb40","5dc4a23d4434d65396389adbfa63cb1638294510d9c00d02822a3e5b609fb059","bf433fb8bd4cdee4981b85512b2b6c4531e986f9fac19a411be77e7f6aa99f63","ca7f7557fe5067d88a4d57257907b9e4079630af404295cc730035f8e912d888","396b7ddaf0b3d4aee5ec140db61f7c2616638e1c3dd5555d0e2f1714a