{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36264},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UL-GapFR2-Config field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":36265},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"gapOffset","paragraph_zero_based":36266},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value gapOffset is the gap offset of the FR2 UL gap pattern with UGRP indicated in the field ugrp. The value range is from 0 to ugrp-1.","paragraph_zero_based":36267},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"refFR2-ServCellAsyncCA","paragraph_zero_based":36268},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the FR2 serving cell identifier whose SFN and subframe is used for FR2 UL gap calculation for this gap pattern with asynchronous CA involving FR2 carrier(s).","paragraph_zero_based":36269},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ugl","paragraph_zero_based":36270},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value ugl is the gap length in ms of the FR2 UL gap. The FR2 UL gap length is according to Table 9.1.11-1 in TS 38.133 [14]. Value ms0dot125 corresponds to 0.125 ms, ms0dot25 corresponds to 0.25 ms and so on. ","paragraph_zero_based":36271},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ugrp","paragraph_zero_based":36272},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value ugrp is the gap repetition period in (ms) of the FR2 UL gap. The FR2 UL gap repetition period is according to Table 9.1.11-1 in TS 38.133 [14].","paragraph_zero_based":36273},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36274},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":36275},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":36276},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"AsyncCA","paragraph_zero_based":36277},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is mandatory present when configuring FR2 UL gap pattern to UE in:","paragraph_zero_based":36278},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"- (NG)EN-DC, NR SA, NE-DC or NR-DC without FR2-FR2 band combination, with asynchronous CA involving FR2 carriers.","paragraph_zero_based":36279},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Otherwise, it is absent.","paragraph_zero_based":36280},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36281},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–UplinkCancellation","paragraph_zero_based":36282},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE UplinkCancellation is used to configure the UE to monitor PDCCH for the CI-RNTI.","paragraph_zero_based":36283},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UplinkCancellation information element","paragraph_zero_based":36284},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":36285},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-UPLINKCANCELLATION-START","paragraph_zero_based":36286},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36287}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["0abec42bb1f54b15dd492dae2ea9507807f0ae6ecd2fdb5701673ffe774a6ce3","2665d845a2eebc4a75961938dff85080c4eff2ecae1fd515625b2f2583dc817f","3d10870a7cfd91c02d8b8cba3968f0540c6c1f2131c36202ed06f5cc46b3f55a","c6e7b97f5037bbeb9e58b154456bd3aaf33e19a7602c3a2d43e5da370ee014cc","ed6c9857574d7e85159e9ef463b41ba594eaf4c839e4ba610de617100c523ec7","dba6fec0746b82bddf85700af1920f75649432e522b5ea9fbcdaad7a5c5c0622","3a83a30f3ddc82b2aac64e0e4827d495a0e9bed86e8002de911a9a11ec3a4210","3f19d0e26ad9446905a3bcee49ce28b06b10d25f3252b0a2fe5e7f65107ba635","783e39f1922275ed6e899f5172c72d9c774436e5bd1a37b26e79e9d7c93dbbda","6632d1b11205d5eb725e63b22f6e899f3fc2db406a0e8aad1ea1d295c23a91cb","58903099595610395707ea12ae9ccd81ce61f1a97827c155cd195a87e46116ca","e2