{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ...","paragraph_zero_based":39840},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":39841},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39842},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-FEATURESETUPLINK-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":39843},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":39844},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39845},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FeatureSetUplink field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":39846},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"featureSetListPerUplinkCC","paragraph_zero_based":39847},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates which features the UE supports on the individual UL carriers of the feature set (and hence of a band entry that refers to the feature set). The UE shall hence include at least as many FeatureSetUplinkPerCC-Id in this list as the number of carriers it supports according to the ca-BandwidthClassUL, except if indicating additional functionality by reducing the number of FeatureSetUplinkPerCC-Id in the feature set (see NOTE 1 in FeatureSetCombination IE description). The order of the elements in this list is not relevant, i.e., the network may configure any of the carriers in accordance with any of the FeatureSetUplinkPerCC-Id in this list.","paragraph_zero_based":39848},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39849},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–FeatureSetUplinkId","paragraph_zero_based":39850},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE FeatureSetUplinkId identifies an uplink feature set. The FeatureSetUplinkId of a FeatureSetUplink is the index position of the FeatureSetUplink in the featureSetsUplink list in the FeatureSets IE. The first element in the list is referred to by FeatureSetUplinkId = 1, and so on. The FeatureSetUplinkId =0 is not used by an actual FeatureSetUplink but means that the UE does not support a carrier in this band of a band combination.","paragraph_zero_based":39851},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FeatureSetUplinkId information element","paragraph_zero_based":39852},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":39853},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-FEATURESETUPLINKID-START","paragraph_zero_based":39854},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39855},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FeatureSetUplinkId ::=                  INTEGER (0..maxUplinkFeatureSets)","paragraph_zero_based":39856},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39857},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-FEATURESETUPLINKID-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":39858},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":39859},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":39860},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–FeatureSetUplinkPerCC","paragraph_zero_based":39861},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE FeatureSetUplinkPerCC indicates a set of features that the UE supports on the corresponding carrier of one band entry of a band combination.","paragraph_zero_based":39862},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FeatureSetUplinkPerCC information element","paragraph_zero_based":39863}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ca202e61af11bd53cbebbf6b4e59d60064fb8d0a24b09203bcf34ec7f0a2a1d6","bc9d93a07ff19b420a5d73a8ade6531f47ec4b2d04e74433b9cc132f8028cd0b","1f7ba9a618e374c596381a6967072899bea1197cf34e7b0970fe8b0833c41ef2","7f1c4dcdc9c9331761f131b6aae7ff2f60ae8d8389ca4ff7d99ac54c7dad73f1","0e829b1ff6f170a6b4c