{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-BTNAMELIST-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":44808},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":44809},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44810},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"BT-NameList field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":44811},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"bt-Name","paragraph_zero_based":44812},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If configured, the UE only performs Bluetooth measurements according to the names identified. For each name, it refers to LOCAL NAME defined in Bluetooth specification [51].","paragraph_zero_based":44813},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44814},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–DedicatedInfoF1c","paragraph_zero_based":44815},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE DedicatedInfoF1c is used to transfer IAB-DU specific F1-C related information between the network and the IAB node. The carried information consists of F1AP message encapsulated in SCTP/IP or F1-C related (SCTP)/IP packet, see TS 38.472 [64]. The RRC layer is transparent for this information.","paragraph_zero_based":44816},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"DedicatedInfoF1c information element","paragraph_zero_based":44817},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":44818},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-DEDICATEDINFOF1C-START","paragraph_zero_based":44819},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44820},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"DedicatedInfoF1c-r17 ::=        OCTET STRING","paragraph_zero_based":44821},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44822},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-DEDICATEDINFOF1C-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":44823},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":44824},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44825},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–EUTRA-AllowedMeasBandwidth","paragraph_zero_based":44826},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE EUTRA-AllowedMeasBandwidth is used to indicate the maximum allowed measurement bandwidth on a carrier frequency as defined by the parameter Transmission Bandwidth Configuration \"NRB\" in TS 36.104 [33]. The values mbw6, mbw15, mbw25, mbw50, mbw75, mbw100 indicate 6, 15, 25, 50, 75 and 100 resource blocks, respectively.","paragraph_zero_based":44827},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EUTRA-AllowedMeasBandwidth information element","paragraph_zero_based":44828},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":44829},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EUTRA-ALLOWEDMEASBANDWIDTH-START","paragraph_zero_based":44830},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44831}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["fdd448fea64080e126502f3b6a82d6962f47609fca7911b0b913628f74c5a95a","18c83073a33722bbe8bff997943692a75cd7c4575a3b76799039fc688477635c","dcd6cd79c4c547e5ad4466e6f5f7f5752846bab29e41d145e310df8064124efd","30d6fbd96a8a1a9bf27f679ed67db0af1caca8b1e326460575c39fd142516cbb","356bdeb6a40752588c0d2050cf4b36f08de3b16bb6bec58ca480a07634bb8dbb","efa2e359e276e46b9c2afd9126ceb94e55baa8e5cf474f61d4d0d0be3c7cd52d","64ed9c57ecefe81e84da892ffed75a88fec4f7aed2fc0d3bb2f59d9405db9636","7a3df5900cd5ffe450579f34468100072dbedd225a459fc29be9a0d95b4b95b7","d619347740f13310e272673c62b12bcdeb84442a0dbe834dedea59ac6cf100d6","476b16dfe05af752c2eac1b8f63af07bad85ebf342d3cee50c824f07536a38f6","c7fcc2b7bea5c64a12896d23dd1612c232ac30effef57123efcd19acecce19c8","71