{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EUTRA-PHYSCELLID-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":44928},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":44929},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44930},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–EUTRA-PhysCellIdRange","paragraph_zero_based":44931},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE EUTRA-PhysCellIdRange is used to encode either a single or a range of physical cell identities. The range is encoded by using a start value and by indicating the number of consecutive physical cell identities (including start) in the range. For fields comprising multiple occurrences of EUTRA-PhysCellIdRange, NW may configure overlapping ranges of physical cell identities.","paragraph_zero_based":44932},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EUTRA-PhysCellIdRange information element","paragraph_zero_based":44933},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":44934},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EUTRA-PHYSCELLIDRANGE-START","paragraph_zero_based":44935},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44936},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EUTRA-PhysCellIdRange ::=       SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":44937},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    start                           EUTRA-PhysCellId,","paragraph_zero_based":44938},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    range                           ENUMERATED {n4, n8, n12, n16, n24, n32, n48, n64, n84, n96,","paragraph_zero_based":44939},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                n128, n168, n252, n504, spare2, spare1}                         OPTIONAL    -- Need N","paragraph_zero_based":44940},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":44941},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44942},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EUTRA-PHYSCELLIDRANGE-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":44943},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":44944},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44945},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–EUTRA-PresenceAntennaPort1","paragraph_zero_based":44946},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE EUTRA-PresenceAntennaPort1 is used to indicate whether all the neighbouring cells use Antenna Port 1. When set to true, the UE may assume that at least two cell-specific antenna ports are used in all neighbouring cells.","paragraph_zero_based":44947},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EUTRA-PresenceAntennaPort1 information element","paragraph_zero_based":44948},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":44949},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EUTRA-PRESENCEANTENNAPORT1-START","paragraph_zero_based":44950},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":44951}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["b2c9cfd0670d75fd4199dd9bbccfbe2ddbd0bc93bb28749ac741b294f997077a","a1107e851d9d00a50c69e7b9fee796175e5850edaabf40c2fce9f7e86827c318","60e63c884cc5781eaec37338b95eabc7c1f596d3d3d15141013c69cb3c2f49af","bf20a7a43d60ff2114206ef4d5969f6265357073414869db6a038d792b0f5bb4","c71c66beecc029f75d09644c4fc59a3cd6e9620b7bf14204f20f89262443ca6a","d9c6f1f10cf135e94e4422fde39976ea63b075b738d3ed16311416b65cf748b4","90921e85610eccfec14cf8ed814e1e3f12b88c00532f0964621fc8a7473c92fc","9910a8ceaeabf5702de7c8490e48f11542351f34cb8eefdd28e026d113bc83f7","24c6a49085f30e9f4c03194781f7e595cc47a9aad8a69a4e1c813ff29c165d6f","24503b656047f1080ec53cb1888ebba4eabddaff7c3eb3089e4e346692da5