{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-PRS-MaxTx-power-r18                  INTEGER (-30..33)                                                    OPTIONAL,    -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":46056},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-PRS-MaxNum-Transmissions-r18         INTEGER(1..32)                                                       OPTIONAL     -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":46057},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":46058},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":46059},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-CBR-Dedicated-SL-PRS-RP-r18 ::= INTEGER (0..100)","paragraph_zero_based":46060},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":46061},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-CBR-COMMONTXDEDICATEDSL-PRS-RP-LIST-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":46062},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":46063},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":46064},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-CBR-CommonTxDedicatedSL-PRS-RP-List field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":46065},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-CBR-RangeDedicatedSL-PRS-RP-List","paragraph_zero_based":46066},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the list of CBR ranges. Each entry of the list indicates in SL-CBR-LevelsConfig-Dedicated-SL-PRS-RP the upper bound of the CBR range for the respective entry. The upper bounds of the CBR ranges are configured in ascending order for consecutive entries of SL-CBR-LevelsConfig-Dedicated-SL-PRS-RP. For the first entry of SL-CBR-LevelsConfig-Dedicated-SL-PRS-RP the lower bound of the CBR range is 0. Value 0 corresponds to 0, value 1 to 0.01, value 2 to 0.02, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":46067},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-CBR-SL-PRS-TxConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":46068},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the list of available SL PRS transmission parameters configurations.","paragraph_zero_based":46069},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PRS-CR-Limit","paragraph_zero_based":46070},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the maximum limit on the occupancy ratio. Value 0 corresponds to 0, value 1 to 0.0001, value 2 to 0.0002, and so on (i.e. in steps of 0.0001) until value 10000, which corresponds to 1.","paragraph_zero_based":46071},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PRS-MaxNum-Transmissions","paragraph_zero_based":46072},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates maximum Number of SL PRS (re-)transmissions.","paragraph_zero_based":46073},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PRS-MaxTx-power","paragraph_zero_based":46074},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates maximum SL PRS transmission power. The unit is dBm.","paragraph_zero_based":46075},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":46076},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-ConfigDedicatedNR","paragraph_zero_based":46077},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-ConfigDedicatedNR specifies the dedicated configuration information for NR sidelink communication/discovery/positioning.","paragraph_zero_based":46078},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-ConfigDedicatedNR information element","paragraph_zero_based":46079}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["40fd2e909690f8ecc21c4f50992104586ed3dd0f8dfc2df15ebcc2ada99c277b","2924daf064fef9f13cc714960e532a91f34258db7d935891549ab9d67040740f","239fe13b6a0bc29c0161118018f5e21ae0688d3212263a9c2644c4367d1d26d6","169577a9e1ecaa062a47fb1cd03fd68c6e5f18cfd66ded89d34ab3eb2b267530","308450ed1840fe6cb308eaee50