{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                               spare5, spare4, spare3, spare2, spare1},","paragraph_zero_based":46272},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-PeriodCG2-r16               INTEGER (1..99)","paragraph_zero_based":46273},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":46274},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":46275},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-CONFIGUREDGRANTCONFIG-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":46276},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":46277},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":46278},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-ConfiguredGrantConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":46279},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"rrc-ConfiguredSidelinkGrant","paragraph_zero_based":46280},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Configuration for \"sidelink configured grant\" transmission with fully RRC-configured SL grant (Type1). If this field is not configured, the UE uses SL grant configured by DCI addressed to SL-CS-RNTI (Type2).","paragraph_zero_based":46281},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-ConfigIndexCG","paragraph_zero_based":46282},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the ID to identify sidelink configured grant.","paragraph_zero_based":46283},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-CG-MaxTransNumList","paragraph_zero_based":46284},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the maximum number of times that a TB can be transmitted using the resources provided by the sidelink configured grant. sl-Priority corresponds to the logical channel priority.","paragraph_zero_based":46285},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-FreqResourceCG-Type1","paragraph_zero_based":46286},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the frequency resource location of sidelink configured grant type 1. An index giving valid combinations of one or two starting sub-channel and length (jointly encoded) as resource indicator value (RIV), as defined in TS 38.214 [19].","paragraph_zero_based":46287},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-HARQ-ProcID-Offset","paragraph_zero_based":46288},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the offset used in deriving the HARQ process ID for sidelink configured grant type 1 or sidelink configured grant type 2, see TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.8.3.","paragraph_zero_based":46289},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-N1PUCCH-AN","paragraph_zero_based":46290},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the PUCCH resource for HARQ feedback for sidelink configured grant type 1. The actual PUCCH-Resource is configured in sl-PUCCH-Config and referred to by its ID.","paragraph_zero_based":46291},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-N1PUCCH-AN-Type2","paragraph_zero_based":46292},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the PUCCH resource for HARQ feedback for PSCCH/PSSCH transmissions without a corresponding PDCCH on sidelink configured grant type 2. The actual PUCCH-Resource is configured in sl-PUCCH-Config and referred to by its ID.","paragraph_zero_based":46293},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-NrOfHARQ-Processes","paragraph_zero_based":46294},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the number of HARQ processes configured for a specific sidelink configured grant. It applies for both type 1 and type 2.","paragraph_zero_based":46295}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["6d54f8aaf276a10b4592f4f2d237364d3e594864ad98d122552459477ec7b58e","bcdafc02610841b