{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the slot offset with respect to logical slot defined by sl-TimeReferenceSFN-Type1-Dedicated-SL-PRS-RP, as specified in TS 38.321 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":46344},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-TimeReferenceSFN-Type1","paragraph_zero_based":46345},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates SFN used for determination of the offset of a resource in time domain. If it is present, the UE uses the 1st logical slot of associated resource pool after the starting time of the closest SFN with the indicated number preceding the reception of the sidelink configured grant configuration type 1 as reference logical slot, see TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.8.3. If it is not present, the reference SFN is 0.","paragraph_zero_based":46346},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-TimeResourceCG-Type1","paragraph_zero_based":46347},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the time resource location of sidelink configured grant type 1. An index giving valid combinations of up to two slot positions (jointly encoded) as time resource indicator value (TRIV), as defined in TS 38.212 [17].","paragraph_zero_based":46348},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PRS-ResourceIndicationFirstType1","paragraph_zero_based":46349},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates SL-PRS Resource ID for the first SL-PRS transmission.","paragraph_zero_based":46350},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-PRS-ResourceIndicationFutureType1","paragraph_zero_based":46351},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates SL-PRS resource IDs for future SL PRS transmissions. An index giving valid combinations of up to two SL PRS resource IDs (jointly encoded) .","paragraph_zero_based":46352},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":46353},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-DestinationIdentity","paragraph_zero_based":46354},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-DestinationIdentity is used to identify a destination of a NR sidelink communication.","paragraph_zero_based":46355},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-DestinationIdentity information element","paragraph_zero_based":46356},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":46357},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-DESTINATIONIDENTITY-START","paragraph_zero_based":46358},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":46359},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-DestinationIdentity-r16 ::=           BIT STRING (SIZE (24))","paragraph_zero_based":46360},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":46361},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-DESTINATIONIDENTITY-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":46362},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":46363},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":46364},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-DRX-Config","paragraph_zero_based":46365},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-DRX-Config is used to configure DRX related parameters for NR sidelink communication/discovery. The SL DRX timers should be calculated in the unit of physical slot.","paragraph_zero_based":46366},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-DRX-Config information element","paragraph_zero_based":46367}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["4933c34132f11dd1557e6dc626d3834fde5f5f035c3197b42f5c1563571d459d","4e902462e8e5f5717a31d2e31ab5c76e1547ae1144ef7b39e3ffa140c4a1a4c4","333380c6d770e7389b8d40d1a13e76d338e2cb8666eaa41ed692386694ba9417","e139928753970df687306b821641261539f93461