{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2405601.zip::R2-2405601 Rapp CR for SL relay_update.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-drx-SlotOffset                       INTEGER (0..31)","paragraph_zero_based":46512},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":46513},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":46514},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-DRX-CONFIGUC-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":46515},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":46516},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":46517},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":46518},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-DRX-ConfigUC field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":46519},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-drx-CycleStartOffset","paragraph_zero_based":46520},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Sidelink drx-Cycle in ms and sidelink drx-StartOffset in multiples of 1 ms.","paragraph_zero_based":46521},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-drx-HARQ-RTT-Timer1, sl-drx-HARQ-RTT-Timer2","paragraph_zero_based":46522},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in number of slot lengths of the BWP where the transport block was received. Value sl0 corresponds to 0 slots, sl1 corresponds to 1 slot, sl2 corresponds to 2 slots, and so on. sl-drx-HARQ-RTT-Timer1 is used for HARQ feedback enabled sidelink retransmission if SCI does not indicate retransmission resource(s). sl-drx-HARQ-RTT-Timer2 is used for HARQ feedback disabled sidelink retransmission in resource pool configured with PSFCH if SCI does not indicate retransmission resource(s).","paragraph_zero_based":46523},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-drx-InactivityTimer","paragraph_zero_based":46524},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in number of slot lengths of the BWP where the transport block was received, sl0 corresponds to 0, sl1 corresponds to 1 slot, sl2 corresponds to 2 slots, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":46525},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-drx-onDurationTimer","paragraph_zero_based":46526},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in multiples of 1/32 ms (subMilliSeconds) or in ms (milliSecond). For the latter, value ms1 corresponds to 1 ms, value ms2 corresponds to 2 ms, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":46527},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-drx-RetransmissionTimer","paragraph_zero_based":46528},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in number of slot lengths of the BWP where the transport block was received. Value sl0 corresponds to 0 slots, sl1 corresponds to 1 slot, sl2 corresponds to 2 slots, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":46529},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-drx-SlotOffset","paragraph_zero_based":46530},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in 1/32 ms. Value 0 corresponds to 0 ms, value 1 corresponds to 1/32 ms, value 2 corresponds to 2/32 ms, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":46531},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":46532},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-DRX-ConfigUC-SemiStatic","paragraph_zero_based":46533},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-DRX-ConfigUC-SemiStatic is used to indicate the semi-static sidelink DRX related parameters for unicast communication.","paragraph_zero_based":46534},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-DRX-ConfigUC-SemiStatic information element","paragraph_zero_based":46535}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"9d1d70d9256212d4b7dc322b4b9f040a9786df5e243754184d613f861ae930ed","original_member_sha256":"cf818f4a328fc82c7558ea21f216bee86ef70a3f095c39da9ef1e843f48973c6","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["4ee6401c84e148a34dabf20eb32857037bce22aa64803fd1f81ba9da452db1ca","8ff4f5987f325fe2fa188163c2752cc9c7470c1bb02d90b7c30ad407fcf501f7","21d99ac050cc7f0bf0c3bcb6d518f886ee7607048ee18fe475426d11485d83ad","5f9a82fe4e22eecdcc5341b